{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SNwVMWQKFUtuxLNBbbkSFe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (SchoolHub scaffold PRD)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t## Overview\n6\t\n7\tThis PRD is a greenfield scaffold: Next.js 14 App Router monolith, Postgres\n8\t16 via Prisma, MUI v9 as the sole UI library, centralized API helpers, and a\n9\trole-aware (but auth-unwired) app shell. Intake reported **100% confidence\n10\tand zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is nothing to flag\n11\there beyond that figure. All 48 requirements are HIGH confidence with no\n12\tclarification log entries.\n13\t\n14\tArchitecturally this is one deployable Next.js app with two route-group\n15\ttrees — `(app)` for the authenticated shell and `(public)` for the marketing\n16\tpage — sharing one design-system layer, one API-helper chokepoint\n17\t(`src/server/http.ts`), and one data model (`SchoolSettings`, a singleton\n18\trow later PRDs will extend). Auth does not exist yet: every place a later\n19\tPRD will wire sign-in (user menu, `/forbidden`, nav role-filtering) is built\n20\tas a placeholder/slot only, per the explicit \"for later PRDs\" language in\n21\tFR-33/FR-39 and the cross-cutting note in `requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n22\tNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n23\t(ADR-1 through ADR-9) already fixed — this document arranges those choices\n24\tinto components and data flow.\n25\t\n26\t## Component Breakdown\n27\t\n28\t| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files |\n29\t|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|\n30\t| 1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline, npm script surface, path alias | `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.eslintrc*` |\n31\t| 2 | Server Infra | Env validation, Prisma client singleton, structured logger, local Postgres | `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/server/db.ts`, `src/lib/logger.ts`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` |\n32\t| 3 | Data Model | Singleton `SchoolSettings` schema + idempotent seed | `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts` |\n33\t| 4 | API Layer | Response envelopes, error mapping, pagination/body parsing, the one concrete endpoint | `src/server/http.ts`, `src/app/api/health/route.ts` |\n34\t| 5 | Design System | Theme + provider tree + 10 shared MUI-composed components | `src/theme/theme.ts`, `src/components/*` |\n35\t| 6 | App Shell (authenticated) | Sidebar/top-bar layout, role-filtered nav config, student-tab extension point, dashboard page | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` |\n36\t| 7 | Public Layout & Pages | Public header/footer, landing page, error/forbidden pages | `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/global-error.tsx`, `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` |\n37\t| 8 | Lint/CI Gate | Banned-import ESLint rule, security headers | `.eslintrc*` (`no-restricted-imports`), `next.config.js` |\n38\t| 9 | Test Harness | Unit/component + e2e/axe coverage of the above | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` |\n39\t\n40\tDependency order between components: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, and 1+2 → 5 → 6/7 (the\n41\tshell and public layout both consume the design system and, for branding,\n42\t`SchoolSettings` from component 3). Component 8 wraps all of 5–7. Component\n43\t9 observes all of 2–7.\n44\t\n45\t## Data Flow\n46\t\n47\t**Page render (authenticated), e.g. `GET /dashboard`:**\n48\t1. `(app)/layout.tsx` (server component) fetches the `SchoolSettings`\n49\t   singleton once (FR-7) for top-bar branding (FR-33) — not re-queried by\n50\t   child components.\n51\t2. Root layout's provider tree (`AppRouterCacheProvider` → `ThemeProvider`\n52\t   (`cssVariables`, light/dark) → `CssBaseline` → `LocalizationProvider`,\n53\t   plus `InitColorSchemeScript`) wraps the shell so every page below inherits\n54\t   theme/mode without a client-side flash (NFR-2's LCP budget depends on\n55\t   this being server-rendered, not client-hydrated).\n56\t3. Sidebar renders from `src/config/navigation.ts`, filtered by current\n57\t   user role (role source is a stub today — no auth yet — filtering logic\n58\t   exists so later PRDs plug a real role in without touching the shell).\n59\t4. `/dashboard` page renders `PageHeader` + `EmptyState` (FR-34) — no data\n60\t   fetch beyond step 1.\n61\t\n62\t**API call, e.g. a future list endpoint or `GET /api/health`:**\n63\t1. Route handler is wrapped in `withHandler(fn)` (ADR-4) — the single\n64\t   chokepoint every route (including `/api/health`) must go through.\n65\t2. Input parsing: `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (Zod) for request shape,\n66\t   `parsePagination` for list endpoints (clamps `pageSize` ≤ 100, `page` ≥ 1).\n67\t3. Handler body runs (for `/api/health`: `SELECT 1` against Prisma with a\n68\t   2000ms budget).\n69\t4. Success → `ok(data)` or `paginated(data, meta)`; failure inside\n70\t   `withHandler` maps `ZodError` → `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `AppError` → its\n71\t   status, Prisma `P2002`/`P2025` → `CONFLICT`/`NOT_FOUND`, anything else →\n72\t   `INTERNAL` (stack logged via `src/lib/logger.ts`, never returned to the\n73\t   client).\n74\t5. Client-side, `DataTable` (for list endpoints) reads `rowCount`/`total`\n75\t   straight from the `paginated()` envelope and syncs page/sort state to URL\n76\t   query params — no separate client-side pagination state machine.\n77\t\n78\t**Env/startup flow:** `src/lib/env.ts` validates `process.env` via Zod\n79\tbefore `src/server/db.ts` or any server entrypoint runs, throwing a\n80\treadable per-variable error on failure — this is a fail-fast boundary, not\n81\ta runtime-checked one.\n82\t\n83\t## Requirements Traceability\n84\t\n85\t| Requirement | Design Element |\n86\t|---|---|\n87\t| FR-1 | Component 1 — Scaffold/Tooling |\n88\t| FR-2 | Component 1 — npm script surface |\n89\t| FR-3 | Component 1 — `tsconfig.json` path alias |\n90\t| FR-4 | Component 2 — `docker-compose.yml` |\n91\t| FR-5 | Component 2 — `.env.example` |\n92\t| FR-6 | Component 2 — `src/lib/env.ts` (startup flow) |\n93\t| FR-7 | Component 3 — `prisma/schema.prisma` (`SchoolSettings`) |\n94\t| FR-8 | Component 2 — `src/server/db.ts` singleton |\n95\t| FR-9 | Component 3 — `prisma/seed.ts` |\n96\t| FR-10 | Component 4 — `ok()` |\n97\t| FR-11 | Component 4 — `paginated()` |\n98\t| FR-12 | Component 4 — `apiError()` |\n99\t| FR-13 | Component 4 — `withHandler()` (API call flow step 1/4) |\n100\t| FR-14 | Component 4 — `parsePagination()` |\n101\t| FR-15 | Component 4 — `parseBody`/`parseQuery` |\n102\t| FR-16 | Component 4 — `GET /api/health` |\n103\t| FR-17 | Component 5 — MUI package set (dependency, see ADR-5) |\n104\t| FR-18 | Component 5 — `theme.ts` + provider tree (page render flow step 2) |\n105\t| FR-19 | Component 8 — ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |\n106\t| FR-20 | Component 5 — `PageHeader` |\n107\t| FR-21 | Component 5 — `DataTable` (API call flow step 5) |\n108\t| FR-22 | Component 5 — `EmptyState` |\n109\t| FR-23 | Component 5 — `ConfirmDialog` |\n110\t| FR-24 | Component 5 — `useToast`/`ToastProvider` |\n111\t| FR-25 | Component 5 — `FormField` helpers |\n112\t| FR-26 | Component 5 — `StatCard` |\n113\t| FR-27 | Component 5 — `UserAvatar` |\n114\t| FR-28 | Component 5 — `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz` (reads `SchoolSettings` tz) |\n115\t| FR-29 | Component 5 — `LoadingSkeleton` |\n116\t| FR-30 | Component 6 — `(app)/layout.tsx` sidebar/top bar |\n117\t| FR-31 | Component 6 — responsive Drawer fork (<1024px) |\n118\t| FR-32 | Component 6 — `src/config/navigation.ts` (page render flow step 3) |\n119\t| FR-33 | Component 6 — top bar branding + user-menu/bell placeholders (auth slot, not wired) |\n120\t| FR-34 | Component 6 — `/dashboard` page (page render flow step 4) |\n121\t| FR-35 | Component 6 — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` extension point |\n122\t| FR-36 | Component 7 — `(public)/layout.tsx` |\n123\t| FR-37 | Component 7 — `/` landing page |\n124\t| FR-38 | Component 7 — `not-found.tsx`/`error.tsx`/`global-error.tsx` |\n125\t| FR-39 | Component 7 — `/forbidden` (auth slot, not wired) |\n126\t| FR-40 | Component 2 — `src/lib/logger.ts` (API call flow step 4) |\n127\t| NFR-1 | Component 8 — MUI-only enforcement (ESLint + MCP-docs process constraint) |\n128\t| NFR-2 | Component 5 + 6 — server-rendered provider tree, no client-side theme flash |\n129\t| NFR-3 | Component 5 + 9 — WCAG AA on shared components, axe-core e2e gate |\n130\t| NFR-4 | Component 6 — responsive shell (360–1920px), generalizes FR-31 |\n131\t| NFR-5 | Component 8 — `next.config.js` security headers |\n132\t| NFR-6 | Component 9 — Vitest/Testing Library + Playwright coverage |\n133\t| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 2 + 3 — fresh-clone bring-up script chain |\n134\t| NFR-8 | Component 8 + 9 — lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e CI gate |\n135\t\n136\t## Status\n137\t\n138\tComplete. All 48 requirement ids are accounted for above; none were dropped.\n139\tNo blockers to carry forward — `arch-api-contracts` can proceed directly to\n140\tderiving the API surface (in practice, just `/api/health` plus the envelope\n141\tcontract every future endpoint must follow).\n142\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b08d788a-3383-488c-88d0-dd68d0d8833c","uuid":"fc1d8474-2a8b-4898-94a8-8a6a193eff58","timestamp":"2026-10-16T15:14:24.645Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (SchoolHub scaffold PRD)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nThis PRD is a greenfield scaffold: Next.js 14 App Router monolith, Postgres\n16 via Prisma, MUI v9 as the sole UI library, centralized API helpers, and a\nrole-aware (but auth-unwired) app shell. Intake reported **100% confidence\nand zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is nothing to flag\nhere beyond that figure. All 48 requirements are HIGH confidence with no\nclarification log entries.\n\nArchitecturally this is one deployable Next.js app with two route-group\ntrees — `(app)` for the authenticated shell and `(public)` for the marketing\npage — sharing one design-system layer, one API-helper chokepoint\n(`src/server/http.ts`), and one data model (`SchoolSettings`, a singleton\nrow later PRDs will extend). Auth does not exist yet: every place a later\nPRD will wire sign-in (user menu, `/forbidden`, nav role-filtering) is built\nas a placeholder/slot only, per the explicit \"for later PRDs\" language in\nFR-33/FR-39 and the cross-cutting note in `requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\nNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9) already fixed — this document arranges those choices\ninto components and data flow.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|\n| 1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline, npm script surface, path alias | `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.eslintrc*` |\n| 2 | Server Infra | Env validation, Prisma client singleton, structured logger, local Postgres | `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/server/db.ts`, `src/lib/logger.ts`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` |\n| 3 | Data Model | Singleton `SchoolSettings` schema + idempotent seed | `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| 4 | API Layer | Response envelopes, error mapping, pagination/body parsing, the one concrete endpoint | `src/server/http.ts`, `src/app/api/health/route.ts` |\n| 5 | Design System | Theme + provider tree + 10 shared MUI-composed components | `src/theme/theme.ts`, `src/components/*` |\n| 6 | App Shell (authenticated) | Sidebar/top-bar layout, role-filtered nav config, student-tab extension point, dashboard page | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` |\n| 7 | Public Layout & Pages | Public header/footer, landing page, error/forbidden pages | `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/global-error.tsx`, `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` |\n| 8 | Lint/CI Gate | Banned-import ESLint rule, security headers | `.eslintrc*` (`no-restricted-imports`), `next.config.js` |\n| 9 | Test Harness | Unit/component + e2e/axe coverage of the above | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` |\n\nDependency order between components: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, and 1+2 → 5 → 6/7 (the\nshell and public layout both consume the design system and, for branding,\n`SchoolSettings` from component 3). Component 8 wraps all of 5–7. Component\n9 observes all of 2–7.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Page render (authenticated), e.g. `GET /dashboard`:**\n1. `(app)/layout.tsx` (server component) fetches the `SchoolSettings`\n   singleton once (FR-7) for top-bar branding (FR-33) — not re-queried by\n   child components.\n2. Root layout's provider tree (`AppRouterCacheProvider` → `ThemeProvider`\n   (`cssVariables`, light/dark) → `CssBaseline` → `LocalizationProvider`,\n   plus `InitColorSchemeScript`) wraps the shell so every page below inherits\n   theme/mode without a client-side flash (NFR-2's LCP budget depends on\n   this being server-rendered, not client-hydrated).\n3. Sidebar renders from `src/config/navigation.ts`, filtered by current\n   user role (role source is a stub today — no auth yet — filtering logic\n   exists so later PRDs plug a real role in without touching the shell).\n4. `/dashboard` page renders `PageHeader` + `EmptyState` (FR-34) — no data\n   fetch beyond step 1.\n\n**API call, e.g. a future list endpoint or `GET /api/health`:**\n1. Route handler is wrapped in `withHandler(fn)` (ADR-4) — the single\n   chokepoint every route (including `/api/health`) must go through.\n2. Input parsing: `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (Zod) for request shape,\n   `parsePagination` for list endpoints (clamps `pageSize` ≤ 100, `page` ≥ 1).\n3. Handler body runs (for `/api/health`: `SELECT 1` against Prisma with a\n   2000ms budget).\n4. Success → `ok(data)` or `paginated(data, meta)`; failure inside\n   `withHandler` maps `ZodError` → `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `AppError` → its\n   status, Prisma `P2002`/`P2025` → `CONFLICT`/`NOT_FOUND`, anything else →\n   `INTERNAL` (stack logged via `src/lib/logger.ts`, never returned to the\n   client).\n5. Client-side, `DataTable` (for list endpoints) reads `rowCount`/`total`\n   straight from the `paginated()` envelope and syncs page/sort state to URL\n   query params — no separate client-side pagination state machine.\n\n**Env/startup flow:** `src/lib/env.ts` validates `process.env` via Zod\nbefore `src/server/db.ts` or any server entrypoint runs, throwing a\nreadable per-variable error on failure — this is a fail-fast boundary, not\na runtime-checked one.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Scaffold/Tooling |\n| FR-2 | Component 1 — npm script surface |\n| FR-3 | Component 1 — `tsconfig.json` path alias |\n| FR-4 | Component 2 — `docker-compose.yml` |\n| FR-5 | Component 2 — `.env.example` |\n| FR-6 | Component 2 — `src/lib/env.ts` (startup flow) |\n| FR-7 | Component 3 — `prisma/schema.prisma` (`SchoolSettings`) |\n| FR-8 | Component 2 — `src/server/db.ts` singleton |\n| FR-9 | Component 3 — `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| FR-10 | Component 4 — `ok()` |\n| FR-11 | Component 4 — `paginated()` |\n| FR-12 | Component 4 — `apiError()` |\n| FR-13 | Component 4 — `withHandler()` (API call flow step 1/4) |\n| FR-14 | Component 4 — `parsePagination()` |\n| FR-15 | Component 4 — `parseBody`/`parseQuery` |\n| FR-16 | Component 4 — `GET /api/health` |\n| FR-17 | Component 5 — MUI package set (dependency, see ADR-5) |\n| FR-18 | Component 5 — `theme.ts` + provider tree (page render flow step 2) |\n| FR-19 | Component 8 — ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |\n| FR-20 | Component 5 — `PageHeader` |\n| FR-21 | Component 5 — `DataTable` (API call flow step 5) |\n| FR-22 | Component 5 — `EmptyState` |\n| FR-23 | Component 5 — `ConfirmDialog` |\n| FR-24 | Component 5 — `useToast`/`ToastProvider` |\n| FR-25 | Component 5 — `FormField` helpers |\n| FR-26 | Component 5 — `StatCard` |\n| FR-27 | Component 5 — `UserAvatar` |\n| FR-28 | Component 5 — `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz` (reads `SchoolSettings` tz) |\n| FR-29 | Component 5 — `LoadingSkeleton` |\n| FR-30 | Component 6 — `(app)/layout.tsx` sidebar/top bar |\n| FR-31 | Component 6 — responsive Drawer fork (<1024px) |\n| FR-32 | Component 6 — `src/config/navigation.ts` (page render flow step 3) |\n| FR-33 | Component 6 — top bar branding + user-menu/bell placeholders (auth slot, not wired) |\n| FR-34 | Component 6 — `/dashboard` page (page render flow step 4) |\n| FR-35 | Component 6 — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` extension point |\n| FR-36 | Component 7 — `(public)/layout.tsx` |\n| FR-37 | Component 7 — `/` landing page |\n| FR-38 | Component 7 — `not-found.tsx`/`error.tsx`/`global-error.tsx` |\n| FR-39 | Component 7 — `/forbidden` (auth slot, not wired) |\n| FR-40 | Component 2 — `src/lib/logger.ts` (API call flow step 4) |\n| NFR-1 | Component 8 — MUI-only enforcement (ESLint + MCP-docs process constraint) |\n| NFR-2 | Component 5 + 6 — server-rendered provider tree, no client-side theme flash |\n| NFR-3 | Component 5 + 9 — WCAG AA on shared components, axe-core e2e gate |\n| NFR-4 | Component 6 — responsive shell (360–1920px), generalizes FR-31 |\n| NFR-5 | Component 8 — `next.config.js` security headers |\n| NFR-6 | Component 9 — Vitest/Testing Library + Playwright coverage |\n| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 2 + 3 — fresh-clone bring-up script chain |\n| NFR-8 | Component 8 + 9 — lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e CI gate |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 48 requirement ids are accounted for above; none were dropped.\nNo blockers to carry forward — `arch-api-contracts` can proceed directly to\nderiving the API surface (in practice, just `/api/health` plus the envelope\ncontract every future endpoint must follow).\n","numLines":142,"startLine":1,"totalLines":142}}}
