{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012jYXxqp5GBcLwehigwX9BN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 requirements, 100% confidence, no blockers).\n5\t\n6\tArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Scaffold/Tooling**, **Data Model**,\n7\t**Server Infra** (DB/env/logging), **API Layer**, **Design System /\n8\tComponent Library**, **App Shell / Layout**, **Routing / Pages**, **Auth\n9\tBoundary (future)**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Test Harness**.\n10\t\n11\t## Functional Requirements\n12\t\n13\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n14\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n15\t| FR-1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline. Drives every other decision's toolchain compatibility (e.g. MUI v9 + React 18 pairing). |\n16\t| FR-2 | Scaffold/Tooling | npm script surface is a contract other phases (dev-planning, CI) will invoke by name — must exist verbatim. |\n17\t| FR-3 | Scaffold/Tooling | `tsconfig.json` path alias; affects every import statement generated in later phases. |\n18\t| FR-4 | Server Infra | `docker-compose.yml` Postgres 16 service — local dev dependency, no app code, but gates NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up). |\n19\t| FR-5 | Server Infra | `.env.example` is the single source of truth for required env vars; must stay in sync with FR-6's Zod schema. |\n20\t| FR-6 | Server Infra | `src/lib/env.ts` — startup validation boundary. Fail-fast module, imported by `src/server/db.ts` and any server entrypoint. |\n21\t| FR-7 | Data Model | `prisma/schema.prisma`, singleton `SchoolSettings` model. First schema entity; later PRDs will add models but this phase only needs this one. |\n22\t| FR-8 | Server Infra | `src/server/db.ts` — Prisma client singleton pattern (globalThis cache) to survive Next.js dev hot-reload. Shared by every API route. |\n23\t| FR-9 | Data Model | `prisma/seed.ts` idempotent seed — upsert semantics on `SchoolSettings`, run by `db:seed` script from FR-2. |\n24\t| FR-10 | API Layer | `ok()` helper — standard success envelope `{ data }` used by every GET/POST handler. |\n25\t| FR-11 | API Layer | `paginated()` helper — list-response envelope; depends on FR-14's pagination parsing shape. |\n26\t| FR-12 | API Layer | `apiError()` + status-code mapping table — standard error envelope, consumed by `withHandler` (FR-13) and by client-side error handling conventions later phases will rely on. |\n27\t| FR-13 | API Layer | `withHandler(fn)` — centralized error-boundary wrapper for route handlers (Zod → VALIDATION_ERROR, AppError → mapped status, Prisma P2002/P2025 → CONFLICT/NOT_FOUND, else INTERNAL). This is the one chokepoint every API route must go through — key reuse surface for api-contracts phase. |\n28\t| FR-14 | API Layer | `parsePagination()` — query-param parsing/clamping, shared by all list endpoints. |\n29\t| FR-15 | API Layer | `parseBody()` / `parseQuery()` — Zod-backed request parsing, paired with `withHandler`'s ZodError branch. |\n30\t| FR-16 | API Layer | `GET /api/health` — first concrete endpoint; exercises DB connectivity (`SELECT 1`) with a 2000ms timeout and the `ok`/error envelope from FR-10/12. This is the only endpoint `arch-api-contracts` has a hard requirement to define. |\n31\t| FR-17 | Design System | MUI v9 package set + React 18 override (`react-is@18.3.1`) — dependency/version decision, belongs in tech-stack ADR, not design doc. |\n32\t| FR-18 | Design System | `theme.ts` (cssVariables, light/dark colorSchemes) + root layout provider stack (`AppRouterCacheProvider` + `ThemeProvider` + `CssBaseline` + `LocalizationProvider`) + `InitColorSchemeScript` + `useColorScheme()` toggle. Cross-cutting: every page renders inside this provider tree. |\n33\t| FR-19 | Lint/CI Gate | ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banning non-MUI UI libs; build-breaking rule, ties directly to NFR-1. No Tailwind config may exist. |\n34\t| FR-20 | Design System | `PageHeader` shared component — used by `/dashboard` (FR-34) and every future page. |\n35\t| FR-21 | Design System | `DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid wrapper) — server-side pagination/sort/search/URL-sync; the heaviest shared component, depends on API list-response shape (FR-11/14) for `rowCount`/`total`. |\n36\t| FR-22 | Design System | `EmptyState` shared component — used by `/dashboard` (FR-34). |\n37\t| FR-23 | Design System | `ConfirmDialog` shared component — async confirm + pending spinner, generic destructive-action pattern for later PRDs. |\n38\t| FR-24 | Design System | `useToast()` + `ToastProvider` — single queued Snackbar/Alert; a global provider mounted once near the root layout. |\n39\t| FR-25 | Design System | `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form `Controller` to MUI inputs — shared form-binding layer every future CRUD form in later PRDs will use. |\n40\t| FR-26 | Design System | `StatCard` shared component — card/label/value/delta/icon, dashboard-oriented. |\n41\t| FR-27 | Design System | `UserAvatar` shared component — deterministic colour from user id; no auth dependency yet, just a pure function + Avatar. |\n42\t| FR-28 | Design System | `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz()` util (`src/lib/dates.ts`) — school-timezone-aware date formatting, depends on `SchoolSettings` (FR-7) holding the timezone. |\n43\t| FR-29 | Design System | `LoadingSkeleton` shared component — table/card/form variants. |\n44\t| FR-30 | App Shell / Layout | `(app)/layout.tsx` — permanent/collapsible sidebar Drawer + AppBar/Toolbar top bar; collapse state persisted to localStorage. Root authenticated-app shell. |\n45\t| FR-31 | App Shell / Layout | Responsive breakpoint (<1024px) swaps sidebar to temporary Drawer — same shell, behavior fork on viewport, ties to NFR-4. |\n46\t| FR-32 | App Shell / Layout | `src/config/navigation.ts` — role-filtered nav item config, active-item highlighting by path prefix. Config-driven, not hardcoded — this is the extension point later PRDs add routes to. |\n47\t| FR-33 | App Shell / Layout | Top bar: school branding (from `SchoolSettings`), theme toggle (FR-18), notification bell placeholder, user menu placeholder. Explicitly flags Profile/Sign-out as **future auth boundary** for PRD-01/03/04 — this phase builds the slot, not the wiring. |\n48\t| FR-34 | Routing / Pages | `/dashboard` page — `PageHeader` + `EmptyState`, first concrete page in the `(app)` route group. |\n49\t| FR-35 | Routing / Pages | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` — empty typed extension-point array for later PRDs to register into. Config-only, no UI yet. |\n50\t| FR-36 | App Shell / Layout | `(public)/layout.tsx` — public header/footer, `SchoolSettings`-driven contact info. Separate layout tree from `(app)` — route-group boundary. |\n51\t| FR-37 | Routing / Pages | `/` public landing page — hero + Sign-in CTA, lives under `(public)` layout. |\n52\t| FR-38 | Routing / Pages | `not-found.tsx` / `error.tsx` (reset()) / `global-error.tsx` — Next.js App Router convention files, app-wide error boundaries. |\n53\t| FR-39 | Routing / Pages | `/forbidden` page — 403 UI, reserved for later PRDs' auth-boundary redirects. |\n54\t| FR-40 | Server Infra | `src/lib/logger.ts` — structured JSON logs in prod, readable in dev. Consumed by `withHandler`'s INTERNAL-error branch (FR-13) for stack logging. |\n55\t\n56\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n57\t\n58\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n59\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n60\t| NFR-1 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only UI library constraint, enforced by the FR-19 ESLint rule; also a process constraint (MUI MCP docs lookup before using any component) that doesn't map to code but should be called out in the design doc's Overview. |\n61\t| NFR-2 | App Shell / Layout + Design System | LCP < 2.5s on `/dashboard` — constrains theme/provider setup (FR-18) and shared component weight (avoid heavy client-side work on first paint); informs server-vs-client component split. |\n62\t| NFR-3 | Design System | WCAG 2.1 AA across shared components + axe-core Playwright checks on `/` and `/dashboard`. Cross-cutting acceptance criterion for every component in FR-20–29. |\n63\t| NFR-4 | App Shell / Layout | 360px–1920px responsive range, no horizontal scroll — generalizes FR-31's breakpoint fork to the whole shell and all pages. |\n64\t| NFR-5 | Server Infra | `next.config.js` security headers (nosniff, Referrer-Policy, X-Frame-Options, CSP) — app-wide config, not component-level. |\n65\t| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest+Testing Library (unit/component) + Playwright (e2e) covering `withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `formatInSchoolTz`, `env.ts`, `DataTable`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast`, the ESLint rule, and axe scenarios. Defines the test-surface boundary `arch-design-system` should make testable (pure functions, isolated handlers). |\n66\t| NFR-7 | Scaffold/Tooling | Fresh-clone bring-up in <5 min via `docker compose up -d && npm install && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed && npm run dev` — validates FR-2/4/9's script wiring end-to-end; no new design element, just an acceptance gate. |\n67\t| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | `lint`/`typecheck`/`test`/`test:e2e` must all pass on fresh clone — ties FR-2's scripts to NFR-6's test harness as the CI gate. |\n68\t\n69\t## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n70\t\n71\t- **Auth is explicitly out of scope** for this phase (FR-33, FR-39 both say \"for later wiring by PRD-01/03/04\"). Design the user-menu/forbidden-page slots as placeholders only — do not invent an auth system to satisfy them.\n72\t- **`SchoolSettings` is a shared read dependency** across FR-28 (timezone), FR-33/36 (branding, contact info) — single singleton row, likely fetched once per request/layout, not re-queried per component.\n73\t- **`withHandler` + `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError` (FR-10–15) is the one mandatory API chokepoint** — `arch-api-contracts` should route every endpoint (including `/api/health`) through it.\n74\t- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond the 100% confidence figure.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b08d788a-3383-488c-88d0-dd68d0d8833c","uuid":"5ec68811-b04f-469e-a5ac-dad6f0f18915","timestamp":"2026-10-16T15:14:30.278Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 requirements, 100% confidence, no blockers).\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Scaffold/Tooling**, **Data Model**,\n**Server Infra** (DB/env/logging), **API Layer**, **Design System /\nComponent Library**, **App Shell / Layout**, **Routing / Pages**, **Auth\nBoundary (future)**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Test Harness**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline. Drives every other decision's toolchain compatibility (e.g. MUI v9 + React 18 pairing). |\n| FR-2 | Scaffold/Tooling | npm script surface is a contract other phases (dev-planning, CI) will invoke by name — must exist verbatim. |\n| FR-3 | Scaffold/Tooling | `tsconfig.json` path alias; affects every import statement generated in later phases. |\n| FR-4 | Server Infra | `docker-compose.yml` Postgres 16 service — local dev dependency, no app code, but gates NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up). |\n| FR-5 | Server Infra | `.env.example` is the single source of truth for required env vars; must stay in sync with FR-6's Zod schema. |\n| FR-6 | Server Infra | `src/lib/env.ts` — start