{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Ur5npe2Yz4ZM85VarMT79","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T21:45:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"sharedEnvelope\": {\n8\t    \"description\": \"Two families of endpoint exist in this PRD. (1) Auth.js (NextAuth v5)'s own catch-all route (/api/auth/callback/credentials, /api/auth/session, /api/auth/signout, /api/auth/csrf) — its request/response wire format is owned by the library, not src/server/http.ts, and is documented per-endpoint below only at the level dev-planning needs (inputs, outcomes, which FRs they satisfy). (2) Four new form-submission endpoints (invite/accept, forgot-password, reset-password, change-password) that are genuinely ours and MUST route through the existing src/server/http.ts chokepoint (ok/apiError/withHandler/parseBody) per NFR-7 — no parallel envelope. That chokepoint's ApiErrorCode union currently only has VALIDATION_ERROR/NOT_FOUND/CONFLICT/INTERNAL (see src/server/http.ts); this PRD needs three more values, which dev-planning/dev must EXTEND that union and errorCodeToStatus map with, not fork a second error-mapping file.\",\n9\t    \"success\": { \"data\": \"<payload>\" },\n10\t    \"error\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object (optional)\" } },\n11\t    \"errorCodeToStatus\": {\n12\t      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n13\t      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n14\t      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n15\t      \"INTERNAL\": 500,\n16\t      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n17\t      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n18\t      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"newErrorCodesForThisPrd\": {\n21\t      \"RATE_LIMITED\": \"Sign-in and forgot-password rate limiters (FR-6, FR-17) short-circuit to this before any DB work.\",\n22\t      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": \"Defense-in-depth on change-password's requireUser() guard (FR-20, FR-23) — middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests, this is the handler-level backstop.\",\n23\t      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": \"Invite/reset token is missing, wrong type, expired, or already used (FR-12, FR-18, FR-19) — distinct from NOT_FOUND because the token row may exist but be unusable; mapped to 410 Gone.\"\n24\t    },\n25\t    \"notModeledAsEndpoints\": \"Component 9's service functions (createUser, createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser — FR-22) are an internal module surface called by prisma/seed.ts (FR-28) and by later PRDs' admin UI, not by any form in this PRD. No endpoint is defined for them here; inventing an admin API now would be scope creep past NFR-8. Likewise /invite/[token] and /reset-password/[token]'s GET render (token validity check for FR-12) happens inside the Server Component itself via a direct Prisma lookup, not a client-side API call — no GET endpoint is defined for that for the same reason.\",\n26\t    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n27\t  },\n28\t\n29\t  \"endpoints\": [\n30\t    {\n31\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n32\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n33\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider callback, invoked internally by signIn('credentials') from the /login page. Runs the authorize() chokepoint: rate-limit check (10/IP/5min) before any DB work, email normalize, status/lockout branch (dummy bcrypt-compare for timing safety on a non-existent user), bcrypt compare (cost 12), failedLoginCount/lockedUntil mutation, audit() writes, and on success stamps id/role/firstName/lastName/email into the JWT. Wire format (form-encoded body, redirect-based response) is owned by Auth.js, not src/server/http.ts.\",\n34\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n35\t        \"email\": \"string\",\n36\t        \"password\": \"string\",\n37\t        \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\",\n38\t        \"callbackUrl\": \"string\"\n39\t      },\n40\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n41\t        \"redirectSuccess\": \"same-origin callbackUrl if relative, else /dashboard (FR-7)\",\n42\t        \"redirectFailure\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — same generic message for unknown-user and wrong-password (FR-4)\",\n43\t        \"redirectLocked\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — locked-account message includes remaining minutes (FR-4)\",\n44\t        \"redirectDisabled\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — distinct disabled-account message (FR-4)\",\n45\t        \"redirectRateLimited\": \"/login?error=RateLimited — 'Too many attempts' message (FR-6)\"\n46\t      },\n47\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\"]\n48\t    },\n49\t    {\n50\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n51\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n52\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js session read. The jwt callback applies the passwordChangedAt invalidation check (throttled to once per 5 minutes per token) before returning session.user; a token issued before the latest passwordChangedAt comes back null, forcing re-login on that device.\",\n53\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n54\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n55\t        \"data\": {\n56\t          \"user\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\" }\n57\t        },\n58\t        \"orNull\": \"null when unauthenticated or invalidated by passwordChangedAt\"\n59\t      },\n60\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n61\t    },\n62\t    {\n63\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n64\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n65\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out, clears the session cookie. Invoked by the top-bar user menu's 'Sign out' action, which then redirects to /login.\",\n66\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\" },\n67\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"redirect\": \"/login\" },\n68\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\"]\n69\t    },\n70\t    {\n71\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n72\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n73\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token issuance, consumed by every auth form (sign-in, sign-out, and this PRD's own POST endpoints reuse the same Auth.js session's CSRF protection) per NFR-1.\",\n74\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n75\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string\" },\n76\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-1\"]\n77\t    },\n78\t    {\n79\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n80\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/invite/accept\",\n81\t      \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit from /invite/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash of the submitted token (must be type INVITE, unused, within 7-day expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, then as one service-layer step: hashes it, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, marks the token used, signs the user in, and audits auth.invite.accepted — kept atomic so a failure partway doesn't leave a used token with no activated account.\",\n82\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n83\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n84\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/dashboard\" } },\n85\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n86\t        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n87\t      },\n88\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]\n89\t    },\n90\t    {\n91\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n92\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n93\t      \"description\": \"Always responds 200 with the same generic message regardless of whether the account exists (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2's intent). Rate-limited 3/email/hr and 10/IP/hr via component 3's limiter — the limiter key is the submitted email/IP itself, not account existence, so a 429 here doesn't leak whether an account exists. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issues a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry), revokes that user's older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\",\n94\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"email\": \"string\" },\n95\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n96\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } },\n97\t        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Try again later.\" } }\n98\t      },\n99\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\"]\n100\t    },\n101\t    {\n102\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n103\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n104\t      \"description\": \"Submit from /reset-password/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash (must be type PASSWORD_RESET, unused, within 60-min expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, sets the new hash and passwordChangedAt, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, marks the token used, and audits auth.password.reset.\",\n105\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n106\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n107\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/login\" } },\n108\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n109\t        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n110\t      },\n111\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-19\"]\n112\t    },\n113\t    {\n114\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n115\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/change-password\",\n116\t      \"description\": \"Submit from /account/security, behind requireUser() (FR-23) — the route handler re-checks the session as a backstop even though middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests. Checks the current password against the stored hash (wrong value is a field-level VALIDATION_ERROR, not a generic failure), validates the new password against the shared policy module, bumps passwordChangedAt (invalidating every other session via the jwt callback's check), and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out by their own action.\",\n117\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"currentPassword\": \"string\", \"newPassword\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n118\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n119\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"Password updated.\" } },\n120\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n121\t        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"message\": \"string\" } }\n122\t      },\n123\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\"]\n124\t    }\n125\t  ],\n126\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n127\t}\n128\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6825f64-e470-4bad-a0ff-8e48240e2db1","uuid":"50607e5d-14af-4753-978d-151c46808f00","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:42:06.473Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T21:45:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"sharedEnvelope\": {\n    \"description\": \"Two families of endpoint exist in this PRD. (1) Auth.js (NextAuth v5)'s own catch-all route (/api/auth/callback/credentials, /api/auth/session, /api/auth/signout, /api/auth/csrf) — its request/response wire format is owned by the library, not src/server/http.ts, and is documented per-endpoint below only at the level dev-planning needs (inputs, outcomes, which FRs they satisfy). (2) Four new form-submission endpoints (invite/accept, forgot-password, reset-password, change-password) that are genuinely ours and MUST route through the existing src/server/http.ts chokepoint (ok/apiError/withHandler/parseBody) per NFR-7 — no parallel envelope. That chokepoint's ApiErrorCode union currently only has VALIDATION_ERROR/NOT_FOUND/CONFLICT/INTERNAL (see src/server/http.ts); this PRD needs three more values, which dev-planning/dev must EXTEND that union and errorCodeToStatus map with, not fork a second error-mapping file.\",\n    \"success\": { \"data\": \"<payload>\" },\n    \"error\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object (optional)\" } },\n    \"errorCodeToStatus\": {\n      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n      \"INTERNAL\": 500,\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410\n    },\n    \"newErrorCodesForThisPrd\": {\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": \"Sign-in and forgot-password rate limiters (FR-6, FR-17) short-circuit to this before any DB work.\",\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": \"Defense-in-depth on change-password's requireUser() guard (FR-20, FR-23) — middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests, this is the handler-level backstop.\",\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": \"Invite/reset token is missing, wrong type, expired, or already used (FR-12, FR-18, FR-19) — distinct from NOT_FOUND because the token row may exist but be unusable; mapped to 410 Gone.\"\n    },\n    \"notModeledAsEndpoints\": \"Component 9's service functions (createUser, createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser — FR-22) are an internal module surface called by prisma/seed.ts (FR-28) and by later PRDs' admin UI, not by any form in this PRD. No endpoint is defined for them here; inventing an admin API now would be scope creep past NFR-8. Likewise /invite/[token] and /reset-password/[token]'s GET render (token validity check for FR-12) happens inside the Server Component itself via a direct Prisma lookup, not a client-side API call — no GET endpoint is defined for that for the same reason.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider callback, invoked internally by signIn('credentials') from the /login page. Runs the authorize() chokepoint: rate-limit check (10/IP/5min) before any DB work, email normalize, status/lockout branch (dummy bcrypt-compare for timing safety on a non-existent user), bcrypt compare (cost 12), failedLoginCount/lockedUntil mutation, audit() writes, and on success stamps id/role/firstName/lastName/email into the JWT. Wire format (form-encoded body, redirect-based response) is owned by Auth.js, not src/server/http.ts.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"email\": \"string\",\n        \"password\": \"string\",\n        \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\",\n        \"callbackUrl\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"redirectSuccess\": \"same-origin callbackUrl if relative, else /dashboard (FR-7)\",\n        \"redirectFailure\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — same generic message for unknown-user and wrong-password (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectLocked\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — locked-account message includes remaining minutes (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectDisabled\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — distinct disabled-account message (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectRateLimited\": \"/login?error=RateLimited — 'Too many attempts' message (FR-6)\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js session read. The jwt callback applies the passwordChangedAt invalidation check (throttled to once per 5 minutes per token) before returning session.user; a token issued before the latest passwordChangedAt comes back null, forcing re-login on that device.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"data\": {\n          \"user\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"orNull\": \"null when unauthenticated or invalidated by passwordChangedAt\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out, clears the session cookie. Invoked by the top-bar user menu's 'Sign out' action, which then redirects to /login.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"redirect\": \"/login\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token issuance, consumed by every auth form (sign-in, sign-out, and this PRD's own POST endpoints reuse the same Auth.js session's CSRF protection) per NFR-1.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/invite/accept\",\n      \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit from /invite/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash of the submitted token (must be type INVITE, unused, within 7-day expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, then as one service-layer step: hashes it, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, marks the token used, signs the user in, and audits auth.invite.accepted — kept atomic so a failure partway doesn't leave a used token with no activated account.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/dashboard\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Always responds 200 with the same generic message regardless of whether the account exists (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2's intent). Rate-limited 3/email/hr and 10/IP/hr via component 3's limiter — the limiter key is the submitted email/IP itself, not account existence, so a 429 here doesn't leak whether an account exists. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issues a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry), revokes that user's older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"email\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } },\n        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Try again later.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit from /reset-password/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash (must be type PASSWORD_RESET, unused, within 60-min expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, sets the new hash and passwordChangedAt, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, marks the token used, and audits auth.password.reset.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/login\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-19\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/change-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit from /account/security, behind requireUser() (FR-23) — the route handler re-checks the session as a backstop even though middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests. Checks the current password against the stored hash (wrong value is a field-level VALIDATION_ERROR, not a generic failure), validates the new password against the shared policy module, bumps passwordChangedAt (invalidating every other session via the jwt callback's check), and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out by their own action.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"currentPassword\": \"string\", \"newPassword\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"Password updated.\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"message\": \"string\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":128,"startLine":1,"totalLines":128}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg6FRo6L6MB4eDQwviKKk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EjVMNEnVHKZ98NDjRZoUcy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10563,"cache_read_input_tokens":34351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10563},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6825f64-e470-4bad-a0ff-8e48240e2db1","uuid":"de66b532-f53c-4b4d-9901-9a23b0977564","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:42:06.946Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6FRnrh32TgpQhERDJh7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EjVMNEnVHKZ98NDjRZoUcy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\n6\tRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\n7\tReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\n8\tNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\n9\tADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\n10\tconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n15\t\n16\t**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n17\t\n18\t**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\n19\tcalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\n20\tactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\n21\tcredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\n22\ta single-provider app.\n23\t\n24\t**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n25\t(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n26\t`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\n27\troute through, not a new auth layer.\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n32\t\n33\t**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n34\t\n35\t**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\n36\tverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\n37\truns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\n38\tso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\n39\tCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\n40\tif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\n41\tto revisit.\n42\t\n43\t**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\n44\tother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n49\t\n50\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n51\t\n52\t**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\n53\tencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\n54\tLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\n55\tlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\n56\tconstant-time comparison outright.\n57\t\n58\t**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n59\t(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\n60\telsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n61\t\n62\t---\n63\t\n64\t## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n65\t\n66\t**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n67\t\n68\t**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\n69\tand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\n70\tMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\n71\tRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n72\t\n73\t**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\n74\tacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n75\t`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n80\t\n81\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n82\t\n83\t**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n84\t`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n85\t`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n86\t`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n87\t\n88\t**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n89\t(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n90\t(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n91\t\n92\t---\n93\t\n94\t## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n95\t\n96\t**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n97\t\n98\t**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n99\t`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\n100\tbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\n101\tpattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\n102\tZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\n103\tstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\n104\tschema, not two.\n105\t\n106\t**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\n107\tUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n112\t\n113\t**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n114\t\n115\t**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\n116\thashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\n117\tintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\n118\tchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\n119\texisting Playwright setup.\n120\t\n121\t**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n122\t(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\n123\tinfra to stand up.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## Status\n128\t\n129\tSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\n130\tspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\n131\tof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n132\t`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6825f64-e470-4bad-a0ff-8e48240e2db1","uuid":"d842be27-175d-401b-9515-25c34029c6f1","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:42:06.959Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\nRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\nNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\nADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\nconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n\n**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\ncalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\nactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\ncredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\na single-provider app.\n\n**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\nroute through, not a new auth layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n\n**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\nverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\nruns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\nso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\nCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\nif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\nto revisit.\n\n**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\nother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n\n**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\nencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\nLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\nlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\nconstant-time comparison outright.\n\n**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\nelsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n\n**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n\n**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\nand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\nMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\nRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n\n**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\nacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n\n**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\nbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\npattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\nZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\nstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\nschema, not two.\n\n**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\nUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n\n**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n\n**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\nhashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\nintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\nchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\nexisting Playwright setup.\n\n**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\ninfra to stand up.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\nspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\nof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
