{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012WSGXsPobsaRQ1hkiTm1Sr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# User Stories — PRD-02: School Settings & Academic Structure (abcd-02)\n2\t\n3\t## School settings\n4\t\n5\t- **FR-2, FR-3** As an admin, I want to edit the school name, logo URL, address, contact details and timezone, so that every page and email shows correct information.\n6\t- **FR-4** As an admin, I want my settings save to leave an audit trail of exactly which fields changed, so that other admins can see who changed what.\n7\t- **FR-5** As an admin or any other signed-in user, I want the top bar and public footer to always reflect the current school settings without refetching per request, so that pages stay fast and consistent.\n8\t\n9\t## Academic years\n10\t\n11\t- **FR-6** As an admin, I want a table of all academic years with their terms count and current status, so that I can see the school's academic structure at a glance.\n12\t- **FR-7** As an admin, I want to create or edit an academic year with validated, non-overlapping dates, so that the calendar of years is never internally inconsistent.\n13\t- **FR-8** As an admin, I want to mark one academic year as current, so that the whole app uses it by default for grading, attendance and reporting.\n14\t- **FR-9** As an admin, I want deletion blocked on an academic year that's in use, so that I can't accidentally destroy records other features depend on.\n15\t- **FR-10** As any part of the app, I want a single helper to fetch the current year/term, so that \"current\" is defined in exactly one place.\n16\t- **FR-11** As an admin, I want a banner when no year is marked current, so that I immediately know to fix a broken default before other features misbehave.\n17\t\n18\t## Terms\n19\t\n20\t- **FR-12** As an admin, I want a detail page per academic year listing its terms in order, so that I can manage a year's terms in one place.\n21\t- **FR-13** As an admin, I want term dates validated against their parent year and against sibling terms, so that terms never fall outside the year or overlap each other.\n22\t- **FR-14** As an admin, I want a \"Generate terms\" shortcut for semesters/trimesters/quarters, so that I don't have to hand-compute equal date ranges for a new year.\n23\t\n24\t## Grade levels\n25\t\n26\t- **FR-15** As an admin, I want to create, edit, reorder and archive grade levels, so that classes can later be organized by grade.\n27\t\n28\t## Subjects\n29\t\n30\t- **FR-16** As an admin, I want to create, edit, search and colour-code subjects with a unique uppercase code, so that classes, timetables and calendars can reference a consistent subject list.\n31\t\n32\t## Rooms\n33\t\n34\t- **FR-17** As an admin, I want to create, edit and archive rooms with building and capacity, so that classes can later be scheduled into a real space.\n35\t\n36\t## Navigation\n37\t\n38\t- **FR-18** As an admin, I want an \"Administration\" sidebar group linking to all five screens above, so that I can find school configuration without hunting for URLs.\n39\t\n40\t## API\n41\t\n42\t- **FR-19** As a frontend or integration client, I want a consistent REST surface (settings, academic-years, terms, grade-levels, subjects, rooms) with role-gated writes and the shared response envelope, so that every screen above has a predictable backend to call.\n43\t\n44\t## Seed data\n45\t\n46\t- **FR-20** As a developer running the seed script, I want a ready-made academic year, terms, grade levels, subjects and rooms, so that every later PRD and local demo has realistic data to build against.\n47\t\n48\t---\n49\t\n50\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n51\t\n52\t- **NFR-1 (Integrity)** Overlap/range checks for years and terms run inside a database transaction, so concurrent requests can't both succeed and corrupt the schedule.\n53\t- **NFR-2 (Performance)** Admin list pages render under 500ms at 50 records.\n54\t- **NFR-3 (Usability)** Every table has an empty state with a \"Create …\" call to action.\n55\t- **NFR-4 (UI discipline)** Every visible element is Material UI only, looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries are blocked by ESLint.\n56\t- **NFR-5 (Timezones)** All timestamps are stored UTC and displayed in `SchoolSettings.timezone`; date-only fields use `@db.Date`.\n57\t- **NFR-6 (AuthZ)** Every write is ADMIN-only, enforced server-side; a non-admin write returns 403.\n58\t- **NFR-7 (Auditability & envelope)** Every write audits via the existing `audit()` helper and responses follow the shared `{ data }` / list / `{ error }` envelope.\n59\t- **NFR-8 (Tests)** Vitest unit + integration coverage for overlap detection, term generation, code normalisation, set-current transaction and delete-in-use conflict; Playwright e2e for the core admin flows.\n60\t- **NFR-9 (Brownfield discipline)** Reuse existing PRD-00/PRD-01 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.\n61\t- **NFR-10 (Scope discipline)** Keep lint/typecheck/test green; don't expand into sections/courses, bell-schedule periods, grading scales or holidays (later PRDs).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd056bf4-3785-420e-8a1f-0c3d146fa266","uuid":"85001c7d-835b-40e3-bac4-2e1e608b8a22","timestamp":"2026-10-19T08:21:22.437Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories — PRD-02: School Settings & Academic Structure (abcd-02)\n\n## School settings\n\n- **FR-2, FR-3** As an admin, I want to edit the school name, logo URL, address, contact details and timezone, so that every page and email shows correct information.\n- **FR-4** As an admin, I want my settings save to leave an audit trail of exactly which fields changed, so that other admins can see who changed what.\n- **FR-5** As an admin or any other signed-in user, I want the top bar and public footer to always reflect the current school settings without refetching per request, so that pages stay fast and consistent.\n\n## Academic years\n\n- **FR-6** As an admin, I want a table of all academic years with their terms count and current status, so that I can see the school's academic structure at a glance.\n- **FR-7** As an admin, I want to create or edit an academic year with validated, non-overlapping dates, so that the calendar of years is never internally inconsistent.\n- **FR-8** As an admin, I want to mark one academic year as current, so that the whole app uses it by default for grading, attendance and reporting.\n- **FR-9** As an admin, I want deletion blocked on an academic year that's in use, so that I can't accidentally destroy records other features depend on.\n- **FR-10** As any part of the app, I want a single helper to fetch the current year/term, so that \"current\" is defined in exactly one place.\n- **FR-11** As an admin, I want a banner when no year is marked current, so that I immediately know to fix a broken default before other features misbehave.\n\n## Terms\n\n- **FR-12** As an admin, I want a detail page per academic year listing its terms in order, so that I can manage a year's terms in one place.\n- **FR-13** As an admin, I want term dates validated against their parent year and against sibling terms, so that terms never fall outside the year or overlap each other.\n- **FR-14** As an admin, I want a \"Generate terms\" shortcut for semesters/trimesters/quarters, so that I don't have to hand-compute equal date ranges for a new year.\n\n## Grade levels\n\n- **FR-15** As an admin, I want to create, edit, reorder and archive grade levels, so that classes can later be organized by grade.\n\n## Subjects\n\n- **FR-16** As an admin, I want to create, edit, search and colour-code subjects with a unique uppercase code, so that classes, timetables and calendars can reference a consistent subject list.\n\n## Rooms\n\n- **FR-17** As an admin, I want to create, edit and archive rooms with building and capacity, so that classes can later be scheduled into a real space.\n\n## Navigation\n\n- **FR-18** As an admin, I want an \"Administration\" sidebar group linking to all five screens above, so that I can find school configuration without hunting for URLs.\n\n## API\n\n- **FR-19** As a frontend or integration client, I want a consistent REST surface (settings, academic-years, terms, grade-levels, subjects, rooms) with role-gated writes and the shared response envelope, so that every screen above has a predictable backend to call.\n\n## Seed data\n\n- **FR-20** As a developer running the seed script, I want a ready-made academic year, terms, grade levels, subjects and rooms, so that every later PRD and local demo has realistic data to build against.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 (Integrity)** Overlap/range checks for years and terms run inside a database transaction, so concurrent requests can't both succeed and corrupt the schedule.\n- **NFR-2 (Performance)** Admin list pages render under 500ms at 50 records.\n- **NFR-3 (Usability)** Every table has an empty state with a \"Create …\" call to action.\n- **NFR-4 (UI discipline)** Every visible element is Material UI only, looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries are blocked by ESLint.\n- **NFR-5 (Timezones)** All timestamps are stored UTC and displayed in `SchoolSettings.timezone`; date-only fields use `@db.Date`.\n- **NFR-6 (AuthZ)** Every write is ADMIN-only, enforced server-side; a non-admin write returns 403.\n- **NFR-7 (Auditability & envelope)** Every write audits via the existing `audit()` helper and responses follow the shared `{ data }` / list / `{ error }` envelope.\n- **NFR-8 (Tests)** Vitest unit + integration coverage for overlap detection, term generation, code normalisation, set-current transaction and delete-in-use conflict; Playwright e2e for the core admin flows.\n- **NFR-9 (Brownfield discipline)** Reuse existing PRD-00/PRD-01 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.\n- **NFR-10 (Scope discipline)** Keep lint/typecheck/test green; don't expand into sections/courses, bell-schedule periods, grading scales or holidays (later PRDs).\n","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62}}}
