{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HBbmEZtvNRcv9LQLYEP7zP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-03\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T14:20:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"note\": \"Derived from system-design.md's Component Breakdown/Data Flow (abcd-03) and the source PRD's explicit API table (03-user-management.md, section 'API'), which fully specifies method/path/role/body for all 18 endpoints. Two items carried forward from system-design.md's Status section, unresolved by this sub-task because they are sequencing/confirmation items for dev-planning, not contract-shape questions: (1) FR-31 is MEDIUM confidence — the unlock contract below assumes it clears exactly lockedUntil/failedLoginCount per prisma/schema.prisma, confirm before implementation; (2) POST /api/users/:id/invite and the session-level effect of POST /api/users/:id/status are written against src/server/services/users.ts's sendInvite(userId) and PRD-01's session/status re-check, neither of which exists in src/ yet (only their schema does) — see handoff-to-dev-planning.json blockers.\",\n8\t\n9\t  \"conventions\": {\n10\t    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<resource or array>\" },\n11\t    \"listEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"[...]\", \"page\": 1, \"pageSize\": 20, \"total\": 0 },\n12\t    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": {} } },\n13\t    \"errorCodes\": [\"VALIDATION_ERROR (400)\", \"UNAUTHENTICATED (401)\", \"FORBIDDEN (403)\", \"NOT_FOUND (404)\", \"CONFLICT (409)\", \"RATE_LIMITED (429)\", \"INTERNAL (500)\"],\n14\t    \"pagination\": \"?page= (default 1), ?pageSize= (default 20, max 100)\",\n15\t    \"sorting\": \"?sort=field&order=asc|desc\",\n16\t    \"search\": \"?q=\",\n17\t    \"auth\": \"Per-endpoint role gate shown in each entry's description, enforced server-side via requireRole()/assertCanViewStudent (never UI-only). Student-scoped reads additionally run assertCanViewStudent, which throws FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND (for STUDENT/PARENT callers, to avoid revealing existence) rather than a blanket 403.\",\n18\t    \"audit\": \"Every write endpoint writes an AuditLog row via audit() with action user.<verb> (e.g. user.created, user.status_changed, user.archived, user.unlocked, user.imported, parent_link.created, parent_link.removed).\",\n19\t    \"privacy\": \"medicalNotes is stripped server-side (never UI-only) from every response reachable by STUDENT/PARENT roles and from every CSV export row (NFR-1).\"\n20\t  },\n21\t\n22\t  \"endpoints\": [\n23\t    {\n24\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n25\t      \"path\": \"/api/users\",\n26\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Paginated, filtered user list backed by the (lastName, firstName, email) index.\",\n27\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"role\": \"Role[]?\", \"status\": \"UserStatus?\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string?\", \"q\": \"string?\", \"includeArchived\": \"boolean? (default false)\", \"page\": \"int?\", \"pageSize\": \"int?\" },\n28\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string|null\", \"gradeLevelName\": \"string|null\", \"lastLoginAt\": \"datetime|null\", \"lockedUntil\": \"datetime|null\" } ], \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" },\n29\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"NFR-2\"]\n30\t    },\n31\t    {\n32\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n33\t      \"path\": \"/api/users\",\n34\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Creates a User + role-specific profile row + any inline parent/student links in one transaction; generates admissionNumber (S<year>-####) or employeeNumber (T-####) where applicable.\",\n35\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"phone\": \"string? (^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$)\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"profile\": \"StudentProfileInput|TeacherProfileInput|ParentProfileInput (shape depends on role; see FR-1)\", \"links\": \"[{ linkedUserId: string, relationship: GuardianRelationship, isPrimary: boolean }]?\", \"sendInvite\": \"boolean (default true)\" },\n36\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"profile\": \"object\" } },\n37\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-1\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-16\"]\n38\t    },\n39\t    {\n40\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n41\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id\",\n42\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Full user + role profile + family links (component 6) + 20 most recent AuditLog rows where actorId=id OR entityId=id.\",\n43\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n44\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"lastLoginAt\": \"datetime|null\", \"profile\": \"object\", \"familyLinks\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"linkedUserId\": \"string\", \"linkedUserName\": \"string\", \"relationship\": \"GuardianRelationship\", \"isPrimary\": \"boolean\" } ], \"recentAuditLogs\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"action\": \"string\", \"actorId\": \"string|null\", \"entityType\": \"string|null\", \"entityId\": \"string|null\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\" } ] } },\n45\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\"]\n46\t    },\n47\t    {\n48\t      \"method\": \"PATCH\",\n49\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id\",\n50\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Updates common + profile fields. role is rejected server-side if present and different from the existing row (FR-9 is a service-layer invariant, not just a form convenience). An email diff invalidates (marks used) any pending AuthToken rows of type INVITE for this user.\",\n51\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"firstName\": \"string?\", \"lastName\": \"string?\", \"email\": \"string?\", \"phone\": \"string?\", \"profile\": \"Partial<StudentProfileInput|TeacherProfileInput|ParentProfileInput>?\" },\n52\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"profile\": \"object\" } },\n53\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n54\t    },\n55\t    {\n56\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n57\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/invite\",\n58\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Resends an invitation email via src/server/services/users.ts's sendInvite(userId) (PRD-01 interface; see note — stub/no-op until PRD-01 lands, call site does not change).\",\n59\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n60\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"inviteSentAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n61\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-7\"]\n62\t    },\n63\t    {\n64\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n65\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/unlock\",\n66\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Clears lockedUntil and failedLoginCount, restoring sign-in access immediately. MEDIUM confidence (FR-31) — field names confirmed against prisma/schema.prisma; verify no other lockout field exists before implementation.\",\n67\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n68\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"lockedUntil\": null, \"failedLoginCount\": 0 } },\n69\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-31\"]\n70\t    },\n71\t    {\n72\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n73\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/status\",\n74\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Sets status to ACTIVE or DISABLED. Rejects self-disable and disabling the last active ADMIN with VALIDATION_ERROR 'At least one active admin is required.' The 'sessions stop working within 5 minutes' effect (FR-12) is PRD-01's session re-check reading status on token refresh, not built here (NFR-7) — this endpoint only guarantees status is correct the instant the write commits.\",\n75\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"status\": \"\\\"ACTIVE\\\"|\\\"DISABLED\\\"\" },\n76\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\" } },\n77\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-14\"]\n78\t    },\n79\t    {\n80\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n81\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/archive\",\n82\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Sets archivedAt=now and status=DISABLED. Same self/last-admin guard as /status. Archived users are excluded from every list/picker query by default (component 3/7/16), enforced at the query layer.\",\n83\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n84\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"archivedAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n85\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\", \"FR-14\"]\n86\t    },\n87\t    {\n88\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n89\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/restore\",\n90\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Clears archivedAt. Does not auto-reactivate status; an admin re-enables separately via /status.\",\n91\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n92\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"archivedAt\": null } },\n93\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\"]\n94\t    },\n95\t    {\n96\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n97\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/import\",\n98\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Re-validates every row server-side (never trusts the client) against the same Zod schemas as the create form, in batches of 200; each batch runs in one prisma.$transaction (all-or-rollback, NFR-3). Grade levels matched case-insensitively by name/shortName; dates parsed strictly as YYYY-MM-DD; rows whose email already exists are skipped, not errored (FR-23).\",\n99\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"type\": \"\\\"STUDENTS\\\"|\\\"TEACHERS\\\"\", \"rows\": \"object[] (raw parsed CSV rows, re-validated server-side)\", \"sendInvites\": \"boolean (default false)\" },\n100\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"createdStudents\": \"int\", \"createdParents\": \"int\", \"linkedExistingParents\": \"int\", \"skipped\": \"int\", \"failed\": \"int\", \"rowResults\": [ { \"rowIndex\": \"int\", \"result\": \"\\\"created\\\"|\\\"skipped\\\"|\\\"error\\\"\", \"reason\": \"string|null\" } ], \"errorReportCsvUrl\": \"string|null\" } },\n101\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-22\", \"FR-23\", \"NFR-3\"]\n102\t    },\n103\t    {\n104\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n105\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/export\",\n106\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Same filters as GET /api/users; returns text/csv. medicalNotes is excluded and every cell passes through escapeCsvCell() (NFR-4) to neutralise formula injection.\",\n107\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"role\": \"Role[]?\", \"status\": \"UserStatus?\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string?\", \"q\": \"string?\", \"includeArchived\": \"boolean?\" },\n108\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"contentType\": \"text/csv\", \"body\": \"csv string, one row per matched user, medicalNotes column omitted\" },\n109\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-5\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-4\"]\n110\t    },\n111\t    {\n112\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n113\t      \"path\": \"/api/users/search\",\n114\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN and TEACHER only. Picker search reusing the list query's filters, capped to 20 rows, projected down, excluding archived users.\",\n115\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"role\": \"Role?\", \"q\": \"string?\" },\n116\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"name\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\" } ] },\n117\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-28\"]\n118\t    },\n119\t    {\n120\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n121\t      \"path\": \"/api/students/:id/parents\",\n122\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Links a parent to a student inside one transaction: rejects a 5th link for the student (VALIDATION_ERROR) and, if isPrimary is true, clears isPrimary on every other link for that student first.\",\n123\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"parentId\": \"string\", \"relationship\": \"GuardianRelationship\", \"isPrimary\": \"boolean\" },\n124\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"parentId\": \"string\", \"studentId\": \"string\", \"relationship\": \"GuardianRelationship\", \"isPrimary\": \"boolean\" } },\n125\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-16\"]\n126\t    },\n127\t    {\n128\t      \"method\": \"DELETE\",\n129\t      \"path\": \"/api/students/:id/parents/:parentId\",\n130\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Removes a parent-student link.\",\n131\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n132\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"deleted\": true } },\n133\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\"]\n134\t    },\n135\t    {\n136\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n137\t      \"path\": \"/api/students/:id\",\n138\t      \"description\": \"Gated by assertCanViewStudent (ADMIN/TEACHER full access; STUDENT self only; PARENT linked children only — FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND otherwise, never revealing existence to STUDENT/PARENT). medicalNotes is stripped in the service layer for STUDENT/PARENT roles before the response is built.\",\n139\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n140\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"admissionNumber\": \"string\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string\", \"gradeLevelName\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"dateOfBirth\": \"date\", \"gender\": \"Gender\", \"addressLine1\": \"string|null\", \"city\": \"string|null\", \"medicalNotes\": \"string|null (omitted entirely for STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"emergencyContact\": \"string|null\", \"emergencyPhone\": \"string|null\", \"familyLinks\": \"[{ linkedUserId, linkedUserName, relationship, isPrimary }]\" } },\n141\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-25\", \"NFR-1\"]\n142\t    },\n143\t    {\n144\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n145\t      \"path\": \"/api/me/children\",\n146\t      \"description\": \"PARENT only. Lists the caller's linked children for the My Children page.\",\n147\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n148\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"name\": \"string\", \"gradeLevelName\": \"string\", \"admissionNumber\": \"string\" } ] },\n149\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-26\"]\n150\t    },\n151\t    {\n152\t      \"method\": \"PATCH\",\n153\t      \"path\": \"/api/me/profile\",\n154\t      \"description\": \"Any authenticated user, self only. Narrower mutation path than /api/users/:id — editable fields are phone, plus occupation/address for PARENT role; name/email/role are read-only here.\",\n155\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"phone\": \"string? (^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$)\", \"occupation\": \"string? (PARENT only)\", \"address\": \"string? (PARENT only)\" },\n156\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"phone\": \"string|null\", \"occupation\": \"string|null\", \"address\": \"string|null\" } },\n157\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-27\"]\n158\t    },\n159\t    {\n160\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n161\t      \"path\": \"/api/audit-logs\",\n162\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Read-only paginated view over the existing AuditLog table; filters by actor, action prefix, and date range. No new write path.\",\n163\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"actorId\": \"string?\", \"actionPrefix\": \"string?\", \"dateFrom\": \"date?\", \"dateTo\": \"date?\", \"page\": \"int?\", \"pageSize\": \"int?\" },\n164\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\", \"actorId\": \"string|null\", \"actorName\": \"string|null\", \"action\": \"string\", \"entityType\": \"string|null\", \"entityId\": \"string|null\", \"ip\": \"string|null\", \"metadata\": \"object|null\" } ], \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" },\n165\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-29\"]\n166\t    }\n167\t  ],\n168\t\n169\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n170\t}\n171\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5a8f152-49e8-4bf2-bd8a-06ac76b7320e","uuid":"ef684c66-e443-4c7e-a5a0-9202bdc6a0a4","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:17:20.947Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-03\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T14:20:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"note\": \"Derived from system-design.md's Component Breakdown/Data Flow (abcd-03) and the source PRD's explicit API table (03-user-management.md, section 'API'), which fully specifies method/path/role/body for all 18 endpoints. Two items carried forward from system-design.md's Status section, unresolved by this sub-task because they are sequencing/confirmation items for dev-planning, not contract-shape questions: (1) FR-31 is MEDIUM confidence — the unlock contract below assumes it clears exactly lockedUntil/failedLoginCount per prisma/schema.prisma, confirm before implementation; (2) POST /api/users/:id/invite and the session-level effect of POST /api/users/:id/status are written against src/server/services/users.ts's sendInvite(userId) and PRD-01's session/status re-check, neither of which exists in src/ yet (only their schema does) — see handoff-to-dev-planning.json blockers.\",\n\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<resource or array>\" },\n    \"listEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"[...]\", \"page\": 1, \"pageSize\": 20, \"total\": 0 },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": {} } },\n    \"errorCodes\": [\"VALIDATION_ERROR (400)\", \"UNAUTHENTICATED (401)\", \"FORBIDDEN (403)\", \"NOT_FOUND (404)\", \"CONFLICT (409)\", \"RATE_LIMITED (429)\", \"INTERNAL (500)\"],\n    \"pagination\": \"?page= (default 1), ?pageSize= (default 20, max 100)\",\n    \"sorting\": \"?sort=field&order=asc|desc\",\n    \"search\": \"?q=\",\n    \"auth\": \"Per-endpoint role gate shown in each entry's description, enforced server-side via requireRole()/assertCanViewStudent (never UI-only). Student-scoped reads additionally run assertCanViewStudent, which throws FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND (for STUDENT/PARENT callers, to avoid revealing existence) rather than a blanket 403.\",\n    \"audit\": \"Every write endpoint writes an AuditLog row via audit() with action user.<verb> (e.g. user.created, user.status_changed, user.archived, user.unlocked, user.imported, parent_link.created, parent_link.removed).\",\n    \"privacy\": \"medicalNotes is stripped server-side (never UI-only) from every response reachable by STUDENT/PARENT roles and from every CSV export row (NFR-1).\"\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Paginated, filtered user list backed by the (lastName, firstName, email) index.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"role\": \"Role[]?\", \"status\": \"UserStatus?\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string?\", \"q\": \"string?\", \"includeArchived\": \"boolean? (default false)\", \"page\": \"int?\", \"pageSize\": \"int?\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string|null\", \"gradeLevelName\": \"string|null\", \"lastLoginAt\": \"datetime|null\", \"lockedUntil\": \"datetime|null\" } ], \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"NFR-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Creates a User + role-specific profile row + any inline parent/student links in one transaction; generates admissionNumber (S<year>-####) or employeeNumber (T-####) where applicable.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"phone\": \"string? (^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$)\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"profile\": \"StudentProfileInput|TeacherProfileInput|ParentProfileInput (shape depends on role; see FR-1)\", \"links\": \"[{ linkedUserId: string, relationship: GuardianRelationship, isPrimary: boolean }]?\", \"sendInvite\": \"boolean (default true)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"profile\": \"object\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-1\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-16\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Full user + role profile + family links (component 6) + 20 most recent AuditLog rows where actorId=id OR entityId=id.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"lastLoginAt\": \"datetime|null\", \"profile\": \"object\", \"familyLinks\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"linkedUserId\": \"string\", \"linkedUserName\": \"string\", \"relationship\": \"GuardianRelationship\", \"isPrimary\": \"boolean\" } ], \"recentAuditLogs\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"action\": \"string\", \"actorId\": \"string|null\", \"entityType\": \"string|null\", \"entityId\": \"string|null\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\" } ] } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"PATCH\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Updates common + profile fields. role is rejected server-side if present and different from the existing row (FR-9 is a service-layer invariant, not just a form convenience). An email diff invalidates (marks used) any pending AuthToken rows of type INVITE for this user.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"firstName\": \"string?\", \"lastName\": \"string?\", \"email\": \"string?\", \"phone\": \"string?\", \"profile\": \"Partial<StudentProfileInput|TeacherProfileInput|ParentProfileInput>?\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"profile\": \"object\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/invite\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Resends an invitation email via src/server/services/users.ts's sendInvite(userId) (PRD-01 interface; see note — stub/no-op until PRD-01 lands, call site does not change).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"inviteSentAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/unlock\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Clears lockedUntil and failedLoginCount, restoring sign-in access immediately. MEDIUM confidence (FR-31) — field names confirmed against prisma/schema.prisma; verify no other lockout field exists before implementation.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"lockedUntil\": null, \"failedLoginCount\": 0 } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-31\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/status\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Sets status to ACTIVE or DISABLED. Rejects self-disable and disabling the last active ADMIN with VALIDATION_ERROR 'At least one active admin is required.' The 'sessions stop working within 5 minutes' effect (FR-12) is PRD-01's session re-check reading status on token refresh, not built here (NFR-7) — this endpoint only guarantees status is correct the instant the write commits.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"status\": \"\\\"ACTIVE\\\"|\\\"DISABLED\\\"\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-14\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/archive\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Sets archivedAt=now and status=DISABLED. Same self/last-admin guard as /status. Archived users are excluded from every list/picker query by default (component 3/7/16), enforced at the query layer.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"archivedAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\", \"FR-14\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/:id/restore\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Clears archivedAt. Does not auto-reactivate status; an admin re-enables separately via /status.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"archivedAt\": null } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/import\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Re-validates every row server-side (never trusts the client) against the same Zod schemas as the create form, in batches of 200; each batch runs in one prisma.$transaction (all-or-rollback, NFR-3). Grade levels matched case-insensitively by name/shortName; dates parsed strictly as YYYY-MM-DD; rows whose email already exists are skipped, not errored (FR-23).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"type\": \"\\\"STUDENTS\\\"|\\\"TEACHERS\\\"\", \"rows\": \"object[] (raw parsed CSV rows, re-validated server-side)\", \"sendInvites\": \"boolean (default false)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"createdStudents\": \"int\", \"createdParents\": \"int\", \"linkedExistingParents\": \"int\", \"skipped\": \"int\", \"failed\": \"int\", \"rowResults\": [ { \"rowIndex\": \"int\", \"result\": \"\\\"created\\\"|\\\"skipped\\\"|\\\"error\\\"\", \"reason\": \"string|null\" } ], \"errorReportCsvUrl\": \"string|null\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-22\", \"FR-23\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/export\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Same filters as GET /api/users; returns text/csv. medicalNotes is excluded and every cell passes through escapeCsvCell() (NFR-4) to neutralise formula injection.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"role\": \"Role[]?\", \"status\": \"UserStatus?\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string?\", \"q\": \"string?\", \"includeArchived\": \"boolean?\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"contentType\": \"text/csv\", \"body\": \"csv string, one row per matched user, medicalNotes column omitted\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-5\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-4\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/users/search\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN and TEACHER only. Picker search reusing the list query's filters, capped to 20 rows, projected down, excluding archived users.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"role\": \"Role?\", \"q\": \"string?\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"name\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\" } ] },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-28\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/students/:id/parents\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Links a parent to a student inside one transaction: rejects a 5th link for the student (VALIDATION_ERROR) and, if isPrimary is true, clears isPrimary on every other link for that student first.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"parentId\": \"string\", \"relationship\": \"GuardianRelationship\", \"isPrimary\": \"boolean\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"parentId\": \"string\", \"studentId\": \"string\", \"relationship\": \"GuardianRelationship\", \"isPrimary\": \"boolean\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-16\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"DELETE\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/students/:id/parents/:parentId\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Removes a parent-student link.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"deleted\": true } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/students/:id\",\n      \"description\": \"Gated by assertCanViewStudent (ADMIN/TEACHER full access; STUDENT self only; PARENT linked children only — FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND otherwise, never revealing existence to STUDENT/PARENT). medicalNotes is stripped in the service layer for STUDENT/PARENT roles before the response is built.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"admissionNumber\": \"string\", \"gradeLevelId\": \"string\", \"gradeLevelName\": \"string\", \"status\": \"UserStatus\", \"dateOfBirth\": \"date\", \"gender\": \"Gender\", \"addressLine1\": \"string|null\", \"city\": \"string|null\", \"medicalNotes\": \"string|null (omitted entirely for STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"emergencyContact\": \"string|null\", \"emergencyPhone\": \"string|null\", \"familyLinks\": \"[{ linkedUserId, linkedUserName, relationship, isPrimary }]\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-25\", \"NFR-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/me/children\",\n      \"description\": \"PARENT only. Lists the caller's linked children for the My Children page.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"name\": \"string\", \"gradeLevelName\": \"string\", \"admissionNumber\": \"string\" } ] },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-26\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"PATCH\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/me/profile\",\n      \"description\": \"Any authenticated user, self only. Narrower mutation path than /api/users/:id — editable fields are phone, plus occupation/address for PARENT role; name/email/role are read-only here.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"phone\": \"string? (^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$)\", \"occupation\": \"string? (PARENT only)\", \"address\": \"string? (PARENT only)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"phone\": \"string|null\", \"occupation\": \"string|null\", \"address\": \"string|null\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-27\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/audit-logs\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Read-only paginated view over the existing AuditLog table; filters by actor, action prefix, and date range. No new write path.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"actorId\": \"string?\", \"actionPrefix\": \"string?\", \"dateFrom\": \"date?\", \"dateTo\": \"date?\", \"page\": \"int?\", \"pageSize\": \"int?\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\", \"actorId\": \"string|null\", \"actorName\": \"string|null\", \"action\": \"string\", \"entityType\": \"string|null\", \"entityId\": \"string|null\", \"ip\": \"string|null\", \"metadata\": \"object|null\" } ], \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-29\"]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":171,"startLine":1,"totalLines":171}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBLwPSimQiELFFDTe8uz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0117qiQYfaPuk6mgQzaE4V1k","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1733,"cache_read_input_tokens":40792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1733},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5a8f152-49e8-4bf2-bd8a-06ac76b7320e","uuid":"57637eff-b57f-436e-a47d-ce10f99820af","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:17:21.143Z","request_id":"req_011CgBLwPE4pBaYx212t48fh"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117qiQYfaPuk6mgQzaE4V1k","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n6\t`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\n7\tfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\n8\tand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\n9\tReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\n10\tevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\n11\treal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\n12\treports no blockers.\n13\t\n14\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n15\t\n16\t- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n17\t  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n18\t  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n19\t  passing with no scope creep.\n20\t- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n21\t  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n22\t- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n23\t  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n24\t  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n25\t\n26\t## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n27\t\n28\t- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n29\t  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n30\t  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n31\t- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n32\t  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n33\t  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n34\t- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n35\t  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n36\t  browser before anything hits the network.\n37\t\n38\t## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n39\t\n40\t- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n41\t  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n42\t- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n43\t  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n44\t  table.\n45\t- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n46\t  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n47\t  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n48\t  request lifetime).\n49\t\n50\t## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n51\t\n52\t- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n53\t  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n54\t  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n55\t  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n56\t- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n57\t  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n58\t  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n59\t- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n60\t  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n61\t\n62\t## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n63\t\n64\t- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n65\t  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n66\t  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n67\t  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n68\t- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n69\t  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n70\t  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n71\t  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n72\t  wrapper design-system package.\n73\t- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n76\t\n77\t- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n78\t  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n79\t  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n80\t- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n81\t  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n82\t  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n83\t- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n84\t  queries unaffected.\n85\t\n86\t## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n87\t\n88\t- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n89\t  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n90\t  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n91\t- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n92\t  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n93\t  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n94\t  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n95\t- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n96\t  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n97\t\n98\t## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n99\t\n100\t- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n101\t  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n102\t  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n103\t  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n104\t- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n105\t  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n106\t  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n107\t  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n108\t  user service.\n109\t- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n110\t  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n111\t  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n112\t  re-implements.\n113\t\n114\t## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n115\t\n116\t- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n117\t  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n118\t- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n119\t  not generated at request time.\n120\t- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n121\t  edit, not a code change.\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5a8f152-49e8-4bf2-bd8a-06ac76b7320e","uuid":"9fac2d87-30bf-4c99-9825-7d564f249b1a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:17:21.148Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n\n## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n\n- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n  browser before anything hits the network.\n\n## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n\n- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n  table.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n  request lifetime).\n\n## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n\n- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n\n## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n\n- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n  wrapper design-system package.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n\n## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n\n- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n  queries unaffected.\n\n## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n\n- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n\n## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n  user service.\n- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n  re-implements.\n\n## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n\n- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n  not generated at request time.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n  edit, not a code change.\n","numLines":122,"startLine":1,"totalLines":122}}}
