{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nXzLBo1FckeAMu4e1i5sP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T06:01:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"note\": \"Derived from system-design.md's Component Breakdown/Data Flow (Components 3, 8, 11, 15, 16, 17) and 04-notifications.md's 'API' table, which fully specifies method/path/role/notes for all endpoints (the table's 'POST /api/notifications/:id/read · /unread' row is two endpoints) — 11 endpoints total, not the 12 mentioned in system-design.md's prose; the PRD table and FR-21's own endpoint list both enumerate 11, confirmed by direct count. Two items carried forward, unresolved here because they are sequencing/confirmation items for dev-planning, not contract-shape questions: (1) every non-ADMIN, non-CRON_SECRET endpoint below calls requireRole(...ALL_ROLES) as the stand-in for a real requireUser() per system-design.md's Overview/Component 12 finding — src/server/auth/permissions.ts does not exist yet (confirmed: only requireRole.ts's ADMIN-placeholder and student-access.ts are present in src/server/auth/), so 'own notifications only' / 'own preferences only' scoping is written against the request's userId param today and must be swapped to the real session identity when PRD-01 lands, not re-derived; ALL_ROLES itself is a local const in src/config/navigation.ts today, not exported — dev-planning needs to export it (or import the four literals) for route call sites to use it; (2) list/count responses use the real paginated()/ok() shapes from src/server/http.ts (data + nested meta for lists, data for single resources), confirmed directly against src/server/http.ts and the existing src/app/api/users/route.ts pattern rather than assumed.\",\n8\t\n9\t  \"conventions\": {\n10\t    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<resource or array>\" },\n11\t    \"listEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"[...]\", \"meta\": { \"page\": 1, \"pageSize\": 20, \"total\": 0 } },\n12\t    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": {} } },\n13\t    \"errorCodes\": [\"VALIDATION_ERROR (400)\", \"UNAUTHENTICATED (401)\", \"FORBIDDEN (403)\", \"NOT_FOUND (404)\", \"CONFLICT (409)\", \"RATE_LIMITED (429)\", \"INTERNAL (500)\", \"INVALID_TOKEN (410)\"],\n14\t    \"pagination\": \"?page= (default 1), ?pageSize= (default 20, max 100), per src/server/http.ts parsePagination()\",\n15\t    \"auth\": \"Own-row routes call requireRole(...ALL_ROLES) (placeholder for PRD-01's requireUser(); see note). ADMIN-only routes call requireRole('ADMIN') directly — already real today via src/server/auth/requireRole.ts. POST /api/internal/email/dispatch checks Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} itself, not requireRole (NFR-8).\",\n16\t    \"security\": \"Notification.link values are validated server-side as '/'-prefixed relative paths before any write that sets them (NFR-5); this is a notify()-time invariant (Component 3), not re-validated at the read endpoints below.\"\n17\t  },\n18\t\n19\t  \"endpoints\": [\n20\t    {\n21\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n22\t      \"path\": \"/api/notifications\",\n23\t      \"description\": \"Any role. Own notifications only (userId scoped server-side). Backs both the /notifications page (paginated, filterable) and, with pageSize=10 and no filters, the bell popover's recent-10 list — one implementation (Component 11), not two query paths.\",\n24\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"unread\": \"boolean?\", \"category\": \"\\\"ACCOUNT\\\"|\\\"ACADEMIC\\\"|\\\"ATTENDANCE\\\"|\\\"COMMUNICATION\\\"|\\\"FINANCE\\\"|\\\"SYSTEM\\\"?\", \"page\": \"int? (default 1)\", \"pageSize\": \"int? (default 20, max 100)\" },\n25\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"type\": \"string\", \"category\": \"string\", \"title\": \"string\", \"body\": \"string|null\", \"link\": \"string|null\", \"readAt\": \"datetime|null\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\" } ], \"meta\": { \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" } },\n26\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n27\t    },\n28\t    {\n29\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n30\t      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/unread-count\",\n31\t      \"description\": \"Any role. Own count only. Backed by the Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt) composite index; must respond under 50ms (NFR-3). Polled by the bell every 30s while the tab is visible.\",\n32\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n33\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"count\": \"int\" } },\n34\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-14\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-7\"]\n35\t    },\n36\t    {\n37\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n38\t      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/:id/read\",\n39\t      \"description\": \"Owner only (the notification's userId must match the caller). Sets readAt=now if not already set; idempotent. NOT_FOUND if the id doesn't belong to the caller (never reveals another user's notification exists).\",\n40\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n41\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"readAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n42\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n43\t    },\n44\t    {\n45\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n46\t      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/:id/unread\",\n47\t      \"description\": \"Owner only. Clears readAt. Same ownership/NOT_FOUND rule as /read.\",\n48\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n49\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"readAt\": null } },\n50\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n51\t    },\n52\t    {\n53\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n54\t      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/read-all\",\n55\t      \"description\": \"Any role. Sets readAt=now on every unread Notification row owned by the caller (bulk UPDATE, not per-row). Backs the popover footer's 'Mark all as read' and the /notifications page's bulk action.\",\n56\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n57\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"updatedCount\": \"int\" } },\n58\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n59\t    },\n60\t    {\n61\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n62\t      \"path\": \"/api/me/notification-preferences\",\n63\t      \"description\": \"Any role. Returns the caller's NotificationPreference rows merged with Component 2's registry defaults for every type visible to the caller's role (so the client never has to do the merge).\",\n64\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n65\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"type\": \"string\", \"category\": \"string\", \"label\": \"string\", \"description\": \"string\", \"mandatoryInApp\": \"boolean\", \"inApp\": \"boolean\", \"email\": \"boolean\" } ] },\n66\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n67\t    },\n68\t    {\n69\t      \"method\": \"PUT\",\n70\t      \"path\": \"/api/me/notification-preferences\",\n71\t      \"description\": \"Any role. Upserts one {type, inApp, email} preference row for the caller. Rejects inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR (FR-22), independent of the disabled-Switch client affordance.\",\n72\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"type\": \"string (registry key, required)\", \"inApp\": \"boolean\", \"email\": \"boolean\" },\n73\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"inApp\": \"boolean\", \"email\": \"boolean\" } },\n74\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-19\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-22\", \"NFR-7\"]\n75\t    },\n76\t    {\n77\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n78\t      \"path\": \"/api/internal/email/dispatch\",\n79\t      \"description\": \"Requires Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}; 401 via the standard error envelope on mismatch (NFR-8), not requireRole. Runs Component 8's dispatchEmails() once (recovers stuck SENDING rows, claims and sends a batch, applies retry backoff, runs the daily purge check). Called by an external scheduler or the npm run worker:email loop script.\",\n80\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"batchSize\": \"int? (default 50)\" },\n81\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"sent\": \"int\", \"failed\": \"int\", \"retried\": \"int\" } },\n82\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-8\"]\n83\t    },\n84\t    {\n85\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n86\t      \"path\": \"/api/admin/email-log\",\n87\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Paginated EmailOutbox rows (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), filterable by status.\",\n88\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"status\": \"\\\"PENDING\\\"|\\\"SENDING\\\"|\\\"SENT\\\"|\\\"FAILED\\\"?\", \"page\": \"int? (default 1)\", \"pageSize\": \"int? (default 20, max 100)\" },\n89\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\", \"recipient\": \"string\", \"subject\": \"string\", \"status\": \"string\", \"attempts\": \"int\", \"lastError\": \"string|null\", \"nextAttemptAt\": \"datetime|null\" } ], \"meta\": { \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" } },\n90\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n91\t    },\n92\t    {\n93\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n94\t      \"path\": \"/api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\",\n95\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Resets the row to attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now — the same shape Component 8's dispatcher expects on its next pass; this endpoint does not send anything itself.\",\n96\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n97\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"PENDING\", \"attempts\": 0, \"nextAttemptAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n98\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n99\t    },\n100\t    {\n101\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n102\t      \"path\": \"/api/admin/notifications/test\",\n103\t      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Calls Component 3's notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [caller.id], ... }) so the admin receives one in-app notification (and, per their own preferences, one EmailOutbox row) to verify delivery end to end.\",\n104\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n105\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"queued\": true } },\n106\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n107\t    }\n108\t  ],\n109\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n110\t}\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe42c453-12ae-4515-b32c-f0603dc8fe6d","uuid":"1c023dfe-7647-455e-a3d7-4b699ff0ea08","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:04:21.115Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T06:01:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"note\": \"Derived from system-design.md's Component Breakdown/Data Flow (Components 3, 8, 11, 15, 16, 17) and 04-notifications.md's 'API' table, which fully specifies method/path/role/notes for all endpoints (the table's 'POST /api/notifications/:id/read · /unread' row is two endpoints) — 11 endpoints total, not the 12 mentioned in system-design.md's prose; the PRD table and FR-21's own endpoint list both enumerate 11, confirmed by direct count. Two items carried forward, unresolved here because they are sequencing/confirmation items for dev-planning, not contract-shape questions: (1) every non-ADMIN, non-CRON_SECRET endpoint below calls requireRole(...ALL_ROLES) as the stand-in for a real requireUser() per system-design.md's Overview/Component 12 finding — src/server/auth/permissions.ts does not exist yet (confirmed: only requireRole.ts's ADMIN-placeholder and student-access.ts are present in src/server/auth/), so 'own notifications only' / 'own preferences only' scoping is written against the request's userId param today and must be swapped to the real session identity when PRD-01 lands, not re-derived; ALL_ROLES itself is a local const in src/config/navigation.ts today, not exported — dev-planning needs to export it (or import the four literals) for route call sites to use it; (2) list/count responses use the real paginated()/ok() shapes from src/server/http.ts (data + nested meta for lists, data for single resources), confirmed directly against src/server/http.ts and the existing src/app/api/users/route.ts pattern rather than assumed.\",\n\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<resource or array>\" },\n    \"listEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"[...]\", \"meta\": { \"page\": 1, \"pageSize\": 20, \"total\": 0 } },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": {} } },\n    \"errorCodes\": [\"VALIDATION_ERROR (400)\", \"UNAUTHENTICATED (401)\", \"FORBIDDEN (403)\", \"NOT_FOUND (404)\", \"CONFLICT (409)\", \"RATE_LIMITED (429)\", \"INTERNAL (500)\", \"INVALID_TOKEN (410)\"],\n    \"pagination\": \"?page= (default 1), ?pageSize= (default 20, max 100), per src/server/http.ts parsePagination()\",\n    \"auth\": \"Own-row routes call requireRole(...ALL_ROLES) (placeholder for PRD-01's requireUser(); see note). ADMIN-only routes call requireRole('ADMIN') directly — already real today via src/server/auth/requireRole.ts. POST /api/internal/email/dispatch checks Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} itself, not requireRole (NFR-8).\",\n    \"security\": \"Notification.link values are validated server-side as '/'-prefixed relative paths before any write that sets them (NFR-5); this is a notify()-time invariant (Component 3), not re-validated at the read endpoints below.\"\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/notifications\",\n      \"description\": \"Any role. Own notifications only (userId scoped server-side). Backs both the /notifications page (paginated, filterable) and, with pageSize=10 and no filters, the bell popover's recent-10 list — one implementation (Component 11), not two query paths.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"unread\": \"boolean?\", \"category\": \"\\\"ACCOUNT\\\"|\\\"ACADEMIC\\\"|\\\"ATTENDANCE\\\"|\\\"COMMUNICATION\\\"|\\\"FINANCE\\\"|\\\"SYSTEM\\\"?\", \"page\": \"int? (default 1)\", \"pageSize\": \"int? (default 20, max 100)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"type\": \"string\", \"category\": \"string\", \"title\": \"string\", \"body\": \"string|null\", \"link\": \"string|null\", \"readAt\": \"datetime|null\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\" } ], \"meta\": { \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/unread-count\",\n      \"description\": \"Any role. Own count only. Backed by the Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt) composite index; must respond under 50ms (NFR-3). Polled by the bell every 30s while the tab is visible.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"count\": \"int\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-14\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/:id/read\",\n      \"description\": \"Owner only (the notification's userId must match the caller). Sets readAt=now if not already set; idempotent. NOT_FOUND if the id doesn't belong to the caller (never reveals another user's notification exists).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"readAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/:id/unread\",\n      \"description\": \"Owner only. Clears readAt. Same ownership/NOT_FOUND rule as /read.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"readAt\": null } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/notifications/read-all\",\n      \"description\": \"Any role. Sets readAt=now on every unread Notification row owned by the caller (bulk UPDATE, not per-row). Backs the popover footer's 'Mark all as read' and the /notifications page's bulk action.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"updatedCount\": \"int\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/me/notification-preferences\",\n      \"description\": \"Any role. Returns the caller's NotificationPreference rows merged with Component 2's registry defaults for every type visible to the caller's role (so the client never has to do the merge).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"type\": \"string\", \"category\": \"string\", \"label\": \"string\", \"description\": \"string\", \"mandatoryInApp\": \"boolean\", \"inApp\": \"boolean\", \"email\": \"boolean\" } ] },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"PUT\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/me/notification-preferences\",\n      \"description\": \"Any role. Upserts one {type, inApp, email} preference row for the caller. Rejects inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR (FR-22), independent of the disabled-Switch client affordance.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"type\": \"string (registry key, required)\", \"inApp\": \"boolean\", \"email\": \"boolean\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"inApp\": \"boolean\", \"email\": \"boolean\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-19\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-22\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/internal/email/dispatch\",\n      \"description\": \"Requires Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}; 401 via the standard error envelope on mismatch (NFR-8), not requireRole. Runs Component 8's dispatchEmails() once (recovers stuck SENDING rows, claims and sends a batch, applies retry backoff, runs the daily purge check). Called by an external scheduler or the npm run worker:email loop script.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"batchSize\": \"int? (default 50)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"sent\": \"int\", \"failed\": \"int\", \"retried\": \"int\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/admin/email-log\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Paginated EmailOutbox rows (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), filterable by status.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"status\": \"\\\"PENDING\\\"|\\\"SENDING\\\"|\\\"SENT\\\"|\\\"FAILED\\\"?\", \"page\": \"int? (default 1)\", \"pageSize\": \"int? (default 20, max 100)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"string\", \"createdAt\": \"datetime\", \"recipient\": \"string\", \"subject\": \"string\", \"status\": \"string\", \"attempts\": \"int\", \"lastError\": \"string|null\", \"nextAttemptAt\": \"datetime|null\" } ], \"meta\": { \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int\", \"total\": \"int\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Resets the row to attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now — the same shape Component 8's dispatcher expects on its next pass; this endpoint does not send anything itself.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"PENDING\", \"attempts\": 0, \"nextAttemptAt\": \"datetime\" } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/admin/notifications/test\",\n      \"description\": \"ADMIN only. Calls Component 3's notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [caller.id], ... }) so the admin receives one in-app notification (and, per their own preferences, one EmailOutbox row) to verify delivery end to end.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"data\": { \"queued\": true } },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-21\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgCz2bxEvTdiwVCgeiL8B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kbxhc8A2W5ByuakZDb4Kn2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":32138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":364},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe42c453-12ae-4515-b32c-f0603dc8fe6d","uuid":"a70b55e9-4353-402f-8c52-807cb91210c5","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:04:21.604Z","request_id":"req_011CgCz2b8tHT6CQe4rPfMd5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kbxhc8A2W5ByuakZDb4Kn2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-04 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\n6\tNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\n7\tMUI v9 + emotion. This PRD is brownfield on top of that stack — the\n8\tdecisions below are only the deltas this PRD's requirements force, not a\n9\tre-litigation of the base stack.\n10\t\n11\t## ADR-1: Email rendering — `@react-email/components` (new dependency)\n12\t\n13\t**Context.** FR-7/FR-8 require branded HTML+plain-text email templates\n14\t(invite, password-reset, generic) sharing a base layout. The codebase has\n15\tno email-rendering layer today (`sendInvite()` in\n16\t`src/server/services/users.ts` is a logging-only stub per FR-9). NFR-1\n17\tscopes MUI to *visible app UI*; it explicitly exempts email templates\n18\tbecause MUI's `sx`/emotion runtime CSS does not survive email-client HTML\n19\tsanitizers (no `<style>` tag support, inconsistent CSS-in-JS rendering in\n20\tOutlook/Gmail clients).\n21\t\n22\t**Decision.** Add `@react-email/components` (+ `@react-email/render`) as\n23\tthe email templating layer, rendered server-side to both an HTML string and\n24\ta plain-text string. This is a new dependency, but it is the one intake\n25\talready named in `detectionNotes` (\"adds Nodemailer + @react-email/components\n26\tfor the email layer\"), and it's the standard choice for React-authored,\n27\temail-client-safe markup (table-based layout, inlined styles) — hand-rolling\n28\tthat is a bigger lift than reusing the library intake already flagged.\n29\tTemplates live under `src/server/email/templates/`, outside the app's React\n30\ttree, so they never import MUI or app-side providers.\n31\t\n32\t**Consequences.** One new runtime dependency. Templates are a separate\n33\tcomponent universe from the app (plain React components, no MUI, no\n34\t`'use client'`) — contributors must know not to reach for app UI components\n35\there. Base layout (logo/name header, footer with school address + manage-\n36\tpreferences link + disclosure sentence) is a single shared component per\n37\tFR-7, so the three templates (FR-8) stay thin.\n38\t\n39\t_Cites: FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, NFR-1, NFR-6_\n40\t\n41\t## ADR-2: Email transport — Nodemailer with a console-transport dev fallback\n42\t\n43\t**Context.** FR-10/FR-13 require sending queued emails via SMTP, with env\n44\tvars `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`, and an\n45\t`EMAIL_TRANSPORT` switch (`smtp|console`, default `console` in dev) so local\n46\tdev never needs real SMTP creds.\n47\t\n48\t**Decision.** Add `nodemailer` as the SMTP client — it's the de facto\n49\tstandard Node SMTP library, zero-config for any provider the school's ops\n50\tteam points `SMTP_HOST` at, and needs no additional service/queue\n51\tinfrastructure. Wrap it behind a one-function `sendMail()` in\n52\t`src/server/email/transport.ts` that switches on `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`: `smtp`\n53\tconstructs a Nodemailer transporter from the env vars, `console` just logs\n54\tsubject/recipient/text (FR-13) and returns success. No new dependency\n55\tbeyond Nodemailer itself — no mail-queue service, no third-party ESP SDK,\n56\tbecause the queue is already modeled in Postgres (`EmailOutbox`, ADR-3).\n57\t\n58\t**Consequences.** Local/dev/CI runs need zero external services. Production\n59\trequires real SMTP credentials in env; if a future PRD needs provider-specific\n60\tfeatures (templates-as-a-service, bounce webhooks), that's a new ADR, not a\n61\tretrofit of this one.\n62\t\n63\t_Cites: FR-10, FR-13_\n64\t\n65\t## ADR-3: Email queue & delivery guarantees — Postgres row-locking, no message broker\n66\t\n67\t**Context.** FR-10/FR-11/FR-12 need an outbox with retries/backoff and a\n68\tdispatcher invocable both as an HTTP endpoint (external cron) and a local\n69\tloop. NFR-4 requires no email is ever sent twice under concurrent\n70\tdispatchers, and that rows stuck `SENDING` for >10 min self-heal back to\n71\t`PENDING`.\n72\t\n73\t**Decision.** Model the queue as the `EmailOutbox` Prisma table (FR-1) and\n74\tdrive the dispatcher with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` (as a\n75\t`prisma.$queryRaw` transaction) to claim a batch — Postgres supports this\n76\tnatively, so no Redis/SQS/BullMQ is needed. This keeps delivery state in\n77\tthe same transactional store as the rest of the app (one DB to operate,\n78\tbackup, and reason about) and satisfies the \"never sent twice\" guarantee\n79\tvia row-level locks instead of a distributed lock service. The 10-minute\n80\tstuck-`SENDING` recovery (NFR-4) is a plain `UPDATE ... WHERE status =\n81\t'SENDING' AND updatedAt < now() - interval '10 minutes'` run at the top of\n82\teach dispatch call — no separate sweeper process.\n83\t\n84\t**Consequences.** Dispatch throughput is bounded by what a single Postgres\n85\ttable can do under `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`; fine at this app's scale\n86\t(schools, not millions of emails/day — NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/2s bar is the\n87\tstated ceiling). If volume ever outgrows a single-table queue, promoting to\n88\ta real broker is a new ADR, not a patch to this one.\n89\t`ponytail: in-memory last-run tracking for purgeOldNotifications() (FR-17)\n90\tis a single-process assumption — acceptable per the PRD's own note that\n91\tre-running after a restart is fine; move to a DB-tracked cursor only if a\n92\tmulti-instance deploy makes double-purges a real cost.`\n93\t\n94\t_Cites: FR-1, FR-10, FR-11, FR-12, NFR-2, NFR-4_\n95\t\n96\t## ADR-4: Dispatcher trigger — HTTP endpoint + optional local loop, no cron infra\n97\t\n98\t**Context.** FR-12 asks for both `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\n99\t(bearer-protected, for an external scheduler) and `npm run worker:email`\n100\t(a local loop calling `dispatchEmails` every 15s) \"for local/simple\n101\tdeployments.\"\n102\t\n103\t**Decision.** Ship both as thin callers of the same `dispatchEmails()`\n104\tfunction — the route handler for the HTTP path, and a small `tsx` script\n105\t(`scripts/worker-email.ts`, matching the existing `tsx`-based scripts\n106\tpattern already used for `db:seed`) for the loop. No new process manager,\n107\tno node-cron dependency: `setInterval`-in-a-script is sufficient for a\n108\t15-second local loop, and the HTTP path is what production actually relies\n109\ton (external scheduler hits the bearer-protected route). Auth is the\n110\texisting bearer-token-against-`CRON_SECRET` pattern (NFR-8), no new auth\n111\tprimitive.\n112\t\n113\t**Consequences.** Production deployments must wire an external scheduler\n114\t(cron, platform's scheduled-task feature, etc.) to hit the dispatch route —\n115\tthis PRD does not provide one. That's explicitly in scope per FR-12's\n116\twording (\"for an external scheduler\") and out of scope per NFR-10 (no new\n117\tinfra beyond what's listed).\n118\t\n119\t_Cites: FR-12, NFR-8_\n120\t\n121\t## ADR-5: Notification type safety — literal union derived from the registry, no new validation library\n122\t\n123\t**Context.** FR-2/FR-3 require a typed registry (`NOTIFICATION_TYPES`) and\n124\t`notify()` rejecting unknown type keys at compile time.\n125\t\n126\t**Decision.** Define `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` as a `const` object and derive the\n127\tkey union via `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (standard TS pattern,\n128\talready idiomatic in a `strict: true` codebase — no new dependency). Runtime\n129\tvalidation of request-boundary inputs (e.g. the `type` field arriving in an\n130\tAPI body) uses `zod`, already a dependency, matching the rest of the\n131\tcodebase's API-input-validation convention.\n132\t\n133\t**Consequences.** None beyond normal TS discipline — adding a notification\n134\ttype later means editing the one registry object, and every caller of\n135\t`notify()` gets the new key for free (or a compile error if they typo it).\n136\t\n137\t_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, NFR-9_\n138\t\n139\t## ADR-6: No new dependency for polling/popover UI\n140\t\n141\t**Context.** FR-14/FR-15 need a 30s-interval unread-count poll (paused on\n142\t`visibilitychange`) and a popover with a notification list.\n143\t\n144\t**Decision.** Use plain `useEffect` + `setInterval` + the\n145\t`document.visibilitychange` event (native browser APIs) for polling, and\n146\tMUI's own `Popover`/`List`/`Badge` components (NFR-1) for the UI — no\n147\tpolling library (no `swr`/`react-query` in the dependency list today, and\n148\tadding one for a single 30s interval is disproportionate to the need).\n149\t\n150\t**Consequences.** If a later PRD needs broader client-side data-fetching\n151\t/caching (multiple polled resources, dedup, retry), that's the point to\n152\tintroduce `swr` or `@tanstack/react-query` as a real ADR — not pre-empted\n153\there for one endpoint.\n154\t\n155\t_Cites: FR-14, FR-15, NFR-1, NFR-10_\n156\t\n157\t## Summary of new dependencies\n158\t\n159\t| Package | Why | Alternative considered & rejected |\n160\t|---|---|---|\n161\t| `nodemailer` | SMTP client for the dispatcher | Provider-specific ESP SDK — rejected, over-fits to one vendor; PRD only asks for generic SMTP env vars |\n162\t| `@react-email/components`, `@react-email/render` | Email-client-safe HTML+text templates | Hand-written HTML strings — rejected, harder to keep DRY across 3+ templates and the shared base layout; MUI — rejected per NFR-1's explicit email exemption |\n163\t\n164\tNo other new dependencies. Everything else (queueing, retries, locking,\n165\tscheduling, type-safety, polling) is covered by Postgres, Prisma, the\n166\tTypeScript compiler, and native browser/Node APIs already in this stack.\n167\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe42c453-12ae-4515-b32c-f0603dc8fe6d","uuid":"ba95d04f-ad97-42bf-bdf9-93ddd28e466b","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:04:21.615Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email\n\nTicket: abcd-04 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n\nBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\nNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nMUI v9 + emotion. This PRD is brownfield on top of that stack — the\ndecisions below are only the deltas this PRD's requirements force, not a\nre-litigation of the base stack.\n\n## ADR-1: Email rendering — `@react-email/components` (new dependency)\n\n**Context.** FR-7/FR-8 require branded HTML+plain-text email templates\n(invite, password-reset, generic) sharing a base layout. The codebase has\nno email-rendering layer today (`sendInvite()` in\n`src/server/services/users.ts` is a logging-only stub per FR-9). NFR-1\nscopes MUI to *visible app UI*; it explicitly exempts email templates\nbecause MUI's `sx`/emotion runtime CSS does not survive email-client HTML\nsanitizers (no `<style>` tag support, inconsistent CSS-in-JS rendering in\nOutlook/Gmail clients).\n\n**Decision.** Add `@react-email/components` (+ `@react-email/render`) as\nthe email templating layer, rendered server-side to both an HTML string and\na plain-text string. This is a new dependency, but it is the one intake\nalready named in `detectionNotes` (\"adds Nodemailer + @react-email/components\nfor the email layer\"), and it's the standard choice for React-authored,\nemail-client-safe markup (table-based layout, inlined styles) — hand-rolling\nthat is a bigger lift than reusing the library intake already flagged.\nTemplates live under `src/server/email/templates/`, outside the app's React\ntree, so they never import MUI or app-side providers.\n\n**Consequences.** One new runtime dependency. Templates are a separate\ncomponent universe from the app (plain React components, no MUI, no\n`'use client'`) — contributors must know not to reach for app UI components\nhere. Base layout (logo/name header, footer with school address + manage-\npreferences link + disclosure sentence) is a single shared component per\nFR-7, so the three templates (FR-8) stay thin.\n\n_Cites: FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, NFR-1, NFR-6_\n\n## ADR-2: Email transport — Nodemailer with a console-transport dev fallback\n\n**Context.** FR-10/FR-13 require sending queued emails via SMTP, with env\nvars `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`, and an\n`EMAIL_TRANSPORT` switch (`smtp|console`, default `console` in dev) so local\ndev never needs real SMTP creds.\n\n**Decision.** Add `nodemailer` as the SMTP client — it's the de facto\nstandard Node SMTP library, zero-config for any provider the school's ops\nteam points `SMTP_HOST` at, and needs no additional service/queue\ninfrastructure. Wrap it behind a one-function `sendMail()` in\n`src/server/email/transport.ts` that switches on `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`: `smtp`\nconstructs a Nodemailer transporter from the env vars, `console` just logs\nsubject/recipient/text (FR-13) and returns success. No new dependency\nbeyond Nodemailer itself — no mail-queue service, no third-party ESP SDK,\nbecause the queue is already modeled in Postgres (`EmailOutbox`, ADR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** Local/dev/CI runs need zero external services. Production\nrequires real SMTP credentials in env; if a future PRD needs provider-specific\nfeatures (templates-as-a-service, bounce webhooks), that's a new ADR, not a\nretrofit of this one.\n\n_Cites: FR-10, FR-13_\n\n## ADR-3: Email queue & delivery guarantees — Postgres row-locking, no message broker\n\n**Context.** FR-10/FR-11/FR-12 need an outbox with retries/backoff and a\ndispatcher invocable both as an HTTP endpoint (external cron) and a local\nloop. NFR-4 requires no email is ever sent twice under concurrent\ndispatchers, and that rows stuck `SENDING` for >10 min self-heal back to\n`PENDING`.\n\n**Decision.** Model the queue as the `EmailOutbox` Prisma table (FR-1) and\ndrive the dispatcher with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` (as a\n`prisma.$queryRaw` transaction) to claim a batch — Postgres supports this\nnatively, so no Redis/SQS/BullMQ is needed. This keeps delivery state in\nthe same transactional store as the rest of the app (one DB to operate,\nbackup, and reason about) and satisfies the \"never sent twice\" guarantee\nvia row-level locks instead of a distributed lock service. The 10-minute\nstuck-`SENDING` recovery (NFR-4) is a plain `UPDATE ... WHERE status =\n'SENDING' AND updatedAt < now() - interval '10 minutes'` run at the top of\neach dispatch call — no separate sweeper process.\n\n**Consequences.** Dispatch throughput is bounded by what a single Postgres\ntable can do under `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`; fine at this app's scale\n(schools, not millions of emails/day — NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/2s bar is the\nstated ceiling). If volume ever outgrows a single-table queue, promoting to\na real broker is a new ADR, not a patch to this one.\n`ponytail: in-memory last-run tracking for purgeOldNotifications() (FR-17)\nis a single-process assumption — acceptable per the PRD's own note that\nre-running after a restart is fine; move to a DB-tracked cursor only if a\nmulti-instance deploy makes double-purges a real cost.`\n\n_Cites: FR-1, FR-10, FR-11, FR-12, NFR-2, NFR-4_\n\n## ADR-4: Dispatcher trigger — HTTP endpoint + optional local loop, no cron infra\n\n**Context.** FR-12 asks for both `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\n(bearer-protected, for an external scheduler) and `npm run worker:email`\n(a local loop calling `dispatchEmails` every 15s) \"for local/simple\ndeployments.\"\n\n**Decision.** Ship both as thin callers of the same `dispatchEmails()`\nfunction — the route handler for the HTTP path, and a small `tsx` script\n(`scripts/worker-email.ts`, matching the existing `tsx`-based scripts\npattern already used for `db:seed`) for the loop. No new process manager,\nno node-cron dependency: `setInterval`-in-a-script is sufficient for a\n15-second local loop, and the HTTP path is what production actually relies\non (external scheduler hits the bearer-protected route). Auth is the\nexisting bearer-token-against-`CRON_SECRET` pattern (NFR-8), no new auth\nprimitive.\n\n**Consequences.** Production deployments must wire an external scheduler\n(cron, platform's scheduled-task feature, etc.) to hit the dispatch route —\nthis PRD does not provide one. That's explicitly in scope per FR-12's\nwording (\"for an external scheduler\") and out of scope per NFR-10 (no new\ninfra beyond what's listed).\n\n_Cites: FR-12, NFR-8_\n\n## ADR-5: Notification type safety — literal union derived from the registry, no new validation library\n\n**Context.** FR-2/FR-3 require a typed registry (`NOTIFICATION_TYPES`) and\n`notify()` rejecting unknown type keys at compile time.\n\n**Decision.** Define `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` as a `const` object and derive the\nkey union via `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (standard TS pattern,\nalready idiomatic in a `strict: true` codebase — no new dependency). Runtime\nvalidation of request-boundary inputs (e.g. the `type` field arriving in an\nAPI body) uses `zod`, already a dependency, matching the rest of the\ncodebase's API-input-validation convention.\n\n**Consequences.** None beyond normal TS discipline — adding a notification\ntype later means editing the one registry object, and every caller of\n`notify()` gets the new key for free (or a compile error if they typo it).\n\n_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, NFR-9_\n\n## ADR-6: No new dependency for polling/popover UI\n\n**Context.** FR-14/FR-15 need a 30s-interval unread-count poll (paused on\n`visibilitychange`) and a popover with a notification list.\n\n**Decision.** Use plain `useEffect` + `setInterval` + the\n`document.visibilitychange` event (native browser APIs) for polling, and\nMUI's own `Popover`/`List`/`Badge` components (NFR-1) for the UI — no\npolling library (no `swr`/`react-query` in the dependency list today, and\nadding one for a single 30s interval is disproportionate to the need).\n\n**Consequences.** If a later PRD needs broader client-side data-fetching\n/caching (multiple polled resources, dedup, retry), that's the point to\nintroduce `swr` or `@tanstack/react-query` as a real ADR — not pre-empted\nhere for one endpoint.\n\n_Cites: FR-14, FR-15, NFR-1, NFR-10_\n\n## Summary of new dependencies\n\n| Package | Why | Alternative considered & rejected |\n|---|---|---|\n| `nodemailer` | SMTP client for the dispatcher | Provider-specific ESP SDK — rejected, over-fits to one vendor; PRD only asks for generic SMTP env vars |\n| `@react-email/components`, `@react-email/render` | Email-client-safe HTML+text templates | Hand-written HTML strings — rejected, harder to keep DRY across 3+ templates and the shared base layout; MUI — rejected per NFR-1's explicit email exemption |\n\nNo other new dependencies. Everything else (queueing, retries, locking,\nscheduling, type-safety, polling) is covered by Postgres, Prisma, the\nTypeScript compiler, and native browser/Node APIs already in this stack.\n","numLines":167,"startLine":1,"totalLines":167}}}
