ls({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
