{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RaY24dhgxp3qU9DZfY8j1W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t## Overview\n6\t\n7\tPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\n8\tstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n9\t(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n10\t(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n11\t(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\n12\tresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n13\t\n14\t**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n15\t`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\n16\tfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\n17\tunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\n18\tgrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\n19\tfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\n20\tMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\n21\titems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\n22\tthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\n23\tregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n24\t`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\n25\tland, with no further schema change.\n26\t\n27\t**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\n28\tPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\n29\tin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n30\t(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n31\t`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n32\t`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n33\t`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\n34\tdoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\n35\tConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\n36\texplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\n37\tschedule that consolidation here.\n38\t\n39\t**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\n40\tservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\n41\tFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\n42\trequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\n43\tchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n44\t`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\n45\tas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\n46\tconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\n47\tfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\n48\tthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\n49\thomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n50\t\n51\t## Component Breakdown\n52\t\n53\t### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n54\t`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n55\t`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\n56\tall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\n57\tFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\n58\treads/writes.\n59\t\n60\t### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\n61\tThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\n62\tFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n63\t(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\n64\tits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\n65\ttech-stack ADR-1):\n66\t\n67\t- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n68\t  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n69\t  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n70\t  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n71\t  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n72\t  route.\n73\t- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n74\t  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n75\t  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n76\t  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n77\t  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n78\t  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n79\t  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n80\t  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n81\t- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n82\t  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n83\t  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n84\t  `audit()`.\n85\t- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n86\t  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n87\t  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n88\t  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n89\t\n90\tFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\n91\tcreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\n92\tsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\n93\tpoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n94\t\n95\tFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\n96\trosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\n97\tapplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\n98\tcourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n99\t\n100\t### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\n101\tCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\n102\tFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\n103\tand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\n104\tadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\n105\treusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\n106\tstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n107\t`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\n108\tenroll/drop.\n109\t\n110\t### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\n111\tCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n112\t(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\n113\tvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\n114\tcheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\n115\trefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\n116\ta non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\n117\tcreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\n118\treused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\n119\tpicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n120\t\n121\t### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\n122\tFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n123\t`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\n124\tDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n125\t`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\n126\tendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\n127\there, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\n128\tstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\n129\tPRD's scope.\n130\t\n131\t### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\n132\tFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\n133\tbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\n134\tmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\n135\tPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n136\t\n137\t### Course public surface\n138\t`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n139\t`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n140\t`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\n141\tSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\n142\tfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\n143\tread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n144\t\n145\t**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\n146\tnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n147\t(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n148\t`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\n149\tand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\n150\tdata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n151\t\n152\t### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\n153\tRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n154\t(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\n155\tenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\n156\tgrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\n157\tno new parent-fanout code).\n158\t\n159\t### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n160\t`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\n161\tflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n162\t`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n163\t\n164\t### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\n165\tNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\n166\tteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\n167\tFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\n168\tstudent page (no new access function).\n169\t\n170\t### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\n171\tEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n172\t→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\n173\texisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\n174\tlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\n175\tthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\n176\tinternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n177\t\n178\t## Data Flow\n179\t\n180\t**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n181\t`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n182\t/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n183\t`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n184\t`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\n185\tuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n186\t`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\n187\tcommit → envelope response.\n188\t\n189\t**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n190\t`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n191\t`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\n192\tCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\n193\tthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n194\t\n195\t**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n196\t`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n197\t(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\n198\tagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n199\t\n200\t**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n201\t/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n202\t.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\n203\tenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n204\t\n205\t**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n206\t/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\n207\texisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n208\t`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n209\t`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n210\t\n211\t## Requirements Traceability\n212\t\n213\t| Requirement | Design Element |\n214\t|---|---|\n215\t| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n216\t| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n217\t| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n218\t| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n219\t| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n220\t| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n221\t| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n222\t| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n223\t| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n224\t| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n225\t| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n226\t| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n227\t| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n228\t| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n229\t| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n230\t| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n231\t| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n232\t| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n233\t| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n234\t| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n235\t| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n236\t| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n237\t| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n238\t| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n239\t| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n240\t| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n241\t| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n242\t| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n243\t| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n244\t| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n245\t| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n246\t\n247\t## Status\n248\t\n249\t`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\n250\topen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\n251\tthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n252\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"663c6c96-740a-404e-b9ed-7275dd3841b6","uuid":"6aca3c45-d5dd-4230-bdc6-74a77d78fd07","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:34:22.693Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\nstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\nresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n\n**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\nfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\nunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\ngrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\nfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\nMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\nitems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\nthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\nregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\nland, with no further schema change.\n\n**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\nPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\nin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\ndoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\nConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\nexplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\nschedule that consolidation here.\n\n**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\nservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\nFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\nrequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\nchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\nas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\nconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\nfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\nthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\nhomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\nall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\nFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\nreads/writes.\n\n### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\nThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\nFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\nits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\ntech-stack ADR-1):\n\n- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n  route.\n- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n  `audit()`.\n- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n\nFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\ncreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\nsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\npoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n\nFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\nrosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\napplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\ncourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n\n### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\nFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\nand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\nadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\nreusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\nstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\nenroll/drop.\n\n### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\nvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\ncheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\nrefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\na non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\ncreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\nreused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\npicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n\n### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\nFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\nDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\nendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\nhere, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\nstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\nPRD's scope.\n\n### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\nFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\nbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\nmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\nPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n\n### Course public surface\n`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\nSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\nfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\nread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n\n**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\nnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\nand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\ndata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n\n### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\nRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\nenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\ngrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\nno new parent-fanout code).\n\n### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\nflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n\n### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\nNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\nteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\nFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\nstudent page (no new access function).\n\n### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\nEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\nexisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\nlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\nthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\ninternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\nuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\ncommit → envelope response.\n\n**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\nCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\nthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n\n**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\nagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n\n**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\nenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n\n**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\nexisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n\n## Status\n\n`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\nopen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\nthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n","numLines":252,"startLine":1,"totalLines":252}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RaY24dhgxp3qU9DZfY8j1W","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
