plicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Auto-drop on section removal: removing a student from a section sets every ACTIVE enrollment in that section's CORE courses to DROPPED with droppedAt = now; elective enrollments are left untouched.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"'Move to section…' single action performs the FR-7 enroll and FR-8 drop steps for the destination/source sections in one database transaction, exposed via POST /api/students/:id/move-section.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; API table row POST /api/students/:id/move-section\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Creating a new CORE course on a section enrolls all of that section's current members (ACTIVE) in the new course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Capacity enforcement: adding a student beyond section or course capacity is refused with a CONFLICT error, message pattern 'Section 7A is full (30/30).', unless the admin explicitly ticks 'Override capacity'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criteria #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Dropped enrollments retain all historical data (attendance, grades) visible to admins and teachers, but dropped students disappear from active rosters and from add-student pickers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses: filters for academic year, grade level, subject, teacher, kind, and free-text search by name/code; table of code, name, subject colour chip (reusing Subject.color, already on the model), section, teacher, enrolled count, kind.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; verified Subject.color already exists on the Subject model in prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (optional, required when kind=CORE), teacher, up to 3 co-teachers, name, code (auto-filled from subject+section, editable, forced uppercase), kind, capacity, description.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses/[id]/enrollment: enrolled-students table with drop/reactivate row actions and an 'Add students' picker; for CORE courses show an info note that membership is managed via the section instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /courses/[courseId] header: subject colour band, course name, code, teacher(s) (including co-teachers), section, room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a course-tabs registry at src/config/course-tabs.ts (same shape as the existing src/config/student-tabs.ts, with a `roles` field) rendered as a scrollable MUI Tabs on the course home page; this PRD registers 'Overview' (description/teachers/counts, all roles that can view the course) and 'Roster' (TEACHER/ADMIN: full student list with avatar/name/admission number/link to student page/status; STUDENT: classmates' names only; PARENT: tab not shown).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; verified against the existing (empty) src/config/student-tabs.ts pattern this PRD is told to mirror\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add src/server/auth/course-access.ts exporting assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN: all; TEACHER: teacher or co-teacher; STUDENT: has an ACTIVE enrollment; PARENT: any linked child has an ACTIVE enrollment) and assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN, teacher, co-teacher) for later write operations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Build /my-courses: TEACHER sees MUI Cards in a responsive Grid for each non-archived course they teach/co-teach this year (name, section, enrolled count); STUDENT sees cards for their ACTIVE enrollments (name, teacher); PARENT sees the same cards grouped by child.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sidebar nav entries: 'My courses' for TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT, and 'Sections'/'Courses' grouped under an 'Administration' section for ADMIN. NavItem currently has no grouping field — src/config/navigation.ts (verified) is a flat array with only Dashboard/Notifications/Email log entries and no 'group' concept, and no admin-facing pages exist yet for the PRD-02/PRD-03 entities (academic years, subjects, rooms, grade levels, users) that would also belong in such a group. The Architect must decide whether to add a lightweight `group` field to NavItem now or ship Sections/Courses as flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav grouping PRD lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; cross-checked against the current flat src/config/navigation.ts and the absence of an 'Administration' grouping or admin pages anywhere under src/app/(app)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Register student tab 'Courses' in src/config/student-tabs.ts (visible to every role that can view the student): a table of the student's courses this year with teacher and enrollment status, plus their section and homeroom teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing getAccessibleStudentIds(user) in src/server/auth/student-access.ts so a TEACHER additionally gets students with ACTIVE enrollments in courses they teach or co-teach, plus members of the section they are homeroom teacher of.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1; verified getAccessibleStudentIds already exists and is exported from src/server/auth/student-access.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Expose the full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Gsega7qEcvT594wcRA1Ko6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT4jr2F8VM858rZBeMBW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D7kkmqEzm6jrjDyYxGkKGi","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_read_input_tokens":28011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575},"output_tokens":56,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"663c6c96-740a-404e-b9ed-7275dd3841b6","uuid":"21ba96ca-6cac-439c-af04-6f9d31dade8a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:34:23.727Z","request_id":"req_011CgT4jqfuPi3PjHp8h8ocK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01D7kkmqEzm6jrjDyYxGkKGi":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D7kkmqEzm6jrjDyYxGkKGi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-05 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\n6\tNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\n7\tMUI v9 + emotion, `zod` for input validation, `date-fns`. This PRD is\n8\tbrownfield on top of that stack — intake's detection notes already confirm\n9\tit \"adds no new frontend framework or dependency,\" only new Prisma models\n10\tand pages. The decisions below are the implementation-pattern deltas this\n11\tPRD's requirements force, not a re-litigation of the base stack. No new\n12\truntime dependency is added by this PRD.\n13\t\n14\t## ADR-1: Bulk enroll/drop writes — `Prisma.$transaction` with batched\n15\t`createMany`/`updateMany`, no job queue\n16\t\n17\t**Context.** NFR-3 requires adding 30 students to a section with 8 core\n18\tcourses (240 resulting enrollments) to complete in under 1 second. FR-7–\n19\tFR-10 describe enroll-on-add, drop-on-remove, move-section, and\n20\tcreate-core-course as all-or-nothing operations touching many `Enrollment`\n21\trows at once.\n22\t\n23\t**Decision.** Implement each of these as a single `prisma.$transaction`\n24\tthat computes the affected (studentId, courseId) pairs in memory first,\n25\tthen issues one `enrollment.createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for new\n26\tACTIVE rows and one `enrollment.updateMany` (keyed on the unique\n27\t`[courseId, studentId]`) to reactivate previously-DROPPED rows, instead of\n28\tlooping `create`/`update` calls per student per course. This is plain\n29\tPrisma batch-write API already in the installed `@prisma/client` — no\n30\tqueue, no background worker, no new dependency. 240 rows in one\n31\t`createMany` plus one `updateMany` comfortably clears the 1-second bar on\n32\tPostgres; a per-row loop (240 round-trips) would not.\n33\t\n34\t**Consequences.** Business logic that decides \"create vs. reactivate\" for\n35\teach pair must be computed with a single prior `findMany`, not per-row\n36\tqueries, to keep the whole operation at a small constant number of\n37\tround-trips. If a future PRD needs enroll/drop across thousands of rows\n38\t(bulk import), that's a new ADR for chunking or a background job — not a\n39\tretrofit of this one.\n40\t\n41\t_Cites: FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10, NFR-3_\n42\t\n43\t## ADR-2: Capacity + uniqueness enforcement — DB unique constraints for\n44\tidentity, in-transaction count check for capacity, no distributed lock\n45\t\n46\t**Context.** NFR-2 requires the one-section-per-student-per-year rule to be\n47\ta database constraint, not just app logic. FR-11 requires capacity\n48\tenforcement (section and course) that refuses with CONFLICT unless an\n49\texplicit \"Override capacity\" flag is set, under concurrent admin actions.\n50\t\n51\t**Decision.** Identity/duplication rules (`@@unique([studentId,\n52\tacademicYearId])` on `SectionMember`, `@@unique([courseId, studentId])` on\n53\t`Enrollment`) are enforced by Postgres unique indexes already specified in\n54\tFR-1; application code catches the Prisma `P2002` violation and maps it to\n55\tthe existing CONFLICT error envelope rather than pre-checking existence\n56\tfirst (avoids a check-then-insert race). Capacity, which is a *computed*\n57\tcount rather than a stored invariant, is checked inside the same\n58\t`$transaction` that performs the insert — `count()` the current\n59\tmembers/enrollments, compare to `capacity`, and only then\n60\t`create`/`createMany`, so a concurrent request either serializes behind the\n61\ttransaction or re-checks and fails cleanly. No advisory lock, no Redis, no\n62\tdistributed-lock library: Postgres's own transactional read-your-writes\n63\twithin one `$transaction` is sufficient at this app's scale (a school\n64\tadmin console, not a high-concurrency storefront).\n65\t\n66\t**Consequences.** Capacity checks are \"good enough\" serialization, not a\n67\thard guarantee under extreme concurrent load from multiple admins hitting\n68\tthe exact same section simultaneously; acceptable because this is an\n69\tinternal admin tool with low write concurrency. If that ever changes,\n70\tupgrading the capacity check to `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` on a row is a small\n71\tfollow-up, not a new ADR.\n72\t\n73\t_Cites: FR-1, FR-11, NFR-2_\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-3: No new dependency for the admin UI (tables, dialogs, pickers)\n76\t\n77\t**Context.** NFR-1 mandates every visible element in the sections/courses/\n78\tenrollment screens come from `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, or MUI\n79\tX, with no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select,\n80\tetc.). FR-2–FR-6, FR-13–FR-19 describe filtered tables, create/edit\n81\tdialogs, multi-select pickers, tabs, and card grids.\n82\t\n83\t**Decision.** Build all of it from the already-installed MUI v9 set plus\n84\tthe existing shared components (`DataTable`, `UserPicker`, `ConfirmDialog`,\n85\t`useToast`, `PageHeader`) per the brownfield reuse already confirmed in\n86\tintake. Multi-select student/subject pickers extend `UserPicker`'s\n87\texisting `role` filter pattern rather than introducing a new\n88\tautocomplete/select component. No new UI dependency.\n89\t\n90\t**Consequences.** None beyond the existing MUI-MCP lookup discipline\n91\t(NFR-1) for any component variant not already used elsewhere in the\n92\tcodebase.\n93\t\n94\t_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-13, FR-14, FR-15, FR-17, FR-19, NFR-1_\n95\t\n96\t## ADR-4: Auth — keep the `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` stand-in, no new\n97\tauth helper\n98\t\n99\t**Context.** NFR-7 flags that `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and\n100\t`requireUser()` described in the platform context don't exist yet — only\n101\t`requireRole.ts` and `student-access.ts` are present. This is the same\n102\tbrownfield gap PRD-04's architect handoff already flagged.\n103\t\n104\t**Decision.** New route handlers in this PRD (sections/courses/enrollment\n105\tCRUD, move-section, roster) continue to use the existing\n106\t`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`-style stand-in, and `assertCanViewCourse`/\n107\t`assertCanManageCourse` (FR-18) are added as plain functions in\n108\t`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` alongside the existing\n109\t`student-access.ts`, not as part of a new `permissions.ts` module. No new\n110\tauth library, no new abstraction invented ahead of PRD-01 landing it\n111\tproperly.\n112\t\n113\t**Consequences.** Role-gating logic stays slightly duplicated across\n114\tper-feature `*-access.ts` files until PRD-01 ships a real\n115\t`permissions.ts`; that consolidation is PRD-01's job, not this one's.\n116\t\n117\t_Cites: FR-18, FR-22, NFR-7_\n118\t\n119\t## Summary of new dependencies\n120\t\n121\tNone. Every requirement in this PRD (bulk transactional writes, capacity\n122\tchecks, uniqueness, admin UI, auth gating) is covered by Prisma 5,\n123\tPostgreSQL, MUI v9, and TypeScript already in the stack — intake's\n124\tconfidence-100% stack detection holds.\n125\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"663c6c96-740a-404e-b9ed-7275dd3841b6","uuid":"0c8e4afc-d66d-4b7c-9f37-6a7154947d43","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:34:23.736Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment\n\nTicket: abcd-05 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n\nBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\nNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nMUI v9 + emotion, `zod` for input validation, `date-fns`. This PRD is\nbrownfield on top of that stack — intake's detection notes already confirm\nit \"adds no new frontend framework or dependency,\" only new Prisma models\nand pages. The decisions below are the implementation-pattern deltas this\nPRD's requirements force, not a re-litigation of the base stack. No new\nruntime dependency is added by this PRD.\n\n## ADR-1: Bulk enroll/drop writes — `Prisma.$transaction` with batched\n`createMany`/`updateMany`, no job queue\n\n**Context.** NFR-3 requires adding 30 students to a section with 8 core\ncourses (240 resulting enrollments) to complete in under 1 second. FR-7–\nFR-10 describe enroll-on-add, drop-on-remove, move-section, and\ncreate-core-course as all-or-nothing operations touching many `Enrollment`\nrows at once.\n\n**Decision.** Implement each of these as a single `prisma.$transaction`\nthat computes the affected (studentId, courseId) pairs in memory first,\nthen issues one `enrollment.createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for new\nACTIVE rows and one `enrollment.updateMany` (keyed on the unique\n`[courseId, studentId]`) to reactivate previously-DROPPED rows, instead of\nlooping `create`/`update` calls per student per course. This is plain\nPrisma batch-write API already in the installed `@prisma/client` — no\nqueue, no background worker, no new dependency. 240 rows in one\n`createMany` plus one `updateMany` comfortably clears the 1-second bar on\nPostgres; a per-row loop (240 round-trips) would not.\n\n**Consequences.** Business logic that decides \"create vs. reactivate\" for\neach pair must be computed with a single prior `findMany`, not per-row\nqueries, to keep the whole operation at a small constant number of\nround-trips. If a future PRD needs enroll/drop across thousands of rows\n(bulk import), that's a new ADR for chunking or a background job — not a\nretrofit of this one.\n\n_Cites: FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10, NFR-3_\n\n## ADR-2: Capacity + uniqueness enforcement — DB unique constraints for\nidentity, in-transaction count check for capacity, no distributed lock\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 requires the one-section-per-student-per-year rule to be\na database constraint, not just app logic. FR-11 requires capacity\nenforcement (section and course) that refuses with CONFLICT unless an\nexplicit \"Override capacity\" flag is set, under concurrent admin actions.\n\n**Decision.** Identity/duplication rules (`@@unique([studentId,\nacademicYearId])` on `SectionMember`, `@@unique([courseId, studentId])` on\n`Enrollment`) are enforced by Postgres unique indexes already specified in\nFR-1; application code catches the Prisma `P2002` violation and maps it to\nthe existing CONFLICT error envelope rather than pre-checking existence\nfirst (avoids a check-then-insert race). Capacity, which is a *computed*\ncount rather than a stored invariant, is checked inside the same\n`$transaction` that performs the insert — `count()` the current\nmembers/enrollments, compare to `capacity`, and only then\n`create`/`createMany`, so a concurrent request either serializes behind the\ntransaction or re-checks and fails cleanly. No advisory lock, no Redis, no\ndistributed-lock library: Postgres's own transactional read-your-writes\nwithin one `$transaction` is sufficient at this app's scale (a school\nadmin console, not a high-concurrency storefront).\n\n**Consequences.** Capacity checks are \"good enough\" serialization, not a\nhard guarantee under extreme concurrent load from multiple admins hitting\nthe exact same section simultaneously; acceptable because this is an\ninternal admin tool with low write concurrency. If that ever changes,\nupgrading the capacity check to `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` on a row is a small\nfollow-up, not a new ADR.\n\n_Cites: FR-1, FR-11, NFR-2_\n\n## ADR-3: No new dependency for the admin UI (tables, dialogs, pickers)\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 mandates every visible element in the sections/courses/\nenrollment screens come from `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, or MUI\nX, with no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select,\netc.). FR-2–FR-6, FR-13–FR-19 describe filtered tables, create/edit\ndialogs, multi-select pickers, tabs, and card grids.\n\n**Decision.** Build all of it from the already-installed MUI v9 set plus\nthe existing shared components (`DataTable`, `UserPicker`, `ConfirmDialog`,\n`useToast`, `PageHeader`) per the brownfield reuse already confirmed in\nintake. Multi-select student/subject pickers extend `UserPicker`'s\nexisting `role` filter pattern rather than introducing a new\nautocomplete/select component. No new UI dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** None beyond the existing MUI-MCP lookup discipline\n(NFR-1) for any component variant not already used elsewhere in the\ncodebase.\n\n_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-13, FR-14, FR-15, FR-17, FR-19, NFR-1_\n\n## ADR-4: Auth — keep the `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` stand-in, no new\nauth helper\n\n**Context.** NFR-7 flags that `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and\n`requireUser()` described in the platform context don't exist yet — only\n`requireRole.ts` and `student-access.ts` are present. This is the same\nbrownfield gap PRD-04's architect handoff already flagged.\n\n**Decision.** New route handlers in this PRD (sections/courses/enrollment\nCRUD, move-section, roster) continue to use the existing\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`-style stand-in, and `assertCanViewCourse`/\n`assertCanManageCourse` (FR-18) are added as plain functions in\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` alongside the existing\n`student-access.ts`, not as part of a new `permissions.ts` module. No new\nauth library, no new abstraction invented ahead of PRD-01 landing it\nproperly.\n\n**Consequences.** Role-gating logic stays slightly duplicated across\nper-feature `*-access.ts` files until PRD-01 ships a real\n`permissions.ts`; that consolidation is PRD-01's job, not this one's.\n\n_Cites: FR-18, FR-22, NFR-7_\n\n## Summary of new dependencies\n\nNone. Every requirement in this PRD (bulk transactional writes, capacity\nchecks, uniqueness, admin UI, auth gating) is covered by Prisma 5,\nPostgreSQL, MUI v9, and TypeScript already in the stack — intake's\nconfidence-100% stack detection holds.\n","numLines":125,"startLine":1,"totalLines":125}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D7kkmqEzm6jrjDyYxGkKGi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
