{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0195tjcoGW8L3risvddCN4wM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n7\t  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n8\t\n9\t  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n10\t    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",\n11\t    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",\n12\t    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",\n13\t    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",\n14\t    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",\n15\t    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",\n16\t    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",\n17\t    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"\n18\t  ],\n19\t\n20\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n21\t    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n22\t    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n23\t    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n24\t    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n25\t    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },\n26\t    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },\n27\t    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n28\t    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },\n29\t    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },\n30\t    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n31\t    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },\n32\t    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },\n33\t    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },\n34\t    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },\n35\t    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n36\t    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },\n37\t    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },\n38\t    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n39\t    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },\n40\t    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },\n41\t    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },\n42\t    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },\n43\t    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },\n44\t    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n45\t    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },\n46\t    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n47\t    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },\n48\t    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },\n49\t    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },\n50\t    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },\n51\t    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n52\t    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },\n53\t    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n54\t    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },\n55\t    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },\n56\t    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n57\t    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }\n58\t  ],\n59\t\n60\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n61\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n62\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n63\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n64\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n65\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n66\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },\n67\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },\n68\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n69\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },\n70\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },\n71\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n72\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }\n73\t  ],\n74\t\n75\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n76\t  \"clarificationLog\": [\n77\t    {\n78\t      \"round\": 1,\n79\t      \"questions\": [\n80\t        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",\n81\t        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",\n82\t        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",\n83\t        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",\n84\t        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",\n85\t        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"\n86\t      ],\n87\t      \"unresolved\": [\n88\t        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",\n89\t        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",\n90\t        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",\n91\t        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"\n92\t      ]\n93\t    }\n94\t  ],\n95\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n96\t}\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"820f2207-bedc-4109-a712-39a38d467e5c","uuid":"3c2dee6e-4b70-4a54-bcbe-3e94606fed6d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:40:54.726Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",\n    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",\n    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",\n    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",\n    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",\n        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",\n        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",\n        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",\n        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",\n        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",\n        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",\n        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",\n        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0195tjcoGW8L3risvddCN4wM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRxUuMFdRhv1r71DmU3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S5Y4nqUd2C9njQjRxwU5JU","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22464,"cache_read_input_tokens":30412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22464},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"820f2207-bedc-4109-a712-39a38d467e5c","uuid":"7189b4c8-465e-42b9-8a11-e4fb4b76f621","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:40:57.163Z","request_id":"req_011CghRxUeyvpdSnQdYGRWt8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01S5Y4nqUd2C9njQjRxwU5JU":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S5Y4nqUd2C9njQjRxwU5JU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:03:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"conventions\": {\n8\t    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention; no /api/v1 prefix - NFR-9 forbids renaming routes)\",\n9\t    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\" },\n10\t    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object?\" } },\n11\t    \"errorCodes\": {\n12\t      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n13\t      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n14\t      \"FORBIDDEN\": 403,\n15\t      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410,\n16\t      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429\n17\t    },\n18\t    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler(parseBody(zodSchema) -> service -> ok()) from src/server/http.ts\",\n19\t    \"csrf\": \"src/middleware.ts rejects non-GET/HEAD /api/* requests whose Origin header is present and differs from the app origin (403 FORBIDDEN). The Auth.js endpoints also use their own CSRF token. Session cookie: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in prod.\",\n20\t    \"unauthenticatedApi\": \"src/middleware.ts returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED for /api/* outside PUBLIC_API_PATHS ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']\",\n21\t    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\", \"NFR-9\", \"FR-12\"]\n22\t  },\n23\t\n24\t  \"endpoints\": [\n25\t    {\n26\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n27\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n28\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint, served by the /api/auth/[...nextauth] catch-all (handlers.GET). Returns the CSRF token that signIn()/signOut() use. Public.\",\n29\t      \"auth\": \"public\",\n30\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n31\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n32\t      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native (not the {data} envelope)\",\n33\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]\n34\t    },\n35\t    {\n36\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n37\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n38\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint (catch-all). Returns the current session or null. Public. Middleware does not gate it.\",\n39\t      \"auth\": \"public\",\n40\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n41\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n42\t        \"oneOf\": [\n43\t          { \"type\": \"null\" },\n44\t          {\n45\t            \"type\": \"object\",\n46\t            \"properties\": {\n47\t              \"user\": {\n48\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n49\t                \"properties\": {\n50\t                  \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n51\t                  \"role\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\", \"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\"] },\n52\t                  \"firstName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n53\t                  \"lastName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n54\t                  \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\" }\n55\t                },\n56\t                \"required\": [\"id\", \"role\", \"firstName\", \"lastName\", \"email\"]\n57\t              },\n58\t              \"expires\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n59\t            }\n60\t          }\n61\t        ]\n62\t      },\n63\t      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n64\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-34\"]\n65\t    },\n66\t    {\n67\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n68\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n69\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js Credentials sign-in (catch-all handlers.POST). Credentials.authorize delegates to authorizeCredentials(): IP rate limit (10 / 5 min) -> trim + lower-case the email -> exactly one bcrypt compare (DUMMY_HASH if the user is missing) -> status/archived/lock checks -> lockout bookkeeping -> audit. On success the jwt callback sets {id, role, firstName, lastName, email, authTime, checkedAt}, maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m. The client calls it through signIn('credentials', {redirect:false}) and reads the error code.\",\n70\t      \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\",\n71\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n72\t        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n73\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n74\t        \"properties\": {\n75\t          \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\" },\n76\t          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n77\t          \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n78\t          \"callbackUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"note\": \"sanitised by safeCallbackUrl(): only a relative path starting with '/' and not '//' or '/\\\\'; otherwise /dashboard\" }\n79\t        },\n80\t        \"required\": [\"email\", \"password\", \"csrfToken\"]\n81\t      },\n82\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n83\t        \"success\": { \"sets-cookie\": \"authjs.session-token (__Secure- prefix in prod)\", \"url\": \"safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)\" },\n84\t        \"failure\": {\n85\t          \"type\": \"object\",\n86\t          \"properties\": {\n87\t            \"error\": { \"const\": \"CredentialsSignin\" },\n88\t            \"code\": {\n89\t              \"type\": \"string\",\n90\t              \"enum\": [\"invalid\", \"disabled\", \"locked:<minutes>\", \"rate_limited\"],\n91\t              \"uiMessages\": {\n92\t                \"invalid\": \"Email or password is incorrect.\",\n93\t                \"disabled\": \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\",\n94\t                \"locked:N\": \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\",\n95\t                \"rate_limited\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n96\t              }\n97\t            }\n98\t          }\n99\t        }\n100\t      },\n101\t      \"sideEffects\": [\n102\t        \"wrong password: failedLoginCount += 1; at 5 -> lockedUntil = now + 15 min, failedLoginCount = 0\",\n103\t        \"success: failedLoginCount = 0, lastLoginAt = now\",\n104\t        \"audit auth.login.success | auth.login.failure {email, reason} | auth.lockout, with the IP from x-forwarded-for\"\n105\t      ],\n106\t      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n107\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-4\"]\n108\t    },\n109\t    {\n110\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n111\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n112\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out (catch-all). Clears the session cookie. The shell calls it through signOut({redirectTo:'/login'}).\",\n113\t      \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\",\n114\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n115\t        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n116\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n117\t        \"properties\": { \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"callbackUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n118\t        \"required\": [\"csrfToken\"]\n119\t      },\n120\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"url\": \"/login\" },\n121\t      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n122\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-32\", \"FR-34\"]\n123\t    },\n124\t    {\n125\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n126\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/accept-invite\",\n127\t      \"description\": \"Activates an invited account. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'INVITE') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> bcrypt.hash(12) -> one transaction {passwordHash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now} + consumeToken -> audit auth.invite.accepted. It does NOT mint a session: on 200 the client calls signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo:'/dashboard'}). Public via the /api/auth/ prefix and protected by the middleware origin check.\",\n128\t      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n129\t      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/accept-invite/route.ts -> services/auth.acceptInvite\",\n130\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n131\t        \"zod\": \"acceptInviteSchema\",\n132\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n133\t        \"properties\": {\n134\t          \"token\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"raw base64url token from /invite/<token>\" },\n135\t          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"≥1 letter, ≥1 digit, != email, not in common-passwords.txt\" },\n136\t          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"must equal password (client and zod refine)\" }\n137\t        },\n138\t        \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]\n139\t      },\n140\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n141\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\" } }, \"required\": [\"email\"] } },\n142\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"password\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n143\t        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\", \"message\": \"Cross-origin request rejected\" } },\n144\t        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" } }\n145\t      },\n146\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"FR-37\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\"]\n147\t    },\n148\t    {\n149\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n150\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n151\t      \"description\": \"Requests a password-reset link. Over 10 requests per IP per hour -> 429. Over 3 requests per email per hour -> silent generic 200 (no enumeration). Only an existing ACTIVE user gets createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min), which invalidates older unused reset tokens, plus sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). Unknown or inactive emails write nothing. The response body is always identical.\",\n152\t      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n153\t      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/forgot-password/route.ts -> services/auth.requestPasswordReset\",\n154\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n155\t        \"zod\": \"forgotPasswordSchema\",\n156\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n157\t        \"properties\": { \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\" } },\n158\t        \"required\": [\"email\"]\n159\t      },\n160\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n161\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"message\": { \"const\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } } } },\n162\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"email\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n163\t        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" } }\n164\t      },\n165\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-19\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-22\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-8\"]\n166\t    },\n167\t    {\n168\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n169\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n170\t      \"description\": \"Completes a reset. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> hash -> one transaction {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null} + consumeToken -> audit auth.password.reset. The client then redirects to /login?reset=1, which shows a useToast success toast. Existing sessions are revoked within 5 min by the jwt callback (passwordChangedAt > authTime).\",\n171\t      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n172\t      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/reset-password/route.ts -> services/auth.resetPassword\",\n173\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n174\t        \"zod\": \"resetPasswordSchema\",\n175\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n176\t        \"properties\": {\n177\t          \"token\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n178\t          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\" },\n179\t          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n180\t        },\n181\t        \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]\n182\t      },\n183\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n184\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"ok\": { \"const\": true } } } },\n185\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"password\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n186\t        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\" } },\n187\t        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n188\t      },\n189\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\"]\n190\t    },\n191\t    {\n192\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n193\t      \"path\": \"/api/account/password\",\n194\t      \"description\": \"Changes the signed-in user's password. Flow: await requireUser() -> bcrypt-compare currentPassword -> assertPasswordAllowed(newPassword, email) -> hash -> update {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now} -> audit auth.password.changed -> unstable_update({reauth:true}), so this session's authTime moves past passwordChangedAt. Other sessions fail the jwt check within 5 min. The UI shows the 'Password updated' toast.\",\n195\t      \"auth\": \"session required (middleware 401 + requireUser())\",\n196\t      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/account/password/route.ts -> services/auth.changePassword\",\n197\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n198\t        \"zod\": \"changePasswordSchema\",\n199\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n200\t        \"properties\": {\n201\t          \"currentPassword\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n202\t          \"newPassword\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\" },\n203\t          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n204\t        },\n205\t        \"required\": [\"currentPassword\", \"newPassword\", \"confirm\"]\n206\t      },\n207\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n208\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"ok\": { \"const\": true } } }, \"sets-cookie\": \"re-issued session token\" },\n209\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"currentPassword\": [\"Current password is incorrect.\"], \"newPassword\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n210\t        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\" } },\n211\t        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\", \"message\": \"Cross-origin request rejected\" } }\n212\t      },\n213\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-23\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n214\t    }\n215\t  ],\n216\t\n217\t  \"changedBehaviourOnExistingEndpoints\": {\n218\t    \"description\": \"Every existing route handler (33 route.ts files) changes from requireRole(...) to await requireRole(...), backed by the real session. Paths, request shapes and response shapes don't change. New possible responses on all of them:\",\n219\t    \"responses\": {\n220\t      \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\" }, \"source\": \"middleware (no session) or requireUser/requireRole (session revoked)\" },\n221\t      \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\" }, \"source\": \"requireRole role mismatch, or the middleware cross-origin check on mutations\" }\n222\t    },\n223\t    \"unchanged\": [\"/api/health stays public\"],\n224\t    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-29\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-9\"]\n225\t  },\n226\t\n227\t  \"explicitlyAbsent\": [\n228\t    { \"item\": \"No sign-up / register endpoint\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-37\"] },\n229\t    { \"item\": \"No admin user-management, SSO, MFA or magic-link endpoints\", \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-11\"] },\n230\t    { \"item\": \"No /api/v1 prefix; existing /api convention kept\", \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-9\"] }\n231\t  ],\n232\t\n233\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n234\t}\n235\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"820f2207-bedc-4109-a712-39a38d467e5c","uuid":"12ee4155-5f65-4135-b89f-df560165116d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:40:57.471Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:03:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention; no /api/v1 prefix - NFR-9 forbids renaming routes)\",\n    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\" },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object?\" } },\n    \"errorCodes\": {\n      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n      \"FORBIDDEN\": 403,\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410,\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429\n    },\n    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler(parseBody(zodSchema) -> service -> ok()) from src/server/http.ts\",\n    \"csrf\": \"src/middleware.ts rejects non-GET/HEAD /api/* requests whose Origin header is present and differs from the app origin (403 FORBIDDEN). The Auth.js endpoints also use their own CSRF token. Session cookie: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in prod.\",\n    \"unauthenticatedApi\": \"src/middleware.ts returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED for /api/* outside PUBLIC_API_PATHS ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\", \"NFR-9\", \"FR-12\"]\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint, served by the /api/auth/[...nextauth] catch-all (handlers.GET). Returns the CSRF token that signIn()/signOut() use. Public.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native (not the {data} envelope)\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint (catch-all). Returns the current session or null. Public. Middleware does not gate it.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"oneOf\": [\n          { \"type\": \"null\" },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"user\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"role\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\", \"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\"] },\n                  \"firstName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"lastName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\" }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\"id\", \"role\", \"firstName\", \"lastName\", \"email\"]\n              },\n              \"expires\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-34\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js Credentials sign-in (catch-all handlers.POST). Credentials.authorize delegates to authorizeCredentials(): IP rate limit (10 / 5 min) -> trim + lower-case the email -> exactly one bcrypt compare (DUMMY_HASH if the user is missing) -> status/archived/lock checks -> lockout bookkeeping -> audit. On success the jwt callback sets {id, role, firstName, lastName, email, authTime, checkedAt}, maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m. The client calls it through signIn('credentials', {redirect:false}) and reads the error code.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\" },\n          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"callbackUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"note\": \"sanitised by safeCallbackUrl(): only a relative path starting with '/' and not '//' or '/\\\\'; otherwise /dashboard\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"email\", \"password\", \"csrfToken\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"success\": { \"sets-cookie\": \"authjs.session-token (__Secure- prefix in prod)\", \"url\": \"safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)\" },\n        \"failure\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"error\": { \"const\": \"CredentialsSignin\" },\n            \"code\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"enum\": [\"invalid\", \"disabled\", \"locked:<minutes>\", \"rate_limited\"],\n              \"uiMessages\": {\n                \"invalid\": \"Email or password is incorrect.\",\n                \"disabled\": \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\",\n                \"locked:N\": \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\",\n                \"rate_limited\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"sideEffects\": [\n        \"wrong password: failedLoginCount += 1; at 5 -> lockedUntil = now + 15 min, failedLoginCount = 0\",\n        \"success: failedLoginCount = 0, lastLoginAt = now\",\n        \"audit auth.login.success | auth.login.failure {email, reason} | auth.lockout, with the IP from x-forwarded-for\"\n      ],\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-4\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out (catch-all). Clears the session cookie. The shell calls it through signOut({redirectTo:'/login'}).\",\n      \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": { \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"callbackUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"required\": [\"csrfToken\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"url\": \"/login\" },\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-32\", \"FR-34\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/accept-invite\",\n      \"description\": \"Activates an invited account. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'INVITE') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> bcrypt.hash(12) -> one transaction {passwordHash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now} + consumeToken -> audit auth.invite.accepted. It does NOT mint a session: on 200 the client calls signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo:'/dashboard'}). Public via the /api/auth/ prefix and protected by the middleware origin check.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/accept-invite/route.ts -> services/auth.acceptInvite\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"acceptInviteSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"token\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"raw base64url token from /invite/<token>\" },\n          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"≥1 letter, ≥1 digit, != email, not in common-passwords.txt\" },\n          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"must equal password (client and zod refine)\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\" } }, \"required\": [\"email\"] } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"password\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\", \"message\": \"Cross-origin request rejected\" } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"FR-37\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Requests a password-reset link. Over 10 requests per IP per hour -> 429. Over 3 requests per email per hour -> silent generic 200 (no enumeration). Only an existing ACTIVE user gets createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min), which invalidates older unused reset tokens, plus sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). Unknown or inactive emails write nothing. The response body is always identical.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/forgot-password/route.ts -> services/auth.requestPasswordReset\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"forgotPasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": { \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\" } },\n        \"required\": [\"email\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"message\": { \"const\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } } } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"email\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-19\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-22\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Completes a reset. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> hash -> one transaction {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null} + consumeToken -> audit auth.password.reset. The client then redirects to /login?reset=1, which shows a useToast success toast. Existing sessions are revoked within 5 min by the jwt callback (passwordChangedAt > authTime).\",\n      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/reset-password/route.ts -> services/auth.resetPassword\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"resetPasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"token\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\" },\n          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"ok\": { \"const\": true } } } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"password\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\" } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/account/password\",\n      \"description\": \"Changes the signed-in user's password. Flow: await requireUser() -> bcrypt-compare currentPassword -> assertPasswordAllowed(newPassword, email) -> hash -> update {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now} -> audit auth.password.changed -> unstable_update({reauth:true}), so this session's authTime moves past passwordChangedAt. Other sessions fail the jwt check within 5 min. The UI shows the 'Password updated' toast.\",\n      \"auth\": \"session required (middleware 401 + requireUser())\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/account/password/route.ts -> services/auth.changePassword\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"changePasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"currentPassword\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"newPassword\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\" },\n          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"currentPassword\", \"newPassword\", \"confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"ok\": { \"const\": true } } }, \"sets-cookie\": \"re-issued session token\" },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"currentPassword\": [\"Current password is incorrect.\"], \"newPassword\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\" } },\n        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\", \"message\": \"Cross-origin request rejected\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-23\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"changedBehaviourOnExistingEndpoints\": {\n    \"description\": \"Every existing route handler (33 route.ts files) changes from requireRole(...) to await requireRole(...), backed by the real session. Paths, request shapes and response shapes don't change. New possible responses on all of them:\",\n    \"responses\": {\n      \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\" }, \"source\": \"middleware (no session) or requireUser/requireRole (session revoked)\" },\n      \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\" }, \"source\": \"requireRole role mismatch, or the middleware cross-origin check on mutations\" }\n    },\n    \"unchanged\": [\"/api/health stays public\"],\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-29\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-9\"]\n  },\n\n  \"explicitlyAbsent\": [\n    { \"item\": \"No sign-up / register endpoint\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-37\"] },\n    { \"item\": \"No admin user-management, SSO, MFA or magic-link endpoints\", \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-11\"] },\n    { \"item\": \"No /api/v1 prefix; existing /api convention kept\", \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-9\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":235,"startLine":1,"totalLines":235}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S5Y4nqUd2C9njQjRxwU5JU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRxUuMFdRhv1r71DmU3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UyGcAMsFt8iN2n98zPkAXK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22464,"cache_read_input_tokens":30412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22464},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"820f2207-bedc-4109-a712-39a38d467e5c","uuid":"19217404-60c3-4571-9b70-5b00dbd639aa","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:40:57.655Z","request_id":"req_011CghRxUeyvpdSnQdYGRWt8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UyGcAMsFt8iN2n98zPkAXK":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyGcAMsFt8iN2n98zPkAXK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBase stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%, confirmed by\n6\t`package.json`): Next.js 14.2 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict,\n7\tPrisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI v9 + emotion, zod 3, react-hook-form,\n8\tdate-fns-tz. The auth dependencies are already installed: `next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25`\n9\tand `bcrypt ^6`. **This PRD adds no new runtime dependency.** The ADRs below\n10\tonly cover the implementation choices this PRD's requirements force.\n11\t\n12\tBrownfield facts checked in the workspace (they correct intake in places):\n13\t- `requireRole()` is sync and returns `{id, role}`. It has **50 call sites in\n14\t  43 files**, not ~94. Every caller is already inside an `async` server page,\n15\t  layout or route handler.\n16\t- `src/server/http.ts` `ApiErrorCode` already includes `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401,\n17\t  `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429 and `INVALID_TOKEN` 410, so no envelope\n18\t  changes are needed.\n19\t- `AuditLog.ip String?` exists. `audit()` has no `request` param.\n20\t\n21\t---\n22\t\n23\t## ADR-1: Auth.js v5 with a split config (edge-safe `auth.config.ts` + Node `auth.ts`)\n24\t\n25\t**Context.** FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12 and FR-34 need credential sign-in, JWT\n26\tsessions and a `middleware.ts` gate. In Next 14, middleware runs on the Edge\n27\truntime, where `bcrypt` (a native addon) and Prisma's Node client can't load.\n28\t\n29\t**Decision.** Use the documented Auth.js v5 split:\n30\t- `src/server/auth/auth.config.ts` (edge-safe): `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`,\n31\t  `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, the `authorized`/`jwt`/`session` shape\n32\t  callbacks, and no providers that touch the DB.\n33\t- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })] })`,\n34\t  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut }`. It also holds the\n35\t  DB-touching `jwt` callback logic (FR-11).\n36\t- `middleware.ts` builds `NextAuth(authConfig).auth`. It only decodes the JWT.\n37\t- `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` re-exports `handlers` (FR-34).\n38\t\n39\tDon't use a Prisma adapter. JWT sessions with Credentials don't need one, and\n40\tthe adapter would require Account/Session/VerificationToken models the PRD\n41\tdoesn't define.\n42\t\n43\t**Consequences.** Middleware can't check `passwordChangedAt` because it has no\n44\tDB access. That check lives in the Node-side `jwt` callback (ADR-4), which\n45\truns whenever `auth()` is called from server code. Because next-auth is a\n46\tbeta, pin the installed version exactly (drop the `^`) so a beta bump can't\n47\tchange callback signatures mid-PRD.\n48\t\n49\t_Cites: FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12, FR-34, NFR-2_\n50\t\n51\t## ADR-2: `requireRole()` / `requireUser()` become async; update all 50 call sites with `await`\n52\t\n53\t**Context.** FR-28 and FR-29 replace `PLACEHOLDER_USER` with the real session.\n54\tAuth.js `auth()` is async. Intake flagged this as a blocker. Options:\n55\t(a) make the helpers async and add `await` at each call site;\n56\t(b) keep them sync by reading identity from headers set by middleware;\n57\t(c) use React `cache()` plus a sync wrapper.\n58\t\n59\t**Decision.** (a). `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole(...roles)`\n60\tbecome `async` with the same arguments and the same `{id, role, ...}` return\n61\tshape, so the signature stays compatible (FR-29). Each of the 50 call sites\n62\tchanges from `requireRole(...)` to `await requireRole(...)`. That's a\n63\tmechanical one-token edit, and every caller is already async. Wrap\n64\t`getCurrentUser` in React `cache()` so a page plus its layout share one\n65\tsession decode per request.\n66\t\n67\tOption (b) was rejected: identity read from headers is a spoofing risk\n68\t(NFR-7), and it skips the FR-11 revocation check. Option (c) can't make an\n69\tasync read sync.\n70\t\n71\t**Consequences.** `tsc` catches every missed `await`, because a `Promise` has\n72\tno `.role` or `.id`. Bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statements don't fail\n73\ttypecheck, though, and a forgotten `await` there silently does nothing.\n74\tEnable `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` for `src/**`, or have\n75\tdev-planning grep for un-awaited calls. Redirect-vs-throw: in server pages,\n76\tuse `redirect('/login')` / `redirect('/forbidden')` from `next/navigation`;\n77\tin route handlers, throw `AppError` (UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN), which\n78\t`withHandler` already maps. Implement this as one helper that the page and\n79\tAPI paths both call, not two copies. `course-access.ts` and\n80\t`student-access.ts` keep taking the resolved user object and aren't modified\n81\t(NFR-9).\n82\t\n83\t_Cites: FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9_\n84\t\n85\t## ADR-3: Password hashing with the existing `bcrypt` at cost 12, plus a dummy compare for unknown users\n86\t\n87\t**Context.** FR-4 sets cost 12. NFR-3 requires constant-ish timing when the\n88\tuser doesn't exist. NFR-4 requires sign-in in under 1 s at p95.\n89\t\n90\t**Decision.** Use `bcrypt.hash(pw, 12)` / `bcrypt.compare`. Precompute one\n91\tmodule-level dummy hash at cost 12 and compare against it when the user is\n92\tmissing, disabled or locked, so every path pays one bcrypt compare. Don't use\n93\targon2 (it's a new native dependency and the PRD specifies bcrypt).\n94\t\n95\t**Consequences.** One cost-12 compare takes about 250 ms on modern hardware,\n96\twhich leaves room under the 1 s budget for the user lookup, the\n97\tfailedLoginCount update and the audit insert. Never call bcrypt twice on one\n98\tsign-in path. bcrypt runs only in Node code, never in middleware (ADR-1).\n99\t\n100\t_Cites: FR-4, FR-6, NFR-3, NFR-4_\n101\t\n102\t## ADR-4: Session revocation via a `passwordChangedAt` check in the jwt callback, throttled to every 5 minutes\n103\t\n104\t**Context.** FR-11 and FR-23 require that a password change or reset\n105\tinvalidates other sessions. Sessions are stateless JWTs (FR-10), so there's\n106\tno session table.\n107\t\n108\t**Decision.** Store `iat` and a `checkedAt` timestamp in the token. In the\n109\tNode `jwt` callback, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, select only\n110\t`passwordChangedAt, status` for `token.id`. If `passwordChangedAt > iat` or\n111\tthe status isn't ACTIVE, return `null` to invalidate the session. Otherwise\n112\tupdate `checkedAt`. For FR-23's \"re-issue current session\", call `unstable_update()`\n113\t(the v5 `update`) after the change, which mints a token with a fresh `iat`.\n114\t\n115\t**Consequences.** Revocation can lag by up to 5 minutes. The PRD explicitly\n116\taccepts that window. Edge middleware can still let a revoked token through\n117\tfor page navigation in that window. The server-side `requireUser()` call\n118\tthen catches it, and that call is the real guard (NFR-7).\n119\t\n120\t_Cites: FR-10, FR-11, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-7_\n121\t\n122\t## ADR-5: Tokens with `node:crypto` only (randomBytes, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual)\n123\t\n124\t**Context.** FR-13 needs a single AuthToken module. NFR-1 requires stored\n125\thashes and constant-time comparison.\n126\t\n127\t**Decision.** `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` uses `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`\n128\tand `createHash('sha256')`. Look up by the hash (the DB index), then confirm\n129\twith `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers. No JWT, nanoid or other library.\n130\t\n131\t**Consequences.** Raw tokens exist only in the returned value and the\n132\temailed or logged link, never in the DB or audit metadata (FR-31). The\n133\t\"invalidate older unused tokens\" step (FR-20, FR-26) is one `updateMany`\n134\tthat sets `usedAt` in the same `$transaction` as the create.\n135\t\n136\t_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1_\n137\t\n138\t## ADR-6: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter (a `Map` of timestamp arrays); no Redis\n139\t\n140\t**Context.** FR-7 (10 per IP per 5 min) and FR-19 (3 per email per hour, 10\n141\tper IP per hour) explicitly ask for an exported in-memory limiter in\n142\t`src/server/rate-limit.ts`. The PRD adds no infrastructure (NFR-11).\n143\t\n144\t**Decision.** One `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs): { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n145\tover a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`, pruning expired timestamps on\n146\teach call. Namespace keys like `login:ip:<ip>` and `forgot:email:<email>`.\n147\tTake the IP from the first entry of `x-forwarded-for`, using the same\n148\thelper `audit()` uses (FR-30). Call it from the Node side (authorize and\n149\troute handlers), not middleware, because Edge isolates don't share memory.\n150\t\n151\t**Consequences.** The ceiling is per process: limits reset on restart and\n152\taren't shared across instances. Mark the code with a\n153\t`ponytail: per-process limiter, swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if\n154\thorizontally scaled` comment. With Credentials, a RATE_LIMITED outcome has\n155\tto go through Auth.js's `CredentialsSignin` subclass `code` to reach the\n156\tlogin form (FR-5, FR-7).\n157\t\n158\t_Cites: FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-8, NFR-11_\n159\t\n160\t## ADR-7: Validation with the existing zod + react-hook-form; one policy schema shared by client and server\n161\t\n162\t**Context.** FR-17 defines the policy. FR-18 needs a live checklist.\n163\tFR-16, FR-21 and FR-23 must enforce the policy server-side.\n164\t\n165\t**Decision.** `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports the zod schema plus a\n166\tpure `passwordChecks(pw, email)` that returns per-rule booleans. The\n167\tchecklist UI and the zod `superRefine` both use that function. The\n168\tcommon-password check needs the file at\n169\t`src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt`, so it runs only on the server: read\n170\tthe file once into a `Set` with `fs` in a server-only module. The client\n171\tchecklist shows the length, letter, digit and not-email rules live, and the\n172\tcommon-password rule is reported from the server response.\n173\t\n174\t**Consequences.** The 1,000-word list never ships in the client bundle. The\n175\tvalidator file has to stay importable from the client, so keep the `fs`\n176\tread in a separate server-only file that adds the common-password refinement.\n177\t\n178\t_Cites: FR-17, FR-18, FR-16, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-5, NFR-8_\n179\t\n180\t## ADR-8: UI with MUI v9 only (Sign-in template patterns), documented through mui-mcp\n181\t\n182\t**Context.** NFR-6 bans non-MUI UI libraries and requires every component to\n183\tbe looked up through mui-mcp. FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24 and FR-32 add auth\n184\tpages and top-bar changes.\n185\t\n186\t**Decision.** Use the installed `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` 9.5:\n187\tCard, TextField, Button, InputAdornment + IconButton (Visibility icons),\n188\tAlert, List/ListItemIcon for the checklist, and Menu/Avatar/Chip in the top\n189\tbar. Use the existing `useToast` for toasts (FR-21, FR-23), not notistack or\n190\tsonner. Auth pages live in a `src/app/(auth)` route group outside the\n191\t`(app)` shell. The mui-mcp server was reachable from this session\n192\t(`useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools were listed), so the NFR-6 blocker doesn't\n193\tstand at architect time. Dev must still check it itself.\n194\t\n195\t**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. `aria-live=\"polite\"` on the form-level\n196\tAlert and focus-first-invalid (via react-hook-form `setFocus`) meet NFR-5.\n197\t\n198\t_Cites: FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-5, NFR-6_\n199\t\n200\t## ADR-9: Schema reconciled additively with one Prisma migration\n201\t\n202\t**Context.** FR-1 and the intake blockers list the divergences: `ip` vs\n203\t`ipAddress`, the extra `ARCHIVED` value, different AuditLog indexes. NFR-9\n204\tsays never rename.\n205\t\n206\t**Decision.** Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED` and keep the\n207\texisting extra indexes. Add only\n208\t`@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to\n209\tAuditLog, plus any User auth fields the diff finds missing\n210\t(failedLoginCount, lockedUntil, lastLoginAt, passwordChangedAt). Apply them\n211\tin one `prisma migrate dev --name auth_reconcile` migration. FR-4's \"status\n212\t!= ACTIVE\" check already rejects ARCHIVED.\n213\t\n214\t**Consequences.** The migration has no destructive steps. It adds indexes and\n215\tnullable or defaulted columns only.\n216\t\n217\t_Cites: FR-1, FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, NFR-9_\n218\t\n219\t## ADR-10: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; no new test tooling\n220\t\n221\t**Decision.** Run unit and integration tests (FR-36) in `vitest`, calling the\n222\tlimiter, tokens, policy and callbackUrl modules as pure functions. Test the\n223\tauthorize function and the service functions against the test DB. Use\n224\t`@playwright/test` (with the installed `@axe-core/playwright` for NFR-5) for\n225\tsign-in/out, the failure message and forgot→reset. The reset link comes from\n226\tthe logged `sendAuthEmail` output (FR-22).\n227\t\n228\t_Cites: FR-22, FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10_\n229\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"820f2207-bedc-4109-a712-39a38d467e5c","uuid":"cdc2a185-4bfc-43ad-9c01-b0231a92f23f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:40:57.677Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: abcd-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nBase stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%, confirmed by\n`package.json`): Next.js 14.2 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict,\nPrisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI v9 + emotion, zod 3, react-hook-form,\ndate-fns-tz. The auth dependencies are already installed: `next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25`\nand `bcrypt ^6`. **This PRD adds no new runtime dependency.** The ADRs below\nonly cover the implementation choices this PRD's requirements force.\n\nBrownfield facts checked in the workspace (they correct intake in places):\n- `requireRole()` is sync and returns `{id, role}`. It has **50 call sites in\n  43 files**, not ~94. Every caller is already inside an `async` server page,\n  layout or route handler.\n- `src/server/http.ts` `ApiErrorCode` already includes `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401,\n  `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429 and `INVALID_TOKEN` 410, so no envelope\n  changes are needed.\n- `AuditLog.ip String?` exists. `audit()` has no `request` param.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js v5 with a split config (edge-safe `auth.config.ts` + Node `auth.ts`)\n\n**Context.** FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12 and FR-34 need credential sign-in, JWT\nsessions and a `middleware.ts` gate. In Next 14, middleware runs on the Edge\nruntime, where `bcrypt` (a native addon) and Prisma's Node client can't load.\n\n**Decision.** Use the documented Auth.js v5 split:\n- `src/server/auth/auth.config.ts` (edge-safe): `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`,\n  `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, the `authorized`/`jwt`/`session` shape\n  callbacks, and no providers that touch the DB.\n- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })] })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut }`. It also holds the\n  DB-touching `jwt` callback logic (FR-11).\n- `middleware.ts` builds `NextAuth(authConfig).auth`. It only decodes the JWT.\n- `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` re-exports `handlers` (FR-34).\n\nDon't use a Prisma adapter. JWT sessions with Credentials don't need one, and\nthe adapter would require Account/Session/VerificationToken models the PRD\ndoesn't define.\n\n**Consequences.** Middleware can't check `passwordChangedAt` because it has no\nDB access. That check lives in the Node-side `jwt` callback (ADR-4), which\nruns whenever `auth()` is called from server code. Because next-auth is a\nbeta, pin the installed version exactly (drop the `^`) so a beta bump can't\nchange callback signatures mid-PRD.\n\n_Cites: FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12, FR-34, NFR-2_\n\n## ADR-2: `requireRole()` / `requireUser()` become async; update all 50 call sites with `await`\n\n**Context.** FR-28 and FR-29 replace `PLACEHOLDER_USER` with the real session.\nAuth.js `auth()` is async. Intake flagged this as a blocker. Options:\n(a) make the helpers async and add `await` at each call site;\n(b) keep them sync by reading identity from headers set by middleware;\n(c) use React `cache()` plus a sync wrapper.\n\n**Decision.** (a). `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole(...roles)`\nbecome `async` with the same arguments and the same `{id, role, ...}` return\nshape, so the signature stays compatible (FR-29). Each of the 50 call sites\nchanges from `requireRole(...)` to `await requireRole(...)`. That's a\nmechanical one-token edit, and every caller is already async. Wrap\n`getCurrentUser` in React `cache()` so a page plus its layout share one\nsession decode per request.\n\nOption (b) was rejected: identity read from headers is a spoofing risk\n(NFR-7), and it skips the FR-11 revocation check. Option (c) can't make an\nasync read sync.\n\n**Consequences.** `tsc` catches every missed `await`, because a `Promise` has\nno `.role` or `.id`. Bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statements don't fail\ntypecheck, though, and a forgotten `await` there silently does nothing.\nEnable `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` for `src/**`, or have\ndev-planning grep for un-awaited calls. Redirect-vs-throw: in server pages,\nuse `redirect('/login')` / `redirect('/forbidden')` from `next/navigation`;\nin route handlers, throw `AppError` (UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN), which\n`withHandler` already maps. Implement this as one helper that the page and\nAPI paths both call, not two copies. `course-access.ts` and\n`student-access.ts` keep taking the resolved user object and aren't modified\n(NFR-9).\n\n_Cites: FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9_\n\n## ADR-3: Password hashing with the existing `bcrypt` at cost 12, plus a dummy compare for unknown users\n\n**Context.** FR-4 sets cost 12. NFR-3 requires constant-ish timing when the\nuser doesn't exist. NFR-4 requires sign-in in under 1 s at p95.\n\n**Decision.** Use `bcrypt.hash(pw, 12)` / `bcrypt.compare`. Precompute one\nmodule-level dummy hash at cost 12 and compare against it when the user is\nmissing, disabled or locked, so every path pays one bcrypt compare. Don't use\nargon2 (it's a new native dependency and the PRD specifies bcrypt).\n\n**Consequences.** One cost-12 compare takes about 250 ms on modern hardware,\nwhich leaves room under the 1 s budget for the user lookup, the\nfailedLoginCount update and the audit insert. Never call bcrypt twice on one\nsign-in path. bcrypt runs only in Node code, never in middleware (ADR-1).\n\n_Cites: FR-4, FR-6, NFR-3, NFR-4_\n\n## ADR-4: Session revocation via a `passwordChangedAt` check in the jwt callback, throttled to every 5 minutes\n\n**Context.** FR-11 and FR-23 require that a password change or reset\ninvalidates other sessions. Sessions are stateless JWTs (FR-10), so there's\nno session table.\n\n**Decision.** Store `iat` and a `checkedAt` timestamp in the token. In the\nNode `jwt` callback, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, select only\n`passwordChangedAt, status` for `token.id`. If `passwordChangedAt > iat` or\nthe status isn't ACTIVE, return `null` to invalidate the session. Otherwise\nupdate `checkedAt`. For FR-23's \"re-issue current session\", call `unstable_update()`\n(the v5 `update`) after the change, which mints a token with a fresh `iat`.\n\n**Consequences.** Revocation can lag by up to 5 minutes. The PRD explicitly\naccepts that window. Edge middleware can still let a revoked token through\nfor page navigation in that window. The server-side `requireUser()` call\nthen catches it, and that call is the real guard (NFR-7).\n\n_Cites: FR-10, FR-11, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-7_\n\n## ADR-5: Tokens with `node:crypto` only (randomBytes, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual)\n\n**Context.** FR-13 needs a single AuthToken module. NFR-1 requires stored\nhashes and constant-time comparison.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` uses `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`\nand `createHash('sha256')`. Look up by the hash (the DB index), then confirm\nwith `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers. No JWT, nanoid or other library.\n\n**Consequences.** Raw tokens exist only in the returned value and the\nemailed or logged link, never in the DB or audit metadata (FR-31). The\n\"invalidate older unused tokens\" step (FR-20, FR-26) is one `updateMany`\nthat sets `usedAt` in the same `$transaction` as the create.\n\n_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1_\n\n## ADR-6: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter (a `Map` of timestamp arrays); no Redis\n\n**Context.** FR-7 (10 per IP per 5 min) and FR-19 (3 per email per hour, 10\nper IP per hour) explicitly ask for an exported in-memory limiter in\n`src/server/rate-limit.ts`. The PRD adds no infrastructure (NFR-11).\n\n**Decision.** One `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs): { ok, retryAfterMs }`\nover a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`, pruning expired timestamps on\neach call. Namespace keys like `login:ip:<ip>` and `forgot:email:<email>`.\nTake the IP from the first entry of `x-forwarded-for`, using the same\nhelper `audit()` uses (FR-30). Call it from the Node side (authorize and\nroute handlers), not middleware, because Edge isolates don't share memory.\n\n**Consequences.** The ceiling is per process: limits reset on restart and\naren't shared across instances. Mark the code with a\n`ponytail: per-process limiter, swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if\nhorizontally scaled` comment. With Credentials, a RATE_LIMITED outcome has\nto go through Auth.js's `CredentialsSignin` subclass `code` to reach the\nlogin form (FR-5, FR-7).\n\n_Cites: FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-8, NFR-11_\n\n## ADR-7: Validation with the existing zod + react-hook-form; one policy schema shared by client and server\n\n**Context.** FR-17 defines the policy. FR-18 needs a live checklist.\nFR-16, FR-21 and FR-23 must enforce the policy server-side.\n\n**Decision.** `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports the zod schema plus a\npure `passwordChecks(pw, email)` that returns per-rule booleans. The\nchecklist UI and the zod `superRefine` both use that function. The\ncommon-password check needs the file at\n`src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt`, so it runs only on the server: read\nthe file once into a `Set` with `fs` in a server-only module. The client\nchecklist shows the length, letter, digit and not-email rules live, and the\ncommon-password rule is reported from the server response.\n\n**Consequences.** The 1,000-word list never ships in the client bundle. The\nvalidator file has to stay importable from the client, so keep the `fs`\nread in a separate server-only file that adds the common-password refinement.\n\n_Cites: FR-17, FR-18, FR-16, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-5, NFR-8_\n\n## ADR-8: UI with MUI v9 only (Sign-in template patterns), documented through mui-mcp\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 bans non-MUI UI libraries and requires every component to\nbe looked up through mui-mcp. FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24 and FR-32 add auth\npages and top-bar changes.\n\n**Decision.** Use the installed `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` 9.5:\nCard, TextField, Button, InputAdornment + IconButton (Visibility icons),\nAlert, List/ListItemIcon for the checklist, and Menu/Avatar/Chip in the top\nbar. Use the existing `useToast` for toasts (FR-21, FR-23), not notistack or\nsonner. Auth pages live in a `src/app/(auth)` route group outside the\n`(app)` shell. The mui-mcp server was reachable from this session\n(`useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools were listed), so the NFR-6 blocker doesn't\nstand at architect time. Dev must still check it itself.\n\n**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. `aria-live=\"polite\"` on the form-level\nAlert and focus-first-invalid (via react-hook-form `setFocus`) meet NFR-5.\n\n_Cites: FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-5, NFR-6_\n\n## ADR-9: Schema reconciled additively with one Prisma migration\n\n**Context.** FR-1 and the intake blockers list the divergences: `ip` vs\n`ipAddress`, the extra `ARCHIVED` value, different AuditLog indexes. NFR-9\nsays never rename.\n\n**Decision.** Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED` and keep the\nexisting extra indexes. Add only\n`@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to\nAuditLog, plus any User auth fields the diff finds missing\n(failedLoginCount, lockedUntil, lastLoginAt, passwordChangedAt). Apply them\nin one `prisma migrate dev --name auth_reconcile` migration. FR-4's \"status\n!= ACTIVE\" check already rejects ARCHIVED.\n\n**Consequences.** The migration has no destructive steps. It adds indexes and\nnullable or defaulted columns only.\n\n_Cites: FR-1, FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, NFR-9_\n\n## ADR-10: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; no new test tooling\n\n**Decision.** Run unit and integration tests (FR-36) in `vitest`, calling the\nlimiter, tokens, policy and callbackUrl modules as pure functions. Test the\nauthorize function and the service functions against the test DB. Use\n`@playwright/test` (with the installed `@axe-core/playwright` for NFR-5) for\nsign-in/out, the failure message and forgot→reset. The reset link comes from\nthe logged `sendAuthEmail` output (FR-22).\n\n_Cites: FR-22, FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10_\n","numLines":229,"startLine":1,"totalLines":229}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UyGcAMsFt8iN2n98zPkAXK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
