nd returns {token, user} or null if the token is missing, has the wrong type, is used or is expired. consumeToken(tokenId, tx?) runs updateMany {id, usedAt: null} and throws AppError('INVALID_TOKEN') when the count is 0. Export the pure hashToken(raw). Unit tests cover hashToken (deterministic, 64 hex chars, never equal to raw). The DB branches are tested in TASK-25.\",\n  [(C,\"src/server/auth/tokens.ts\"),(C,\"tests/unit/tokens.test.ts\")], [\"TASK-1\"], 1.5, [\"FR-13\",\"FR-20\",\"FR-26\",\"FR-31\",\"FR-36\",\"NFR-1\"])\nt(\"Credential verification (C3): authorizeCredentials(input, request). Order: rateLimit('login:ip:'+ip, 10, 5 min) → AuthError('rate_limited'); signInSchema parse; user lookup; then exactly ONE bcrypt.compare against the user's hash or a module-level DUMMY_HASH (cost 12). Rejections happen only after that compare. Branches: missing → invalid; DISABLED → disabled; status!==ACTIVE or archivedAt set → invalid; lockedUntil>now → 'locked:'+ceil(ms/60000); wrong password → increment failedLoginCount, and when the count reaches 5 apply the lock (computeLockout) → invalid or locked:15; success → failedLoginCount=0, lastLoginAt=now. Pure computeLockout(count, now) returns {failedLoginCount, lockedUntil|null}. Audit auth.login.success, auth.login.failure {email, reason} and auth.lockout, passing the request. Define `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. Unit-test computeLockout.\",\n  [(C,\"src/server/auth/credentials.ts\"),(C,\"tests/unit/lockout.test.ts\")], [\"TASK-2\",\"TASK-4\",\"TASK-5\"], 2.5, [\"FR-4\",\"FR-5\",\"FR-6\",\"FR-7\",\"FR-9\",\"NFR-3\",\"NFR-4\",\"NFR-12\"])\nt(\"Auth.js core (C2, ADR-1). auth.config.ts must be edge-safe (no Prisma or bcrypt): session jwt with maxAge 8h and updateAge 15m, pages.signIn '/login', providers [], a session callback that copies id/role/firstName/lastName/email, a redirect callback that uses safeCallbackUrl, and trustHost: true. auth.ts (Node) spreads authConfig with Credentials({authorize: (c,