-up path. src/middleware.ts is `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => ...)` and runs, in order: (1) a non-GET/HEAD /api/* request with an Origin that differs from the app origin → 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope (skip Auth.js's own catch-all endpoints, which have their own CSRF); (2) public path → next(); (3) no session: /api → 401 {error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',message}}, pages → redirect /login?callbackUrl=<path+search>; (4) next() with an x-pathname request header. The matcher excludes _next/static, _next/image, favicon.ico and file extensions. Don't import Prisma or bcrypt.\",\n  [(C,\"src/config/public-routes.ts\"),(C,\"src/middleware.ts\")], [\"TASK-8\"], 1.5, [\"FR-12\",\"FR-37\",\"NFR-2\",\"NFR-7\",\"NFR-8\"])\nt(\"Rewrite requireRole.ts (C7, ADR-2): delete PLACEHOLDER_USER. SessionUser is {id, role, firstName, lastName, email}. getCurrentUser = cache(async () => (await auth())?.user ?? null). requireUser() and requireRole(...roles) are async and throw AppError UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN. requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(...roles) redirect to /login?callbackUrl=<x-pathname header or /dashboard> or to /forbidden. Both pairs share one internal resolver; there is no flag parameter. No permissions.ts and no can(). NOTE: typecheck is red until TASK-12..14 land, so run them right after this task.\",\n  [(M,\"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts\")], [\"TASK-8\"], 1, [\"FR-28\",\"FR-29\",\"NFR-7\",\"NFR-9\"])\nt(\"Await requireRole in the 13 academic-years / audit-logs / courses / enrollments / me route handlers. Mechanical: `requireRole(` → `await requireRole(`. No path, request or response shape changes. withHandler already maps the thrown AppError to 401/403.\",\n  [(M,p) for p in routesA], [\"TASK-11\"], 0.5, [\"FR-29\",\"NFR-7\",\"NFR-9\"])\nt(\"Await requireRole in the 20 sections / students / users route handlers. Mechanical: `requireRole(` → `await requireRole(`. No path, request or response shape changes.\",\n  [(M,p) for p in routesB], [\"TASK-11\"], 0.5, [\"FR-29\",\"NFR-7\",\"NFR-9\"])\nt(\"Switch the 8 server pages/layouts from requireRole( to `await requirePageRole(`, with the same role arguments, so an unauthorized visit redirects instead of rendering error.tsx. Don't change course-access.ts or student-access.ts, which still receive the resolved {id, role}.\",\n  [(M,p) for p in pages], [\"TASK-11\"], 0.5, [\"FR-29\",\"NFR-7\",\"NFR-9\"])\nt(\"Guardrail for missed awaits: in .eslintrc.json, add an override for src/**/*.{ts,tsx} with parserOptions.project './tsconfig.json' and '@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises': 'error'. Fix any newly reported floating promises with an await or a `void` prefix. `npm run lint` must pass.\",\n  [(M,\".eslintrc.json\")], [\"TASK-12\",\"TASK-13\",\"TASK-14\"], 0.5, [\"NFR-10\",\"FR-29\"])\nt(\"Auth services (C9), Node only. acceptInvite({token,password}, req): verifyToken INVITE (null → AppError INVALID_TOKEN), assertPasswordAllowed, bcrypt.hash 12, then one $transaction {passwordHash, status ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt now} + consumeToken(tx). Audit auth.invite.accepted and return {email}. requestPasswordReset({email}, req): rateLimit forgot:ip 10/h → RATE_LIMITED; rateLimit forgot:email 3/h → silently return the generic message; only an ACTIVE user gets createToken PASSWORD_RESET {minutes:60} + sendAuthEmail. Always return {message:\\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\"}. resetPassword: verify PASSWORD_RESET, policy check, hash, then one transaction {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt, failedLoginCount 0, lockedUntil null} + consume. Audit auth.password.reset. changePassword(user, {currentPassword,newPassword}, req): a wrong current password → VALIDATION_ERROR details.fieldErrors.currentPassword ['Current password is incorrect.']; then policy check, hash, update passwordHash + passwordChangedAt, audit auth.password.changed. Audit metadata is explicit and never includes passwords or tokens.\",\n  [(C,\"src/server/services/auth.ts\")], [