ep the existing schoolShortName prop. In shell.tsx, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER. Render the existing UserAvatar (initials), the full name and a role Chip from props. Add an 'Account security' menu item → /account/security. Sign out calls signOut({redirectTo:'/login'}) from next-auth/react. There is no SessionProvider. Look up Menu, MenuItem and Chip through mui-mcp first.\",\n  [(M,\"src/app/(app)/layout.tsx\"),(M,\"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx\")], [\"TASK-11\"], 2, [\"FR-24\",\"FR-32\",\"FR-33\",\"NFR-6\",\"NFR-7\"])\nt(\"Account security page (C13): await requirePageUser(). A client form with current, new and confirm password fields plus PasswordChecklist (react-hook-form + zodResolver changePasswordSchema, shouldFocusError, aria-live Alert). It POSTs /api/account/password. On 200, show the useToast 'Password updated' toast and reset the form. Map details.fieldErrors.currentPassword to that field via setError. Optionally show lastLoginAt with the existing DateDisplay in SchoolSettings.timezone.\",\n  [(C,\"src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx\")], [\"TASK-17\",\"TASK-19\",\"TASK-22\"], 1.5, [\"FR-23\",\"NFR-5\",\"NFR-6\",\"NFR-7\",\"NFR-12\"])\nt(\"Seed (C14). Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe: admin@, teacher@, teacher2@, student@, student2@ and parent@schoolhub.test, all ACTIVE, with passwordHash bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!',12) and passwordChangedAt now. Upsert invited@schoolhub.test as INVITED, then call createInviteToken and log the link with logger.info. Keep the office@ and SchoolSettings seeding unchanged. Importing from src/ runs src/lib/env.ts validation, so make sure `npm run db:seed` loads .env (e.g. `tsx --env-file=.env` or import 'dotenv/config' if it's already installed). Don't add a new dependency.\",\n  [(M,\"prisma/seed.ts\")], [\"TASK-1\",\"TASK-18\"], 1, [\"FR-35\",\"FR-13\"])\nt(\"Integration tests (C15), run against DATABASE_URL (docker-compose Postgres). Extend vitest.config.ts to include tests/integration/**/*.test.ts with environment 'node' for that folder (environmentMatchGlobs). Keep the unit tests on jsdom. auth-credentials.test.ts covers every authorizeCredentials branch: invalid, unknown user (the compare still runs), disabled, invited, archived, locked with minutes, 5th failure locks, rate_limited after 10, and success resets the count + sets lastLoginAt. Call __resetRateLimits between tests. auth-services.test.ts covers acceptInvite (activates, consumes, a second use → INVALID_TOKEN), verifyToken expired/used/wrong-type branches, createToken invalidating older tokens, requestPasswordReset (unknown email → no row; the 4th request per email is silent), resetPassword (clears the lockout), changePassword (wrong current → fieldErrors.currentPassword), and that no AuditLog.metadata contains a password, hash or raw token.\",\n  [(M,\"vitest.config.ts\"),(C,\"tests/integration/auth-credentials.test.ts\"),(C,\"tests/integration/auth-services.test.ts\")], [\"TASK-7\",\"TASK-16\",\"TASK-18\"], 3, [\"FR-36\",\"FR-4\",\"FR-6\",\"FR-13\",\"FR-31\",\"NFR-3\"])\nt(\"Playwright (C15). helpers/auth.ts has signIn(page, email, password='SchoolHub123!') and createResetLink(email), which calls createToken through the app modules because the raw token can't be recovered from the DB. auth.spec.ts covers: unauthenticated /dashboard → /login?callbackUrl; sign in as admin@ → shell shows the name/role; sign out → /login; a wrong password shows 'Email or password is incorrect.'; forgot → reset → /login?reset=1 toast → sign in with the new password; and @axe-core/playwright with zero serious/critical violations on /login, /forgot-password and the invite/reset pages. Update dashboard.spec.ts to sign in first, because /dashboard now redirects unauthenticated visitors.\",\n  [(C,\"tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts\"),(C,\"tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts\"),(M,\"tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts\")], [\"TASK-20\",\"TASK-21\",\"TASK-22\",\"TASK-24\"], 3, [\"FR-36\",\"FR-3\",\"FR-5\",\"FR-21\",\"FR-32\",\"NFR-5\"])\n\n# validation\nreq = json.load(open(os.path.join(root,\"artifacts/intake/requirements.json\")))\nvalid = {r[\"id\"] for r in req[\"functionalRequirements\"]+req[\"nonFunctionalRequirements\"]}\nids = [x[\"id\"] for x in T]; idx = {i:n for n,i in enumerate(ids)}\nseen = {}\nfor x in T:\n    assert set(x[\"requirementIds\"]) <= valid, x[\"id\"]\n    for d in x[\"dependencies\"]: assert idx[d] < idx[x[\"id\"]], (x[\"id\"], d)  # topological order => DAG\n    for op,p in x[\"files\"]:\n        assert p not in seen, (\"dup\", p); seen[p] = x[\"id\"]\n        assert (op==M) == os.path.exists(os.path.join(root,p)), (op,p)\ncovered = {r for x in T for r in x[\"requirementIds\"]}\nprint(\"uncovered reqs:\", sorted(valid-covered))\n\nout = os.path.join(root,\"artifacts/dev-planning\")\nmatrix = dict(ticketId=TID, timestamp=TS, phase=\"dev-planning\", version=\"1.0\",\n    entries=[dict(path=p, taskId=x[\"id\"], operation=op) for x in T for op,p in x[\"files\"]])\njson.dump(matrix, open(f\"{out}/file-ownership-matrix.json\",\"w\"), indent=2)\n\nfs = {}\nfor p in seen:\n    d, _, f = p.rpartition(\"/\")\n    fs.setdefault((d or \".\")+\"/\", []).append(f)\nplan = dict(ticketId=TID, version=\"1.0\", timestamp=TS, phase=\"dev-planning\",\n    tasks=[{**x, \"files\":[p for _,p in x[\"files\"]]} for x in T],\n    fileStructure={k: sorted(v) for k,v in sorted(fs.items())},\n    totalEstimateHours=sum(x[\"estimateHours\"] for x in T),\n    nxpPatterns=[], status=\"complete\")\njson.dump(plan, open(f\"{out}/implementation-plan.json\",\"w\"), indent=2)  # written LAST\nprint(len(T), \"tasks,\", len(seen), \"files,\", plan[\"totalEstimateHours\"], \"h\")\nEOF\npython3 -I /tmp/abcd1-plan/gen.py /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds","description":"Generate and validate ownership matrix and implementation plan"}}}
