{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTwii1yLeeACqhi41Az","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-4 dev-planning phase is finished. All four artifacts are in `artifacts/dev-planning/`, and they replace the old plan files there, which were for ticket abcd-1.\n\n- **`implementation-plan.json`** (written last, `status: complete`): 21 tasks, 36.5 estimated hours in total.\n- **`file-ownership-matrix.json`**: 45 file entries (38 new files, 7 changes to existing files). Each file belongs to exactly one task.\n- **`module-dependencies.json`**: how the folders depend on each other (separate from task order).\n- **`file-structure.md`**: the planned file tree, with the owning task marked on each file.\n\n**Task order:**\n1. Database migration, the notification type list, and the shared validators.\n2. Email templates, retry timing and email sending.\n3. Login emails (invite and password reset) now go into the outbox; then the `notify()` service and the dispatcher plus old-notification cleanup.\n4. API routes: user notifications, preferences, admin, and the internal dispatch endpoint (including the middleware change from finding B1).\n5. Background email worker.\n6. Screens: the bell, the notifications page, the preferences page and the admin email log.\n7. Seed data, then unit, integration and Playwright tests.\n\n**Checks:** I generated the plan and the ownership matrix from one task list, so they can't disagree. The script also checks that every requirement ID exists in `requirements.json`, that each task depends only on earlier tasks (so there are no cycles), and that no file is listed twice. `file-structure.md` was written by hand, so its paths weren't checked automatically against the matrix.\n\n**Things to know before the dev phase:**\n- **Migration folder name:** I fixed it to `20261104120000_notifications_email` so the path in the matrix is exact. Dev has to rename the folder Prisma generates to this name, or the downstream file check will flag it.\n- **mui-mcp:** it must be reachable before the four screen tasks (TASK-14 to TASK-17). This is the NFR-10 rule carried over from the architect phase, and dev must stop if it isn't available.\n- **NFR-17:** it has no task on purpose, because it only lists what is out of scope."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":997,"cache_read_input_tokens":63503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":997},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01342abc-2768-44d6-a3f9-0083d13d7230","uuid":"65b134bd-d388-42aa-b6aa-5a4da704e604","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:07:07.052Z","request_id":"req_011CghTwiSekFGUsUzejogke"}
