{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012mhYwaHXTMtNEHqmb2sRNY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),\n6\t`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n7\t`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),\n8\t`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).\n9\tBrownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`\n10\tclient (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in\n11\t`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## 1. Overview\n16\t\n17\tPRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:\n18\t\n19\t1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).\n20\t2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).\n21\t3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).\n22\t\n23\tAll of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing\n24\tis renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).\n25\t\n26\t### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)\n27\t\n28\t| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n29\t|---|---|\n30\t| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |\n31\t| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |\n32\t| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |\n33\t| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |\n34\t| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |\n35\t| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |\n36\t\n37\t### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)\n38\t\n39\t| # | Decision | Reason |\n40\t|---|---|---|\n41\t| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |\n42\t| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |\n43\t| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |\n44\t| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |\n45\t| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |\n46\t| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |\n47\t| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |\n48\t| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |\n49\t| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |\n50\t\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)\n54\t\n55\tNew migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only\n56\t`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.\n57\tGenerate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.\n58\t\n59\t```prisma\n60\tenum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }\n61\t\n62\tmodel Period {\n63\t  id        String          @id @default(cuid())\n64\t  name      String\n65\t  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n66\t  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n67\t  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)\n68\t  order     Int             @unique\n69\t  slots     TimetableSlot[]\n70\t  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())\n71\t  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt\n72\t}\n73\t\n74\tmodel SchoolDay {\n75\t  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun\n76\t  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)\n77\t}\n78\t\n79\tmodel TimetableSlot {\n80\t  id             String       @id @default(cuid())\n81\t  academicYearId String\n82\t  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n83\t  courseId       String\n84\t  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n85\t  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7\n86\t  periodId       String\n87\t  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service\n88\t  roomId         String?\n89\t  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n90\t  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())\n91\t  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt\n92\t\n93\t  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n94\t  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n95\t}\n96\t```\n97\t\n98\tAdditive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,\n99\t`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`\n100\t(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.\n101\t`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are\n102\tguaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.\n103\t\n104\t---\n105\t\n106\t## 3. Component Breakdown\n107\t\n108\t### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)\n109\t\n110\tThese are shared by the forms and the handlers.\n111\t\n112\t| Schema | Shape |\n113\t|---|---|\n114\t| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |\n115\t| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |\n116\t| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |\n117\t| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |\n118\t| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |\n119\t| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |\n120\t| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |\n121\t| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |\n122\t| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |\n123\t| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |\n124\t| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |\n125\t\n126\t`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).\n127\t\n128\t### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)\n129\t\n130\t```ts\n131\texport function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }\n132\t//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }\n133\texport function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(\n134\t  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\tThe functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view\n138\t(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.\n139\tA 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.\n140\t\n141\t### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)\n142\t\n143\tThis is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the\n144\tNFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.\n145\t\n146\t```ts\n147\ttype ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';\n148\ttype Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };\n149\t\n150\tinterface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }\n151\tinterface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }\n152\tinterface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }\n153\t\n154\tfunction clashesForCell(\n155\t  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,\n156\t  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot\n157\t  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students\n158\t): Clash[]\n159\t```\n160\t\n161\tThe rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):\n162\t\n163\t| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |\n164\t|---|---|---|\n165\t| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |\n166\t| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |\n167\t| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |\n168\t| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |\n169\t| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |\n170\t| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |\n171\t\n172\t`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.\n173\t\n174\t### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)\n175\t\n176\t`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.\n177\t\n178\t| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |\n179\t|---|---|---|\n180\t| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n181\t| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |\n182\t| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |\n183\t| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |\n184\t| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |\n185\t| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |\n186\t| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n187\t| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |\n188\t| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |\n189\t| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |\n190\t| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |\n191\t| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |\n192\t| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |\n193\t\n194\t### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)\n195\t\n196\t| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |\n197\t|---|---|---|---|\n198\t| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |\n199\t| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n200\t| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |\n201\t| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |\n202\t| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |\n203\t| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |\n204\t| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |\n205\t| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n206\t| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n207\t| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |\n208\t\n209\t**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.\n210\tADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.\n211\t\n212\tThe detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n213\t\n214\t### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)\n215\t\n216\tThis follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:\n217\t\n218\t```ts\n219\t<TimetableGrid\n220\t  periods days slots\n221\t  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"\n222\t  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period\n223\t  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging\n224\t  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18\n225\t/>\n226\t```\n227\t\n228\t- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).\n229\t- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).\n230\t- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.\n231\t- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.\n232\t- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).\n233\t- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.\n234\t\n235\t### 3.7 Pages\n236\t\n237\t| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |\n238\t|---|---|---|---|\n239\t| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |\n240\t| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |\n241\t| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |\n242\t| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |\n243\t| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |\n244\t\n245\tNavigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`\n246\t(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`\n247\t`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).\n248\t\n249\t### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)\n250\t\n251\tSeeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.\n252\t\n253\t1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).\n254\t2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).\n255\t3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**\n256\t4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.\n257\t   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.\n258\t\n259\t---\n260\t\n261\t## 4. Data Flow\n262\t\n263\t### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)\n264\t\n265\t```\n266\tdrag start (course card or slot)\n267\t  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)\n268\t     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored\n269\tdrop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)\n270\t  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }\n271\t  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }\n272\t       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {\n273\t                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]\n274\t                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved\n275\t                 insert / update\n276\t               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }\n277\t  client:\n278\t    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache\n279\t    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)\n280\t          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)\n281\tdrop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)\n282\tclick slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)\n283\t```\n284\t\n285\tConcurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set\n286\tand both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and\n287\treturns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).\n288\t\n289\t### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)\n290\t\n291\t`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.\n292\t`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.\n293\tTeaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm\n294\tdialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit\n295\t`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.\n296\t\n297\t### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)\n298\t\n299\t```\n300\t/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)\n301\t  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()\n302\t  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now\n303\t```\n304\t\n305\tClient-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same\n306\taccess rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).\n307\t\n308\t### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)\n309\t\n310\tPRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from\n311\t`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in\n312\t`SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n313\t\n314\t### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)\n315\t\n316\t`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),\n317\t`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).\n318\t`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.\n319\t\n320\t---\n321\t\n322\t## 5. Cross-cutting\n323\t\n324\t| Concern | Design | Reqs |\n325\t|---|---|---|\n326\t| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |\n327\t| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n328\t| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |\n329\t| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |\n330\t| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |\n331\t| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |\n332\t| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |\n333\t| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |\n334\t\n335\t### Tests (ADR-7)\n336\t\n337\t| File | Covers | Reqs |\n338\t|---|---|---|\n339\t| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |\n340\t| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |\n341\t| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |\n342\t| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |\n343\t| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |\n344\t\n345\t---\n346\t\n347\t## 6. File Map (new unless marked)\n348\t\n349\t```\n350\tprisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)\n351\tprisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)\n352\tprisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)\n353\tpackage.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")\n354\tsrc/lib/validators/timetable.ts\n355\tsrc/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)\n356\tsrc/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\n357\tsrc/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\n358\tsrc/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts\n359\tsrc/app/api/school-days/route.ts\n360\tsrc/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts\n361\tsrc/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts\n362\tsrc/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\n363\tsrc/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)\n364\tsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx\n365\tsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx\n366\tsrc/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx\n367\tsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx\n368\tsrc/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx\n369\tsrc/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)\n370\tapp-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")\n371\ttests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts\n372\ttests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts\n373\ttests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts\n374\t```\n375\t\n376\tThe `(app)` route group was checked on disk: `src/app/(app)/admin` already exists.\n377\t\n378\t---\n379\t\n380\t## 7. Requirements Traceability\n381\t\n382\t| Req | Design element |\n383\t|---|---|\n384\t| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |\n385\t| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |\n386\t| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |\n387\t| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |\n388\t| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |\n389\t| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |\n390\t| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |\n391\t| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |\n392\t| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |\n393\t| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |\n394\t| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |\n395\t| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |\n396\t| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |\n397\t| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |\n398\t| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |\n399\t| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |\n400\t| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |\n401\t| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |\n402\t| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |\n403\t| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |\n404\t| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |\n405\t| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |\n406\t| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |\n407\t| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |\n408\t| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |\n409\t| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |\n410\t| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |\n411\t| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |\n412\t| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |\n413\t| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |\n414\t| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |\n415\t| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |\n416\t| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |\n417\t| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |\n418\t| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |\n419\t| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |\n420\t| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |\n421\t| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |\n422\t| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |\n423\t| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |\n424\t| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |\n425\t| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |\n426\t| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |\n427\t| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |\n428\t| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |\n429\t| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |\n430\t| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |\n431\t| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |\n432\t| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |\n433\t| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |\n434\t| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |\n435\t| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |\n436\t| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |\n437\t| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |\n438\t| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |\n439\t| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |\n440\t| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |\n441\t| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |\n442\t| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |\n443\t| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |\n444\t| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |\n445\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d4e282d-2f0d-4b8c-b946-a1776a0c1082","uuid":"79e916da-bb44-44c1-9723-ba3c75ec81f5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:21:14.331Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).\nBrownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`\nclient (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in\n`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:\n\n1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).\n2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).\n3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).\n\nAll of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing\nis renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |\n| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |\n| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |\n| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |\n| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |\n\n### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |\n| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |\n| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |\n| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |\n| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |\n| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |\n| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |\n| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |\n| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)\n\nNew migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only\n`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.\nGenerate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.\n\n```prisma\nenum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }\n\nmodel Period {\n  id        String          @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String\n  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)\n  order     Int             @unique\n  slots     TimetableSlot[]\n  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel SchoolDay {\n  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun\n  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)\n}\n\nmodel TimetableSlot {\n  id             String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId String\n  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  courseId       String\n  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7\n  periodId       String\n  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service\n  roomId         String?\n  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n}\n```\n\nAdditive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,\n`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`\n(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.\n`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are\nguaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)\n\nThese are shared by the forms and the handlers.\n\n| Schema | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |\n| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |\n| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |\n| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |\n| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |\n| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |\n| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |\n| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |\n| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |\n| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |\n| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |\n\n`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).\n\n### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)\n\n```ts\nexport function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }\n//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }\nexport function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(\n  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }\n```\n\nThe functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view\n(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.\nA 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.\n\n### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)\n\nThis is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the\nNFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.\n\n```ts\ntype ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';\ntype Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };\n\ninterface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }\ninterface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }\ninterface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }\n\nfunction clashesForCell(\n  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,\n  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot\n  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students\n): Clash[]\n```\n\nThe rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):\n\n| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |\n| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |\n| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |\n| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |\n| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |\n| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |\n\n`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.\n\n### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)\n\n`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.\n\n| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |\n| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |\n| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |\n| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |\n| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |\n| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |\n| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |\n\n### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |\n| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |\n| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |\n| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |\n| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |\n| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |\n\n**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.\nADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.\n\nThe detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)\n\nThis follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:\n\n```ts\n<TimetableGrid\n  periods days slots\n  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"\n  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period\n  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging\n  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18\n/>\n```\n\n- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).\n- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).\n- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.\n- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.\n- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).\n- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.\n\n### 3.7 Pages\n\n| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |\n| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |\n| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |\n| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |\n\nNavigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`\n(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`\n`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).\n\n### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)\n\nSeeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.\n\n1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).\n2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).\n3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**\n4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.\n   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)\n\n```\ndrag start (course card or slot)\n  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)\n     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored\ndrop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)\n  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }\n  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }\n       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {\n                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]\n                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved\n                 insert / update\n               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }\n  client:\n    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache\n    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)\n          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)\ndrop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)\nclick slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)\n```\n\nConcurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set\nand both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and\nreturns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).\n\n### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)\n\n`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.\n`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.\nTeaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm\ndialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit\n`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.\n\n### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)\n\n```\n/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)\n  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()\n  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now\n```\n\nClient-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same\naccess rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).\n\n### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nPRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from\n`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in\n`SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)\n\n`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),\n`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).\n`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n| Concern | Design | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |\n| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |\n| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |\n| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |\n| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |\n| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |\n| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |\n\n### Tests (ADR-7)\n\n| File | Covers | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |\n| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File Map (new unless marked)\n\n```\nprisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)\nprisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)\nprisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)\npackage.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")\nsrc/lib/validators/timetable.ts\nsrc/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)\nsrc/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\nsrc/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\nsrc/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/school-days/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\nsrc/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx\nsrc/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)\napp-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")\ntests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts\ntests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts\ntests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts\n```\n\nThe `(app)` route group was checked on disk: `src/app/(app)/admin` already exists.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |\n| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |\n| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |\n| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |\n| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |\n| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |\n| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |\n| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |\n| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |\n| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |\n| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |\n| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |\n| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |\n| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |\n| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |\n| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |\n| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |\n| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |\n| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |\n| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |\n| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |\n| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |\n| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |\n| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |\n| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |\n| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |\n| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |\n| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |\n| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |\n| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |\n| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |\n| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |\n| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |\n| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |\n| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |\n| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |\n| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |\n| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |\n| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |\n| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |\n| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |\n| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |\n| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |\n| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |\n| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |\n| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |\n| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |\n| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |\n| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |\n| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |\n| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |\n| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |\n| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |\n| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |\n","numLines":445,"startLine":1,"totalLines":445}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012mhYwaHXTMtNEHqmb2sRNY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
