{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjLFA4KQwJFFkXKazmvL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-1 dev-planning phase is done, and the plan is marked `complete`. The dev-planning files already on disk belonged to an earlier ticket (SH-6), so I replaced all four. `implementation-plan.json` was written last.\n\n**The plan:** 14 tasks covering 22 files, estimated at 25.5 hours in total. This ticket adds pages, wiring, seed data and tests only. Nothing under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/` or the other existing auth modules is touched.\n\n| Task | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Add the missing User index in a new migration. AuditLog's `ip` column keeps its name. |\n| 2 | Seed six active users and one invited user. The invite link is logged, not emailed. |\n| 3, 4 | Login page and form, plus a unit test for the sign-in error messages |\n| 5 | Forgot-password page |\n| 6, 7 | Reset-password and invite pages. Each gets a small client file because the existing password form needs a submit callback. |\n| 8 | Remove the placeholder user from the app shell. The shell now gets the real signed-in user, and the menu gets \"Account security\" and a working \"Sign out\". |\n| 9 | Account security page for changing the password |\n| 10–12 | Integration tests for sign-in, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password |\n| 13 | A shared sign-in helper for browser tests. `dashboard.spec.ts` uses it, so it doesn't break once `/dashboard` requires login. |\n| 14 | End-to-end browser tests for sign-in, sign-out and forgot → reset |\n\n**Checks:** a script compared the files: task files match the ownership list exactly, the dependency order has no cycles, every requirement id cited exists in `requirements.json`, and all files carry ticket id SH-1.\n\nFour requirements aren't cited by any task: FR-9, FR-24, NFR-4 and NFR-10. Each describes behaviour the existing code already has and this ticket doesn't change.\n\n**Decisions and open items:**\n- **Invited seed user:** the PRD gives no name or role, so I used the architect's default of \"Ivy Invited\", a teacher. Dev can change it.\n- **Optional change skipped:** the architect said `notifications.spec.ts` could also switch to the new sign-in helper. I didn't plan that.\n- **Needs your sign-off:** keeping AuditLog's column as `ip` instead of renaming it to `ipAddress` (FR-32).\n- **Dev blocker:** dev must look up every UI component through the `mui-mcp` docs server before writing UI code, and stop if it can't reach it.\n- **Stale files from SH-6:** they're still in `artifacts/dev/`, `artifacts/qa/` and `artifacts/ui-verification/`. The later phases will need to regenerate them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":770,"cache_read_input_tokens":63093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":770},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95d2735-afe9-4e17-abf3-81d9c26b2b8a","uuid":"7935d340-9e02-495c-8558-5fd389dd5c8b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:47:21.002Z","request_id":"req_011CgjLF9qR1HGRH5akkY8B8"}
