{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014NoajXcCw4eCCcHiozkydh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n5\t`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n6\t`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n7\t\n8\t> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n9\t> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## 1. Overview\n14\t\n15\tSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\n16\tCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n17\t(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\n18\tlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n19\t\n20\t**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n21\t`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n22\t(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n23\t\n24\t### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n25\t\n26\t| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n27\t|---|---|---|\n28\t| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n29\t| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n30\t| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n31\t| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n32\t| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n33\t\n34\t### Additional risks found during design\n35\t\n36\t- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n37\t  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n38\t  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n39\t- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n40\t  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n41\t- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n42\t  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n43\t\n44\t---\n45\t\n46\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n47\t\n48\t### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n49\t\n50\t| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n51\t|---|---|---|\n52\t| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n53\t| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n54\t| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n55\t| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n56\t| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n57\t| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n58\t| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n59\t| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n60\t| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n61\t\n62\tDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n63\t\n64\t### 2.2 New and modified components\n65\t\n66\t| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n67\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n68\t| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n69\t| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n70\t| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n71\t| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n72\t| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n73\t| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n74\t| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n75\t| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n76\t| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n77\t\n78\t**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n79\t`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n80\t`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\n81\tCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n82\t\n83\t---\n84\t\n85\t## 3. Data Flow\n86\t\n87\t**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n88\t```\n89\t/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n90\t       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\n91\tlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\n92\tC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n93\t       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n97\t```\n98\t/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\n99\tC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\n100\tC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\t**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n104\t```\n105\t/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n106\t   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n107\t   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n108\t```\n109\t\n110\t**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n111\t```\n112\trequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n113\t           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n114\t```\n115\t\n116\t---\n117\t\n118\t## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n119\t\n120\t1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n121\t   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n122\t   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n123\t2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n124\t   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n125\t3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n126\t   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n127\t4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n128\t   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n129\t5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n130\t   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n131\t6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n132\t\n133\t---\n134\t\n135\t## 5. Requirements Traceability\n136\t\n137\t| Req | Design element |\n138\t|---|---|\n139\t| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n140\t| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n141\t| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n142\t| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n143\t| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n144\t| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n145\t| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n146\t| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n147\t| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n148\t| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n149\t| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n150\t| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n151\t| FR-13 | C3 |\n152\t| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n153\t| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n154\t| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n155\t| FR-17 | C1 |\n156\t| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n157\t| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n158\t| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n159\t| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n160\t| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n161\t| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n162\t| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n163\t| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n164\t| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n165\t| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n166\t| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n167\t| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n168\t| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n169\t| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n170\t| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n171\t| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n172\t| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n173\t| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n174\t| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n175\t| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n176\t| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n177\t| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n178\t| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n179\t| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n180\t| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n181\t| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n182\t| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n183\t| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n184\t| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n185\t| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n186\t\n187\t---\n188\t\n189\t## 6. Change Footprint\n190\t\n191\t- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n192\t  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n193\t  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n194\t  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n195\t- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n196\t- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n197\t  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n198\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e695f9e3-b58d-43ba-a40f-80582ccbd08f","uuid":"166e75ae-5888-4af0-885e-e7298c531d61","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:31:57.624Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\nCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\nlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n\n**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n\n### Additional risks found during design\n\n- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n\nDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 New and modified components\n\n| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n\n**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\nCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n```\n/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\nlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n```\n\n**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n```\n/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\nC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n```\n\n**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n```\n/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n```\n\n**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n```\nrequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n\n1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n| FR-13 | C3 |\n| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-17 | C1 |\n| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Change Footprint\n\n- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n","numLines":198,"startLine":1,"totalLines":198}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014NoajXcCw4eCCcHiozkydh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
