{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KY9ih6Ni8p8UmkZL5JYXGy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:40:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t  \"conventions\": {\n7\t    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention; no /api/v1 prefix — NFR-13 forbids renaming routes)\",\n8\t    \"scope\": \"SH-1 adds NO new endpoints (system-design.md §1, ADR-1, NFR-13). Every contract below documents an EXISTING route that the new pages (C1–C5), shell (C7) and tests (C8, C9) call. Dev must not modify src/app/api/** or src/server/**.\",\n9\t    \"successEnvelope\": {\n10\t      \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\"\n11\t    },\n12\t    \"errorEnvelope\": {\n13\t      \"error\": {\n14\t        \"code\": \"string\",\n15\t        \"message\": \"string\",\n16\t        \"details\": \"unknown?\"\n17\t      }\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"errorCodes\": {\n20\t      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n21\t      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n22\t      \"FORBIDDEN\": 403,\n23\t      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n24\t      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n25\t      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410,\n26\t      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n27\t      \"INTERNAL\": 500\n28\t    },\n29\t    \"validationErrorDetails\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR details are Zod flatten() output: { formErrors: string[], fieldErrors: { [field]: string[] } }. Service-raised policy errors use the same { fieldErrors } shape, so applyFieldErrors() handles both.\",\n30\t    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler → (requireUser) → parseBody(schema from src/lib/validators/auth.ts) → services/auth.ts → ok(). All helpers in src/server/http.ts.\",\n31\t    \"requirementIds\": [\n32\t      \"NFR-10\",\n33\t      \"NFR-11\",\n34\t      \"NFR-13\"\n35\t    ]\n36\t  },\n37\t  \"sharedSchemas\": {\n38\t    \"Email\": {\n39\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n40\t      \"format\": \"email\",\n41\t      \"note\": \"trimmed and lower-cased by emailField before use\"\n42\t    },\n43\t    \"NewPassword\": {\n44\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n45\t      \"minLength\": 10,\n46\t      \"maxLength\": 128,\n47\t      \"note\": \"≥1 letter, ≥1 digit, ≠ user email, not in common-passwords.txt (server-side only). FR-15.\"\n48\t    },\n49\t    \"Ok\": {\n50\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n51\t      \"required\": [\n52\t        \"ok\"\n53\t      ],\n54\t      \"properties\": {\n55\t        \"ok\": {\n56\t          \"const\": true\n57\t        }\n58\t      }\n59\t    },\n60\t    \"FieldErrors\": {\n61\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n62\t      \"properties\": {\n63\t        \"formErrors\": {\n64\t          \"type\": \"array\",\n65\t          \"items\": {\n66\t            \"type\": \"string\"\n67\t          }\n68\t        },\n69\t        \"fieldErrors\": {\n70\t          \"type\": \"object\",\n71\t          \"additionalProperties\": {\n72\t            \"type\": \"array\",\n73\t            \"items\": {\n74\t              \"type\": \"string\"\n75\t            }\n76\t          }\n77\t        }\n78\t      }\n79\t    }\n80\t  },\n81\t  \"endpoints\": [\n82\t    {\n83\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n84\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n85\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js credentials sign-in (served by /api/auth/[...nextauth]). Called ONLY through signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false }) from next-auth/react, which fetches the CSRF token itself. Runs authorizeCredentials: IP rate limit (10 / 5 min), user lookup, bcrypt or DUMMY_HASH compare, status and lock checks, lockout counter, audit. Used by the existing /login (verify only), C4 post-invite sign-in, and the C9 e2e signInAs helper.\",\n86\t      \"auth\": \"public\",\n87\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n88\t        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n89\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n90\t        \"required\": [\n91\t          \"email\",\n92\t          \"password\",\n93\t          \"csrfToken\"\n94\t        ],\n95\t        \"properties\": {\n96\t          \"email\": {\n97\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Email\"\n98\t          },\n99\t          \"password\": {\n100\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n101\t            \"minLength\": 1\n102\t          },\n103\t          \"csrfToken\": {\n104\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n105\t            \"note\": \"from GET /api/auth/csrf; added automatically by signIn()\"\n106\t          },\n107\t          \"callbackUrl\": {\n108\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n109\t            \"note\": \"sanitised by the redirect callback; the client also applies safeCallbackUrl()\"\n110\t          }\n111\t        }\n112\t      },\n113\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n114\t        \"note\": \"Not the {data} envelope — Auth.js framework response. signIn(..., { redirect: false }) resolves to the object below.\",\n115\t        \"success\": {\n116\t          \"ok\": true,\n117\t          \"error\": null,\n118\t          \"sideEffects\": \"sets the HttpOnly session cookie (8h JWT); failedLoginCount=0, lastLoginAt=now; audit auth.login.success\"\n119\t        },\n120\t        \"failure\": {\n121\t          \"ok\": false,\n122\t          \"error\": \"CredentialsSignin\",\n123\t          \"code\": {\n124\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n125\t            \"enum\": [\n126\t              \"invalid\",\n127\t              \"disabled\",\n128\t              \"rate_limited\",\n129\t              \"locked:<N>\"\n130\t            ],\n131\t            \"uiMapping\": {\n132\t              \"locked:<N>\": \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\",\n133\t              \"disabled\": \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\",\n134\t              \"rate_limited\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\",\n135\t              \"*\": \"Email or password is incorrect.\"\n136\t            },\n137\t            \"note\": \"Mapped by the existing loginErrorMessage(code) in src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx (already handles rate_limited, R3). Each failure audits auth.login.failure { email, reason }; the 5th consecutive failure also audits auth.lockout and returns locked:15.\"\n138\t          }\n139\t        }\n140\t      },\n141\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n142\t        \"FR-2\",\n143\t        \"FR-3\",\n144\t        \"FR-4\",\n145\t        \"FR-5\",\n146\t        \"FR-6\",\n147\t        \"FR-7\",\n148\t        \"FR-8\",\n149\t        \"FR-9\",\n150\t        \"NFR-2\",\n151\t        \"NFR-3\",\n152\t        \"NFR-4\",\n153\t        \"NFR-14\"\n154\t      ]\n155\t    },\n156\t    {\n157\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n158\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n159\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token (served by /api/auth/[...nextauth]). Called implicitly by signIn()/signOut(). C9 signs in through the UI, so no test calls it directly.\",\n160\t      \"auth\": \"public\",\n161\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n162\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n163\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n164\t        \"required\": [\n165\t          \"csrfToken\"\n166\t        ],\n167\t        \"properties\": {\n168\t          \"csrfToken\": {\n169\t            \"type\": \"string\"\n170\t          }\n171\t        }\n172\t      },\n173\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n174\t        \"NFR-2\"\n175\t      ]\n176\t    },\n177\t    {\n178\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n179\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n180\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out (served by /api/auth/[...nextauth]). Called only through signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' }) from the shell user menu (C7). Clears the session cookie.\",\n181\t      \"auth\": \"session cookie (no-op if absent)\",\n182\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n183\t        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n184\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n185\t        \"required\": [\n186\t          \"csrfToken\"\n187\t        ],\n188\t        \"properties\": {\n189\t          \"csrfToken\": {\n190\t            \"type\": \"string\"\n191\t          }\n192\t        }\n193\t      },\n194\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n195\t        \"note\": \"Framework redirect; client navigates to /login.\"\n196\t      },\n197\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n198\t        \"FR-26\",\n199\t        \"NFR-2\"\n200\t      ]\n201\t    },\n202\t    {\n203\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n204\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n205\t      \"description\": \"Request a password reset link (C1 /forgot-password). Always returns the same 200 body whether or not the account exists (no enumeration). IP limit 10/h → 429; per-email limit 3/h is SILENT (still 200, no token). For an ACTIVE, non-archived user: createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min), sendAuthEmail('password-reset') → EmailOutbox, audit auth.password.reset_requested. UI (C1): 2xx → success Alert with data.message; 429 → error Alert 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' (IP-scoped, so it reveals nothing about the account).\",\n206\t      \"auth\": \"public\",\n207\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n208\t        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n209\t        \"zod\": \"forgotPasswordSchema\",\n210\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n211\t        \"required\": [\n212\t          \"email\"\n213\t        ],\n214\t        \"properties\": {\n215\t          \"email\": {\n216\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Email\"\n217\t          }\n218\t        }\n219\t      },\n220\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n221\t        \"200\": {\n222\t          \"data\": {\n223\t            \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\"\n224\t          }\n225\t        },\n226\t        \"400\": {\n227\t          \"error\": {\n228\t            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n229\t            \"details\": {\n230\t              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n231\t            }\n232\t          }\n233\t        },\n234\t        \"429\": {\n235\t          \"error\": {\n236\t            \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\",\n237\t            \"message\": \"Too many requests. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n238\t          }\n239\t        }\n240\t      },\n241\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n242\t        \"FR-17\",\n243\t        \"FR-18\",\n244\t        \"FR-31\",\n245\t        \"NFR-1\",\n246\t        \"NFR-10\"\n247\t      ]\n248\t    },\n249\t    {\n250\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n251\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n252\t      \"description\": \"Set a new password from a reset link (C2 page → C4 TokenPasswordForm mode=reset). verifyToken(PASSWORD_RESET) → policy → bcrypt 12 → transaction(consume token, set hash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null) → audit auth.password.reset. Success → router.replace('/login?reset=1'). 410 → C4 switches to the invalid-link Alert. Other sessions are revoked within 5 min through the passwordChangedAt recheck.\",\n253\t      \"auth\": \"public (token-gated)\",\n254\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n255\t        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n256\t        \"zod\": \"resetPasswordSchema\",\n257\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n258\t        \"required\": [\n259\t          \"token\",\n260\t          \"password\",\n261\t          \"confirm\"\n262\t        ],\n263\t        \"properties\": {\n264\t          \"token\": {\n265\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n266\t            \"minLength\": 1,\n267\t            \"note\": \"raw token from the URL; never logged or audited\"\n268\t          },\n269\t          \"password\": {\n270\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/NewPassword\"\n271\t          },\n272\t          \"confirm\": {\n273\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n274\t            \"note\": \"must equal password. Field is `confirm`, NOT `confirmPassword` (system-design C4 wording is wrong). SetPasswordForm's onSubmit(password, confirm) already uses this name.\"\n275\t          }\n276\t        }\n277\t      },\n278\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n279\t        \"200\": {\n280\t          \"data\": {\n281\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Ok\"\n282\t          }\n283\t        },\n284\t        \"400\": {\n285\t          \"error\": {\n286\t            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n287\t            \"details\": {\n288\t              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n289\t            },\n290\t            \"note\": \"policy failures come back under fieldErrors.password (incl. 'This password is too common. Choose another.')\"\n291\t          }\n292\t        },\n293\t        \"410\": {\n294\t          \"error\": {\n295\t            \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\",\n296\t            \"message\": \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"\n297\t          }\n298\t        }\n299\t      },\n300\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n301\t        \"FR-12\",\n302\t        \"FR-15\",\n303\t        \"FR-19\",\n304\t        \"FR-10\",\n305\t        \"NFR-1\",\n306\t        \"NFR-8\",\n307\t        \"NFR-10\"\n308\t      ]\n309\t    },\n310\t    {\n311\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n312\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/accept-invite\",\n313\t      \"description\": \"Activate an invited account (C3 page → C4 TokenPasswordForm mode=invite). verifyToken(INVITE) → policy → bcrypt 12 → transaction(consume token, set hash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now) → audit auth.invite.accepted. Does NOT create a session: C4 then calls signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false }) and router.replace('/dashboard'). On 410 C4 renders the FR-13 copy ('This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'), not the service message.\",\n314\t      \"auth\": \"public (token-gated)\",\n315\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n316\t        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n317\t        \"zod\": \"acceptInviteSchema\",\n318\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n319\t        \"required\": [\n320\t          \"token\",\n321\t          \"password\",\n322\t          \"confirm\"\n323\t        ],\n324\t        \"properties\": {\n325\t          \"token\": {\n326\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n327\t            \"minLength\": 1\n328\t          },\n329\t          \"password\": {\n330\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/NewPassword\"\n331\t          },\n332\t          \"confirm\": {\n333\t            \"type\": \"string\"\n334\t          }\n335\t        }\n336\t      },\n337\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n338\t        \"200\": {\n339\t          \"data\": {\n340\t            \"type\": \"object\",\n341\t            \"required\": [\n342\t              \"email\"\n343\t            ],\n344\t            \"properties\": {\n345\t              \"email\": {\n346\t                \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Email\"\n347\t              }\n348\t            }\n349\t          }\n350\t        },\n351\t        \"400\": {\n352\t          \"error\": {\n353\t            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n354\t            \"details\": {\n355\t              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n356\t            }\n357\t          }\n358\t        },\n359\t        \"410\": {\n360\t          \"error\": {\n361\t            \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\",\n362\t            \"message\": \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"\n363\t          }\n364\t        }\n365\t      },\n366\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n367\t        \"FR-12\",\n368\t        \"FR-13\",\n369\t        \"FR-14\",\n370\t        \"FR-15\",\n371\t        \"NFR-1\",\n372\t        \"NFR-8\",\n373\t        \"NFR-10\",\n374\t        \"NFR-14\"\n375\t      ]\n376\t    },\n377\t    {\n378\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n379\t      \"path\": \"/api/account/password\",\n380\t      \"description\": \"Signed-in password change (C5 /account/security). requireUser → changePasswordSchema → bcrypt compare current → policy → update hash + passwordChangedAt → audit auth.password.changed → unstable_update({ reauth: true }) re-issues THIS session so only other sessions are revoked (within 5 min). Success → useToast 'Password updated', form reset, router.refresh().\",\n381\t      \"auth\": \"session required (requireUser; middleware returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON without a session)\",\n382\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n383\t        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n384\t        \"zod\": \"changePasswordSchema\",\n385\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n386\t        \"required\": [\n387\t          \"currentPassword\",\n388\t          \"newPassword\",\n389\t          \"confirm\"\n390\t        ],\n391\t        \"properties\": {\n392\t          \"currentPassword\": {\n393\t            \"type\": \"string\",\n394\t            \"minLength\": 1\n395\t          },\n396\t          \"newPassword\": {\n397\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/NewPassword\"\n398\t          },\n399\t          \"confirm\": {\n400\t            \"type\": \"string\"\n401\t          }\n402\t        }\n403\t      },\n404\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n405\t        \"200\": {\n406\t          \"data\": {\n407\t            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Ok\"\n408\t          }\n409\t        },\n410\t        \"400\": {\n411\t          \"error\": {\n412\t            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n413\t            \"details\": {\n414\t              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n415\t            }\n416\t          },\n417\t          \"cases\": {\n418\t            \"wrongCurrent\": \"{ message: 'Current password is incorrect.', details: { fieldErrors: { currentPassword: ['Current password is incorrect.'] } } }\",\n419\t            \"policyFailure\": \"details.fieldErrors.password (NOT newPassword): assertPasswordAllowed (src/server/auth/password-policy.ts) hard-codes the `password` key. ChangePasswordForm must remap password → newPassword before applyFieldErrors(), or the error renders nowhere. Client-side Zod already catches every rule except common-password, so in practice this case only appears for common passwords.\"\n420\t          }\n421\t        },\n422\t        \"401\": {\n423\t          \"error\": {\n424\t            \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\"\n425\t          }\n426\t        }\n427\t      },\n428\t      \"requirementIds\": [\n429\t        \"FR-10\",\n430\t        \"FR-15\",\n431\t        \"FR-20\",\n432\t        \"FR-23\",\n433\t        \"NFR-9\",\n434\t        \"NFR-10\",\n435\t        \"NFR-11\"\n436\t      ]\n437\t    }\n438\t  ],\n439\t  \"unauthenticatedBehaviour\": {\n440\t    \"description\": \"middleware.ts (existing): unauthenticated /api/* requests other than /api/health, /api/auth/* and public-routes.ts paths return 401 { error: { code: 'UNAUTHENTICATED' } }; unauthenticated (app) page requests redirect to /login?callbackUrl=<path>.\",\n441\t    \"requirementIds\": [\n442\t      \"FR-11\",\n443\t      \"NFR-9\"\n444\t    ]\n445\t  },\n446\t  \"designCorrections\": [\n447\t    \"system-design.md C4 posts `confirmPassword`; the real field is `confirm` (resetPasswordSchema / acceptInviteSchema / changePasswordSchema in src/lib/validators/auth.ts). Body is { token, password, confirm }.\",\n448\t    \"system-design.md C5 doesn't cover common-password errors on /api/account/password: they arrive under fieldErrors.password and must be remapped to newPassword in ChangePasswordForm. Fix it on the client, not in the service (NFR-13).\",\n449\t    \"system-design.md R2 is confirmed: INVALID_TOKEN → HTTP 410 (src/server/http.ts). It is not in the NFR-10 list; it is kept as-is.\"\n450\t  ],\n451\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n452\t}\n453\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e695f9e3-b58d-43ba-a40f-80582ccbd08f","uuid":"469f5d8a-9c42-4646-b7eb-a1ff2ae3da3b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:31:58.447Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:40:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention; no /api/v1 prefix — NFR-13 forbids renaming routes)\",\n    \"scope\": \"SH-1 adds NO new endpoints (system-design.md §1, ADR-1, NFR-13). Every contract below documents an EXISTING route that the new pages (C1–C5), shell (C7) and tests (C8, C9) call. Dev must not modify src/app/api/** or src/server/**.\",\n    \"successEnvelope\": {\n      \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\"\n    },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": {\n      \"error\": {\n        \"code\": \"string\",\n        \"message\": \"string\",\n        \"details\": \"unknown?\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"errorCodes\": {\n      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n      \"FORBIDDEN\": 403,\n      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410,\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n      \"INTERNAL\": 500\n    },\n    \"validationErrorDetails\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR details are Zod flatten() output: { formErrors: string[], fieldErrors: { [field]: string[] } }. Service-raised policy errors use the same { fieldErrors } shape, so applyFieldErrors() handles both.\",\n    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler → (requireUser) → parseBody(schema from src/lib/validators/auth.ts) → services/auth.ts → ok(). All helpers in src/server/http.ts.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\n      \"NFR-10\",\n      \"NFR-11\",\n      \"NFR-13\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"sharedSchemas\": {\n    \"Email\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"format\": \"email\",\n      \"note\": \"trimmed and lower-cased by emailField before use\"\n    },\n    \"NewPassword\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 10,\n      \"maxLength\": 128,\n      \"note\": \"≥1 letter, ≥1 digit, ≠ user email, not in common-passwords.txt (server-side only). FR-15.\"\n    },\n    \"Ok\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"ok\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"ok\": {\n          \"const\": true\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"FieldErrors\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"formErrors\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"fieldErrors\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js credentials sign-in (served by /api/auth/[...nextauth]). Called ONLY through signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false }) from next-auth/react, which fetches the CSRF token itself. Runs authorizeCredentials: IP rate limit (10 / 5 min), user lookup, bcrypt or DUMMY_HASH compare, status and lock checks, lockout counter, audit. Used by the existing /login (verify only), C4 post-invite sign-in, and the C9 e2e signInAs helper.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"email\",\n          \"password\",\n          \"csrfToken\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"email\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Email\"\n          },\n          \"password\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"csrfToken\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"note\": \"from GET /api/auth/csrf; added automatically by signIn()\"\n          },\n          \"callbackUrl\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"note\": \"sanitised by the redirect callback; the client also applies safeCallbackUrl()\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"note\": \"Not the {data} envelope — Auth.js framework response. signIn(..., { redirect: false }) resolves to the object below.\",\n        \"success\": {\n          \"ok\": true,\n          \"error\": null,\n          \"sideEffects\": \"sets the HttpOnly session cookie (8h JWT); failedLoginCount=0, lastLoginAt=now; audit auth.login.success\"\n        },\n        \"failure\": {\n          \"ok\": false,\n          \"error\": \"CredentialsSignin\",\n          \"code\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"invalid\",\n              \"disabled\",\n              \"rate_limited\",\n              \"locked:<N>\"\n            ],\n            \"uiMapping\": {\n              \"locked:<N>\": \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\",\n              \"disabled\": \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\",\n              \"rate_limited\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\",\n              \"*\": \"Email or password is incorrect.\"\n            },\n            \"note\": \"Mapped by the existing loginErrorMessage(code) in src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx (already handles rate_limited, R3). Each failure audits auth.login.failure { email, reason }; the 5th consecutive failure also audits auth.lockout and returns locked:15.\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-2\",\n        \"FR-3\",\n        \"FR-4\",\n        \"FR-5\",\n        \"FR-6\",\n        \"FR-7\",\n        \"FR-8\",\n        \"FR-9\",\n        \"NFR-2\",\n        \"NFR-3\",\n        \"NFR-4\",\n        \"NFR-14\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token (served by /api/auth/[...nextauth]). Called implicitly by signIn()/signOut(). C9 signs in through the UI, so no test calls it directly.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"csrfToken\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"csrfToken\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"NFR-2\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out (served by /api/auth/[...nextauth]). Called only through signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' }) from the shell user menu (C7). Clears the session cookie.\",\n      \"auth\": \"session cookie (no-op if absent)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"csrfToken\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"csrfToken\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"note\": \"Framework redirect; client navigates to /login.\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-26\",\n        \"NFR-2\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Request a password reset link (C1 /forgot-password). Always returns the same 200 body whether or not the account exists (no enumeration). IP limit 10/h → 429; per-email limit 3/h is SILENT (still 200, no token). For an ACTIVE, non-archived user: createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min), sendAuthEmail('password-reset') → EmailOutbox, audit auth.password.reset_requested. UI (C1): 2xx → success Alert with data.message; 429 → error Alert 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' (IP-scoped, so it reveals nothing about the account).\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n        \"zod\": \"forgotPasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"email\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"email\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Email\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"400\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n            \"details\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"429\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\",\n            \"message\": \"Too many requests. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-17\",\n        \"FR-18\",\n        \"FR-31\",\n        \"NFR-1\",\n        \"NFR-10\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Set a new password from a reset link (C2 page → C4 TokenPasswordForm mode=reset). verifyToken(PASSWORD_RESET) → policy → bcrypt 12 → transaction(consume token, set hash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null) → audit auth.password.reset. Success → router.replace('/login?reset=1'). 410 → C4 switches to the invalid-link Alert. Other sessions are revoked within 5 min through the passwordChangedAt recheck.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public (token-gated)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n        \"zod\": \"resetPasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"token\",\n          \"password\",\n          \"confirm\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"token\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1,\n            \"note\": \"raw token from the URL; never logged or audited\"\n          },\n          \"password\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/NewPassword\"\n          },\n          \"confirm\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"note\": \"must equal password. Field is `confirm`, NOT `confirmPassword` (system-design C4 wording is wrong). SetPasswordForm's onSubmit(password, confirm) already uses this name.\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Ok\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"400\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n            \"details\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n            },\n            \"note\": \"policy failures come back under fieldErrors.password (incl. 'This password is too common. Choose another.')\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"410\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\",\n            \"message\": \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-12\",\n        \"FR-15\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"FR-10\",\n        \"NFR-1\",\n        \"NFR-8\",\n        \"NFR-10\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/accept-invite\",\n      \"description\": \"Activate an invited account (C3 page → C4 TokenPasswordForm mode=invite). verifyToken(INVITE) → policy → bcrypt 12 → transaction(consume token, set hash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now) → audit auth.invite.accepted. Does NOT create a session: C4 then calls signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false }) and router.replace('/dashboard'). On 410 C4 renders the FR-13 copy ('This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'), not the service message.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public (token-gated)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n        \"zod\": \"acceptInviteSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"token\",\n          \"password\",\n          \"confirm\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"token\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"password\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/NewPassword\"\n          },\n          \"confirm\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"email\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"email\": {\n                \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Email\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"400\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n            \"details\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"410\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\",\n            \"message\": \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-12\",\n        \"FR-13\",\n        \"FR-14\",\n        \"FR-15\",\n        \"NFR-1\",\n        \"NFR-8\",\n        \"NFR-10\",\n        \"NFR-14\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/account/password\",\n      \"description\": \"Signed-in password change (C5 /account/security). requireUser → changePasswordSchema → bcrypt compare current → policy → update hash + passwordChangedAt → audit auth.password.changed → unstable_update({ reauth: true }) re-issues THIS session so only other sessions are revoked (within 5 min). Success → useToast 'Password updated', form reset, router.refresh().\",\n      \"auth\": \"session required (requireUser; middleware returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON without a session)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n        \"zod\": \"changePasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"currentPassword\",\n          \"newPassword\",\n          \"confirm\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"currentPassword\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"newPassword\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/NewPassword\"\n          },\n          \"confirm\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/Ok\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"400\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n            \"details\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/FieldErrors\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"cases\": {\n            \"wrongCurrent\": \"{ message: 'Current password is incorrect.', details: { fieldErrors: { currentPassword: ['Current password is incorrect.'] } } }\",\n            \"policyFailure\": \"details.fieldErrors.password (NOT newPassword): assertPasswordAllowed (src/server/auth/password-policy.ts) hard-codes the `password` key. ChangePasswordForm must remap password → newPassword before applyFieldErrors(), or the error renders nowhere. Client-side Zod already catches every rule except common-password, so in practice this case only appears for common passwords.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"401\": {\n          \"error\": {\n            \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-10\",\n        \"FR-15\",\n        \"FR-20\",\n        \"FR-23\",\n        \"NFR-9\",\n        \"NFR-10\",\n        \"NFR-11\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unauthenticatedBehaviour\": {\n    \"description\": \"middleware.ts (existing): unauthenticated /api/* requests other than /api/health, /api/auth/* and public-routes.ts paths return 401 { error: { code: 'UNAUTHENTICATED' } }; unauthenticated (app) page requests redirect to /login?callbackUrl=<path>.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\n      \"FR-11\",\n      \"NFR-9\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"designCorrections\": [\n    \"system-design.md C4 posts `confirmPassword`; the real field is `confirm` (resetPasswordSchema / acceptInviteSchema / changePasswordSchema in src/lib/validators/auth.ts). Body is { token, password, confirm }.\",\n    \"system-design.md C5 doesn't cover common-password errors on /api/account/password: they arrive under fieldErrors.password and must be remapped to newPassword in ChangePasswordForm. Fix it on the client, not in the service (NFR-13).\",\n    \"system-design.md R2 is confirmed: INVALID_TOKEN → HTTP 410 (src/server/http.ts). It is not in the NFR-10 list; it is kept as-is.\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":453,"startLine":1,"totalLines":453}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KY9ih6Ni8p8UmkZL5JYXGy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6qGZ4GmUSi5W4QGHQ4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WSPSJzD1L6LC2L9tNyxwkg","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2928,"cache_read_input_tokens":28076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2928},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e695f9e3-b58d-43ba-a40f-80582ccbd08f","uuid":"d284c924-0e3d-469c-a039-ac51a79414ff","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:31:58.635Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk6qGLR7mZvZBictJeUz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WSPSJzD1L6LC2L9tNyxwkg":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WSPSJzD1L6LC2L9tNyxwkg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\n6\tconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\n7\tnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n8\t@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\n9\tVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n10\t**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n11\t\n12\tThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\n13\tcover only the remaining gaps.\n14\t\n15\t**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n16\t\n17\t- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n18\t- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n19\t- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n20\t- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n21\t- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n22\t- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n23\t- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n24\t- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n25\t- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n30\t\n31\t**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\n32\tpiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n33\t\n34\t**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\n35\tor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n36\t`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n37\t\n38\t**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n39\t\n40\t## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n41\t\n42\t**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\n43\tthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\n44\tneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n45\t\n46\t**Decision.**\n47\t- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n48\t- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n49\t- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n50\t\n51\t**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\n52\tfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n53\t\n54\t## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n55\t\n56\t**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\n57\ton success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\n58\tFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\n59\ttokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n60\t\n61\t**Decision.**\n62\t- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n63\t- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n64\t  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n65\t  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n66\t- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n67\t- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n68\t- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n69\t\n70\t**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\n71\tadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n72\t\n73\t## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n74\t\n75\t**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\n76\tand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\n77\tNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n78\t\n79\t**Decision.**\n80\t- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n81\t- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n82\t  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n83\t  - wrong-password message\n84\t  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n85\t  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n86\t  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n87\t\n88\t  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n89\t\n90\t**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\n91\tPlaywright process.\n92\t\n93\t## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n94\t\n95\t**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\n96\tmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n97\t\n98\t**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\n99\tare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n100\t\n101\t**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n102\t\n103\t---\n104\t\n105\t## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n106\t\n107\t- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n108\t- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n109\t- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n110\t- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e695f9e3-b58d-43ba-a40f-80582ccbd08f","uuid":"716707e8-72b3-4d05-b19c-3b8cfd6aefb5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:31:58.662Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\nadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n\n## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\nand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\nNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n  - wrong-password message\n  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n\n  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\nPlaywright process.\n\n## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n\n**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\nmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n\n**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\nare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WSPSJzD1L6LC2L9tNyxwkg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
