{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6uT6geNaEs64v7FrP7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011PQtrAxER2bANAcqFpJnLr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/sh1-plan && cat > /tmp/sh1-plan/gen.py <<'EOF'\nimport json, sys\nroot = sys.argv[1]\nA = root + \"/artifacts/\"\nTS = \"2026-11-05T17:55:00Z\"\nMOD = {\"src/app/(app)/layout.tsx\", \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx\", \"tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts\", \"tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts\"}\nGATE = \"NFR-6 gate: run mui-mcp useMuiDocs -> fetchDocs (@mui/material@9.5.0) for every MUI component used before writing JSX; stop and report if unreachable. \"\ntasks = [\n dict(id=\"TASK-1\", description=\"C1 /forgot-password. \" + GATE + \"page.tsx (server) renders a heading plus ForgotPasswordForm. ForgotPasswordForm.tsx ('use client'): RHF + zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema), TextFormField email, postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email}). 2xx -> success Alert showing data.message (do not retype the copy); 429 -> error Alert 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'; 400 -> applyFieldErrors. Single aria-live='polite' Alert, 'Back to sign in' MUI Link component={NextLink} href='/login'. Same success copy for known and unknown emails (no enumeration).\",\n      files=[\"src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx\", \"src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/ForgotPasswordForm.tsx\"], dependencies=[], estimateHours=1.5,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\", \"NFR-5\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-11\", \"NFR-15\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-2\", description=\"C4 shared TokenPasswordForm ('use client'). \" + GATE + \"Props {mode: 'invite'|'reset', token, email, name?, invalidMessage}. Wraps the existing SetPasswordForm({name, email, submitLabel, onSubmit}). onSubmit(password, confirm) -> postJson(mode==='invite' ? '/api/auth/accept-invite' : '/api/auth/reset-password', {token, password, confirm}). The body field is `confirm`, NOT confirmPassword (api-contracts designCorrections). On error.status 410 switch to local invalid state and render an Alert with invalidMessage (plus a link to /forgot-password for reset). Return any other ApiFailure so SetPasswordForm calls applyFieldErrors. Invite success: signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false}) from next-auth/react, then router.replace('/dashboard'). Reset success: router.replace('/login?reset=1') (the existing LoginForm toast fires). Never log the token or password.\",\n      files=[\"src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx\"], dependencies=[], estimateHours=2,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-14\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-19\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-5\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-8\", \"NFR-12\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-3\", description=\"C2 /reset-password/[token] server page. const v = await verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET') from src/server/auth/tokens.ts (read-only, does not consume). If null, render an Alert 'This link is invalid or has expired.' plus a Link to /forgot-password. Otherwise render <TokenPasswordForm mode='reset' token email={v.user.email} invalidMessage='This link is invalid or has expired.' />. Check the actual verifyToken return shape before use. No hashing outside tokens.ts.\",\n      files=[\"src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx\"], dependencies=[\"TASK-2\"], estimateHours=1,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-12\", \"FR-19\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-8\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-4\", description=\"C3 /invite/[token] server page. verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE'). If null, render an Alert with the FR-13 copy 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' Otherwise render <TokenPasswordForm mode='invite' token name={firstName + ' ' + lastName} email invalidMessage={FR-13 copy} />. No sign-up affordance (NFR-14).\",\n      files=[\"src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx\"], dependencies=[\"TASK-2\"], estimateHours=1,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-14\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-5\", description=\"C5 /account/security. \" + GATE + \"page.tsx (server): const user = await requirePageUser(); render a heading plus <ChangePasswordForm email={user.email} />. ChangePasswordForm.tsx ('use client'): RHF + zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email)); three password TextFields (currentPassword, newPassword, confirm) with passwordInputSlot; PasswordChecklist under newPassword; one aria-live='polite' Alert. Submit with postJson('/api/account/password', {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}). On 400, REMAP details.fieldErrors.password -> newPassword (the common-password policy error uses the `password` key, see api-contracts designCorrections) before applyFieldErrors; fieldErrors.currentPassword shows 'Current password is incorrect.' Success: useToast 'Password updated', reset(), router.refresh().\",\n      files=[\"src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx\", \"src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx\"], dependencies=[], estimateHours=2.5,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-10\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\", \"NFR-5\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-9\", \"NFR-11\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-6\", description=\"C6 + C7 shell wiring (one task because the prop type couples both files). \" + GATE + \"layout.tsx: const user = await requirePageUser() (keep the schoolSettings read); pass user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}} to AppShell. shell.tsx: delete PLACEHOLDER_USER; add `user: SessionUser` to AppShellProps (import type from src/server/auth/requireRole); navigationForRole(user.role); UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}; menu header shows full name in Typography plus role Chip; replace the two placeholder MenuItems with 'Account security' (MenuItem component={Link} href='/account/security') and 'Sign out' (signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' }) from next-auth/react, the v5 option; ADR-2's callbackUrl wording is outdated). No SessionProvider or useSession. Done when `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing.\",\n      files=[\"src/app/(app)/layout.tsx\", \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx\"], dependencies=[\"TASK-5\"], estimateHours=2,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-21\", \"FR-23\", \"FR-25\", \"FR-26\", \"FR-27\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-9\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-7\", description=\"C8 integration tests. '// @vitest-environment node' plus describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL), following tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts. Reset the rate limiter in beforeEach and create or clean up its own users. authorize: unknown email, wrong password, DISABLED, archived, locked -> locked:N, 5th failure locks and audits auth.lockout, rate_limited after 10 per IP, success resets failedLoginCount, sets lastLoginAt and audits auth.login.success. acceptInvite: ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt set, token consumed, reuse -> INVALID_TOKEN. requestPasswordReset: known email -> token + EmailOutbox row; unknown -> no token. resetPassword clears lockout fields; token reuse fails. changePassword: wrong current -> fieldErrors.currentPassword; success bumps passwordChangedAt. Assert that no AuditLog metadata contains 'password' or 'token' values. Also confirms FR-6 (R3): loginErrorMessage already handles rate_limited, so build nothing for it.\",\n      files=[\"tests/integration/auth.test.ts\"], dependencies=[], estimateHours=3,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-3\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-8\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-18\", \"FR-19\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-24\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-8\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-8\", description=\"C9 shared e2e sign-in (R1). helpers/auth.ts: export signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!'), moved from the local signIn in notifications.spec.ts (GET /api/auth/csrf -> POST /api/auth/callback/credentials form, then assert that /api/auth/session has the email). notifications.spec.ts: delete the local signIn and call signInAs(page, ADMIN.email, ADMIN.password); keep its own user upsert and cleanup. dashboard.spec.ts: add a beforeEach that calls signInAs(page, 'admin@schoolhub.test'), because the (app) layout now calls requirePageUser (TASK-6).\",\n      files=[\"tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts\", \"tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts\", \"tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts\"], dependencies=[\"TASK-6\"], estimateHours=1,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-11\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-13\"]),\n dict(id=\"TASK-9\", description=\"C9 auth.spec.ts with test.describe.configure({mode:'serial'}). (1) UI sign-in as admin@schoolhub.test / SchoolHub123! lands on /dashboard; the user menu shows 'Alice Admin' and ADMIN; 'Sign out' lands on /login. (2) Wrong password shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' (3) Unauthenticated /dashboard -> /login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard. (4) Forgot -> reset for student2@schoolhub.test: submit /forgot-password, read the newest EmailOutbox row via @prisma/client in the test process (no test-only app route), extract the /reset-password/ link, set a new password, see the /login reset toast, sign in with the new password. Restore the student2 password in afterAll (it is not ADMIN, so parallel specs are not affected). (5) One AxeBuilder scan of /login and /forgot-password: zero serious or critical violations.\",\n      files=[\"tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts\"], dependencies=[\"TASK-1\", \"TASK-3\", \"TASK-6\", \"TASK-8\"], estimateHours=3,\n      requirementIds=[\"FR-2\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-19\", \"FR-26\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-31\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-5\"]),\n]\n\n# --- validation ---\nreq = json.load(open(A + \"intake/requirements.json\"))\nids = {r[\"id\"] for r in req[\"functionalRequirements\"] + req[\"nonFunctionalRequirements\"]}\nbad = [(t[\"id\"], r) for t in tasks for r in t[\"requirementIds\"] if r not in ids]\nassert not bad, bad\norder = [t[\"id\"] for t in tasks]\nfor i, t in enumerate(tasks):  # deps must point to earlier tasks -> DAG\n    assert all(d in order[:i] for d in t[\"dependencies\"]), t[\"id\"]\npaths = [f for t in tasks for f in t[\"files\"]]\nassert len(paths) == len(set(paths)), \"file owned by two tasks\"\nassert MOD <= set(paths)\ncovered = {r for t in tasks for r in t[\"requirementIds\"]}\nreuse_only = sorted(ids - covered)  # satisfied by existing code (system-design §2.1), no task needed\n\nentries = [dict(path=f, taskId=t[\"id\"], operation=\"MODIFY\" if f in MOD else \"CREATE\") for t in tasks for f in t[\"files\"]]\njson.dump(dict(ticketId=\"SH-1\", timestamp=TS, phase=\"dev-planning\", version=\"1.0\", entries=entries),\n          open(A + \"dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json\", \"w\"), indent=2)\n\nplan = dict(\n  ticketId=\"SH-1\", version=\"1.0\", timestamp=TS, phase=\"dev-planning\",\n  sourceDesign=\"artifacts/architect/system-design.md (2026-11-05T17:30Z, C1-C9) + api-contracts.json (17:40Z)\",\n  tasks=tasks,\n  fileStructure={\n    \"src/app/(auth)/\": [\"TokenPasswordForm.tsx\", \"forgot-password/\", \"reset-password/[token]/\", \"invite/[token]/\"],\n    \"src/app/(app)/\": [\"layout.tsx (MOD)\", \"shell.tsx (MOD)\", \"account/security/\"],\n    \"tests/integration/\": [\"auth.test.ts\"],\n    \"tests/e2e/\": [\"helpers/\", \"auth.spec.ts\", \"dashboard.spec.ts (MOD)\", \"notifications.spec.ts (MOD)\"],\n  },\n  totalEstimateHours=sum(t[\"estimateHours\"] for t in tasks),\n  nxpPatterns=[],\n  doNotModify=[\"src/server/**\", \"src/app/api/**\", \"src/middleware.ts\", \"src/app/(auth)/login/**\", \"src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx\",\n               \"src/components/PasswordChecklist/**\", \"src/lib/validators/auth.ts\", \"prisma/**\", \"package.json\", \"package-lock.json\",\n               \"src/server/auth/course-access.ts\", \"src/server/auth/student-access.ts\"],\n  requirementsSatisfiedByExistingCode=reuse_only,\n  designCorrectionsApplied=[\n    \"Token form body uses `confirm`, not `confirmPassword` (TASK-2).\",\n    \"ChangePasswordForm remaps fieldErrors.password -> newPassword (TASK-5).\",\n    \"signOut uses { redirectTo: '/login' } (next-auth v5), per system-design C7 over the ADR-2 wording (TASK-6).\",\n    \"/forgot-password shows an error Alert on 429, 