{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8srSJuakDWLvzrAeQn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the SH-7 dev-planning artifacts to `artifacts/dev-planning/`. The plan has 19 tasks covering 36 files, estimated at 37.5 hours, with status `complete`. The four files that were already there were left over from SH-1 (they didn't match SH-7), so I replaced them.\n\nA script checked the following:\n- Every file and task id in `implementation-plan.json` matches `file-ownership-matrix.json` exactly.\n- Every requirement id exists in `requirements.json`, and every one of the 41 FRs and 10 NFRs is covered by at least one task.\n- No task depends on a later task, so there are no cycles.\n- `implementation-plan.json` was written last.\n\n**How the tasks are ordered:**\n1. **Base (TASK-1 to TASK-6):** schema and migration, validators, notification types, school settings, the pure attendance rules with their unit tests, and the school-wide schedule helper.\n2. **Service and tests (TASK-7, TASK-8):** the attendance service, then its integration tests.\n3. **API routes (TASK-9 to TASK-11):** all 10 routes from the design.\n4. **Screens (TASK-12 to TASK-16):** the register form, the take-attendance pages, the student and course attendance tabs, and the admin page.\n5. **Wiring and data (TASK-17 to TASK-19):** tab and navigation entries, seed data, and the end-to-end test.\n\n**Where the plan differs from the architect's design:**\n- **Folder names in URLs:** the design writes the student and course API folders as `[studentId]` and `[courseId]`, but the existing code names them `[id]`. Next.js doesn't allow two different names at the same folder level, so the plan uses `src/app/api/students/[id]/attendance`, `src/app/api/courses/[id]/attendance` and `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/attendance`. Course pages keep `[courseId]`, which is what the existing code uses there.\n- **Integration test name:** it's `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts`, following the repo's convention, rather than the design's `.int.test.ts`. Both names get picked up by the test runner.\n- **Service file:** `attendance-service.ts` has one owner, TASK-7. That makes it the largest task at 5 hours, but splitting it would give one file two owners in the ownership matrix.\n\n**Still open:**\n- Before writing any screen (TASK-12 to TASK-16), the dev phase must reach the MUI docs server and look up each component. If the server can't be reached, it has to stop and report.\n- The three choices the architect made on intake's defaults still need human sign-off if you want them changed: the admin settings route, the daily register URL, and the settings for the two new notification types."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4608,"cache_read_input_tokens":68175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4608},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3cd4e907-dfed-4f4b-860d-7c1eb7adabfc","uuid":"2604d484-77d9-4d7c-b454-13fa58e6141d","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:39:29.186Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8sqwYSYGb6mGfcC2TM"}
