{"duration_api_ms":177468,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3cd4e907-dfed-4f4b-860d-7c1eb7adabfc","total_cost_usd":1.0352322,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62828,"cache_read_input_tokens":696881,"output_tokens":19656,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3842},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":62828,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":988,"cache_read_input_tokens":68175,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4608,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4608},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":19656,"cacheReadInputTokens":696881,"cacheCreationInputTokens":62828,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0352322,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3842,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":62828,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":16,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the SH-7 dev-planning artifacts to `artifacts/dev-planning/`. The plan has 19 tasks covering 36 files, estimated at 37.5 hours, with status `complete`. The four files that were already there were left over from SH-1 (they didn't match SH-7), so I replaced them.\n\nA script checked the following:\n- Every file and task id in `implementation-plan.json` matches `file-ownership-matrix.json` exactly.\n- Every requirement id exists in `requirements.json`, and every one of the 41 FRs and 10 NFRs is covered by at least one task.\n- No task depends on a later task, so there are no cycles.\n- `implementation-plan.json` was written last.\n\n**How the tasks are ordered:**\n1. **Base (TASK-1 to TASK-6):** schema and migration, validators, notification types, school settings, the pure attendance rules with their unit tests, and the school-wide schedule helper.\n2. **Service and tests (TASK-7, TASK-8):** the attendance service, then its integration tests.\n3. **API routes (TASK-9 to TASK-11):** all 10 routes from the design.\n4. **Screens (TASK-12 to TASK-16):** the register form, the take-attendance pages, the student and course attendance tabs, and the admin page.\n5. **Wiring and data (TASK-17 to TASK-19):** tab and navigation entries, seed data, and the end-to-end test.\n\n**Where the plan differs from the architect's design:**\n- **Folder names in URLs:** the design writes the student and course API folders as `[studentId]` and `[courseId]`, but the existing code names them `[id]`. Next.js doesn't allow two different names at the same folder level, so the plan uses `src/app/api/students/[id]/attendance`, `src/app/api/courses/[id]/attendance` and `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/attendance`. Course pages keep `[courseId]`, which is what the existing code uses there.\n- **Integration test name:** it's `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts`, following the repo's convention, rather than the design's `.int.test.ts`. Both names get picked up by the test runner.\n- **Service file:** `attendance-service.ts` has one owner, TASK-7. That makes it the largest task at 5 hours, but splitting it would give one file two owners in the ownership matrix.\n\n**Still open:**\n- Before writing any screen (TASK-12 to TASK-16), the dev phase must reach the MUI docs server and look up each component. If the server can't be reached, it has to stop and report.\n- The three choices the architect made on intake's defaults still need human sign-off if you want them changed: the admin settings route, the daily register URL, and the settings for the two new notification types.","ttft_ms":3205,"type":"result","duration_ms":181133,"uuid":"7ded85db-ac8b-4cb7-ab88-f76c237b29a8","ttft_stream_ms":2159,"time_to_request_ms":152,"first_content_frame_ms":2160,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":19656,"cacheReadInputTokens":696881,"cacheCreationInputTokens":62828,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0352322,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3842,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":62828,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
