{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011L9G2WL81Rmkvx9CHbDkNQ","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/architect:\ntotal 192\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  7 00:00 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16669 Nov  6 10:35 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1572 Nov  6 10:36 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16145 Nov  6 23:49 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  33679 Nov  7 00:00 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  14349 Nov  6 23:49 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    396 Nov  7 01:31 threat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\ntotal 80\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  6 23:47 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1979 Nov  6 23:47 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  24096 Nov  6 23:47 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    812 Nov  6 23:47 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   4857 Nov  6 23:47 user-stories.md\n==> artifacts/architect/system-design.md <==\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n\n==> artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md <==\n# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict (`moduleResolution: bundler`), Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5 beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers with `AdapterDateFns` already in `src/app/providers.tsx`, x-charts), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1, date-fns/date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `package.json` declares `engines.node >=18.18.0`, and local Node is 24.11.1. Nothing in the requirements calls for a different stack. The ADRs below cover how this feature fits into the existing stack and pin the new dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 limits new dependencies to file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The latest file-type (22.x) declares `engines.node >=22` and 21.x declares `>=20`. Either would break the repo's `>=18.18.0` engine contract. All five packages are ESM-only.\n\n**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n| Package | Version | Why this version |\n|---|---|---|\n| `file-type` | `20.5.0` | Newest line with `engines.node >=18`. Use `fileTypeFromBuffer` (FR-5, FR-6). |\n| `react-markdown` | `10.1.0` | Peer is `react >=18` (FR-31). |\n| `remark-gfm` | `4.0.1` | Supports tables and strikethrough for FR-25 and FR-31. |\n| `rehype-sanitize` | `6.0.0` | Provides NFR-2 sanitisation. |\n| `@dnd-kit/sortable` | `10.0.0` | Peer is `@dnd-kit/core ^6.3.0`, which matches the installed 6.3.1 (FR-23). |\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T18:45:06.101Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"workflow-start\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"pid\": 70760\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3eb9ad0-5f4d-48cd-9610-8332118a48b3","uuid":"c0931771-0f4c-4778-970b-ae33d958bdc4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T20:31:57.255Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"artifacts/architect:\ntotal 192\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  7 00:00 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16669 Nov  6 10:35 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1572 Nov  6 10:36 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16145 Nov  6 23:49 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  33679 Nov  7 00:00 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  14349 Nov  6 23:49 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    396 Nov  7 01:31 threat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\ntotal 80\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  6 23:47 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1979 Nov  6 23:47 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  24096 Nov  6 23:47 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    812 Nov  6 23:47 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   4857 Nov  6 23:47 user-stories.md\n==> artifacts/architect/system-design.md <==\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n\n==> artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md <==\n# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict (`moduleResolution: bundler`), Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5 beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers with `AdapterDateFns` already in `src/app/providers.tsx`, x-charts), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1, date-fns/date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `package.json` declares `engines.node >=18.18.0`, and local Node is 24.11.1. Nothing in the requirements calls for a different stack. The ADRs below cover how this feature fits into the existing stack and pin the new dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 limits new dependencies to file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The latest file-type (22.x) declares `engines.node >=22` and 21.x declares `>=20`. Either would break the repo's `>=18.18.0` engine contract. All five packages are ESM-only.\n\n**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n| Package | Version | Why this version |\n|---|---|---|\n| `file-type` | `20.5.0` | Newest line with `engines.node >=18`. Use `fileTypeFromBuffer` (FR-5, FR-6). |\n| `react-markdown` | `10.1.0` | Peer is `react >=18` (FR-31). |\n| `remark-gfm` | `4.0.1` | Supports tables and strikethrough for FR-25 and FR-31. |\n| `rehype-sanitize` | `6.0.0` | Provides NFR-2 sanitisation. |\n| `@dnd-kit/sortable` | `10.0.0` | Peer is `@dnd-kit/core ^6.3.0`, which matches the installed 6.3.1 (FR-23). |\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T18:45:06.101Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"workflow-start\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"pid\": 70760\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011L9G2WL81Rmkvx9CHbDkNQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
