{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qm78YNyjcXBUb376CGrdsf","type":"tool_result","content":"9:## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n13:**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n28:## ADR-2: Parse multipart uploads with `busboy` (already installed via Next.js), not `request.formData()`\n32:**Decision.** `POST /api/files` (FR-3) runs on the Node runtime (`export const runtime = 'nodejs'`). It pipes `Readable.fromWeb(req.body)` into `busboy({ headers, limits: { files: 1, fileSize: MAX_UPLOAD_MB*1024*1024 } })`. The file stream goes through a `crypto.createHash('sha256')` tap and into `storage.saveFile()` (FR-2), which writes to a temp path under `UPLOAD_DIR` and then `rename`s it to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>` (FR-1). Busboy's `limit` event aborts the upload, deletes the temp file and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'` (FR-4). Type sniffing (ADR-3) runs on the first chunk(s) before the write is committed. The `context` field must come before the file part in the multipart body because the logo rules (FR-40, FR-41) depend on it. FileUpload (FR-13) appends `context` first.\n38:## ADR-3: Validate file types with an extension allowlist plus `file-type` sniffing of the head buffer, using an explicit table\n42:**Decision.** In `src/server/files/validate.ts`, keep one `ALLOWED: Record<ext, { mimes: string[]; sniff: 'required' | 'none' | 'zip-or-ooxml' }>` table:\n53:## ADR-4: Store files on local disk outside `public/`, serve them only through a Node route handler, and set headers per response\n57:**Decision.**\n67:## ADR-5: Allow the video-embed origins in the site CSP via `frame-src`\n71:**Decision.** Add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com;` to the CSP string in `next.config.js`. The URL parser lives in `src/lib/video.ts` as a pure function shared by the Zod validator (FR-16) and the viewer (FR-32). It only emits those two origins.\n77:## ADR-6: Render Markdown with react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize, map every element to MUI, and restrict images to same origin\n81:**Decision.** `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` is a client-safe component (no hooks, so it also renders on the server) with `remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}` and `rehypePlugins={[[rehypeSanitize, schema]]}`. `schema` extends `defaultSchema` and limits `img` `src` to relative paths: `protocols.src: []` plus a check that the value starts with `/`. The default schema already drops `javascript:` hrefs. A `components` map converts h1–h6, p, a, ul/ol/li, table/thead/tbody/tr/th/td, hr, blockquote, code and pre into MUI Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External `a` elements get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The editor Preview tab (FR-25) uses the same component.\n87:## ADR-7: Implement reordering with @dnd-kit/sortable, persist the whole order in one transaction, and provide keyboard IconButtons\n91:**Decision.** Each module's lesson List is a `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`, all inside one `DndContext`, and cross-container moves are handled in `onDragOver`. Up/down `IconButton`s modify the same client order array. The server validates that every submitted module and lesson id belongs to the course and that the set equals the existing set. It then writes `position`/`moduleId` for all rows inside one `prisma.$transaction`. A course has at most about 200 lessons (NFR-4), so updating every row is acceptable.\n97:## ADR-8: Read content with a bounded number of Prisma queries and compute visibility in TypeScript\n101:**Decision.** `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` and the Content tab server component call `content-service.listCourseContent(user, courseId)`. That function makes one `module.findMany` with `include: { lessons: { include: { _count: { select: { attachments: true } } } } }` ordered by position, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany` for the student's lessons in that course when the caller is a STUDENT. That is two queries in total. `isVisible(entity, now)` is a pure function in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` and is unit tested (FR-48). Both module and lesson must be visible. Add an `@@index([courseId, position])` on Module and an `@@index([moduleId, position])` on Lesson.\n107:## ADR-9: Use existing stack pieces for scheduling, timezones, autosave and notifications\n111:**Decision.**\n./.eslintrc.json\n.eslintrc.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T20:31:35.326Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"consideredKeywords\": [\n    \"authentication\",\n    \"authorization\",\n    \"encryption\",\n    \"pii\",\n    \"secrets\",\n    \"input validation\"\n  ],\n  \"missingConsiderations\": [\n    \"authentication\",\n    \"authorization\",\n    \"encryption\",\n    \"pii\",\n    \"secrets\",\n    \"input validation\"\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3eb9ad0-5f4d-48cd-9610-8332118a48b3","uuid":"c0fea8f8-5704-4bfa-8a9a-2f37e5e451e6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T20:49:03.769Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9:## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n13:**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n28:## ADR-2: Parse multipart uploads with `busboy` (already installed via Next.js), not `request.formData()`\n32:**Decision.** `POST /api/files` (FR-3) runs on the Node runtime (`export const runtime = 'nodejs'`). It pipes `Readable.fromWeb(req.body)` into `busboy({ headers, limits: { files: 1, fileSize: MAX_UPLOAD_MB*1024*1024 } })`. The file stream goes through a `crypto.createHash('sha256')` tap and into `storage.saveFile()` (FR-2), which writes to a temp path under `UPLOAD_DIR` and then `rename`s it to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>` (FR-1). Busboy's `limit` event aborts the upload, deletes the temp file and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'` (FR-4). Type sniffing (ADR-3) runs on the first chunk(s) before the write is committed. The `context` field must come before the file part in the multipart body because the logo rules (FR-40, FR-41) depend on it. FileUpload (FR-13) appends `context` first.\n38:## ADR-3: Validate file types with an extension allowlist plus `file-type` sniffing of the head buffer, using an explicit table\n42:**Decision.** In `src/server/files/validate.ts`, keep one `ALLOWED: Record<ext, { mimes: string[]; sniff: 'required' | 'none' | 'zip-or-ooxml' }>` table:\n53:## ADR-4: Store files on local disk outside `public/`, serve them only through a Node route handler, and set headers per response\n57:**Decision.**\n67:## ADR-5: Allow the video-embed origins in the site CSP via `frame-src`\n71:**Decision.** Add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com;` to the CSP string in `next.config.js`. The URL parser lives in `src/lib/video.ts` as a pure function shared by the Zod validator (FR-16) and the viewer (FR-32). It only emits those two origins.\n77:## ADR-6: Render Markdown with react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize, map every element to MUI, and restrict images to same origin\n81:**Decision.** `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` is a client-safe component (no hooks, so it also renders on the server) with `remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}` and `rehypePlugins={[[rehypeSanitize, schema]]}`. `schema` extends `defaultSchema` and limits `img` `src` to relative paths: `protocols.src: []` plus a check that the value starts with `/`. The default schema already drops `javascript:` hrefs. A `components` map converts h1–h6, p, a, ul/ol/li, table/thead/tbody/tr/th/td, hr, blockquote, code and pre into MUI Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External `a` elements get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The editor Preview tab (FR-25) uses the same component.\n87:## ADR-7: Implement reordering with @dnd-kit/sortable, persist the whole order in one transaction, and provide keyboard IconButtons\n91:**Decision.** Each module's lesson List is a `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`, all inside one `DndContext`, and cross-container moves are handled in `onDragOver`. Up/down `IconButton`s modify the same client order array. The server validates that every submitted module and lesson id belongs to the course and that the set equals the existing set. It then writes `position`/`moduleId` for all rows inside one `prisma.$transaction`. A course has at most about 200 lessons (NFR-4), so updating every row is acceptable.\n97:## ADR-8: Read content with a bounded number of Prisma queries and compute visibility in TypeScript\n101:**Decision.** `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` and the Content tab server component call `content-service.listCourseContent(user, courseId)`. That function makes one `module.findMany` with `include: { lessons: { include: { _count: { select: { attachments: true } } } } }` ordered by position, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany` for the student's lessons in that course when the caller is a STUDENT. That is two queries in total. `isVisible(entity, now)` is a pure function in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` and is unit tested (FR-48). Both module and lesson must be visible. Add an `@@index([courseId, position])` on Module and an `@@index([moduleId, position])` on Lesson.\n107:## ADR-9: Use existing stack pieces for scheduling, timezones, autosave and notifications\n111:**Decision.**\n./.eslintrc.json\n.eslintrc.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T20:31:35.326Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"consideredKeywords\": [\n    \"authentication\",\n    \"authorization\",\n    \"encryption\",\n    \"pii\",\n    \"secrets\",\n    \"input validation\"\n  ],\n  \"missingConsiderations\": [\n    \"authentication\",\n    \"authorization\",\n    \"encryption\",\n    \"pii\",\n    \"secrets\",\n    \"input validation\"\n  ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qm78YNyjcXBUb376CGrdsf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
