{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnPE8pyrBLZN79iReoyE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-8 dev-planning phase is finished. All four artifacts in `artifacts/dev-planning/` are written for SH-8 and replace the old SH-7 files. `implementation-plan.json` was written last and has `status: \"complete\"`.\n\nThe plan has 21 tasks that touch 62 files, estimated at 63 hours in total. The generator script checked that:\n- the tasks and the file-ownership matrix list exactly the same file/task pairs;\n- every requirement ID exists in `requirements.json`, and all 48 functional and 12 non-functional requirements are covered by at least one task;\n- task dependencies only point to earlier tasks, so there are no cycles;\n- no file is owned by more than one task.\n\n| Tasks | What gets built |\n|---|---|\n| TASK-1–2 | The five pinned dependencies, env and `.gitignore` setup, the Prisma schema, and the `add_files_and_content` migration |\n| TASK-3–8 | File storage, type validation, the access registry, the file service, orphan purge, and the `/api/files` routes |\n| TASK-9–11 | Content validation, the content service, and 13 content endpoints |\n| TASK-12 | Integration tests |\n| TASK-13–14 | Shared UI: FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, StatusChip, VideoEmbed, and the type-to-confirm option on ConfirmDialog |\n| TASK-15–19 | Content tab, lesson editor, lesson viewer, Learning tab, and the admin logo/settings page |\n| TASK-20–21 | Seed data and the Playwright end-to-end test |\n\nThings to know before the dev phase:\n- **`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json` is out of date.** It still belongs to SH-7, so I took the 15 endpoints from section 2.5 of the system design instead. Response shapes follow the existing `ok()` response conventions, but no exact SH-8 contracts were written. Re-run the architect's API contracts step if you need them.\n- **The settings PATCH change goes beyond the design.** The existing `PATCH /api/settings/school` only accepts the attendance fields, so TASK-19 adds a new `src/lib/validators/settings.ts` to let it also accept `logoFileId`.\n- **The logo only appears where it does today.** Showing the logo in the app shell and on the login page is mentioned in the design's data flow but not in any requirement, so no task does it. Emails are the only place the logo is displayed.\n- **The MUI docs lookup is a hard blocker.** As the design says, the dev agent must look up each MUI component through mui-mcp before writing UI (TASK-13 to TASK-19). If that server is unreachable, dev stops."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":588,"cache_read_input_tokens":70945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":588},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3eb9ad0-5f4d-48cd-9610-8332118a48b3","uuid":"056f23c6-99b4-4a16-b283-bead7c3347f5","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:28:14.238Z","request_id":"req_011CgnPE8d59RzXvoa236N57"}
