{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Rb2TKhntPnGQv6e4MZPHe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n6\t\n7\tNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n12\t\n13\t**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n14\t\n15\t**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n16\t| Need | Use | Req |\n17\t|---|---|---|\n18\t| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n19\t| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n20\t| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n21\t| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n22\t| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n23\t| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n24\t\n25\t**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n30\t\n31\t**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n32\t\n33\t**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n34\t\n35\t**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n40\t\n41\t**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n42\t\n43\t**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n44\t\n45\t**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n50\t\n51\t**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n52\t\n53\t**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n54\t\n55\t**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n60\t\n61\t**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n62\t\n63\t**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n64\t- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n65\t- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n66\t- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n67\t- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n68\t\n69\tUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n70\t\n71\t**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n76\t\n77\t**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n78\t\n79\t**Decision.**\n80\t- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n81\t- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n82\t- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n83\t\n84\t**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n85\t\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n89\t\n90\t**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n91\t\n92\t**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n93\t\n94\t**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n95\t\n96\t---\n97\t\n98\t## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n99\t\n100\t**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n101\t\n102\t**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n103\t\n104\t**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n105\t\n106\t---\n107\t\n108\t## Blockers carried forward\n109\t\n110\t1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n111\t2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n112\t3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n113\t4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f7fec35-982c-43e2-a849-2d541adb85ed","uuid":"d11aa920-b744-4960-9585-1b5c5e059367","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:32:36.204Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n\nNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n\n**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n\n**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n\n**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n\n**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n\n**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n\n**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n\n**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n\n**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n\n**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n\nUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n\n**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n\n**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n\n**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n\n**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n\n---\n\n## Blockers carried forward\n\n1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n","numLines":114,"startLine":1,"totalLines":114}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016Rb2TKhntPnGQv6e4MZPHe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
