{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016CX188ToShrtjzb1ChJSMK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n6\t\n7\tIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`). None of the NFRs pushes toward a different stack. NFR-2 (300 concurrent autosaves, <50 ms) is one indexed upsert per request, well within what Postgres handles. FR-15 calls this \"offline\", but it only means a localStorage retry queue, not offline-first sync. Nothing is realtime: the timer is display-only (FR-16). **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7).**\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n12\t\n13\t**Context.** NFR-7 forbids new dependencies and re-scaffolding. NFR-4 allows only MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X for UI. Every capability PRD-10 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n14\t\n15\t**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n16\t\n17\t| Need | Use | Req |\n18\t|---|---|---|\n19\t| Score maths | `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-3, FR-22, FR-25, NFR-7 |\n20\t| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-2, NFR-6 |\n21\t| Question reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable with MUI list items. Up/Down buttons are the keyboard fallback. | FR-7, NFR-3 |\n22\t| Availability window inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-6 |\n23\t| Score histogram | `@mui/x-charts` `BarChart` (first use in `src/`; look it up via mui-mcp) | FR-26, NFR-4 |\n24\t| Attempts and grading tables | Existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid) | FR-11, FR-24, FR-27 |\n25\t| Markdown prompts and images | Existing `MarkdownEditor`, `MarkdownView`, `FileUpload` | FR-39 |\n26\t| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-27 |\n27\t| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog`, `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-12, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n28\t| Notifications and audit | `notify()` and `audit()` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-38 |\n29\t| Debounce and retry | `setTimeout`/`setInterval` in one small client hook (no lodash) | FR-15 |\n30\t\n31\t**Consequences.** The lockfile doesn't change. Anything dev reaches for outside this table is a scope smell. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banned-library rule still guards NFR-4.\n32\t\n33\t---\n34\t\n35\t## ADR-2: Data model in one Prisma migration, with a partial unique index in raw SQL\n36\t\n37\t**Context.** FR-1 adds 5 enums and 5 models. FR-19 requires at most one IN_PROGRESS attempt per (quiz, student), and `@@unique` can't express that because it is conditional on status. Intake's key-risks list calls out the race. The repo already has a precedent: `20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql` hand-adds `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... WHERE ...`, and `schema.prisma` notes this in a comment.\n38\t\n39\t**Decision.**\n40\t- Create a single migration (`prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then edit it), for example `20261110000000_add_quizzes`. Run it after `20261109000000_add_assignments`.\n41\t- In `schema.prisma`, add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` on QuizAttempt and `@@id([attemptId, questionId])` (or `@@unique`) on QuizAnswer. The QuizAnswer key is what makes the NFR-2 upsert a single statement.\n42\t- In the migration SQL, add `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\" ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';`. Add a schema comment pointing to it, as the attendance comment does.\n43\t- Start-or-resume (FR-19, FR-23, FR-32) runs in a `prisma.$transaction`. On a P2002 unique violation, re-read and return the existing IN_PROGRESS attempt. No advisory locks.\n44\t- Store all points and scores as `Decimal` columns. All timestamps are `timestamptz`/UTC (NFR-6).\n45\t\n46\t**Consequences.** The database enforces race safety, so two tabs both clicking Start get the same attempt. `prisma db push` would drop the partial index, so dev and CI must use `migrate`. That is already the norm.\n47\t\n48\t---\n49\t\n50\t## ADR-3: Grading and deadline logic as pure functions in `src/server/quiz/`\n51\t\n52\t**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests for every grading rule, the deadline maths with accommodations, and the scoring policies. NFR-7 sets the `src/server/<feature>/` layout (PRD-05/09 precedent).\n53\t\n54\t**Decision.** Use plain TypeScript modules with no Prisma imports in the pure files:\n55\t- `grading.ts`: `gradeAnswer(question, response)` for SINGLE/TRUE_FALSE all-or-nothing, MULTIPLE_CHOICE partial credit `points × max(0,(c−i)/totalCorrect)`, SHORT_ANSWER normalise and match (trim, collapse whitespace, optional case folding), and ESSAY returns `needsReview` (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5).\n56\t- `deadline.ts`: `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)` returns min(start + limit + extra, availableUntil). An untimed quiz returns availableUntil (FR-13, FR-28).\n57\t- `scoring.ts`: `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)` for HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE (FR-22).\n58\t- `shuffle.ts`: a deterministic seeded shuffle with a small inline PRNG (mulberry32) seeded from a hash of the attempt id. No dependency (FR-13).\n59\t- `quiz-service.ts` / `attempt-service.ts` do the Prisma I/O and call the pure functions.\n60\t\n61\t**Consequences.** The NFR-8 unit tests run in Vitest with no database. Regrade (FR-10) is just a loop over these functions. The shuffle stays reproducible for the life of an attempt.\n62\t\n63\t---\n64\t\n65\t## ADR-4: The server owns the deadline, and the autosave path stays one query\n66\t\n67\t**Context.** NFR-2 sets the autosave budget at under 50 ms for 300 concurrent students. FR-16 makes the server the authority on the deadline (30 s grace, 409 after it). FR-18 auto-submits lazily on load.\n68\t\n69\t**Decision.**\n70\t- `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` reads only the QuizAttempt row (`studentId`, `status`, `deadlineAt`). It then does one `quizAnswer.upsert` on the composite key. If `now > deadlineAt + 30s`, it auto-submits and throws `AppError('CONFLICT')`; `src/server/http.ts` already maps CONFLICT to 409. It never loads the quiz or the questions on this path.\n71\t- Lazy auto-submit runs in a shared `ensureNotExpired(attempt)` called by GET attempt, the player page and the teacher views. The maintenance run calls `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` (ADR-6).\n72\t- The client timer derives its value from the `deadlineAt` the server returns. It never counts down from local start time.\n73\t- Autosave client: one hook with an 800 ms debounce, a failed-save queue in localStorage keyed by attempt id, and a 5 s retry interval (FR-15). The localStorage pattern already exists in `attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` and `SubmissionPanel.tsx`.\n74\t\n75\t**Consequences.** Clock skew or a tampered client can't extend an attempt. The hot path stays at about 2 queries per save. No WebSockets or SSE are needed.\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive\n80\t\n81\t**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.\n82\t\n83\t**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.\n84\t\n85\t**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.\n86\t\n87\t---\n88\t\n89\t## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner\n90\t\n91\t**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.\n92\t\n93\t**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:\n94\t- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.\n95\t- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.\n96\t\n97\tNo BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.\n98\t\n99\t**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.\n100\t\n101\t---\n102\t\n103\t## ADR-7: UI is MUI-only, and the mui-mcp lookup is a hard gate\n104\t\n105\t**Context.** NFR-4 bans non-MUI UI libraries, allows styling only via theme, `sx` and `styled()`, and requires every component to be looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs). An unreachable MCP is a blocker. NFR-3 requires native radio/checkbox inputs and `aria-live` timer announcements.\n106\t\n107\t**Decision.** Player: `RadioGroup`/`Radio`, `FormGroup`/`Checkbox`, `TextField` (multiline for essays, with a 10,000-character counter), `LinearProgress`, a navigator grid of `Button`s, and a sticky header built with `AppBar position=\"sticky\"` or `Box` + `sx`. Timer: a `Typography` with an `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region that announces only at 5 and 1 minutes and turns `error.main` under 2 minutes (FR-14, NFR-3). Status pill: `Chip`. Builder: `Accordion` or `Card` items in a dnd-kit `SortableContext`. Analytics: x-charts `BarChart` and `DataTable`. Dev must look up each component in mui-mcp before using it. If the MCP is unreachable, dev records a blocker and does not guess.\n108\t\n109\t**Consequences.** QA's banned-import and resolvable-MUI-import checks (NFR-4) pass by construction. Dev's first use of x-charts needs the docs lookup, because `src/` has no existing usage to copy.\n110\t\n111\t---\n112\t\n113\t## ADR-8: Testing uses only the existing toolchain\n114\t\n115\t**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests, integration tests and one Playwright e2e, and `npm run lint && typecheck && test` must stay green.\n116\t\n117\t**Decision.**\n118\t- Unit tests in Vitest: grading.ts, deadline.ts, scoring.ts, shuffle.ts determinism, serializers (absence of the `correct` key) and `resultsVisible`.\n119\t- Integration tests in Vitest against the test database, using the existing harness: autosave returns 409 after deadline + grace, auto-submit on load, regrade, and a concurrent start returning one attempt (ADR-2).\n120\t- One e2e in Playwright: teacher builds a 4-question quiz, student takes it with a mid-attempt `page.reload()`, teacher grades the essay, student sees results.\n121\t\n122\t**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The seed data (FR-36) gives the e2e and manual QA a ready-made state.\n123\t\n124\t---\n125\t\n126\t## Out of scope (NFR-10)\n127\t\n128\tNo lockdown browser, proctoring, question banks or LaTeX, so there is no evaluation of KaTeX/MathJax or media-capture libraries.\n129\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b645f7e9-4c81-4aba-958f-4af4a7329b6d","uuid":"ded3c738-1cd0-4eb3-b2e7-dcc7e011f39e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:10:07.539Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams\n\nTicket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`). None of the NFRs pushes toward a different stack. NFR-2 (300 concurrent autosaves, <50 ms) is one indexed upsert per request, well within what Postgres handles. FR-15 calls this \"offline\", but it only means a localStorage retry queue, not offline-first sync. Nothing is realtime: the timer is display-only (FR-16). **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-7 forbids new dependencies and re-scaffolding. NFR-4 allows only MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X for UI. Every capability PRD-10 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-3, FR-22, FR-25, NFR-7 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-2, NFR-6 |\n| Question reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable with MUI list items. Up/Down buttons are the keyboard fallback. | FR-7, NFR-3 |\n| Availability window inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-6 |\n| Score histogram | `@mui/x-charts` `BarChart` (first use in `src/`; look it up via mui-mcp) | FR-26, NFR-4 |\n| Attempts and grading tables | Existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid) | FR-11, FR-24, FR-27 |\n| Markdown prompts and images | Existing `MarkdownEditor`, `MarkdownView`, `FileUpload` | FR-39 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-27 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog`, `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-12, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` and `audit()` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-38 |\n| Debounce and retry | `setTimeout`/`setInterval` in one small client hook (no lodash) | FR-15 |\n\n**Consequences.** The lockfile doesn't change. Anything dev reaches for outside this table is a scope smell. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banned-library rule still guards NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Data model in one Prisma migration, with a partial unique index in raw SQL\n\n**Context.** FR-1 adds 5 enums and 5 models. FR-19 requires at most one IN_PROGRESS attempt per (quiz, student), and `@@unique` can't express that because it is conditional on status. Intake's key-risks list calls out the race. The repo already has a precedent: `20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql` hand-adds `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... WHERE ...`, and `schema.prisma` notes this in a comment.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Create a single migration (`prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then edit it), for example `20261110000000_add_quizzes`. Run it after `20261109000000_add_assignments`.\n- In `schema.prisma`, add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` on QuizAttempt and `@@id([attemptId, questionId])` (or `@@unique`) on QuizAnswer. The QuizAnswer key is what makes the NFR-2 upsert a single statement.\n- In the migration SQL, add `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\" ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';`. Add a schema comment pointing to it, as the attendance comment does.\n- Start-or-resume (FR-19, FR-23, FR-32) runs in a `prisma.$transaction`. On a P2002 unique violation, re-read and return the existing IN_PROGRESS attempt. No advisory locks.\n- Store all points and scores as `Decimal` columns. All timestamps are `timestamptz`/UTC (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** The database enforces race safety, so two tabs both clicking Start get the same attempt. `prisma db push` would drop the partial index, so dev and CI must use `migrate`. That is already the norm.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Grading and deadline logic as pure functions in `src/server/quiz/`\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests for every grading rule, the deadline maths with accommodations, and the scoring policies. NFR-7 sets the `src/server/<feature>/` layout (PRD-05/09 precedent).\n\n**Decision.** Use plain TypeScript modules with no Prisma imports in the pure files:\n- `grading.ts`: `gradeAnswer(question, response)` for SINGLE/TRUE_FALSE all-or-nothing, MULTIPLE_CHOICE partial credit `points × max(0,(c−i)/totalCorrect)`, SHORT_ANSWER normalise and match (trim, collapse whitespace, optional case folding), and ESSAY returns `needsReview` (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5).\n- `deadline.ts`: `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)` returns min(start + limit + extra, availableUntil). An untimed quiz returns availableUntil (FR-13, FR-28).\n- `scoring.ts`: `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)` for HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE (FR-22).\n- `shuffle.ts`: a deterministic seeded shuffle with a small inline PRNG (mulberry32) seeded from a hash of the attempt id. No dependency (FR-13).\n- `quiz-service.ts` / `attempt-service.ts` do the Prisma I/O and call the pure functions.\n\n**Consequences.** The NFR-8 unit tests run in Vitest with no database. Regrade (FR-10) is just a loop over these functions. The shuffle stays reproducible for the life of an attempt.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: The server owns the deadline, and the autosave path stays one query\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 sets the autosave budget at under 50 ms for 300 concurrent students. FR-16 makes the server the authority on the deadline (30 s grace, 409 after it). FR-18 auto-submits lazily on load.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` reads only the QuizAttempt row (`studentId`, `status`, `deadlineAt`). It then does one `quizAnswer.upsert` on the composite key. If `now > deadlineAt + 30s`, it auto-submits and throws `AppError('CONFLICT')`; `src/server/http.ts` already maps CONFLICT to 409. It never loads the quiz or the questions on this path.\n- Lazy auto-submit runs in a shared `ensureNotExpired(attempt)` called by GET attempt, the player page and the teacher views. The maintenance run calls `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` (ADR-6).\n- The client timer derives its value from the `deadlineAt` the server returns. It never counts down from local start time.\n- Autosave client: one hook with an 800 ms debounce, a failed-save queue in localStorage keyed by attempt id, and a 5 s retry interval (FR-15). The localStorage pattern already exists in `attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` and `SubmissionPanel.tsx`.\n\n**Consequences.** Clock skew or a tampered client can't extend an attempt. The hot path stays at about 2 queries per save. No WebSockets or SSE are needed.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive\n\n**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.\n\n**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner\n\n**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.\n\n**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.\n- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.\n\nNo BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.\n\n**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: UI is MUI-only, and the mui-mcp lookup is a hard gate\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 bans non-MUI UI libraries, allows styling only via theme, `sx` and `styled()`, and requires every component to be looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs). An unreachable MCP is a blocker. NFR-3 requires native radio/checkbox inputs and `aria-live` timer announcements.\n\n**Decision.** Player: `RadioGroup`/`Radio`, `FormGroup`/`Checkbox`, `TextField` (multiline for essays, with a 10,000-character counter), `LinearProgress`, a navigator grid of `Button`s, and a sticky header built with `AppBar position=\"sticky\"` or `Box` + `sx`. Timer: a `Typography` with an `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region that announces only at 5 and 1 minutes and turns `error.main` under 2 minutes (FR-14, NFR-3). Status pill: `Chip`. Builder: `Accordion` or `Card` items in a dnd-kit `SortableContext`. Analytics: x-charts `BarChart` and `DataTable`. Dev must look up each component in mui-mcp before using it. If the MCP is unreachable, dev records a blocker and does not guess.\n\n**Consequences.** QA's banned-import and resolvable-MUI-import checks (NFR-4) pass by construction. Dev's first use of x-charts needs the docs lookup, because `src/` has no existing usage to copy.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Testing uses only the existing toolchain\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests, integration tests and one Playwright e2e, and `npm run lint && typecheck && test` must stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Unit tests in Vitest: grading.ts, deadline.ts, scoring.ts, shuffle.ts determinism, serializers (absence of the `correct` key) and `resultsVisible`.\n- Integration tests in Vitest against the test database, using the existing harness: autosave returns 409 after deadline + grace, auto-submit on load, regrade, and a concurrent start returning one attempt (ADR-2).\n- One e2e in Playwright: teacher builds a 4-question quiz, student takes it with a mid-attempt `page.reload()`, teacher grades the essay, student sees results.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The seed data (FR-36) gives the e2e and manual QA a ready-made state.\n\n---\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-10)\n\nNo lockdown browser, proctoring, question banks or LaTeX, so there is no evaluation of KaTeX/MathJax or media-capture libraries.\n","numLines":129,"startLine":1,"totalLines":129}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016CX188ToShrtjzb1ChJSMK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
