{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Awx9TpwGAE5roqFcn7ugN2","type":"tool_result","content":"   3   \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n   7   \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",\n   7   \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-011 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-11.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Assignment.categoryId, Quiz.categoryId, Course.gradingScaleId and every PRD-11 model (GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride, ReportCard) are missing from prisma/schema.prisma. They need a new migration.\",\n    \"GradeExemption (schema.prisma ~L801) already exists. Its comment says a row is the PRD-11 'exclude from gradebook' flag, so sync maps it to Grade.excused = true.\",\n    \"Submission has finalScore and returnedAt. A submission counts as returned when returnedAt is non-null.\",\n    \"Quiz.isPractice exists. Practice quizzes must never sync.\",\n    \"No function named getStudentQuizScore exists. The closest helpers are src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) and quiz-service scoreOf. The architect should create or name getStudentQuizScore from these instead of duplicating them.\",\n    \"Section.homeroomTeacherId exists. Homeroom access already exists in src/server/auth/student-access.ts and attendance-service.\",\n    \"src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts has Decimal helpers, and src/server/csv.ts has CSV export. Reuse both.\",\n    \"src/config/student-tabs.ts has courses, attendance and assignments. Add grades and report-cards here.\",\n    \"No gradebook:backfill npm script exists yet. Seeding runs through 'db:seed' (tsx prisma/seed.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums GradeItemSource (ASSIGNMENT, QUIZ, MANUAL) and ReportCardStatus (DRAFT, PUBLISHED), plus the models GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride and ReportCard, exactly as specified, in a new prisma migrate migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Course.gradingScaleId (nullable, null = school default scale) and nullable categoryId to Assignment and Quiz. Add a category select to the assignment editor and the quiz editor.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 trailing paragraph\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a GradeItem (source + sourceId, title, maxPoints, dueAt, category). Its term is the one containing dueAt (assignment) or availableUntil (quiz), falling back to the current term.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Unpublishing or archiving the source sets GradeItem.isVisible = false. Deleting the source deletes the GradeItem.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"When a submission is returned, upsert its Grade with score = finalScore. Saving a grade without returning it must not sync.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; AC-3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"A grade exemption (the existing GradeExemption row) sets Grade.excused = true. Removing the exemption clears it.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2 'Exemptions set excused = true'; schema.prisma GradeExemption comment. The PRD does not state the clearing behaviour.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and its results are visible, upsert Grade.score from the student's policy-applied quiz score (getStudentQuizScore), scaled to the quiz maxScore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Add an idempotent one-time backfill script, `npm run gradebook:backfill`. It creates GradeItems and Grades for assignments, quizzes, submissions and attempts that existed before this PRD, and the seed runs it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4; Test Requirements (backfill idempotency)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI and API except for comment. Grades on manual items are fully editable.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5; API PATCH /api/grade-items/:id notes\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Add pure grade-calculation functions in src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts. They consider only visible items in the term whose grade is not excused. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and marked missing (counts as 0). Ungraded items not marked missing are ignored.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Per category, drop the dropLowest lowest item percentages (never dropping every item). categoryPercent = Σscore / Σmax × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; AC-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Course percent is the weighted mean of category percentages, using only categories with at least one counted item and re-normalising weights to those categories. Uncategorised items form an implicit 'Uncategorised' category. A course with no categories uses total points earned / total possible × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Round the percent half-up to 1 decimal place, then pick the first band of the effective scale (course scale, else school default) where percent >= minPercent. Example: 89.95 → 90.0 → A− in the seed scale.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; Test Requirements (89.95 → 90.0)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"TermGradeOverride percent and letter replace the computed values when set. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; AC-6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The calculation must reproduce the worked example: Homework 40% (18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60% (70/100) gives 78.0% C+. The gradebook and the student Grades tab must both show it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6; AC-1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Add an admin page /admin/grading-scales with CRUD for grading scales and a band editor (letter, minimum %, optional GPA, descriptor). Validate that bands are strictly descending, the lowest minimum is 0, letters are unique, and exactly one scale is the default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add course Gradebook settings where the teacher manages categories (name, weight, drop lowest, order). A live sum indicator shows the weight total, and saving is refused unless weights total 100. Settings also include a course grading scale select that defaults to the school default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Gradebook' tab for TEACHER/ADMIN with a term selector and an MUI X DataGrid (MIT). Columns are: students sorted by last name first, then items grouped by category via columnGroupingModel (header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages, then term percent + letter in bold. Use a sticky header (no pinned columns), horizontal scrolling and virtualisation for up to 60 students × 120 items.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Grid cells show the score, 'EX' (excused), 'M' (missing, red) or '—' (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Manual-item cells are editable through processRowUpdate. A user types a number, Enter or arrow keys move between cells, E marks excused, M marks missing and Delete clears. Changes save on blur with an optimistic update and per-cell error state.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; Test Requirements (Playwright keyboard editing)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a synced cell opens its source (the submission grading page or the quiz attempt).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Add manual item' dialog with title, category, max points, date and term (POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.5; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a student row action, 'Override term grade / comment', that opens a dialog with percent, letter and teacher comment (max 1,000 chars) and calls PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.6; FR-1 TermGradeOverride; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Item column menu actions: hide/show the item to students (isVisible), set all ungraded grades to missing (only after the due date), and view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Export CSV' exports the grid as displayed, reusing src/server/csv.ts or papaparse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Grades' in src/config/student-tabs.ts. For the selected term it shows one card per course with percent, letter and colour (≥80 green, 60–79 amber, <60 red). Expanding a card shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Add a /grades page for STUDENT and PARENT (parents get a child selector) that shows the same content as the Grades tab. Add a sidebar nav entry in src/config/navigation.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Platform Context 'A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry'\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course tab 'Grades' for STUDENT/PARENT that shows that course's items only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Add /admin/report-cards: select a term, then see a table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated / Draft / Published) and missing-data warnings (for example ungraded items, or no teacher comment for a course).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"'Generate drafts' (POST /api/report-cards/generate) builds a snapshot for each filtered student. It contains the school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year. For each course it records subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor and teacher comment. It also records the term attendance summary (rate, absences, lates) and the grading scale legend.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Regenerating refreshes the snapshot of DRAFT cards only. PUBLISHED cards are never changed by regeneration or by later grade edits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; AC-8; Test Requirements (snapshot immutability)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a per-card review page with a rendered preview. The homeroom comment is editable by the homeroom teacher or an admin, and the principal comment by an admin only (PATCH /api/report-cards/:id).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a /report-cards page where homeroom teachers list their section's drafts to write comments. Add a nav entry for TEACHER.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; Platform Context nav convention\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Publish (per card or in bulk for the filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED, publishedAt and publishedById, and sends report_card.published to the student and parents. Unpublish is admin only, requires a reason and writes an audit entry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.4; API POST /api/report-cards/publish · /unpublish\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Add a print view /report-cards/[id]/print: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for the principal and homeroom teacher, and @media print rules that hide the app sidebar. A 'Print / Save as PDF' button calls window.print(). Bulk 'Print all' renders the filtered published cards with page breaks.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Report cards' that lists published cards (students/parents) or all cards (admin/teacher). Each card opens the print view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Report card access: ADMIN; the student's teachers; and the student and their parents only when the card is published. Any other student (for example in 7B) gets FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API GET /api/report-cards/:id; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register notification types grade.posted (student + parents when a manual item grade is entered, default email false, one notification per student per item) and report_card.published (default email true) in src/server/notifications/types.ts, sent via notify().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9; FR-8.4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Implement the REST endpoints in the API table with the listed roles. 'manage' and 'view' reuse the existing course-access checks, and GET /api/grading-scales is open to any authenticated user. Handlers are thin: Zod validators in src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts, then services in src/server/gradebook/, then the standard response and error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories replaces the full category list and validates that weights total 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed data: the default scale 'Standard A–F' (A 93, A− 90, B+ 87, B 83, B− 80, C+ 77, C 73, C− 70, D+ 67, D 63, D− 60, F 0, with descriptors); categories Homework 30 / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 (drop lowest 1 homework) for all 7A courses; a manual item 'Oral presentation' in ENG-7A graded for all students; and draft Semester 1 report cards for 7A with teacher comments for MATH and ENG.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"GET /api/students/:id/grades returns only visible items and only synced (returned or results-visible) scores, under the existing student-access rules (own student, linked parent, teacher, admin).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; NFR-4 Privacy; Roles\"}\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Correctness: grade calculation lives in pure functions, all arithmetic uses Decimal (Prisma.Decimal / the existing grading-math helpers), and an exhaustive unit test matrix covers no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides and rounding at band edges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-1; Test Requirements (Unit)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses during report card generation finishes in under 30 s, using batched queries rather than per-student N+1 calls.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Auditability: every manual grade change, term override and report card unpublish writes an AuditLog row via audit(), with old and new values.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-3; FR-8.4; Platform Context audit rule\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Privacy: hidden items, unreturned assignment scores, not-yet-visible quiz results and unpublished report cards never appear in student or parent responses. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-4; FR-2.2; AC-3; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Access control: every handler and server page enforces roles server-side (requireUser/requireRole plus per-entity checks). Teachers see only courses they teach and their homeroom section; parents see only linked students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Code layout & Roles\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/x-scheduler) at the installed 9.5.0. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs and fetchDocs) before use, and only documented props are used. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Recharts, @tanstack/react-table, notistack, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. Toasts use useToast(), confirmations use Dialog and searchable selects use Autocomplete. QA verifies there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1–6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"DataGrid features are limited to the MIT tier: column groups and cell editing are allowed; pinned columns and other Pro/Premium-only features are not.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models, services and helpers (course access, student-access, csv.ts, grading-math, quiz grading, notify, audit, logger, DataTable, useToast). Do not re-scaffold, rename routes or models, or add console.log. New code goes in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC and shown in SchoolSettings.timezone. 'Past due' and term-containment checks use the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Assumptions ('school timezone is the reference for every date rule')\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Print view: each student's card fits on A4 portrait pages without the app chrome.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test pass. Add tests: unit (calculation matrix); integration (assignment-return and quiz-grading sync hooks, backfill idempotency, snapshot immutability); Playwright (teacher keyboard-edits manual grades, admin generates and publishes report cards, parent views a report card).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Constraints; Test Requirements\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope: standards-based grading, GPA/class rank and multi-year transcripts are out of scope. GPA on a band is stored only and never computed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; FR-1 bands gpa?\"}\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-6: When a GradeExemption is removed, should the Grade revert to excused = false and re-sync the score?\",\n        \"FR-7: The PRD names getStudentQuizScore, but that function doesn't exist. Should the gradebook use the quiz's ScoringPolicy (best/latest/average) via applyScoringPolicy?\",\n        \"FR-13: The seed has a separate A− band at 90, so 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A−. Does the test requirement's label 'A' mean the A-band family?\",\n        \"FR-27/FR-33: Should /grades and /report-cards get sidebar nav entries?\",\n        \"NFR-10: Is 'past due' for missing items evaluated against dueAt in UTC or at end of day in the school timezone?\",\n        \"FR-3 term fallback: if dueAt falls outside every term and there is no current term, should the item be skipped or the sync error out?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-6 exemption removal behaviour. Assumption: excused = false and the score re-syncs from source.\",\n        \"FR-7 quiz score source. Assumption: getStudentQuizScore is a new helper built on applyScoringPolicy + resultsVisible.\",\n        \"FR-13 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A− under the seed scale. Assumption: the test asserts 90.0 rounding and the letter of the 90 band (A−).\",\n        \"FR-27/FR-33 nav entries. Assumption: add them per the platform convention.\",\n        \"NFR-10 'past due' = now > dueAt (exact instant).\",\n        \"FR-3 no-term fallback. Assumption: skip creating the item and log a warning.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T17:45:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 20,\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"20 endpoint entries across 15 route files, matching system-design §2.3 and the PRD API table. POST /api/grade-items/:id/mark-missing is the only route not in the PRD (FR-24 bulk action).\",\n    \"Base path is /api (existing convention), not /api/v1. Envelopes and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. No endpoint is paginated.\",\n    \"Decimals: input number|string ≤ 2 dp (validators/assignments.ts `decimal` pattern). Output: points and weights are fixed2 strings; computed percents are 1 dp strings or null.\",\n    \"Shared shapes live in api-contracts.json `components` (StudentTermResult, ReportCardSnapshotV1, Bands, …). validators/gradebook.ts and snapshot.ts should mirror them.\",\n    \"Contract decisions beyond system-design: PUT grade and PUT term-override return the recomputed StudentTermResult. PATCH scale isDefault:false on the current default is a VALIDATION_ERROR. The first scale created always becomes the default. mark-missing works on any source but only touches score-null rows. Report-card comments are max 1,000 chars. Unpublish reason is 1–500 chars. GET /api/report-cards mode A includes NOT_GENERATED rows.\",\n    \"No HTTP surface (by design) for FR-1, FR-3–FR-7, FR-41 (migration, sync hooks, seed), NFR-7/NFR-9/NFR-12 (UI, reuse and test rules). These are covered in system-design §2.1, §2.2, §2.5 and §6. Print pages call services directly (nonHttpContracts).\",\n    \"Stale leftovers from SH-10: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/*, artifacts/qa/* and artifacts/ui-verification/* must be regenerated for SH-11, not reused.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"devGates\": [\n    \"NFR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component, especially the DataGrid keyboard editing for FR-20. If it's unreachable, stop and report. This does not block dev-planning.\",\n    \"FR-1/ADR-3: the partial unique index grading_scale_one_default is raw SQL in the migration. Use prisma migrate, never db push.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"055adbad-09fd-4ef0-894f-863fb13f0fba","uuid":"1ba3c397-1073-4c1c-b3c6-367a84613a68","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:12:26.189Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"   3   \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n   7   \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",\n   7   \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-011 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-11.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Assignment.categoryId, Quiz.categoryId, Course.gradingScaleId and every PRD-11 model (GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride, ReportCard) are missing from prisma/schema.prisma. They need a new migration.\",\n    \"GradeExemption (schema.prisma ~L801) already exists. Its comment says a row is the PRD-11 'exclude from gradebook' flag, so sync maps it to Grade.excused = true.\",\n    \"Submission has finalScore and returnedAt. A submission counts as returned when returnedAt is non-null.\",\n    \"Quiz.isPractice exists. Practice quizzes must never sync.\",\n    \"No function named getStudentQuizScore exists. The closest helpers are src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) and quiz-service scoreOf. The architect should create or name getStudentQuizScore from these instead of duplicating them.\",\n    \"Section.homeroomTeacherId exists. Homeroom access already exists in src/server/auth/student-access.ts and attendance-service.\",\n    \"src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts has Decimal helpers, and src/server/csv.ts has CSV export. Reuse both.\",\n    \"src/config/student-tabs.ts has courses, attendance and assignments. Add grades and report-cards here.\",\n    \"No gradebook:backfill npm script exists yet. Seeding runs through 'db:seed' (tsx prisma/seed.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums GradeItemSource (ASSIGNMENT, QUIZ, MANUAL) and ReportCardStatus (DRAFT, PUBLISHED), plus the models GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride and ReportCard, exactly as specified, in a new prisma migrate migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Course.gradingScaleId (nullable, null = school default scale) and nullable categoryId to Assignment and Quiz. Add a category select to the assignment editor and the quiz editor.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 trailing paragraph\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a GradeItem (source + sourceId, title, maxPoints, dueAt, category). Its term is the one containing dueAt (assignment) or availableUntil (quiz), falling back to the current term.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Unpublishing or archiving the source sets GradeItem.isVisible = false. Deleting the source deletes the GradeItem.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"When a submission is returned, upsert its Grade with score = finalScore. Saving a grade without returning it must not sync.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; AC-3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"A grade exemption (the existing GradeExemption row) sets Grade.excused = true. Removing the exemption clears it.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2 'Exemptions set excused = true'; schema.prisma GradeExemption comment. The PRD does not state the clearing behaviour.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and its results are visible, upsert Grade.score from the student's policy-applied quiz score (getStudentQuizScore), scaled to the quiz maxScore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Add an idempotent one-time backfill script, `npm run gradebook:backfill`. It creates GradeItems and Grades for assignments, quizzes, submissions and attempts that existed before this PRD, and the seed runs it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4; Test Requirements (backfill idempotency)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI and API except for comment. Grades on manual items are fully editable.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5; API PATCH /api/grade-items/:id notes\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Add pure grade-calculation functions in src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts. They consider only visible items in the term whose grade is not excused. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and marked missing (counts as 0). Ungraded items not marked missing are ignored.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Per category, drop the dropLowest lowest item percentages (never dropping every item). categoryPercent = Σscore / Σmax × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; AC-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Course percent is the weighted mean of category percentages, using only categories with at least one counted item and re-normalising weights to those categories. Uncategorised items form an implicit 'Uncategorised' category. A course with no categories uses total points earned / total possible × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Round the percent half-up to 1 decimal place, then pick the first band of the effective scale (course scale, else school default) where percent >= minPercent. Example: 89.95 → 90.0 → A− in the seed scale.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; Test Requirements (89.95 → 90.0)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"TermGradeOverride percent and letter replace the computed values when set. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; AC-6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The calculation must reproduce the worked example: Homework 40% (18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60% (70/100) gives 78.0% C+. The gradebook and the student Grades tab must both show it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6; AC-1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Add an admin page /admin/grading-scales with CRUD for grading scales and a band editor (letter, minimum %, optional GPA, descriptor). Validate that bands are strictly descending, the lowest minimum is 0, letters are unique, and exactly one scale is the default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add course Gradebook settings where the teacher manages categories (name, weight, drop lowest, order). A live sum indicator shows the weight total, and saving is refused unless weights total 100. Settings also include a course grading scale select that defaults to the school default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Gradebook' tab for TEACHER/ADMIN with a term selector and an MUI X DataGrid (MIT). Columns are: students sorted by last name first, then items grouped by category via columnGroupingModel (header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages, then term percent + letter in bold. Use a sticky header (no pinned columns), horizontal scrolling and virtualisation for up to 60 students × 120 items.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Grid cells show the score, 'EX' (excused), 'M' (missing, red) or '—' (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Manual-item cells are editable through processRowUpdate. A user types a number, Enter or arrow keys move between cells, E marks excused, M marks missing and Delete clears. Changes save on blur with an optimistic update and per-cell error state.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; Test Requirements (Playwright keyboard editing)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a synced cell opens its source (the submission grading page or the quiz attempt).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Add manual item' dialog with title, category, max points, date and term (POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.5; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a student row action, 'Override term grade / comment', that opens a dialog with percent, letter and teacher comment (max 1,000 chars) and calls PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.6; FR-1 TermGradeOverride; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Item column menu actions: hide/show the item to students (isVisible), set all ungraded grades to missing (only after the due date), and view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Export CSV' exports the grid as displayed, reusing src/server/csv.ts or papaparse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Grades' in src/config/student-tabs.ts. For the selected term it shows one card per course with percent, letter and colour (≥80 green, 60–79 amber, <60 red). Expanding a card shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Add a /grades page for STUDENT and PARENT (parents get a child selector) that shows the same content as the Grades tab. Add a sidebar nav entry in src/config/navigation.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Platform Context 'A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry'\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course tab 'Grades' for STUDENT/PARENT that shows that course's items only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Add /admin/report-cards: select a term, then see a table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated / Draft / Published) and missing-data warnings (for example ungraded items, or no teacher comment for a course).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"'Generate drafts' (POST /api/report-cards/generate) builds a snapshot for each filtered student. It contains the school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year. For each course it records subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor and teacher comment. It also records the term attendance summary (rate, absences, lates) and the grading scale legend.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Regenerating refreshes the snapshot of DRAFT cards only. PUBLISHED cards are never changed by regeneration or by later grade edits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; AC-8; Test Requirements (snapshot immutability)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a per-card review page with a rendered preview. The homeroom comment is editable by the homeroom teacher or an admin, and the principal comment by an admin only (PATCH /api/report-cards/:id).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a /report-cards page where homeroom teachers list their section's drafts to write comments. Add a nav entry for TEACHER.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; Platform Context nav convention\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Publish (per card or in bulk for the filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED, publishedAt and publishedById, and sends report_card.published to the student and parents. Unpublish is admin only, requires a reason and writes an audit entry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.4; API POST /api/report-cards/publish · /unpublish\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Add a print view /report-cards/[id]/print: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for the principal and homeroom teacher, and @media print rules that hide the app sidebar. A 'Print / Save as PDF' button calls window.print(). Bulk 'Print all' renders the filtered published cards with page breaks.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Report cards' that lists published cards (students/parents) or all cards (admin/teacher). Each card opens the print view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Report card access: ADMIN; the student's teachers; and the student and their parents only when the card is published. Any other student (for example in 7B) gets FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API GET /api/report-cards/:id; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register notification types grade.posted (student + parents when a manual item grade is entered, default email false, one notification per student per item) and report_card.published (default email true) in src/server/notifications/types.ts, sent via notify().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9; FR-8.4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Implement the REST endpoints in the API table with the listed roles. 'manage' and 'view' reuse the existing course-access checks, and GET /api/grading-scales is open to any authenticated user. Handlers are thin: Zod validators in src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts, then services in src/server/gradebook/, then the standard response and error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories replaces the full category list and validates that weights total 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed data: the default scale 'Standard A–F' (A 93, A− 90, B+ 87, B 83, B− 80, C+ 77, C 73, C− 70, D+ 67, D 63, D− 60, F 0, with descriptors); categories Homework 30 / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 (drop lowest 1 homework) for all 7A courses; a manual item 'Oral presentation' in ENG-7A graded for all students; and draft Semester 1 report cards for 7A with teacher comments for MATH and ENG.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"GET /api/students/:id/grades returns only visible items and only synced (returned or results-visible) scores, under the existing student-access rules (own student, linked parent, teacher, admin).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; NFR-4 Privacy; Roles\"}\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Correctness: grade calculation lives in pure functions, all arithmetic uses Decimal (Prisma.Decimal / the existing grading-math helpers), and an exhaustive unit test matrix covers no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides and rounding at band edges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-1; Test Requirements (Unit)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses during report card generation finishes in under 30 s, using batched queries rather than per-student N+1 calls.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Auditability: every manual grade change, term override and report card unpublish writes an AuditLog row via audit(), with old and new values.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-3; FR-8.4; Platform Context audit rule\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Privacy: hidden items, unreturned assignment scores, not-yet-visible quiz results and unpublished report cards never appear in student or parent responses. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-4; FR-2.2; AC-3; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Access control: every handler and server page enforces roles server-side (requireUser/requireRole plus per-entity checks). Teachers see only courses they teach and their homeroom section; parents see only linked students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Code layout & Roles\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/x-scheduler) at the installed 9.5.0. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs and fetchDocs) before use, and only documented props are used. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Recharts, @tanstack/react-table, notistack, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. Toasts use useToast(), confirmations use Dialog and searchable selects use Autocomplete. QA verifies there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1–6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"DataGrid features are limited to the MIT tier: column groups and cell editing are allowed; pinned columns and other Pro/Premium-only features are not.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models, services and helpers (course access, student-access, csv.ts, grading-math, quiz grading, notify, audit, logger, DataTable, useToast). Do not re-scaffold, rename routes or models, or add console.log. New code goes in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC and shown in SchoolSettings.timezone. 'Past due' and term-containment checks use the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Assumptions ('school timezone is the reference for every date rule')\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Print view: each student's card fits on A4 portrait pages without the app chrome.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test pass. Add tests: unit (calculation matrix); integration (assignment-return and quiz-grading sync hooks, backfill idempotency, snapshot immutability); Playwright (teacher keyboard-edits manual grades, admin generates and publishes report cards, parent views a report card).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Constraints; Test Requirements\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope: standards-based grading, GPA/class rank and multi-year transcripts are out of scope. GPA on a band is stored only and never computed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; FR-1 bands gpa?\"}\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-6: When a GradeExemption is removed, should the Grade revert to excused = false and re-sync the score?\",\n        \"FR-7: The PRD names getStudentQuizScore, but that function doesn't exist. Should the gradebook use the quiz's ScoringPolicy (best/latest/average) via applyScoringPolicy?\",\n        \"FR-13: The seed has a separate A− band at 90, so 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A−. Does the test requirement's label 'A' mean the A-band family?\",\n        \"FR-27/FR-33: Should /grades and /report-cards get sidebar nav entries?\",\n        \"NFR-10: Is 'past due' for missing items evaluated against dueAt in UTC or at end of day in the school timezone?\",\n        \"FR-3 term fallback: if dueAt falls outside every term and there is no current term, should the item be skipped or the sync error out?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-6 exemption removal behaviour. Assumption: excused = false and the score re-syncs from source.\",\n        \"FR-7 quiz score source. Assumption: getStudentQuizScore is a new helper built on applyScoringPolicy + resultsVisible.\",\n        \"FR-13 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A− under the seed scale. Assumption: the test asserts 90.0 rounding and the letter of the 90 band (A−).\",\n        \"FR-27/FR-33 nav entries. Assumption: add them per the platform convention.\",\n        \"NFR-10 'past due' = now > dueAt (exact instant).\",\n        \"FR-3 no-term fallback. Assumption: skip creating the item and log a warning.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T17:45:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 20,\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"20 endpoint entries across 15 route files, matching system-design §2.3 and the PRD API table. POST /api/grade-items/:id/mark-missing is the only route not in the PRD (FR-24 bulk action).\",\n    \"Base path is /api (existing convention), not /api/v1. Envelopes and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. No endpoint is paginated.\",\n    \"Decimals: input number|string ≤ 2 dp (validators/assignments.ts `decimal` pattern). Output: points and weights are fixed2 strings; computed percents are 1 dp strings or null.\",\n    \"Shared shapes live in api-contracts.json `components` (StudentTermResult, ReportCardSnapshotV1, Bands, …). validators/gradebook.ts and snapshot.ts should mirror them.\",\n    \"Contract decisions beyond system-design: PUT grade and PUT term-override return the recomputed StudentTermResult. PATCH scale isDefault:false on the current default is a VALIDATION_ERROR. The first scale created always becomes the default. mark-missing works on any source but only touches score-null rows. Report-card comments are max 1,000 chars. Unpublish reason is 1–500 chars. GET /api/report-cards mode A includes NOT_GENERATED rows.\",\n    \"No HTTP surface (by design) for FR-1, FR-3–FR-7, FR-41 (migration, sync hooks, seed), NFR-7/NFR-9/NFR-12 (UI, reuse and test rules). These are covered in system-design §2.1, §2.2, §2.5 and §6. Print pages call services directly (nonHttpContracts).\",\n    \"Stale leftovers from SH-10: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/*, artifacts/qa/* and artifacts/ui-verification/* must be regenerated for SH-11, not reused.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"devGates\": [\n    \"NFR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component, especially the DataGrid keyboard editing for FR-20. If it's unreachable, stop and report. This does not block dev-planning.\",\n    \"FR-1/ADR-3: the partial unique index grading_scale_one_default is raw SQL in the migration. Use prisma migrate, never db push.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Awx9TpwGAE5roqFcn7ugN2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsLHLHororapHY3eqJkd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HBzMUrAT49g29JSmVxpWL9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9246,"cache_read_input_tokens":27760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9246},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"055adbad-09fd-4ef0-894f-863fb13f0fba","uuid":"d7d19303-a463-4b5a-a1ae-5e4b5762efd8","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:12:27.597Z","request_id":"req_011CgsLHL3gEhJYDa3Wzprxn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HBzMUrAT49g29JSmVxpWL9":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HBzMUrAT49g29JSmVxpWL9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n2\t\n3\tTicket: **SH-11** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T17:30:00Z · Status: **complete**\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (42 FR + 13 NFR), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-10), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B19, R1–R7), and the source PRD `11-gradebook.md`.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Overview\n10\t\n11\tPRD-11 adds a gradebook to SchoolHub, a brownfield Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/PostgreSQL + MUI 9.5.0 app. It has four parts:\n12\t\n13\t1. **Sync.** Published assignments and quizzes become `GradeItem`s. Returned submissions and released quiz results become `Grade`s.\n14\t2. **Calculation.** A pure Decimal function turns items, grades, categories, a scale and an override into a term percent and letter.\n15\t3. **Views.** A teacher grid (MIT DataGrid), student/parent grade views, and admin pages for scales and categories.\n16\t4. **Report cards.** Frozen JSON snapshots per student and term, with a draft → published workflow, notifications and an A4 print view.\n17\t\n18\tThe design adds **no dependencies** (ADR-1). New server code lives only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/` (NFR-9). Existing services gain one-line calls into the sync module.\n19\t\n20\t### 1.1 Intake blockers\n21\t\n22\t`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. There is nothing to escalate. The flagged assumptions are resolved in §1.2.\n23\t\n24\t### 1.2 Assumptions and design decisions (need product sign-off, none block dev)\n25\t\n26\t| # | Topic | Decision | Req |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| A1 | Exemption removal | Unexempt sets `excused = false` and re-derives `score` from the source: `finalScore` if the submission is RETURNED, otherwise `null`. | FR-6 |\n29\t| A2 | Quiz score source | **Intake's correction:** `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` **already exists** in `src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts` (L359, labelled \"PRD-11 export\"). Call it as is. It does **not** check visibility, so the sync gates on `resultsVisible()` first. This replaces ADR-6's \"add a helper to grading.ts\". Don't create a second one. | FR-7, NFR-9 |\n30\t| A3 | 89.95 rounding | 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale (A is 93). The unit test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter. | FR-13 |\n31\t| A4 | Nav entries | Add `/grades` (STUDENT, PARENT), `/report-cards` (TEACHER), and `/admin/grading-scales` and `/admin/report-cards` (ADMIN, group `Administration`). | FR-16, FR-27, FR-29, FR-33 |\n32\t| A5 | Past due | `now > dueAt` as a UTC instant. Term containment compares school-local dates (`SchoolSettings.timezone`). | NFR-10 |\n33\t| A6 | No term | If no term of the course's academic year contains the date and no term contains today, skip the item and `logger.warn`. | FR-3 |\n34\t| A7 | Teacher hide vs source visibility (R2) | **No extra column** (FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\"). Source sync writes `isVisible` only on source visibility **transitions**: publish / publishOnce → `true`, archive → `false`. Plain edits to an already-published source never touch `isVisible`, so a teacher's hide survives re-saves. | FR-4, FR-24 |\n35\t| A8 | Uncategorised weight (R3) | If the course has categories, the implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket is **shown with its subtotal but has weight 0**, so it's excluded from the weighted mean. If no category has a counted item, fall back to the points total over **all** counted items. If the course has no categories, use the points total. | FR-12 |\n36\t| A9 | `grade.posted` dedupe (R4) | No marker column. Notify only when a MANUAL grade's `score` goes from `null` to a value. That gives one notification per student per item. Later edits are audited but not notified. | FR-38 |\n37\t| A10 | Term drift (R5) | Re-derive `GradeItem.termId` only when `dueAt`/`availableUntil` changes. | FR-3 |\n38\t| A11 | Scale delete (R6) | Return `CONFLICT` if the scale is the default or any `Course.gradingScaleId` references it. Published snapshots embed their own legend, so they're unaffected. | FR-16 |\n39\t| A12 | Percent-only override | Re-derive the letter from the effective scale using the override percent. | FR-14 |\n40\t| A13 | Report card edits | Comments are editable only while `DRAFT`. Unpublish returns the card to `DRAFT` and clears `publishedAt`/`publishedById`. | FR-32, FR-34 |\n41\t| A14 | `Grade.updatedById` on system writes | Sync uses the acting user (grader/teacher) when there is one. Otherwise (auto-graded quiz, maintenance release, backfill) it uses `quiz.createdById`, `assignment.createdById` or, for backfill, `course.teacherId`. The column has no FK, as specified. | FR-1, FR-5, FR-7, FR-8 |\n42\t| A15 | Quiz CLOSED | A CLOSED quiz is **not** unpublished. Its item stays visible. Quizzes have no archive. `deleteQuiz` deletes the item. A practice toggle after publish deletes the item. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n43\t\n44\t---\n45\t\n46\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n47\t\n48\t### 2.1 Data model (one migration: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_gradebook/`)\n49\t\n50\tThe models and enums are **exactly the PRD FR-1 block** (FR-1). On top of that:\n51\t\n52\t- **Additive columns (FR-2):** `Course.gradingScaleId String?` → `GradingScale` (`onDelete: SetNull`). `Assignment.categoryId String?` and `Quiz.categoryId String?` → `GradeCategory` (`onDelete: SetNull`), so deleting a category never deletes sources.\n53\t- **Relation fields:** add only the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.gradeItems`, `Course.gradeCategories`, `Term.gradeItems`, `GradeCategory.items/assignments/quizzes`). There are no new scalar columns beyond the spec.\n54\t- **Keys already in the spec make sync race-safe (B19):** `GradeItem.sourceId @unique`, `Grade @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])`, `TermGradeOverride @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])`, `ReportCard @@unique([studentId, termId])`.\n55\t- **Indexes added:**\n56\t  - `GradeItem @@index([courseId, termId])` (NFR-2, NFR-3)\n57\t  - `TermGradeOverride @@index([termId])` (NFR-3)\n58\t  - `ReportCard @@index([termId, status])` (FR-29)\n59\t- **Raw SQL in the migration:** a partial unique index `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX grading_scale_one_default ON \"GradingScale\" (\"isDefault\") WHERE \"isDefault\";` as the backstop for \"exactly one default\" (FR-16, ADR-3).\n60\t- **Types:** `bands Json` holds `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }[]`, sorted descending and validated by Zod (`bandsSchema`). `gpa` is stored and never computed (NFR-13).\n61\t\n62\t### 2.2 Server modules\n63\t\n64\t| Module | Responsibility | Reuses | Req |\n65\t|---|---|---|---|\n66\t| `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` | **Pure** functions with no Prisma client import (types only): `computeStudentTerm(input)`, `categoryPercent`, `applyDropLowest`, `roundHalfUp1`, `letterFor(percent, bands)`, `applyOverride`, `effectiveScale(course, default)`, `gradeColour(percent)`. Everything is `Decimal`, and rounding happens once at the end. | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `assignments/grading-math.ts` | FR-10–FR-15, FR-26, NFR-1 |\n67\t| `src/server/gradebook/term-placement.ts` | Pure `termFor(date, terms, tz, now)`: picks the containing term in school-local dates, falls back to the term containing today, else returns `null`. | `schoolToday` (attendance-rules), `getSchoolTimezone` | FR-3, NFR-10, A6 |\n68\t| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts` (file name from the PRD) | Idempotent upserts. `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`, `upsertItemFromQuiz(tx, id)`, `hideItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `deleteItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `syncSubmissionGrade(tx, assignmentId, studentId, actorId?)`, `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, `syncQuizGrades(quizId)`. It also exports **pure row builders** (`itemFromAssignment`, `gradeFromSubmission`, `gradeFromQuizScore`) that the backfill shares. | `isAssignmentVisible`, `getStudentQuizScore`, `resultsVisible`, `applyScoringPolicy`, `logger` | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-5 |\n69\t| `src/server/gradebook/backfill.ts` | `backfillGradebook()`. Batch-loads per course and runs the same row builders with `upsert`. Idempotent through the unique keys. | `applyScoringPolicy` in memory (no per-student `getStudentQuizScore`) | FR-8, NFR-3 |\n70\t| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-service.ts` | `getGradebook(user, courseId, termId)`, `createManualItem`, `updateItem`, `deleteItem`, `putGrade`, `markAllMissing`, `putTermOverride`, `exportGradebookCsv`. Loads the data, calls grade-calc, enforces FR-9 and writes audit entries. | `assertCanManageCourse`, `audit`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `toCsv` | FR-9, FR-18–FR-25, FR-38, NFR-2, NFR-4 |\n71\t| `src/server/gradebook/categories-service.ts` | `getCategories`, `replaceCategories` (in a transaction: delete removed ids, upsert the rest, `dec(sum).eq(100)`), and `setCourseScale`. | `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` | FR-17, FR-40 |\n72\t| `src/server/gradebook/scales-service.ts` | CRUD. `setDefault` runs in a transaction that clears the other defaults. Delete is guarded (A11). | `requireRole('ADMIN')`, `audit` | FR-16 |\n73\t| `src/server/gradebook/student-grades-service.ts` | `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId, courseId?)`. Uses the visible-only serializer. Reuses grade-calc and passes **visible items only** into it, so the computed totals match what the student sees. | `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42, NFR-5 |\n74\t| `src/server/gradebook/load.ts` | Shared batched loader: `loadCourseTermData(courseIds[], termId, studentIds?)` returns `{items, grades, categories, overrides, scales}` in 5 `findMany` calls with `in` filters, grouped in memory. Used by the gradebook, student grades and report-card generation. | Prisma | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n75\t| `src/server/report-cards/snapshot.ts` | Zod `snapshotSchema` (`v: 1`) and the pure `buildSnapshot(student, courses, computed, attendance, school, scale)`. | grade-calc | FR-30 |\n76\t| `src/server/report-cards/report-card-service.ts` | `listReportCards` (with warnings), `generateDrafts`, `getReportCard`, `patchComments`, `publish`, `unpublish`, `listForStudent`. | `load.ts`, attendance `getReport`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `audit` | FR-29–FR-34, FR-36, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n77\t| `src/server/report-cards/access.ts` | `assertCanViewReportCard(user, card)`, `canEditHomeroomComment`. | `student-access`, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `Enrollment` | FR-32, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n78\t| `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts` | Zod: `bandsSchema`, `scaleSchema`, `categoriesPutSchema`, `manualItemSchema`, `itemPatchSchema`, `gradePutSchema`, `termOverrideSchema` (comment ≤ 1000), `reportCardPatchSchema`, `generateSchema`, `publishSchema`, `unpublishSchema` (reason required). These are shared by client forms and handlers. | Zod | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23, FR-39, FR-40 |\n79\t| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (edit) | Register `grade.posted` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: false`) and `report_card.published` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: true`). | existing registry | FR-38 |\n80\t\n81\t**Hook edits to existing services** (each is one call; behaviour is otherwise unchanged, per NFR-9):\n82\t\n83\t| Existing site | Added call | Req |\n84\t|---|---|---|\n85\t| `assignments-service` `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` / `publishOnce` | `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`. This sets `isVisible` only on a visibility transition (A7). It re-places the term only if `dueAt` changed (A10). | FR-3, FR-4 |\n86\t| `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | archive → `hideItemForSource`; hard delete → `deleteItemForSource` in the same transaction (B9) | FR-4 |\n87\t| `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline` | `syncSubmissionGrade` when the submission **is** RETURNED after the write. This covers re-grades of returned work. Nothing happens otherwise (AC-3). | FR-5, NFR-5 |\n88\t| `setExemption` (both branches) | `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) | FR-6 |\n89\t| `quiz-service` `updateQuiz` (→PUBLISHED, or edits to a published quiz) / `deleteQuiz` | `upsertItemFromQuiz` / `deleteItemForSource`. Practice quizzes are skipped; turning practice on deletes the item. Wrap `deleteQuiz` in a transaction. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n90\t| After callers of `recomputeAttempt` commit (`submitAttempt`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `regradeQuiz`) | `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`: no-op unless GRADED, `resultsVisible` and not practice | FR-7 |\n91\t| `releaseResults` (MANUAL) and `quiz/maintenance.ts` AFTER_CLOSE claim (`count === 1`) | `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` (bulk). Without this, delayed-visibility quizzes never sync (R1). | FR-7, NFR-5 |\n92\t| Assignment and quiz Zod validators and editors | Optional nullable `categoryId` plus one MUI `Select` of the course's categories | FR-2 |\n93\t\n94\t### 2.3 API layer (`src/app/api/**/route.ts`, thin: `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok()`)\n95\t\n96\tThese match the PRD API table exactly. `api-contracts.json` (next sub-task) owns the shapes.\n97\t\n98\t| Route | Role check | Service | Req |\n99\t|---|---|---|---|\n100\t| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/[id]` | GET: `requireUser`; writes: ADMIN | scales-service | FR-16, FR-39 |\n101\t| `GET/PUT /api/courses/[id]/grade-categories` | view / manage | categories-service (PUT body also carries `gradingScaleId`) | FR-17, FR-40 |\n102\t| `GET /api/courses/[id]/gradebook?termId=` (`&format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | gradebook-service | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, FR-25, NFR-2 |\n103\t| `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items` | manage | createManualItem | FR-22 |\n104\t| `PATCH/DELETE /api/grade-items/[id]` | manage (via the item's course) | updateItem / deleteItem. Non-MANUAL items accept only `isVisible`, and DELETE is MANUAL only. | FR-9, FR-24 |\n105\t| `POST /api/grade-items/[id]/mark-missing` | manage | markAllMissing (`now > dueAt`, ungraded rows only) | FR-24 |\n106\t| `PUT /api/grade-items/[id]/grades/[studentId]` | manage + enrolled student | putGrade. Non-MANUAL items accept only `comment` (FR-9). | FR-9, FR-20, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n107\t| `PUT /api/courses/[id]/term-overrides/[studentId]` | manage | putTermOverride | FR-14, FR-23, NFR-4 |\n108\t| `GET /api/students/[id]/grades?termId=&courseId=` | `assertCanViewStudent` | student-grades-service | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42 |\n109\t| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=&studentId=` | ADMIN; homeroom TEACHER (own sections); with `studentId`, view-student rules plus PUBLISHED-only for student/parent | listReportCards / listForStudent | FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n110\t| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | generateDrafts | FR-30, FR-31, NFR-3 |\n111\t| `GET /api/report-cards/[id]` | `assertCanViewReportCard` | getReportCard | FR-37 |\n112\t| `PATCH /api/report-cards/[id]` | field-level (§4) | patchComments | FR-32 |\n113\t| `POST /api/report-cards/publish`, `POST /api/report-cards/unpublish` | ADMIN | publish / unpublish | FR-34 |\n114\t\n115\t`mark-missing` is the only route not in the PRD table. It implements the FR-24 column action server-side, because a client loop of N PUTs would write N audit rows and be slow. The `?format=csv` and `courseId`/`studentId` query parameters extend existing PRD routes rather than adding new ones.\n116\t\n117\t### 2.4 UI (`src/app/(app)/…`, MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, per NFR-7)\n118\t\n119\t| Page / component | Notes | Req |\n120\t|---|---|---|\n121\t| `admin/grading-scales/page.tsx` + `ScaleEditorDialog` | `DataTable` list. The dialog uses a band editor (TextField rows, add/remove) with Zod errors inline and a \"Default\" `Switch`. | FR-16 |\n122\t| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/settings/page.tsx` | Category rows (name, weight, drop lowest, order), a live `Σ weights / 100` `Chip` (error colour ≠ 100, Save disabled), and a scale `Select` (\"School default\" = null). | FR-17 |\n123\t| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/page.tsx` + `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx` | The single client component that owns the DataGrid (ADR-4, R7). Term `Select`, `columnGroupingModel` by category, custom `renderHeader` (title, due date, max, source icon), `renderCell` (score / EX / M red / — / late `AccessTime` icon), and `isCellEditable` = MANUAL only. Editing runs through `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), then `processRowUpdate` → PUT, `onProcessRowUpdateError` → per-cell error, and `hideFooter`. There are **no pinned columns**. Toolbar: \"Add manual item\", \"Export CSV\", \"Settings\". | FR-18–FR-25, NFR-8 |\n124\t| `AddManualItemDialog`, `TermOverrideDialog`, `ItemStatsDialog` | Dialogs. Stats (average, median, high, low) are computed client-side from the payload over counted scores. | FR-22, FR-23, FR-24 |\n125\t| `src/components/gradebook/StudentGradesView.tsx` | Course `Card`s with percent, letter and `gradeColour` `Chip`. `Accordion` expands to items and category subtotals. One component serves three hosts: | FR-26–FR-28 |\n126\t| ↳ `students/[id]/grades/page.tsx` | student tab | FR-26 |\n127\t| ↳ `grades/page.tsx` | STUDENT: self. PARENT: child `Select` from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-27 |\n128\t| ↳ `courses/[courseId]/grades/page.tsx` | filtered to one course | FR-28 |\n129\t| `admin/report-cards/page.tsx` | Term / grade level / section filters, `DataTable` with status `Chip` and warnings, and \"Generate drafts\", \"Publish all\", \"Print all\" actions. Confirmations use `ConfirmDialog`. | FR-29, FR-30, FR-34, FR-35 |\n130\t| `report-cards/page.tsx` | Homeroom TEACHER: their sections' cards for the selected term | FR-33 |\n131\t| `report-cards/[id]/page.tsx` | Review page: `ReportCardDocument` preview plus homeroom/principal comment fields (disabled per role or when PUBLISHED), and Publish / Unpublish (reason dialog) for ADMIN | FR-32, FR-34 |\n132\t| `report-cards/[id]/print/page.tsx`, `report-cards/print/page.tsx?termId=&…` | Server components rendering `ReportCardDocument` from the **snapshot only**. `GlobalStyles`: `@page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 12mm }`, `@media print` hides the app shell and buttons, each card gets `break-after: page`, and rows get `break-inside: avoid`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. Bulk print shows filtered PUBLISHED cards only. | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n133\t| `students/[id]/report-cards/page.tsx` | List of cards, each linking to the print view | FR-36 |\n134\t| Config | `courseTabs`: `gradebook` (ADMIN, TEACHER) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). `studentTabs`: `grades` and `report-cards`. `navigation`: the four entries from A4. | FR-18, FR-26–FR-28, FR-33, FR-36 |\n135\t\n136\tEvery page server-checks the role with `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the same entity assert as its API (NFR-6). It never relies on hidden links.\n137\t\n138\t### 2.5 Scripts and seed\n139\t\n140\t- `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. The script calls `backfillGradebook()` and exits (FR-8, ADR-7).\n141\t- `prisma/seed.ts`:\n142\t  1. scale \"Standard A–F\" (default)\n143\t  2. Homework 30 (drop 1) / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 for each 7A course\n144\t  3. `backfillGradebook()`\n145\t  4. ENG-7A manual item \"Oral presentation\" graded for all enrolled students\n146\t  5. Semester 1 `TermGradeOverride.teacherComment` for MATH-7A and ENG-7A\n147\t  6. `generateDrafts(S1, 7A students)`\n148\t\n149\t  Categories go in before the backfill so seeded assignments and quizzes can be attached to them (FR-41).\n150\t\n151\t---\n152\t\n153\t## 3. Data Flow\n154\t\n155\t### 3.1 Source → gradebook sync (write path)\n156\t\n157\t```\n158\tTeacher publishes assignment ─► assignments-service (tx) ─► upsertItemFromAssignment(tx)\n159\t                                                              ├─ termFor(dueAt, courseYearTerms, tz)  → null ⇒ warn+skip\n160\t                                                              └─ GradeItem upsert by sourceId (isVisible only on transition)\n161\tTeacher returns submission  ─► gradeSubmission/bulkReturn/gradeOffline (tx)\n162\t                                  └─ status==RETURNED ? syncSubmissionGrade(tx): Grade upsert {score: finalScore,\n163\t                                                                                  excused: exemption exists}\n164\tQuiz attempt graded         ─► recomputeAttempt → commit → syncQuizGrade(quiz, student)\n165\t                                  └─ GRADED ∧ resultsVisible ∧ ¬isPractice ? getStudentQuizScore → scale to maxPoints → upsert\n166\tResults released / closed   ─► releaseResults | maintenance claim ─► syncQuizGrades(quiz)  (bulk, batched)\n167\t```\n168\t\n169\tBecause unreleased scores are **never written** into `Grade`, privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers (NFR-5, layer 1 of 3).\n170\t\n171\tQuiz scaling: `score = result.score / result.maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, where `maxPoints = quiz maxScore`, in Decimal with `fixed2` at write.\n172\t\n173\t### 3.2 Calculation (pure, `grade-calc.ts`)\n174\t\n175\t```\n176\tinput: { items[], grades by itemId, categories[], bands, override?, now }\n177\tcounted(item) = item.isVisible ∧ ¬grade.excused ∧ (grade.score ≠ null ∨ (grade.missing ∧ item.dueAt ∧ now > item.dueAt))\n178\tearned = score ?? 0\n179\tper category: sort counted by pct asc (tie: dueAt, id) → drop min(dropLowest, n−1) → Σearned/Σmax×100\n180\tcourse: categories present with ≥1 counted ⇒ Σ(w·pct)/Σw   (Uncategorised w = 0, A8)\n181\t        no categories / none counted       ⇒ Σearned/Σmax×100 over all counted\n182\t        nothing counted                    ⇒ percent = null, letter = null (\"—\")\n183\tpercent = round half-up to 1 dp (only here) → letter = first band with percent ≥ minPercent\n184\toverride: percent? → replaces percent (letter re-derived unless letter set, A12); letter? → replaces letter only\n185\t```\n186\t\n187\tThe output per student is `{ categories: [{id, name, weight, percent, earned, possible, droppedItemIds}], percent, letter, descriptor, computedPercent, computedLetter, overridden }`. The gradebook, the student views and report-card generation all call this **one** function, which guarantees FR-15 / AC-1 (78.0% C+ in both places).\n188\t\n189\t### 3.3 Gradebook read (NFR-2: 35×80 < 800 ms)\n190\t\n191\t`GET gradebook` → `assertCanManageCourse` → `load.ts`:\n192\t\n193\t1. active enrollments + students, sorted by last name\n194\t2. items `(courseId, termId)`\n195\t3. grades for those item ids\n196\t4. categories\n197\t5. override rows + course scale or default\n198\t\n199\tThen two lookup queries for click-through and late flags: `Submission {id, isLate}` by `assignmentId in` and `QuizAttempt {id}` by `quizId in`. That's seven indexed queries in total. The pure calc runs for each student in memory, and the response is one denormalised payload. The client builds the columns, and the grid virtualises rows and columns.\n200\t\n201\t### 3.4 Manual grade edit\n202\t\n203\t```\n204\tcell edit ─► processRowUpdate ─► PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId\n205\t   service (tx): load old grade → reject non-comment fields if item.source ≠ MANUAL (FR-9)\n206\t                 → upsert → audit('grade.update', {old, new})\n207\t   after commit: old.score == null ∧ new.score ≠ null ∧ MANUAL ⇒ notifyStudentAndParents('grade.posted')  (A9)\n208\t   response: updated grade + recomputed student row (so the term % cell refreshes)\n209\t```\n210\t\n211\tOn error the client rolls back the optimistic value and flags the cell.\n212\t\n213\t### 3.5 Report card lifecycle\n214\t\n215\t```\n216\tgenerate {termId, studentIds} (ADMIN)\n217\t  ├─ load once: students (+section, homeroom, gradeLevel), school settings, term+year, default scale,\n218\t  │             enrollments for those students in courses of the term's year,\n219\t  │             load.ts for all those courseIds (in-filters), attendance getReport(term range) ×1\n220\t  ├─ compute in memory: grade-calc per (student, course) → buildSnapshot(v:1)\n221\t  └─ write (chunks of 100, tx): createMany(skipDuplicates) for new;\n222\t                                updateMany({ where:{ id, status:'DRAFT' }, data:{ snapshot, generatedAt } }) for existing\n223\t     PUBLISHED rows are filtered out by the WHERE clause, which enforces immutability (FR-31 / AC-8)\n224\tpublish {ids}   ─► updateMany({ id in ids, status:'DRAFT' } → PUBLISHED, publishedAt, publishedById)\n225\t                   → audit('reportCard.publish') → after commit notify report_card.published per card\n226\tunpublish {ids, reason} ─► PUBLISHED → DRAFT, clear publishedAt/ById, audit('reportCard.unpublish', {old, new, reason})\n227\tprint            ─► reads snapshot only; never recomputes\n228\t```\n229\t\n230\tNothing in `src/server/gradebook/` imports `src/server/report-cards/` or writes `ReportCard`. Grade edits therefore cannot touch snapshots.\n231\t\n232\t**Snapshot v1 shape**, owned by `snapshotSchema`:\n233\t\n234\t```\n235\t{ v: 1,\n236\t  school:     { name, logoUrl },\n237\t  student:    { name, admissionNumber, gradeLevel, section, homeroomTeacher },\n238\t  term:       { name, startDate, endDate, academicYear },\n239\t  courses:    [{ subject, code, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacherComment }],\n240\t  attendance: { rate, absences, lates, ...counts },\n241\t  scale:      { name, bands } }\n242\t```\n243\t\n244\t`attendance.rate` uses the same formula the existing attendance report consumers use; dev must not invent a new one (B13). Each course's letter uses that course's effective scale. The legend shows the default scale and also lists any course-specific scale used.\n245\t\n246\t**Missing-data warnings (FR-29)** are computed in the same batched pass:\n247\t\n248\t- a count of courses with eligible-but-ungraded items (visible, past due, no score, not missing, not excused)\n249\t- courses with no `teacherComment` override for the student\n250\t\n251\t### 3.6 Student/parent read (privacy, NFR-5 layers 2 and 3)\n252\t\n253\t`GET /api/students/:id/grades`: `assertCanViewStudent` → `load.ts` with `isVisible = true` filtered **in the query** → calc → serializer emits only whitelisted fields (no `updatedById`, no hidden items).\n254\t\n255\tReport-card endpoints apply `assertCanViewReportCard`. STUDENT and PARENT pass only if `card.status === 'PUBLISHED'` and they're the student or a linked parent. Anyone else unauthorised gets **NOT_FOUND**, so a 7B student can't tell that Sam's card exists (AC-7).\n256\t\n257\t---\n258\t\n259\t## 4. Access Control Matrix (NFR-6)\n260\t\n261\t| Action | ADMIN | TEACHER | STUDENT | PARENT |\n262\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n263\t| Read scales | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\n264\t| Write scales | ✓ | — | — | — |\n265\t| Categories GET | ✓ | view course | view course | view course |\n266\t| Categories PUT | ✓ | teaches course | — | — |\n267\t| Gradebook / items / grades / overrides | ✓ | teaches course (`assertCanManageCourse`) | — | — |\n268\t| Student grades | ✓ | teaches student or is homeroom (existing student-access) | self | linked child |\n269\t| Report cards list / generate | list + generate | list: own homeroom sections | own published (via `studentId`) | child's published |\n270\t| Report card GET | ✓ | teaches any course of the student, or is homeroom | self, PUBLISHED only | linked, PUBLISHED only |\n271\t| `homeroomComment` PATCH | ✓ | homeroom teacher of the student's section, DRAFT only | — | — |\n272\t| `principalComment` PATCH | ✓ (DRAFT only) | — | — | — |\n273\t| Publish / unpublish | ✓ | — | — | — |\n274\t\n275\t---\n276\t\n277\t## 5. Cross-cutting\n278\t\n279\t- **Audit (NFR-4):**\n280\t  - required: `grade.update` (manual, and comment edits on synced grades), `grade.markMissing`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (with reason), each carrying `{old, new}`\n281\t  - extra: `reportCard.publish`, `gradingScale.create/update/delete`, `gradeCategories.replace`\n282\t- **Notifications (FR-38):** sent after commit, using `notify()`, which never throws, so a notification failure can't roll back a grade.\n283\t- **Errors:** `AppError` codes `VALIDATION_ERROR` (weights ≠ 100, bad bands, non-MANUAL field edit, mark-missing before due), `CONFLICT` (scale in use, editing a PUBLISHED card), `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN`.\n284\t- **Logging:** `logger` only, never `console.log` (NFR-9).\n285\t- **Timezone (NFR-10):** all date rules go through `getSchoolTimezone()` + `schoolToday`. UI dates use `DateDisplay`.\n286\t- **Out of scope (NFR-13):** no GPA computation, class rank, transcripts or standards-based grading.\n287\t\n288\t---\n289\t\n290\t## 6. Test Plan Mapping (NFR-12)\n291\t\n292\t| Layer | File | Covers |\n293\t|---|---|---|\n294\t| Unit | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.test.ts` | no categories, empty categories, Uncategorised (A8), drop lowest (AC-2) and never-drop-all, missing vs ungraded vs excused (AC-5), past-due boundary, overrides (letter-only AC-6, percent-only A12), rounding 89.95 → 90.0 → A−, 77.0 → C+, the FR-15 golden 78.0 C+ |\n295\t| Unit | `term-placement.test.ts` | containment at tz day boundaries, current-term fallback, null |\n296\t| Integration | `gradebook-sync.test.ts` | return → Grade, save-without-return → none (AC-3), exemption on/off, quiz GRADED + IMMEDIATE / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL release, practice skipped, archive hides, delete removes, teacher hide survives re-save (A7) |\n297\t| Integration | `backfill.test.ts` | run twice → identical counts |\n298\t| Integration | `report-cards.test.ts` | generate → publish → edit grade → snapshot unchanged (AC-8), regenerate skips PUBLISHED, 7B student gets NOT_FOUND (AC-7), notifications sent |\n299\t| Integration | `perf` (optional, CI-skippable) | 35×80 gradebook < 800 ms, 600×8 generation < 30 s |\n300\t| Playwright | `gradebook.spec.ts`, `report-cards.spec.ts` | keyboard edits (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), admin generate + publish, parent opens print view with sidebar hidden under print media |\n301\t\n302\t---\n303\t\n304\t## 7. Requirements Traceability\n305\t\n306\t| Req | Design element(s) |\n307\t|---|---|\n308\t| FR-1 | §2.1 migration: PRD FR-1 models verbatim, plus indexes and the partial unique default index |\n309\t| FR-2 | §2.1 `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment/Quiz.categoryId` (SetNull). §2.2 validator and editor `Select` hooks. |\n310\t| FR-3 | `gradebook-sync.upsertItemFromAssignment/Quiz`, `term-placement.termFor` (A6, A10). Hooks in §2.2. |\n311\t| FR-4 | `hideItemForSource`, `deleteItemForSource` (same transaction). A7, A15. |\n312\t| FR-5 | `syncSubmissionGrade` from `gradeSubmission` / `bulkReturn` / `gradeOffline`, only when RETURNED (§3.1) |\n313\t| FR-6 | `setExemption` → `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) |\n314\t| FR-7 | `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers, `syncQuizGrades` on release and close, existing `getStudentQuizScore` + `resultsVisible` (A2) |\n315\t| FR-8 | `gradebook/backfill.ts`, `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, npm script, seed call (§2.5) |\n316\t| FR-9 | `putGrade` / `updateItem` reject non-comment and non-`isVisible` fields on synced items. Grid `isCellEditable`. |\n317\t| FR-10 | `grade-calc.ts` `counted()` predicate (§3.2) |\n318\t| FR-11 | `applyDropLowest`, `categoryPercent` |\n319\t| FR-12 | course aggregation with renormalised weights, Uncategorised bucket, points fallback (A8) |\n320\t| FR-13 | `roundHalfUp1` + `letterFor`, `effectiveScale` (A3) |\n321\t| FR-14 | `applyOverride` (A12), `putTermOverride` |\n322\t| FR-15 | single shared calc for the gradebook and student views. Golden unit test. |\n323\t| FR-16 | `scales-service`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `bandsSchema`, partial unique index (A11) |\n324\t| FR-17 | `categories-service`, gradebook settings page with live sum, scale select |\n325\t| FR-18 | `GradebookGrid` (MIT DataGrid, column groups, virtualisation, sticky header), `getGradebook`, `courseTabs.gradebook` |\n326\t| FR-19 | `GradebookGrid` `renderCell`. The payload carries `isLate`. |\n327\t| FR-20 | `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` + `processRowUpdate`, PUT grade, optimistic update with per-cell error (§3.4) |\n328\t| FR-21 | payload `submissionId` / `attemptId` → links to the existing grading and attempt pages |\n329\t| FR-22 | `AddManualItemDialog`, `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items`, `createManualItem` |\n330\t| FR-23 | `TermOverrideDialog`, `PUT term-overrides`, `termOverrideSchema` (≤ 1000) |\n331\t| FR-24 | column menu: `PATCH isVisible`, `POST mark-missing`, `ItemStatsDialog` |\n332\t| FR-25 | `exportGradebookCsv` via `toCsv`, `?format=csv` |\n333\t| FR-26 | `StudentGradesView`, `studentTabs.grades`, `gradeColour` |\n334\t| FR-27 | `/grades` page with parent child select, nav entry (A4) |\n335\t| FR-28 | `courses/[courseId]/grades`, `courseTabs.grades` |\n336\t| FR-29 | `/admin/report-cards`, `listReportCards` with warnings (§3.5) |\n337\t| FR-30 | `generateDrafts`, `buildSnapshot` v1, attendance `getReport` |\n338\t| FR-31 | DRAFT-only `updateMany`. Gradebook never writes ReportCard (§3.5). |\n339\t| FR-32 | `report-cards/[id]` review page, `patchComments`, field-level access (§4, A13) |\n340\t| FR-33 | `/report-cards` homeroom list, TEACHER nav entry |\n341\t| FR-34 | `publish` / `unpublish`, notify after commit, audit with reason (A13) |\n342\t| FR-35 | print pages, `ReportCardDocument`, `@page` A4 + `@media print` GlobalStyles, `PrintButton` |\n343\t| FR-36 | `studentTabs['report-cards']`, `listForStudent` (PUBLISHED-only for student/parent) |\n344\t| FR-37 | `report-cards/access.assertCanViewReportCard` (NOT_FOUND for others) |\n345\t| FR-38 | `types.ts` registrations, `grade.posted` on first score (A9), `report_card.published` |\n346\t| FR-39 | §2.3 route table: `withHandler` → `validators/gradebook.ts` → services, existing course-access |\n347\t| FR-40 | `categories-service.replaceCategories` (transaction, `dec(sum).eq(100)`) |\n348\t| FR-41 | `prisma/seed.ts` sequence (§2.5) |\n349\t| FR-42 | `student-grades-service` (visible-only query + whitelist serializer) |\n350\t| NFR-1 | `grade-calc.ts` pure Decimal, single final rounding, unit matrix (§6) |\n351\t| NFR-2 | `load.ts` 7 indexed queries, in-memory calc, DataGrid virtualisation, `GradeItem(courseId, termId)` index |\n352\t| NFR-3 | batched `load.ts` with `in` filters, one attendance groupBy, chunked writes (§3.5) |\n353\t| NFR-4 | `audit()` calls listed in §5 with `{old, new}` |\n354\t| NFR-5 | three layers: sync gating (§3.1), visible-only serializer (§3.6), PUBLISHED-only card guard |\n355\t| NFR-6 | §4 matrix. Every route and server page calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the entity asserts. |\n356\t| NFR-7 | §2.4 MUI-only components looked up via mui-mcp, `useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`, `Autocomplete` |\n357\t| NFR-8 | `GradebookGrid` MIT props only, no pinned columns |\n358\t| NFR-9 | new code only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/`, one-line hooks, reuse table (§2.2), `logger` |\n359\t| NFR-10 | `term-placement` (tz dates), instant past-due (A5), `DateDisplay` |\n360\t| NFR-11 | A4 `@page`, print media rules, `break-after` / `break-inside` |\n361\t| NFR-12 | §6 test plan |\n362\t| NFR-13 | `gpa` stored only. No rank or transcript components. |\n363\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"055adbad-09fd-4ef0-894f-863fb13f0fba","uuid":"daedd9cc-54ca-4e97-9e0b-0ead1d91b4e2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:12:27.958Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: **SH-11** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T17:30:00Z · Status: **complete**\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (42 FR + 13 NFR), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-10), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B19, R1–R7), and the source PRD `11-gradebook.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-11 adds a gradebook to SchoolHub, a brownfield Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/PostgreSQL + MUI 9.5.0 app. It has four parts:\n\n1. **Sync.** Published assignments and quizzes become `GradeItem`s. Returned submissions and released quiz results become `Grade`s.\n2. **Calculation.** A pure Decimal function turns items, grades, categories, a scale and an override into a term percent and letter.\n3. **Views.** A teacher grid (MIT DataGrid), student/parent grade views, and admin pages for scales and categories.\n4. **Report cards.** Frozen JSON snapshots per student and term, with a draft → published workflow, notifications and an A4 print view.\n\nThe design adds **no dependencies** (ADR-1). New server code lives only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/` (NFR-9). Existing services gain one-line calls into the sync module.\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. There is nothing to escalate. The flagged assumptions are resolved in §1.2.\n\n### 1.2 Assumptions and design decisions (need product sign-off, none block dev)\n\n| # | Topic | Decision | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Exemption removal | Unexempt sets `excused = false` and re-derives `score` from the source: `finalScore` if the submission is RETURNED, otherwise `null`. | FR-6 |\n| A2 | Quiz score source | **Intake's correction:** `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` **already exists** in `src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts` (L359, labelled \"PRD-11 export\"). Call it as is. It does **not** check visibility, so the sync gates on `resultsVisible()` first. This replaces ADR-6's \"add a helper to grading.ts\". Don't create a second one. | FR-7, NFR-9 |\n| A3 | 89.95 rounding | 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale (A is 93). The unit test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter. | FR-13 |\n| A4 | Nav entries | Add `/grades` (STUDENT, PARENT), `/report-cards` (TEACHER), and `/admin/grading-scales` and `/admin/report-cards` (ADMIN, group `Administration`). | FR-16, FR-27, FR-29, FR-33 |\n| A5 | Past due | `now > dueAt` as a UTC instant. Term containment compares school-local dates (`SchoolSettings.timezone`). | NFR-10 |\n| A6 | No term | If no term of the course's academic year contains the date and no term contains today, skip the item and `logger.warn`. | FR-3 |\n| A7 | Teacher hide vs source visibility (R2) | **No extra column** (FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\"). Source sync writes `isVisible` only on source visibility **transitions**: publish / publishOnce → `true`, archive → `false`. Plain edits to an already-published source never touch `isVisible`, so a teacher's hide survives re-saves. | FR-4, FR-24 |\n| A8 | Uncategorised weight (R3) | If the course has categories, the implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket is **shown with its subtotal but has weight 0**, so it's excluded from the weighted mean. If no category has a counted item, fall back to the points total over **all** counted items. If the course has no categories, use the points total. | FR-12 |\n| A9 | `grade.posted` dedupe (R4) | No marker column. Notify only when a MANUAL grade's `score` goes from `null` to a value. That gives one notification per student per item. Later edits are audited but not notified. | FR-38 |\n| A10 | Term drift (R5) | Re-derive `GradeItem.termId` only when `dueAt`/`availableUntil` changes. | FR-3 |\n| A11 | Scale delete (R6) | Return `CONFLICT` if the scale is the default or any `Course.gradingScaleId` references it. Published snapshots embed their own legend, so they're unaffected. | FR-16 |\n| A12 | Percent-only override | Re-derive the letter from the effective scale using the override percent. | FR-14 |\n| A13 | Report card edits | Comments are editable only while `DRAFT`. Unpublish returns the card to `DRAFT` and clears `publishedAt`/`publishedById`. | FR-32, FR-34 |\n| A14 | `Grade.updatedById` on system writes | Sync uses the acting user (grader/teacher) when there is one. Otherwise (auto-graded quiz, maintenance release, backfill) it uses `quiz.createdById`, `assignment.createdById` or, for backfill, `course.teacherId`. The column has no FK, as specified. | FR-1, FR-5, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| A15 | Quiz CLOSED | A CLOSED quiz is **not** unpublished. Its item stays visible. Quizzes have no archive. `deleteQuiz` deletes the item. A practice toggle after publish deletes the item. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data model (one migration: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_gradebook/`)\n\nThe models and enums are **exactly the PRD FR-1 block** (FR-1). On top of that:\n\n- **Additive columns (FR-2):** `Course.gradingScaleId String?` → `GradingScale` (`onDelete: SetNull`). `Assignment.categoryId String?` and `Quiz.categoryId String?` → `GradeCategory` (`onDelete: SetNull`), so deleting a category never deletes sources.\n- **Relation fields:** add only the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.gradeItems`, `Course.gradeCategories`, `Term.gradeItems`, `GradeCategory.items/assignments/quizzes`). There are no new scalar columns beyond the spec.\n- **Keys already in the spec make sync race-safe (B19):** `GradeItem.sourceId @unique`, `Grade @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])`, `TermGradeOverride @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])`, `ReportCard @@unique([studentId, termId])`.\n- **Indexes added:**\n  - `GradeItem @@index([courseId, termId])` (NFR-2, NFR-3)\n  - `TermGradeOverride @@index([termId])` (NFR-3)\n  - `ReportCard @@index([termId, status])` (FR-29)\n- **Raw SQL in the migration:** a partial unique index `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX grading_scale_one_default ON \"GradingScale\" (\"isDefault\") WHERE \"isDefault\";` as the backstop for \"exactly one default\" (FR-16, ADR-3).\n- **Types:** `bands Json` holds `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }[]`, sorted descending and validated by Zod (`bandsSchema`). `gpa` is stored and never computed (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 Server modules\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reuses | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` | **Pure** functions with no Prisma client import (types only): `computeStudentTerm(input)`, `categoryPercent`, `applyDropLowest`, `roundHalfUp1`, `letterFor(percent, bands)`, `applyOverride`, `effectiveScale(course, default)`, `gradeColour(percent)`. Everything is `Decimal`, and rounding happens once at the end. | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `assignments/grading-math.ts` | FR-10–FR-15, FR-26, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/term-placement.ts` | Pure `termFor(date, terms, tz, now)`: picks the containing term in school-local dates, falls back to the term containing today, else returns `null`. | `schoolToday` (attendance-rules), `getSchoolTimezone` | FR-3, NFR-10, A6 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts` (file name from the PRD) | Idempotent upserts. `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`, `upsertItemFromQuiz(tx, id)`, `hideItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `deleteItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `syncSubmissionGrade(tx, assignmentId, studentId, actorId?)`, `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, `syncQuizGrades(quizId)`. It also exports **pure row builders** (`itemFromAssignment`, `gradeFromSubmission`, `gradeFromQuizScore`) that the backfill shares. | `isAssignmentVisible`, `getStudentQuizScore`, `resultsVisible`, `applyScoringPolicy`, `logger` | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-5 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/backfill.ts` | `backfillGradebook()`. Batch-loads per course and runs the same row builders with `upsert`. Idempotent through the unique keys. | `applyScoringPolicy` in memory (no per-student `getStudentQuizScore`) | FR-8, NFR-3 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-service.ts` | `getGradebook(user, courseId, termId)`, `createManualItem`, `updateItem`, `deleteItem`, `putGrade`, `markAllMissing`, `putTermOverride`, `exportGradebookCsv`. Loads the data, calls grade-calc, enforces FR-9 and writes audit entries. | `assertCanManageCourse`, `audit`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `toCsv` | FR-9, FR-18–FR-25, FR-38, NFR-2, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/categories-service.ts` | `getCategories`, `replaceCategories` (in a transaction: delete removed ids, upsert the rest, `dec(sum).eq(100)`), and `setCourseScale`. | `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` | FR-17, FR-40 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/scales-service.ts` | CRUD. `setDefault` runs in a transaction that clears the other defaults. Delete is guarded (A11). | `requireRole('ADMIN')`, `audit` | FR-16 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/student-grades-service.ts` | `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId, courseId?)`. Uses the visible-only serializer. Reuses grade-calc and passes **visible items only** into it, so the computed totals match what the student sees. | `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42, NFR-5 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/load.ts` | Shared batched loader: `loadCourseTermData(courseIds[], termId, studentIds?)` returns `{items, grades, categories, overrides, scales}` in 5 `findMany` calls with `in` filters, grouped in memory. Used by the gradebook, student grades and report-card generation. | Prisma | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| `src/server/report-cards/snapshot.ts` | Zod `snapshotSchema` (`v: 1`) and the pure `buildSnapshot(student, courses, computed, attendance, school, scale)`. | grade-calc | FR-30 |\n| `src/server/report-cards/report-card-service.ts` | `listReportCards` (with warnings), `generateDrafts`, `getReportCard`, `patchComments`, `publish`, `unpublish`, `listForStudent`. | `load.ts`, attendance `getReport`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `audit` | FR-29–FR-34, FR-36, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/report-cards/access.ts` | `assertCanViewReportCard(user, card)`, `canEditHomeroomComment`. | `student-access`, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `Enrollment` | FR-32, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts` | Zod: `bandsSchema`, `scaleSchema`, `categoriesPutSchema`, `manualItemSchema`, `itemPatchSchema`, `gradePutSchema`, `termOverrideSchema` (comment ≤ 1000), `reportCardPatchSchema`, `generateSchema`, `publishSchema`, `unpublishSchema` (reason required). These are shared by client forms and handlers. | Zod | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (edit) | Register `grade.posted` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: false`) and `report_card.published` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: true`). | existing registry | FR-38 |\n\n**Hook edits to existing services** (each is one call; behaviour is otherwise unchanged, per NFR-9):\n\n| Existing site | Added call | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `assignments-service` `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` / `publishOnce` | `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`. This sets `isVisible` only on a visibility transition (A7). It re-places the term only if `dueAt` changed (A10). | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | archive → `hideItemForSource`; hard delete → `deleteItemForSource` in the same transaction (B9) | FR-4 |\n| `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline` | `syncSubmissionGrade` when the submission **is** RETURNED after the write. This covers re-grades of returned work. Nothing happens otherwise (AC-3). | FR-5, NFR-5 |\n| `setExemption` (both branches) | `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) | FR-6 |\n| `quiz-service` `updateQuiz` (→PUBLISHED, or edits to a published quiz) / `deleteQuiz` | `upsertItemFromQuiz` / `deleteItemForSource`. Practice quizzes are skipped; turning practice on deletes the item. Wrap `deleteQuiz` in a transaction. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| After callers of `recomputeAttempt` commit (`submitAttempt`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `regradeQuiz`) | `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`: no-op unless GRADED, `resultsVisible` and not practice | FR-7 |\n| `releaseResults` (MANUAL) and `quiz/maintenance.ts` AFTER_CLOSE claim (`count === 1`) | `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` (bulk). Without this, delayed-visibility quizzes never sync (R1). | FR-7, NFR-5 |\n| Assignment and quiz Zod validators and editors | Optional nullable `categoryId` plus one MUI `Select` of the course's categories | FR-2 |\n\n### 2.3 API layer (`src/app/api/**/route.ts`, thin: `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\nThese match the PRD API table exactly. `api-contracts.json` (next sub-task) owns the shapes.\n\n| Route | Role check | Service | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/[id]` | GET: `requireUser`; writes: ADMIN | scales-service | FR-16, FR-39 |\n| `GET/PUT /api/courses/[id]/grade-categories` | view / manage | categories-service (PUT body also carries `gradingScaleId`) | FR-17, FR-40 |\n| `GET /api/courses/[id]/gradebook?termId=` (`&format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | gradebook-service | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, FR-25, NFR-2 |\n| `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items` | manage | createManualItem | FR-22 |\n| `PATCH/DELETE /api/grade-items/[id]` | manage (via the item's course) | updateItem / deleteItem. Non-MANUAL items accept only `isVisible`, and DELETE is MANUAL only. | FR-9, FR-24 |\n| `POST /api/grade-items/[id]/mark-missing` | manage | markAllMissing (`now > dueAt`, ungraded rows only) | FR-24 |\n| `PUT /api/grade-items/[id]/grades/[studentId]` | manage + enrolled student | putGrade. Non-MANUAL items accept only `comment` (FR-9). | FR-9, FR-20, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| `PUT /api/courses/[id]/term-overrides/[studentId]` | manage | putTermOverride | FR-14, FR-23, NFR-4 |\n| `GET /api/students/[id]/grades?termId=&courseId=` | `assertCanViewStudent` | student-grades-service | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42 |\n| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=&studentId=` | ADMIN; homeroom TEACHER (own sections); with `studentId`, view-student rules plus PUBLISHED-only for student/parent | listReportCards / listForStudent | FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | generateDrafts | FR-30, FR-31, NFR-3 |\n| `GET /api/report-cards/[id]` | `assertCanViewReportCard` | getReportCard | FR-37 |\n| `PATCH /api/report-cards/[id]` | field-level (§4) | patchComments | FR-32 |\n| `POST /api/report-cards/publish`, `POST /api/report-cards/unpublish` | ADMIN | publish / unpublish | FR-34 |\n\n`mark-missing` is the only route not in the PRD table. It implements the FR-24 column action server-side, because a client loop of N PUTs would write N audit rows and be slow. The `?format=csv` and `courseId`/`studentId` query parameters extend existing PRD routes rather than adding new ones.\n\n### 2.4 UI (`src/app/(app)/…`, MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, per NFR-7)\n\n| Page / component | Notes | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `admin/grading-scales/page.tsx` + `ScaleEditorDialog` | `DataTable` list. The dialog uses a band editor (TextField rows, add/remove) with Zod errors inline and a \"Default\" `Switch`. | FR-16 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/settings/page.tsx` | Category rows (name, weight, drop lowest, order), a live `Σ weights / 100` `Chip` (error colour ≠ 100, Save disabled), and a scale `Select` (\"School default\" = null). | FR-17 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/page.tsx` + `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx` | The single client component that owns the DataGrid (ADR-4, R7). Term `Select`, `columnGroupingModel` by category, custom `renderHeader` (title, due date, max, source icon), `renderCell` (score / EX / M red / — / late `AccessTime` icon), and `isCellEditable` = MANUAL only. Editing runs through `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), then `processRowUpdate` → PUT, `onProcessRowUpdateError` → per-cell error, and `hideFooter`. There are **no pinned columns**. Toolbar: \"Add manual item\", \"Export CSV\", \"Settings\". | FR-18–FR-25, NFR-8 |\n| `AddManualItemDialog`, `TermOverrideDialog`, `ItemStatsDialog` | Dialogs. Stats (average, median, high, low) are computed client-side from the payload over counted scores. | FR-22, FR-23, FR-24 |\n| `src/components/gradebook/StudentGradesView.tsx` | Course `Card`s with percent, letter and `gradeColour` `Chip`. `Accordion` expands to items and category subtotals. One component serves three hosts: | FR-26–FR-28 |\n| ↳ `students/[id]/grades/page.tsx` | student tab | FR-26 |\n| ↳ `grades/page.tsx` | STUDENT: self. PARENT: child `Select` from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-27 |\n| ↳ `courses/[courseId]/grades/page.tsx` | filtered to one course | FR-28 |\n| `admin/report-cards/page.tsx` | Term / grade level / section filters, `DataTable` with status `Chip` and warnings, and \"Generate drafts\", \"Publish all\", \"Print all\" actions. Confirmations use `ConfirmDialog`. | FR-29, FR-30, FR-34, FR-35 |\n| `report-cards/page.tsx` | Homeroom TEACHER: their sections' cards for the selected term | FR-33 |\n| `report-cards/[id]/page.tsx` | Review page: `ReportCardDocument` preview plus homeroom/principal comment fields (disabled per role or when PUBLISHED), and Publish / Unpublish (reason dialog) for ADMIN | FR-32, FR-34 |\n| `report-cards/[id]/print/page.tsx`, `report-cards/print/page.tsx?termId=&…` | Server components rendering `ReportCardDocument` from the **snapshot only**. `GlobalStyles`: `@page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 12mm }`, `@media print` hides the app shell and buttons, each card gets `break-after: page`, and rows get `break-inside: avoid`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. Bulk print shows filtered PUBLISHED cards only. | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| `students/[id]/report-cards/page.tsx` | List of cards, each linking to the print view | FR-36 |\n| Config | `courseTabs`: `gradebook` (ADMIN, TEACHER) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). `studentTabs`: `grades` and `report-cards`. `navigation`: the four entries from A4. | FR-18, FR-26–FR-28, FR-33, FR-36 |\n\nEvery page server-checks the role with `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the same entity assert as its API (NFR-6). It never relies on hidden links.\n\n### 2.5 Scripts and seed\n\n- `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. The script calls `backfillGradebook()` and exits (FR-8, ADR-7).\n- `prisma/seed.ts`:\n  1. scale \"Standard A–F\" (default)\n  2. Homework 30 (drop 1) / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 for each 7A course\n  3. `backfillGradebook()`\n  4. ENG-7A manual item \"Oral presentation\" graded for all enrolled students\n  5. Semester 1 `TermGradeOverride.teacherComment` for MATH-7A and ENG-7A\n  6. `generateDrafts(S1, 7A students)`\n\n  Categories go in before the backfill so seeded assignments and quizzes can be attached to them (FR-41).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Source → gradebook sync (write path)\n\n```\nTeacher publishes assignment ─► assignments-service (tx) ─► upsertItemFromAssignment(tx)\n                                                              ├─ termFor(dueAt, courseYearTerms, tz)  → null ⇒ warn+skip\n                                                              └─ GradeItem upsert by sourceId (isVisible only on transition)\nTeacher returns submission  ─► gradeSubmission/bulkReturn/gradeOffline (tx)\n                                  └─ status==RETURNED ? syncSubmissionGrade(tx): Grade upsert {score: finalScore,\n                                                                                  excused: exemption exists}\nQuiz attempt graded         ─► recomputeAttempt → commit → syncQuizGrade(quiz, student)\n                                  └─ GRADED ∧ resultsVisible ∧ ¬isPractice ? getStudentQuizScore → scale to maxPoints → upsert\nResults released / closed   ─► releaseResults | maintenance claim ─► syncQuizGrades(quiz)  (bulk, batched)\n```\n\nBecause unreleased scores are **never written** into `Grade`, privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers (NFR-5, layer 1 of 3).\n\nQuiz scaling: `score = result.score / result.maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, where `maxPoints = quiz maxScore`, in Decimal with `fixed2` at write.\n\n### 3.2 Calculation (pure, `grade-calc.ts`)\n\n```\ninput: { items[], grades by itemId, categories[], bands, override?, now }\ncounted(item) = item.isVisible ∧ ¬grade.excused ∧ (grade.score ≠ null ∨ (grade.missing ∧ item.dueAt ∧ now > item.dueAt))\nearned = score ?? 0\nper category: sort counted by pct asc (tie: dueAt, id) → drop min(dropLowest, n−1) → Σearned/Σmax×100\ncourse: categories present with ≥1 counted ⇒ Σ(w·pct)/Σw   (Uncategorised w = 0, A8)\n        no categories / none counted       ⇒ Σearned/Σmax×100 over all counted\n        nothing counted                    ⇒ percent = null, letter = null (\"—\")\npercent = round half-up to 1 dp (only here) → letter = first band with percent ≥ minPercent\noverride: percent? → replaces percent (letter re-derived unless letter set, A12); letter? → replaces letter only\n```\n\nThe output per student is `{ categories: [{id, name, weight, percent, earned, possible, droppedItemIds}], percent, letter, descriptor, computedPercent, computedLetter, overridden }`. The gradebook, the student views and report-card generation all call this **one** function, which guarantees FR-15 / AC-1 (78.0% C+ in both places).\n\n### 3.3 Gradebook read (NFR-2: 35×80 < 800 ms)\n\n`GET gradebook` → `assertCanManageCourse` → `load.ts`:\n\n1. active enrollments + students, sorted by last name\n2. items `(courseId, termId)`\n3. grades for those item ids\n4. categories\n5. override rows + course scale or default\n\nThen two lookup queries for click-through and late flags: `Submission {id, isLate}` by `assignmentId in` and `QuizAttempt {id}` by `quizId in`. That's seven indexed queries in total. The pure calc runs for each student in memory, and the response is one denormalised payload. The client builds the columns, and the grid virtualises rows and columns.\n\n### 3.4 Manual grade edit\n\n```\ncell edit ─► processRowUpdate ─► PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId\n   service (tx): load old grade → reject non-comment fields if item.source ≠ MANUAL (FR-9)\n                 → upsert → audit('grade.update', {old, new})\n   after commit: old.score == null ∧ new.score ≠ null ∧ MANUAL ⇒ notifyStudentAndParents('grade.posted')  (A9)\n   response: updated grade + recomputed student row (so the term % cell refreshes)\n```\n\nOn error the client rolls back the optimistic value and flags the cell.\n\n### 3.5 Report card lifecycle\n\n```\ngenerate {termId, studentIds} (ADMIN)\n  ├─ load once: students (+section, homeroom, gradeLevel), school settings, term+year, default scale,\n  │             enrollments for those students in courses of the term's year,\n  │             load.ts for all those courseIds (in-filters), attendance getReport(term range) ×1\n  ├─ compute in memory: grade-calc per (student, course) → buildSnapshot(v:1)\n  └─ write (chunks of 100, tx): createMany(skipDuplicates) for new;\n                                updateMany({ where:{ id, status:'DRAFT' }, data:{ snapshot, generatedAt } }) for existing\n     PUBLISHED rows are filtered out by the WHERE clause, which enforces immutability (FR-31 / AC-8)\npublish {ids}   ─► updateMany({ id in ids, status:'DRAFT' } → PUBLISHED, publishedAt, publishedById)\n                   → audit('reportCard.publish') → after commit notify report_card.published per card\nunpublish {ids, reason} ─► PUBLISHED → DRAFT, clear publishedAt/ById, audit('reportCard.unpublish', {old, new, reason})\nprint            ─► reads snapshot only; never recomputes\n```\n\nNothing in `src/server/gradebook/` imports `src/server/report-cards/` or writes `ReportCard`. Grade edits therefore cannot touch snapshots.\n\n**Snapshot v1 shape**, owned by `snapshotSchema`:\n\n```\n{ v: 1,\n  school:     { name, logoUrl },\n  student:    { name, admissionNumber, gradeLevel, section, homeroomTeacher },\n  term:       { name, startDate, endDate, academicYear },\n  courses:    [{ subject, code, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacherComment }],\n  attendance: { rate, absences, lates, ...counts },\n  scale:      { name, bands } }\n```\n\n`attendance.rate` uses the same formula the existing attendance report consumers use; dev must not invent a new one (B13). Each course's letter uses that course's effective scale. The legend shows the default scale and also lists any course-specific scale used.\n\n**Missing-data warnings (FR-29)** are computed in the same batched pass:\n\n- a count of courses with eligible-but-ungraded items (visible, past due, no score, not missing, not excused)\n- courses with no `teacherComment` override for the student\n\n### 3.6 Student/parent read (privacy, NFR-5 layers 2 and 3)\n\n`GET /api/students/:id/grades`: `assertCanViewStudent` → `load.ts` with `isVisible = true` filtered **in the query** → calc → serializer emits only whitelisted fields (no `updatedById`, no hidden items).\n\nReport-card endpoints apply `assertCanViewReportCard`. STUDENT and PARENT pass only if `card.status === 'PUBLISHED'` and they're the student or a linked parent. Anyone else unauthorised gets **NOT_FOUND**, so a 7B student can't tell that Sam's card exists (AC-7).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Access Control Matrix (NFR-6)\n\n| Action | ADMIN | TEACHER | STUDENT | PARENT |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Read scales | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\n| Write scales | ✓ | — | — | — |\n| Categories GET | ✓ | view course | view course | view course |\n| Categories PUT | ✓ | teaches course | — | — |\n| Gradebook / items / grades / overrides | ✓ | teaches course (`assertCanManageCourse`) | — | — |\n| Student grades | ✓ | teaches student or is homeroom (existing student-access) | self | linked child |\n| Report cards list / generate | list + generate | list: own homeroom sections | own published (via `studentId`) | child's published |\n| Report card GET | ✓ | teaches any course of the student, or is homeroom | self, PUBLISHED only | linked, PUBLISHED only |\n| `homeroomComment` PATCH | ✓ | homeroom teacher of the student's section, DRAFT only | — | — |\n| `principalComment` PATCH | ✓ (DRAFT only) | — | — | — |\n| Publish / unpublish | ✓ | — | — | — |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n- **Audit (NFR-4):**\n  - required: `grade.update` (manual, and comment edits on synced grades), `grade.markMissing`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (with reason), each carrying `{old, new}`\n  - extra: `reportCard.publish`, `gradingScale.create/update/delete`, `gradeCategories.replace`\n- **Notifications (FR-38):** sent after commit, using `notify()`, which never throws, so a notification failure can't roll back a grade.\n- **Errors:** `AppError` codes `VALIDATION_ERROR` (weights ≠ 100, bad bands, non-MANUAL field edit, mark-missing before due), `CONFLICT` (scale in use, editing a PUBLISHED card), `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN`.\n- **Logging:** `logger` only, never `console.log` (NFR-9).\n- **Timezone (NFR-10):** all date rules go through `getSchoolTimezone()` + `schoolToday`. UI dates use `DateDisplay`.\n- **Out of scope (NFR-13):** no GPA computation, class rank, transcripts or standards-based grading.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Test Plan Mapping (NFR-12)\n\n| Layer | File | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.test.ts` | no categories, empty categories, Uncategorised (A8), drop lowest (AC-2) and never-drop-all, missing vs ungraded vs excused (AC-5), past-due boundary, overrides (letter-only AC-6, percent-only A12), rounding 89.95 → 90.0 → A−, 77.0 → C+, the FR-15 golden 78.0 C+ |\n| Unit | `term-placement.test.ts` | containment at tz day boundaries, current-term fallback, null |\n| Integration | `gradebook-sync.test.ts` | return → Grade, save-without-return → none (AC-3), exemption on/off, quiz GRADED + IMMEDIATE / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL release, practice skipped, archive hides, delete removes, teacher hide survives re-save (A7) |\n| Integration | `backfill.test.ts` | run twice → identical counts |\n| Integration | `report-cards.test.ts` | generate → publish → edit grade → snapshot unchanged (AC-8), regenerate skips PUBLISHED, 7B student gets NOT_FOUND (AC-7), notifications sent |\n| Integration | `perf` (optional, CI-skippable) | 35×80 gradebook < 800 ms, 600×8 generation < 30 s |\n| Playwright | `gradebook.spec.ts`, `report-cards.spec.ts` | keyboard edits (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), admin generate + publish, parent opens print view with sidebar hidden under print media |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 migration: PRD FR-1 models verbatim, plus indexes and the partial unique default index |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment/Quiz.categoryId` (SetNull). §2.2 validator and editor `Select` hooks. |\n| FR-3 | `gradebook-sync.upsertItemFromAssignment/Quiz`, `term-placement.termFor` (A6, A10). Hooks in §2.2. |\n| FR-4 | `hideItemForSource`, `deleteItemForSource` (same transaction). A7, A15. |\n| FR-5 | `syncSubmissionGrade` from `gradeSubmission` / `bulkReturn` / `gradeOffline`, only when RETURNED (§3.1) |\n| FR-6 | `setExemption` → `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) |\n| FR-7 | `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers, `syncQuizGrades` on release and close, existing `getStudentQuizScore` + `resultsVisible` (A2) |\n| FR-8 | `gradebook/backfill.ts`, `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, npm script, seed call (§2.5) |\n| FR-9 | `putGrade` / `updateItem` reject non-comment and non-`isVisible` fields on synced items. Grid `isCellEditable`. |\n| FR-10 | `grade-calc.ts` `counted()` predicate (§3.2) |\n| FR-11 | `applyDropLowest`, `categoryPercent` |\n| FR-12 | course aggregation with renormalised weights, Uncategorised bucket, points fallback (A8) |\n| FR-13 | `roundHalfUp1` + `letterFor`, `effectiveScale` (A3) |\n| FR-14 | `applyOverride` (A12), `putTermOverride` |\n| FR-15 | single shared calc for the gradebook and student views. Golden unit test. |\n| FR-16 | `scales-service`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `bandsSchema`, partial unique index (A11) |\n| FR-17 | `categories-service`, gradebook settings page with live sum, scale select |\n| FR-18 | `GradebookGrid` (MIT DataGrid, column groups, virtualisation, sticky header), `getGradebook`, `courseTabs.gradebook` |\n| FR-19 | `GradebookGrid` `renderCell`. The payload carries `isLate`. |\n| FR-20 | `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` + `processRowUpdate`, PUT grade, optimistic update with per-cell error (§3.4) |\n| FR-21 | payload `submissionId` / `attemptId` → links to the existing grading and attempt pages |\n| FR-22 | `AddManualItemDialog`, `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items`, `createManualItem` |\n| FR-23 | `TermOverrideDialog`, `PUT term-overrides`, `termOverrideSchema` (≤ 1000) |\n| FR-24 | column menu: `PATCH isVisible`, `POST mark-missing`, `ItemStatsDialog` |\n| FR-25 | `exportGradebookCsv` via `toCsv`, `?format=csv` |\n| FR-26 | `StudentGradesView`, `studentTabs.grades`, `gradeColour` |\n| FR-27 | `/grades` page with parent child select, nav entry (A4) |\n| FR-28 | `courses/[courseId]/grades`, `courseTabs.grades` |\n| FR-29 | `/admin/report-cards`, `listReportCards` with warnings (§3.5) |\n| FR-30 | `generateDrafts`, `buildSnapshot` v1, attendance `getReport` |\n| FR-31 | DRAFT-only `updateMany`. Gradebook never writes ReportCard (§3.5). |\n| FR-32 | `report-cards/[id]` review page, `patchComments`, field-level access (§4, A13) |\n| FR-33 | `/report-cards` homeroom list, TEACHER nav entry |\n| FR-34 | `publish` / `unpublish`, notify after commit, audit with reason (A13) |\n| FR-35 | print pages, `ReportCardDocument`, `@page` A4 + `@media print` GlobalStyles, `PrintButton` |\n| FR-36 | `studentTabs['report-cards']`, `listForStudent` (PUBLISHED-only for student/parent) |\n| FR-37 | `report-cards/access.assertCanViewReportCard` (NOT_FOUND for others) |\n| FR-38 | `types.ts` registrations, `grade.posted` on first score (A9), `report_card.published` |\n| FR-39 | §2.3 route table: `withHandler` → `validators/gradebook.ts` → services, existing course-access |\n| FR-40 | `categories-service.replaceCategories` (transaction, `dec(sum).eq(100)`) |\n| FR-41 | `prisma/seed.ts` sequence (§2.5) |\n| FR-42 | `student-grades-service` (visible-only query + whitelist serializer) |\n| NFR-1 | `grade-calc.ts` pure Decimal, single final rounding, unit matrix (§6) |\n| NFR-2 | `load.ts` 7 indexed queries, in-memory calc, DataGrid virtualisation, `GradeItem(courseId, termId)` index |\n| NFR-3 | batched `load.ts` with `in` filters, one attendance groupBy, chunked writes (§3.5) |\n| NFR-4 | `audit()` calls listed in §5 with `{old, new}` |\n| NFR-5 | three layers: sync gating (§3.1), visible-only serializer (§3.6), PUBLISHED-only card guard |\n| NFR-6 | §4 matrix. Every route and server page calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the entity asserts. |\n| NFR-7 | §2.4 MUI-only components looked up via mui-mcp, `useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`, `Autocomplete` |\n| NFR-8 | `GradebookGrid` MIT props only, no pinned columns |\n| NFR-9 | new code only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/`, one-line hooks, reuse table (§2.2), `logger` |\n| NFR-10 | `term-placement` (tz dates), instant past-due (A5), `DateDisplay` |\n| NFR-11 | A4 `@page`, print media rules, `break-after` / `break-inside` |\n| NFR-12 | §6 test plan |\n| NFR-13 | `gpa` stored only. No rank or transcript components. |\n","numLines":363,"startLine":1,"totalLines":363}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HBzMUrAT49g29JSmVxpWL9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsLHLHororapHY3eqJkd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AfAJS2PEPnjpjHSKgo716z","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9246,"cache_read_input_tokens":27760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9246},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"055adbad-09fd-4ef0-894f-863fb13f0fba","uuid":"a311440d-e0e9-472d-8860-6c0561bd8bc4","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:12:28.054Z","request_id":"req_011CgsLHL3gEhJYDa3Wzprxn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AfAJS2PEPnjpjHSKgo716z":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AfAJS2PEPnjpjHSKgo716z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n6\t\n7\tIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n8\t\n9\t- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n10\t- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n11\t- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n12\t\n13\tNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n18\t\n19\t**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n20\t\n21\t**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n22\t\n23\t| Need | Use | Req |\n24\t|---|---|---|\n25\t| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n26\t| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n27\t| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n28\t| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n29\t| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n30\t| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n31\t| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n32\t| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n33\t| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n34\t| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n35\t| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n36\t| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n37\t| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n38\t| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n39\t| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n40\t\n41\t**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n46\t\n47\t**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n48\t\n49\t**Decision.**\n50\t- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n51\t- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n52\t- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n53\t- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n54\t\n55\t**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n60\t\n61\t**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n62\t\n63\t**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n64\t\n65\t**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n70\t\n71\t**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n72\t\n73\t**Decision.**\n74\t- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n75\t- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n76\t- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n77\t- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n78\t\n79\t**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n80\t\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n84\t\n85\t**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n86\t\n87\t**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n88\t- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n89\t- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n90\t- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n91\t\n92\t**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n97\t\n98\t**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n99\t\n100\t**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n101\t\n102\t**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n103\t\n104\t---\n105\t\n106\t## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n107\t\n108\t**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n109\t\n110\t**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n111\t\n112\t**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n113\t\n114\t---\n115\t\n116\t## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n117\t\n118\t**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n119\t\n120\t**Decision.**\n121\t- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n122\t- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n123\t  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n124\t  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n125\t  - the scale\n126\t  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n127\t- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n128\t- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n129\t\n130\t**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n131\t\n132\t---\n133\t\n134\t## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n135\t\n136\t**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n137\t\n138\t**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n139\t\n140\t**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n141\t\n142\t---\n143\t\n144\t## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n145\t\n146\t**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n147\t\n148\t**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n149\t\n150\t**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n151\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"055adbad-09fd-4ef0-894f-863fb13f0fba","uuid":"28451829-4652-4ab0-b2cc-ef342b0614f2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:12:28.073Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n\n- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n\nNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n\n**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n\n**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n\n**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n\n**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n\n**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n\n**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n\n**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n\n**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n\n**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n\n**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n\n**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n\n**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n\n**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n  - the scale\n  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n\n**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n\n**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n\n**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n\n**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n\n**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n","numLines":151,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AfAJS2PEPnjpjHSKgo716z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
