{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RLejnverU7iJUT3Z4PXL9P","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design: PRD-12 Announcements & News\n2\t\n3\tTicket: **SH-12** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T19:00:00Z · Status: **complete**\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 FR, 11 NFR, 94% confidence), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B22, R1–R11, A1–A8), and the FR-1 Prisma block in `12-announcements.md`.\n6\t\n7\t> This file replaces the SH-11 version that was here before.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## 1. Overview\n12\t\n13\tAnnouncements is a brownfield feature inside the existing Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/PostgreSQL + MUI 9 app. **No new dependencies** (ADR-1). The work is:\n14\t\n15\t- one Prisma migration (FR-1)\n16\t- a generic **audience service** (FR-3..FR-8)\n17\t- an **announcements service** with permissions, visibility, publishing, stats and reminders (FR-9..FR-31)\n18\t- 12 thin route handlers (FR-34)\n19\t- 6 pages plus a course tab, a nav badge and seed data (FR-13..FR-35)\n20\t\n21\tThe two design centres are:\n22\t\n23\t1. **One set of audience rules, three consumers.** A per-user `AudienceKeys` set drives a pure matcher (`isUserInAudience`), a Prisma `where` fragment (feed, unread-count), and the inverse `resolveAudienceUserIds` expansion (preview, stats, notify). The read path never expands recipients (NFR-2).\n24\t2. **Visibility is decided at read time.** One `visibleWhere(now)` predicate is used everywhere. The cron only sends the one notification, claiming `notifiedAt` atomically (FR-16, FR-27).\n25\t\n26\t### Blockers from intake\n27\t\n28\t`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`**. There are no blockers to surface.\n29\t\n30\t### Assumptions and decisions carried into the design\n31\t\n32\t| # | Item | Decision | Req |\n33\t|---|---|---|---|\n34\t| A1 | Section membership scope | `SectionMember` rows of the targeted section. A section belongs to one academic year, so this is the current-year membership whenever the section is current. Composer pickers offer only current-year sections. | FR-5 |\n35\t| A2 | Zero-recipient drafts | Allowed. The zero-recipient refusal (`VALIDATION_ERROR`) runs only on the transition to PUBLISHED or SCHEDULED. | FR-15 |\n36\t| A3 | Parent expansion | Parents are reached only through ACTIVE, non-archived students. The ACTIVE/non-archived filter is applied to every final user. The matcher follows the same rule. | FR-3..FR-6 |\n37\t| A4 | Pins beyond 3 | The 3 newest pinned items go on top of page 1. Any further pinned items fall into newest-first order. | FR-17 |\n38\t| A5 | AC-8 fixture | The seed stays skip-if-missing. The integration/e2e fixture creates Pat's 6A child and the `ParentStudentLink`. | FR-22, FR-35, NFR-10 |\n39\t| A6 | Archived courses | Courses with `archivedAt != null` are excluded from every teacher branch and from the COURSE student branch. Not stated in the PRD, so flagged here. | FR-4..FR-6 |\n40\t| A7 | Archive is terminal | Archive is terminal for authors: PATCH on an ARCHIVED row by a non-admin returns 409 CONFLICT. Admins may still edit. | FR-12 |\n41\t| A8 | Reminder throttle | Nullable `Announcement.lastRemindedAt` column. A refused reminder returns **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ADR-4). | FR-25 |\n42\t| A9 | `mandatoryInApp` per instance | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is static (B9). Keep the **single type key `announcement.published`** with `mandatoryInApp: false`, and add an optional `mandatoryInApp?: boolean` override to `NotifyInput`. `notify()` passes `{ ...def, mandatoryInApp: input.mandatoryInApp ?? def.mandatoryInApp }` to `resolvePrefs`. Announcements set it to `requiresAck`. This is a one-line change to a shared function, and it keeps the type name exactly as FR-26 states. The rejected alternative was a second `announcement.published_ack` type. | FR-26 |\n43\t| A10 | Non-member responses | Detail, ack, stats and remind return **404 NOT_FOUND** to callers who are not allowed to see the announcement, so its existence is not leaked. Targeting violations on create/update/preview return **403 FORBIDDEN** (AC-3). | NFR-3, NFR-6, FR-10 |\n44\t| A11 | Publish timestamp | Publish-now sets `publishAt = now`, so one column orders the feed and drives visibility (R4). | FR-16, FR-17 |\n45\t\n46\t### Deliberate additions to the FR-1 schema\n47\t\n48\tFR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". These additions are the minimum the other requirements force, and each is listed with its reason:\n49\t\n50\t- `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?`: needed by FR-25 (A8). Intake pre-approved it.\n51\t- Indexes: `AnnouncementAudience @@index([announcementId])` and `@@index([type, refId])`, `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])`, `@@index([authorId])`, `@@index([isPublic, status])`, and `AnnouncementRead @@index([userId])`. These serve NFR-2.\n52\t- Back-relations needed for Prisma to compile: `User.announcements Announcement[]`, `FileObject.announcementAttachments AnnouncementAttachment[]`. `AnnouncementRead.user` is a relation to `User` (`User.announcementReads`, cascade on user delete is not used; users are archived, not deleted) so the stats table can join names.\n53\t\n54\tEverything else matches the PRD block field for field. That includes `coverFileId` as a plain scalar with no FK relation, and `AnnouncementAudience` having no timestamps.\n55\t\n56\t---\n57\t\n58\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n59\t\n60\t### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + `prisma/migrations/20261112000000_add_announcements/` (FR-1)\n61\t\n62\t```prisma\n63\tenum AnnouncementStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED ARCHIVED }\n64\tenum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }\n65\t\n66\tmodel Announcement {\n67\t  // ...PRD fields verbatim...\n68\t  lastRemindedAt DateTime?                       // FR-25 addition\n69\t  @@index([status, publishAt])\n70\t  @@index([authorId])\n71\t  @@index([isPublic, status])\n72\t}\n73\tmodel AnnouncementAudience { /* PRD verbatim */ @@index([announcementId]) @@index([type, refId]) }\n74\tmodel AnnouncementAttachment { /* PRD verbatim */ @@index([announcementId]) }\n75\tmodel AnnouncementRead {\n76\t  /* PRD verbatim */\n77\t  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])\n78\t  @@index([userId])\n79\t}\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t### 2.2 Validation: `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts` (FR-2, FR-34)\n83\t\n84\tThis module is isomorphic: it is used by both the composer form (react-hook-form + zodResolver) and the handlers.\n85\t\n86\t- `audienceRowSchema`: `{ type, refId?, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers }`, with these refinements:\n87\t  - `refId` is required unless the type is SCHOOL or STAFF.\n88\t  - For ROLE, `refId` must be a `Role` value.\n89\t  - For GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE, at least one include flag must be true.\n90\t- `announcementInputSchema`, with these fields:\n91\t  - `title`: trimmed, 1..150 characters\n92\t  - `body`: 1..20,000 characters\n93\t  - `audiences`: 0..20 rows of `audienceRowSchema`\n94\t  - `pinned`, `requiresAck`, `isPublic`\n95\t  - `coverFileId?`, `attachmentFileIds` (0..10)\n96\t  - `mode`: `'draft' | 'publish' | 'schedule'`\n97\t  - `publishAt?` (ISO), `expiresAt?` (ISO)\n98\t\n99\t  Refinements on `announcementInputSchema`:\n100\t  - `mode === 'schedule'` requires `publishAt > now`.\n101\t  - `expiresAt` must be later than `publishAt ?? now`.\n102\t- `announcementPatchSchema`: `announcementInputSchema.partial()`.\n103\t- `feedQuerySchema`: `{ tab: 'all' | 'unread' | 'ack', courseId?, page, pageSize }`.\n104\t- `statsQuerySchema`: `{ filter?: 'unread' | 'unacked', format?: 'csv' }`.\n105\t- `previewAudienceSchema`: `{ audiences }`.\n106\t\n107\t### 2.3 Audience service: `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (FR-3..FR-8, NFR-2)\n108\t\n109\tThis module is generic. It never imports Announcement models (FR-8), and its input type is `AudienceRow = { type: AudienceType; refId: string | null; includeStudents: boolean; includeParents: boolean; includeTeachers: boolean }`. PRD-14 imports it unchanged.\n110\t\n111\t**`getAudienceKeys(userId) → AudienceKeys`** loads one user's keys with at most about 4 indexed queries. The keys are:\n112\t\n113\t```ts\n114\ttype AudienceKeys = {\n115\t  userId: string;\n116\t  role: Role;\n117\t  active: boolean;\n118\t  // As a STUDENT (own) or PARENT (per linked ACTIVE child)\n119\t  gradeLevelIds: Set<string>;\n120\t  sectionIds: Set<string>;   // SectionMember rows\n121\t  courseIds: Set<string>;    // ACTIVE enrollment, non-archived course\n122\t  // As a TEACHER\n123\t  teachCourseIds: Set<string>;   // teacherId or coTeacherIds has, non-archived\n124\t  teachSectionIds: Set<string>;  // homeroom ∪ Course.sectionId of taught courses\n125\t  teachGradeLevelIds: Set<string>; // Section.gradeLevelId of taught current-year courses\n126\t  // Parent only: which child produced each key (FR-22)\n127\t  childByKey: Map<string, { id: string; firstName: string }[]>; // key = `${type}:${refId}`\n128\t};\n129\t```\n130\t\n131\tAll the functions below use these keys.\n132\t\n133\t- **`matchesAudience(row, keys) → boolean`** is a pure function and the single source of the rules (R1). For an inactive user it returns false. Otherwise it matches by type:\n134\t\n135\t  | Type | Matches when |\n136\t  |---|---|\n137\t  | SCHOOL | always |\n138\t  | STAFF | role is ADMIN or TEACHER |\n139\t  | ROLE | role equals `refId` |\n140\t  | GRADE_LEVEL | (`includeStudents` and the user is a STUDENT and `gradeLevelIds` has `refId`) or (`includeParents` and the user is a PARENT and `gradeLevelIds` has `refId`) or (`includeTeachers` and `teachGradeLevelIds` has `refId`) |\n141\t  | SECTION | the same pattern with `sectionIds` and `teachSectionIds` |\n142\t  | COURSE | the same pattern with `courseIds` and `teachCourseIds` |\n143\t\n144\t- **`isUserInAudience(user, rows)`** returns `rows.some(r => matchesAudience(r, keys))`. Keys are passed in when the caller already has them (FR-7).\n145\t- **`audienceWhere(keys) → Prisma.AnnouncementAudienceWhereInput`** builds the SQL form of the same table: an `OR` of `{ type, refId: { in: [...] }, include<Flag>: true }` branches, built only for the non-empty key sets. The feed uses it as `audiences: { some: audienceWhere(keys) }`, which compiles to `EXISTS` (ADR-2).\n146\t- **`resolveAudienceUserIds(rows) → string[]`** expands recipients. It runs one `user.findMany({ select: { id } })` per row/flag branch, takes the union in a `Set`, and then applies one final `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null` filter. Students that feed the parent branches are filtered to ACTIVE first (A3).\n147\t- **`countAudienceByRole(rows)`** runs `resolveAudienceUserIds` and then `user.groupBy(role)`. It serves the preview and reach figures.\n148\t- **`audienceLabels(rows) → string[]`** batch-loads GradeLevel, Section and Course names and produces chips such as \"Grade 7 · Parents\" or \"MATH-7A · Students, Parents\" (FR-18).\n149\t\n150\tAgreement between the matcher and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is not assumed. NFR-10's property test checks `isUserInAudience(u, rows) === resolveAudienceUserIds(rows).includes(u.id)` for every seed user and every seed row.\n151\t\n152\t### 2.4 Announcements service: `src/server/announcements/announcements-service.ts` (FR-9..FR-31, FR-36)\n153\t\n154\t| Function | Responsibility | Req |\n155\t|---|---|---|\n156\t| `visibleWhere(now)` | `status IN (SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) AND publishAt <= now AND (expiresAt IS NULL OR expiresAt > now)`. Used by the feed, detail, ack, unread-count, files and public news. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-6 |\n157\t| `isVisible(a, now)` | The same predicate in JS, for single rows. | FR-16 |\n158\t| `displayStatus(a, now)` | Derives SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED, EXPIRED, ARCHIVED or DRAFT for the manage view, so the status is correct between cron ticks (R5). | FR-23 |\n159\t| `assertCanTarget(user, rows, isPublic)` | ADMIN may target anything. TEACHER may target only COURSE rows for courses where they are `teacherId` or in `coTeacherIds` (the same test as `course-access.ts`), and SECTION rows where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Every other case, including `isPublic`, throws 403 FORBIDDEN. | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-3 |\n160\t| `createAnnouncement(user, input)` | `requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)` at the route, then `assertCanTarget`, then the zero-recipient check if the mode is not draft (FR-15). A transaction creates the announcement, audience rows and attachment rows and calls `attachFiles(tx, 'announcement', id, [cover, ...attachments])`. Files are attached even for drafts (R9, B7). After commit, `mode = publish` calls `claimAndNotify(id, now)`. | FR-11, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-27 |\n161\t| `updateAnnouncement(user, id, patch)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN, otherwise 404. ARCHIVED rows edited by a non-admin return 409 (A7). If `audiences` or `isPublic` is in the patch, it re-runs `assertCanTarget` on the **resulting** values (R8). The audience is replaced wholesale inside the transaction, and attachments are re-synced (attach new, detach removed). A transition to publish or schedule re-checks for zero recipients. It never clears `notifiedAt` (FR-29). An admin editing someone else's row triggers `audit('announcement.update')`. | FR-12, FR-29 |\n162\t| `archiveAnnouncement(user, id)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN. Sets `status = ARCHIVED`. An admin archiving someone else's row triggers `audit('announcement.archive')`. | FR-12 |\n163\t| `listFeed(user, { tab, courseId, page })` | Loads the keys, then queries `visibleWhere ∧ audiences.some(audienceWhere(keys))`, adding the `courseId` filter when present (`audiences.some{type: COURSE, refId}` after `assertCanViewCourse`). The `tab` filter: `unread` → `reads.none{userId}`; `ack` → `requiresAck ∧ reads.none{userId, acknowledgedAt not null}`. Page 1 prepends up to 3 pinned items (`take 3`, ordered by `publishAt desc`) and excludes them from the main list (A4). The main list is ordered by `publishAt desc, id desc`. Each row includes `reads where userId`, `_count.attachments` and the author name and role. DTOs add `excerpt`, `labels` and, for parents, `forChildren`. | FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-2 |\n164\t| `unreadCount(user)` | `count` over the same `where` as the feed plus `reads.none{userId}`. | FR-32 |\n165\t| `getForViewer(user, id)` | Visible to ADMIN, the author, or a user for whom `isVisible ∧ isUserInAudience` holds. Everyone else gets 404. For audience members only, it upserts `AnnouncementRead { readAt }` and keeps the existing `readAt`. Returns the body (rendered client-side with `MarkdownView`), attachments, the viewer's read row and `canEdit`. | FR-19, NFR-6 |\n166\t| `acknowledge(user, id)` | Requires `isVisible ∧ isUserInAudience`, otherwise 404. A row with `!requiresAck` returns 409 CONFLICT. Upserts with `acknowledgedAt` set once; repeat calls are idempotent and return the original time. | FR-20 |\n167\t| `previewAudience(user, rows)` | `assertCanTarget(user, rows, false)` first, so teachers cannot probe the sizes of other audiences. Then `countAudienceByRole`. Returns `{ total, byRole }`. | FR-14 |\n168\t| `listManage(user, page)` | No visibility filter. TEACHER sees `authorId = me`; ADMIN sees everything. For each row on the page it computes `reach = resolveAudienceUserIds(rows).length`, `read% = reads(readAt) ∩ recipients / reach`, and `ack%` when `requiresAck`. `ponytail:` live reach is computed per page row (pageSize ≤ 50). Snapshot a `recipientCount` if this gets slow. | FR-23 |\n169\t| `getStats(user, id, filter)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN, otherwise 404. Recipients come from the live `resolveAudienceUserIds`, left-joined to reads. Returns the counts `{ recipients, read, acknowledged, readPct, ackPct }` and the rows `{ name, role, readAt, acknowledgedAt }`, filtered by unread or unacked. Reads from users who have left the audience are excluded (R11). | FR-24 |\n170\t| `statsCsv(rows)` | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` with the columns Name, Role, Read at and Acknowledged at, formatted in the school timezone. | FR-24, NFR-7 |\n171\t| `sendReminder(user, id, now)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN, otherwise 404. Requires `requiresAck ∧ isVisible`, otherwise 409. Claims atomically with `updateMany({ where: { id, OR: [{ lastRemindedAt: null }, { lastRemindedAt: { lte: now − 24h } }] }, data: { lastRemindedAt: now } })`. A count of 0 throws 429 RATE_LIMITED with `{ retryAfter }`. Otherwise it notifies `recipients − acknowledged` with `announcement.reminder` and returns `{ notified }`. | FR-25, AC-5 |\n172\t| `claimAndNotify(id, now)` | `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null, ...visibleWhere(now) }, data: { notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED } })`. If the count is 1, it resolves recipients and calls `notify()` in chunks of 1,000 (R7). This is the only code path that sends `announcement.published`. | FR-27, FR-29 |\n173\t| `getPublicNews({ page })` | `isPublic ∧ visibleWhere(now)`. The DTO is `{ id, title, excerpt, body, publishAt, coverFileId, attachments[{ id, name }] }`, with no author email and no audience. | FR-31 |\n174\t\n175\tHelpers that live beside the service:\n176\t\n177\t- **`src/server/announcements/excerpt.ts`**: `toPlainText(md, max)`, a regex strip plus truncation (ADR-5). Its output is only ever rendered as escaped text (NFR-4). It produces the 200-character card excerpt (FR-18) and the 300-character email body (FR-28).\n178\t- **`src/server/announcements/maintenance.ts`**: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)`. It does `findMany({ where: { status: SCHEDULED, notifiedAt: null, publishAt: { lte: now } }, take: 50, select: { id } })`, then runs `claimAndNotify` for each id and logs `{ claimed }`. It copies the claim pattern in `quiz/maintenance.ts` (FR-27, NFR-11).\n179\t- **`src/server/announcements/files.ts`**: `announcementFileResolver(user, file)`. It loads the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic ∧ isVisible`, it allows access (including when `user` is null). Otherwise:\n180\t  - no user: deny\n181\t  - ADMIN or author: allow\n182\t  - `isVisible ∧ isUserInAudience`: allow\n183\t  - anything else: deny\n184\t\n185\t  It is registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` in `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (FR-30, B8).\n186\t\n187\t### 2.5 Existing modules touched (NFR-8)\n188\t\n189\t| File | Change | Req |\n190\t|---|---|---|\n191\t| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `'announcement.published'` (COMMUNICATION, `defaultEmail: true`, `mandatoryInApp: false`, roles ALL) and `'announcement.reminder'` (COMMUNICATION, `defaultEmail: true`, `mandatoryInApp: true`, roles ALL). | FR-26 |\n192\t| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | Optional `NotifyInput.mandatoryInApp` override (A9). | FR-26 |\n193\t| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await publishDueAnnouncements(now) } catch (e) { logger.error }` block alongside the existing passes. | FR-27 |\n194\t| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `register('announcement', announcementFileResolver)`. | FR-30 |\n195\t| `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Add `'/api/public/news'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. | FR-31 |\n196\t| `src/config/navigation.ts` + sidebar component | Add an optional `badgeEndpoint?: string` to `NavItem`, and an Announcements entry for all roles with `badgeEndpoint: '/api/announcements/unread-count'`. The sidebar wraps the icon in MUI `Badge` and polls every 30 s, gated by visibility, copying `NotificationBell`. | FR-32 |\n197\t| `src/config/course-tabs.ts` | `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => '/courses/' + id + '/announcements', roles: ALL_ROLES }`. | FR-21 |\n198\t| `prisma/seed.ts` | Six announcements, idempotent by `(title, authorId)`. MATH-7A and Grade 7 targets are skipped when missing. Already-published seeds get `notifiedAt = now`, so seeding never sends notifications. | FR-35 |\n199\t\n200\t### 2.6 API layer: `src/app/api/**` (FR-34)\n201\t\n202\tEvery handler is `withHandler` → `requireUser` or `requireRole` → `parseQuery` or `parseBody` (Zod) → one service call → `ok` or `paginated`. No business logic lives in routes.\n203\t\n204\t| Route file | Methods | Role gate |\n205\t|---|---|---|\n206\t| `announcements/route.ts` | GET (feed), POST (create) | any / ADMIN, TEACHER |\n207\t| `announcements/unread-count/route.ts` | GET | any |\n208\t| `announcements/preview-audience/route.ts` | POST | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n209\t| `announcements/manage/route.ts` | GET | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n210\t| `announcements/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH | any (service gates) / ADMIN, TEACHER |\n211\t| `announcements/[id]/archive/route.ts` | POST | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n212\t| `announcements/[id]/ack/route.ts` | POST | any (service gates) |\n213\t| `announcements/[id]/stats/route.ts` | GET (`?format=csv` → `text/csv` + `Content-Disposition`) | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n214\t| `announcements/[id]/remind/route.ts` | POST | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n215\t| `public/news/route.ts` | GET (no auth, `rateLimit` by IP, `parsePagination` clamp) | public |\n216\t\n217\tSTUDENT and PARENT callers hitting the ADMIN/TEACHER routes get 403 from `requireRole` (FR-11). The exact request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n218\t\n219\t### 2.7 UI layer: `src/app/(app)/announcements/**` (FR-13..FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-1, NFR-5)\n220\t\n221\tEach page is a server component that enforces access through the same service calls (NFR-3) and renders client components. All UI uses MUI only, and every component is looked up through mui-mcp before use.\n222\t\n223\t| Route | Components |\n224\t|---|---|\n225\t| `/announcements` | `PageHeader` with a \"New announcement\" button for ADMIN and TEACHER (FR-33). MUI `Tabs` for All, Unread and Requires acknowledgement. A list of `AnnouncementCard` (`Card`, `CardMedia` cover thumbnail via `/api/files/:id`, title, author and role, date in the school timezone, `Chip` labels, excerpt, attachment count, a \"For Sam\" `Chip` for parents, and an unread dot with `visuallyHidden` \"Unread\"). `Pagination` and `EmptyState`. |\n226\t| `/announcements/[id]` | Title and metadata, then `MarkdownView` for the body (NFR-4) and `FileList` for attachments. When `requiresAck`, a `Button` reading \"I acknowledge\" that becomes a disabled \"Acknowledged on 14 Sep\" (`formatInSchoolTz`, NFR-7). Edit and Stats links for the author and admins. |\n227\t| `/announcements/new`, `/announcements/[id]/edit` | `AnnouncementComposer` (react-hook-form + zodResolver): `TextField` title, `MarkdownEditor`, `FileUpload` (cover, context `announcement`), `FileUpload` + `FileList` (attachments), and `AudienceBuilder`. `AudienceBuilder` has rows of `Select` type → `Autocomplete` entity (grade levels, sections, courses, roles; teachers see only their own courses and homeroom) → three `Checkbox`es, plus a debounced (400 ms) preview line \"Will reach N people: …\". Further fields: `Switch`es for pinned, requires acknowledgement and public (admins only), a `RadioGroup` for Publish now / Schedule / Save draft, and `DateTimePicker`s for publishAt and expiresAt, converted from the school timezone to UTC on submit. Server errors surface through `useToast()`. |\n228\t| `/announcements/manage` | `DataTable` with the columns status chip (`displayStatus`), title, audience summary, reach, read % and ack %. Row actions are Edit, Stats and Archive (`ConfirmDialog`). |\n229\t| `/announcements/[id]/stats` | `StatCard`s for recipients, read % and ack %. A `DataTable` of recipients with an Unread / Not acknowledged `ToggleButtonGroup`, an \"Export CSV\" link (`?format=csv`) and \"Send reminder\" (`ConfirmDialog`; a 429 response is shown as a toast with the retry time). |\n230\t| `/courses/[id]/announcements` | The feed list component with `courseId`, behind `assertCanViewCourse`. |\n231\t\n232\t---\n233\t\n234\t## 3. Data Flow\n235\t\n236\t### 3.1 Create and publish now (FR-10, FR-13..FR-15, FR-27, FR-28)\n237\t\n238\t```\n239\tComposer ──POST /api/announcements──► withHandler → requireRole(ADMIN,TEACHER) → parseBody(announcementInputSchema)\n240\t  → assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)          ── 403 on violation (AC-3)\n241\t  → countAudienceByRole(audiences).total === 0 ?        ── 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (not for drafts)\n242\t  → $transaction: create Announcement{status:PUBLISHED, publishAt:now} + audiences + attachments; attachFiles(...)\n243\t  → (after commit) claimAndNotify(id, now)\n244\t       updateMany(id, notifiedAt null, visible) → count 1\n245\t       → resolveAudienceUserIds → notify({type:'announcement.published', userIds (chunks of 1k), title,\n246\t           body: toPlainText(body,300), link:/announcements/id, mandatoryInApp: requiresAck,\n247\t           email:{template:'generic-notification', data:{title, body, link, ctaLabel:'Read announcement'}}})\n248\t  → 201 { announcement }\n249\t```\n250\t\n251\t### 3.2 Scheduled publish (FR-16, FR-27, AC-4)\n252\t\n253\t```\n254\tCreate with mode=schedule → status SCHEDULED, publishAt=T, notifiedAt null   (no notify)\n255\tBefore T: visibleWhere excludes it (publishAt > now)  → absent from feed, detail 404 for non-authors\n256\tAt/after T: visibleWhere includes it immediately on read (no cron needed)\n257\tCron  POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (CRON_SECRET) → publishDueAnnouncements(now)\n258\t       → findMany(SCHEDULED, notifiedAt null, publishAt<=now, take 50)\n259\t       → claimAndNotify(id) per row; concurrent runs: only one updateMany gets count 1 → exactly one send\n260\t```\n261\t\n262\t### 3.3 Feed read (FR-17, FR-22, NFR-2)\n263\t\n264\t```\n265\tGET /api/announcements?tab=&courseId=&page=\n266\t  → getAudienceKeys(user)            ~4 indexed queries (parent: children → profiles, section members, enrollments)\n267\t  → findMany(visibleWhere(now) ∧ audiences.some(audienceWhere(keys)) ∧ tab filter)\n268\t       EXISTS over AnnouncementAudience(type, refId) index; Announcement(status, publishAt) index\n269\t  → page 1: pinned take 3 first, then the rest newest-first\n270\t  → DTO: excerpt (toPlainText 200), labels (audienceLabels, batched), unread flag, forChildren (keys.childByKey)\n271\t```\n272\t\n273\tThe target is under 200 ms for a parent with 3 children and 2,000 announcements. NFR-10 includes an optional timing check in the integration suite.\n274\t\n275\t### 3.4 Detail, read and acknowledge (FR-19, FR-20)\n276\t\n277\t```\n278\tGET /:id → admin|author|(visible ∧ member) else 404 → member: upsert AnnouncementRead{readAt}\n279\tPOST /:id/ack → visible ∧ member else 404; !requiresAck → 409 → upsert {acknowledgedAt: existing ?? now}\n280\t```\n281\t\n282\t### 3.5 Stats and reminder (FR-24, FR-25, AC-5)\n283\t\n284\t```\n285\tGET /:id/stats → author|admin else 404 → recipients = resolveAudienceUserIds; join reads\n286\t   50 recipients, 30 acked → ackPct 60\n287\tPOST /:id/remind → claim lastRemindedAt (≤ now−24h) → 0 rows → 429 {retryAfter}\n288\t   → notify('announcement.reminder', recipients − acked)  → { notified: 20 }\n289\t```\n290\t\n291\t### 3.6 Files and public news (FR-30, FR-31, AC-7)\n292\t\n293\t```\n294\tGET /api/files/:id (already public route) → access registry → announcementFileResolver(user|null, file)\n295\tGET /api/public/news?page= (no session) → getPublicNews → isPublic ∧ visible → public DTO\n296\t```\n297\t\n298\t---\n299\t\n300\t## 4. Cross-cutting Rules\n301\t\n302\t- **Security (NFR-3, NFR-6).** Every handler and server page calls `requireUser` or `requireRole`. Ownership, membership and targeting checks live in the service, so pages and routes share them. Non-members get 404; targeting violations get 403.\n303\t- **Sanitisation (NFR-4).** The body renders only through `MarkdownView` (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize). Excerpts and email bodies are plain text from `toPlainText`, rendered as escaped text and never through `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.\n304\t- **Timezones (NFR-7).** All columns are UTC. Composer inputs are interpreted in `getSchoolTimezone()` (imported from `assignments-service.ts`, B15) and converted with `date-fns-tz`. All dates are displayed with `formatInSchoolTz`.\n305\t- **Logging (NFR-11).** All new server code logs through `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. `console.*` is used only in the existing seed style.\n306\t- **UI rule (NFR-1).** MUI only. Toasts go through `useToast`, confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`, pickers through `Autocomplete` and `DateTimePicker`. The existing `eslint-no-restricted-imports` unit test guards against banned libraries. If mui-mcp is unreachable during development, report a blocker.\n307\t- **Scope (NFR-9).** No comments, reactions, translation, SMS or public website pages. Only `getPublicNews` and `/api/public/news` are exposed.\n308\t\n309\t## 5. Test Plan Mapping (NFR-10)\n310\t\n311\t| Layer | File | Covers |\n312\t|---|---|---|\n313\t| Unit | `tests/unit/announcements/audience-match.test.ts` | `matchesAudience` for every type × flag combination × role, using hand-built keys and no DB (FR-3..FR-6). |\n314\t| Unit | `tests/unit/announcements/permissions.test.ts` | `assertCanTarget` for admin, teacher course, co-teacher, homeroom, foreign course, SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL and `isPublic` (FR-9, FR-10). |\n315\t| Unit | `tests/unit/announcements/excerpt.test.ts` | `toPlainText` stripping and truncation (FR-18, FR-28). |\n316\t| Unit | `tests/unit/validators/announcements.test.ts` | Zod limits and refinements (FR-2). |\n317\t| Integration | `tests/integration/announcements/audience-agreement.test.ts` | For every seed and fixture user × every audience row, `isUserInAudience` equals membership in `resolveAudienceUserIds` (FR-7). |\n318\t| Integration | `tests/integration/announcements/publish.test.ts` | `publishDueAnnouncements` run twice and concurrently produces one notification set; FR-29 no re-notify on PATCH; AC-4. |\n319\t| Integration | `tests/integration/announcements/api.test.ts` | AC-1, AC-2, AC-3 (403), AC-5 (60%, 20 notified, 429), AC-6, AC-7, AC-8 (the fixture creates Pat's 6A child). |\n320\t| E2E | `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts` | Admin composes a Grade 7 parents announcement with ack, Pat reads and acknowledges, admin opens stats. |\n321\t\n322\t---\n323\t\n324\t## 6. Requirements Traceability\n325\t\n326\t| Req | Design element(s) |\n327\t|---|---|\n328\t| FR-1 | §2.1 schema and migration `20261112000000_add_announcements`; additions listed in §1 |\n329\t| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts` |\n330\t| FR-3 | §2.3 `resolveAudienceUserIds`, `matchesAudience` (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE); ACTIVE filter (A3) |\n331\t| FR-4 | §2.3 GRADE_LEVEL branches, `teachGradeLevelIds` (current year, non-archived, A6) |\n332\t| FR-5 | §2.3 SECTION branches, SectionMember plus homeroom plus section courses (A1) |\n333\t| FR-6 | §2.3 COURSE branches, ACTIVE enrollment, `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` |\n334\t| FR-7 | §2.3 `isUserInAudience` on `AudienceKeys`; §5 agreement test |\n335\t| FR-8 | §2.3 generic `AudienceRow` input, no Announcement imports |\n336\t| FR-9 | §2.4 `assertCanTarget` ADMIN branch |\n337\t| FR-10 | §2.4 `assertCanTarget` TEACHER branch on create, PATCH and preview; A10 |\n338\t| FR-11 | §2.6 `requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)` on write routes |\n339\t| FR-12 | §2.4 `updateAnnouncement`, `archiveAnnouncement`, `audit()`; A7 |\n340\t| FR-13 | §2.7 `AnnouncementComposer`, `AudienceBuilder` |\n341\t| FR-14 | §2.4 `previewAudience`, §2.3 `countAudienceByRole`; §2.7 debounced preview line |\n342\t| FR-15 | §2.4 zero-recipient check on publish or schedule only (A2) |\n343\t| FR-16 | §2.4 `visibleWhere`, `isVisible`; §3.2 |\n344\t| FR-17 | §2.4 `listFeed` (tabs, pinned 3, newest first, pagination); A4, A11 |\n345\t| FR-18 | §2.4 feed DTO, `excerpt.ts`, `audienceLabels`; §2.7 `AnnouncementCard` |\n346\t| FR-19 | §2.4 `getForViewer` with read upsert; §2.7 detail page with `MarkdownView` |\n347\t| FR-20 | §2.4 `acknowledge`; §2.7 ack button with `formatInSchoolTz` |\n348\t| FR-21 | §2.5 course-tabs entry; §2.4 `listFeed` `courseId` filter with `assertCanViewCourse`; §2.7 course tab page |\n349\t| FR-22 | §2.3 `childByKey`; §2.4 `forChildren` in the DTO; §2.7 \"For Sam\" chip |\n350\t| FR-23 | §2.4 `listManage`, `displayStatus`; §2.7 manage page |\n351\t| FR-24 | §2.4 `getStats`, `statsCsv`; §2.6 `?format=csv`; §2.7 stats page |\n352\t| FR-25 | §2.4 `sendReminder`, `lastRemindedAt` claim, 429 (A8) |\n353\t| FR-26 | §2.5 `types.ts` entries plus the `notify` `mandatoryInApp` override (A9) |\n354\t| FR-27 | §2.4 `claimAndNotify`, `maintenance.ts` `publishDueAnnouncements`; §2.5 dispatch route hook; §3.1, §3.2 |\n355\t| FR-28 | §3.1 notify email data (`generic-notification`, `toPlainText` 300, \"Read announcement\") |\n356\t| FR-29 | §2.4 `updateAnnouncement` never touches `notifiedAt`; the `claimAndNotify` claim |\n357\t| FR-30 | §2.4 `files.ts` `announcementFileResolver`; §2.5 `contexts.ts` registration |\n358\t| FR-31 | §2.4 `getPublicNews`; §2.6 `public/news/route.ts`; §2.5 `public-routes.ts` |\n359\t| FR-32 | §2.5 `NavItem.badgeEndpoint` plus sidebar `Badge`; §2.4 `unreadCount` |\n360\t| FR-33 | §2.7 feed `PageHeader` button for ADMIN and TEACHER |\n361\t| FR-34 | §2.6 route table, `withHandler` and Zod |\n362\t| FR-35 | §2.5 `prisma/seed.ts` (6 announcements, skip-if-missing, `notifiedAt` preset) |\n363\t| FR-36 | §2.3 and §2.4 files under `src/server/announcements/` |\n364\t| NFR-1 | §2.7 MUI-only components; §4 UI rule |\n365\t| NFR-2 | §2.1 indexes; §2.3 `audienceWhere` `EXISTS`; §3.3 |\n366\t| NFR-3 | §2.4 `assertCanTarget`; §2.6 role gates; §4 security |\n367\t| NFR-4 | §2.4 `excerpt.ts`; §2.7 `MarkdownView`; §4 sanitisation |\n368\t| NFR-5 | §2.7 unread dot with `visuallyHidden` \"Unread\" |\n369\t| NFR-6 | §2.4 `visibleWhere`, 404 for non-members; A10 |\n370\t| NFR-7 | §2.7 `DateTimePicker` in the school timezone; §4 timezones |\n371\t| NFR-8 | §2.5 existing modules reused; ADR-1 |\n372\t| NFR-9 | §4 scope |\n373\t| NFR-10 | §5 test plan |\n374\t| NFR-11 | §2.4 `maintenance.ts` logging; §4 logging |\n375\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b1bd2b-11e1-4a1f-b283-c14aefbd3b9a","uuid":"bf51fbfa-3044-416e-94f6-978c5b165e33","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:36:53.143Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-12 Announcements & News\n\nTicket: **SH-12** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T19:00:00Z · Status: **complete**\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 FR, 11 NFR, 94% confidence), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B22, R1–R11, A1–A8), and the FR-1 Prisma block in `12-announcements.md`.\n\n> This file replaces the SH-11 version that was here before.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nAnnouncements is a brownfield feature inside the existing Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/PostgreSQL + MUI 9 app. **No new dependencies** (ADR-1). The work is:\n\n- one Prisma migration (FR-1)\n- a generic **audience service** (FR-3..FR-8)\n- an **announcements service** with permissions, visibility, publishing, stats and reminders (FR-9..FR-31)\n- 12 thin route handlers (FR-34)\n- 6 pages plus a course tab, a nav badge and seed data (FR-13..FR-35)\n\nThe two design centres are:\n\n1. **One set of audience rules, three consumers.** A per-user `AudienceKeys` set drives a pure matcher (`isUserInAudience`), a Prisma `where` fragment (feed, unread-count), and the inverse `resolveAudienceUserIds` expansion (preview, stats, notify). The read path never expands recipients (NFR-2).\n2. **Visibility is decided at read time.** One `visibleWhere(now)` predicate is used everywhere. The cron only sends the one notification, claiming `notifiedAt` atomically (FR-16, FR-27).\n\n### Blockers from intake\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`**. There are no blockers to surface.\n\n### Assumptions and decisions carried into the design\n\n| # | Item | Decision | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Section membership scope | `SectionMember` rows of the targeted section. A section belongs to one academic year, so this is the current-year membership whenever the section is current. Composer pickers offer only current-year sections. | FR-5 |\n| A2 | Zero-recipient drafts | Allowed. The zero-recipient refusal (`VALIDATION_ERROR`) runs only on the transition to PUBLISHED or SCHEDULED. | FR-15 |\n| A3 | Parent expansion | Parents are reached only through ACTIVE, non-archived students. The ACTIVE/non-archived filter is applied to every final user. The matcher follows the same rule. | FR-3..FR-6 |\n| A4 | Pins beyond 3 | The 3 newest pinned items go on top of page 1. Any further pinned items fall into newest-first order. | FR-17 |\n| A5 | AC-8 fixture | The seed stays skip-if-missing. The integration/e2e fixture creates Pat's 6A child and the `ParentStudentLink`. | FR-22, FR-35, NFR-10 |\n| A6 | Archived courses | Courses with `archivedAt != null` are excluded from every teacher branch and from the COURSE student branch. Not stated in the PRD, so flagged here. | FR-4..FR-6 |\n| A7 | Archive is terminal | Archive is terminal for authors: PATCH on an ARCHIVED row by a non-admin returns 409 CONFLICT. Admins may still edit. | FR-12 |\n| A8 | Reminder throttle | Nullable `Announcement.lastRemindedAt` column. A refused reminder returns **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ADR-4). | FR-25 |\n| A9 | `mandatoryInApp` per instance | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is static (B9). Keep the **single type key `announcement.published`** with `mandatoryInApp: false`, and add an optional `mandatoryInApp?: boolean` override to `NotifyInput`. `notify()` passes `{ ...def, mandatoryInApp: input.mandatoryInApp ?? def.mandatoryInApp }` to `resolvePrefs`. Announcements set it to `requiresAck`. This is a one-line change to a shared function, and it keeps the type name exactly as FR-26 states. The rejected alternative was a second `announcement.published_ack` type. | FR-26 |\n| A10 | Non-member responses | Detail, ack, stats and remind return **404 NOT_FOUND** to callers who are not allowed to see the announcement, so its existence is not leaked. Targeting violations on create/update/preview return **403 FORBIDDEN** (AC-3). | NFR-3, NFR-6, FR-10 |\n| A11 | Publish timestamp | Publish-now sets `publishAt = now`, so one column orders the feed and drives visibility (R4). | FR-16, FR-17 |\n\n### Deliberate additions to the FR-1 schema\n\nFR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". These additions are the minimum the other requirements force, and each is listed with its reason:\n\n- `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?`: needed by FR-25 (A8). Intake pre-approved it.\n- Indexes: `AnnouncementAudience @@index([announcementId])` and `@@index([type, refId])`, `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])`, `@@index([authorId])`, `@@index([isPublic, status])`, and `AnnouncementRead @@index([userId])`. These serve NFR-2.\n- Back-relations needed for Prisma to compile: `User.announcements Announcement[]`, `FileObject.announcementAttachments AnnouncementAttachment[]`. `AnnouncementRead.user` is a relation to `User` (`User.announcementReads`, cascade on user delete is not used; users are archived, not deleted) so the stats table can join names.\n\nEverything else matches the PRD block field for field. That includes `coverFileId` as a plain scalar with no FK relation, and `AnnouncementAudience` having no timestamps.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + `prisma/migrations/20261112000000_add_announcements/` (FR-1)\n\n```prisma\nenum AnnouncementStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED ARCHIVED }\nenum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }\n\nmodel Announcement {\n  // ...PRD fields verbatim...\n  lastRemindedAt DateTime?                       // FR-25 addition\n  @@index([status, publishAt])\n  @@index([authorId])\n  @@index([isPublic, status])\n}\nmodel AnnouncementAudience { /* PRD verbatim */ @@index([announcementId]) @@index([type, refId]) }\nmodel AnnouncementAttachment { /* PRD verbatim */ @@index([announcementId]) }\nmodel AnnouncementRead {\n  /* PRD verbatim */\n  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])\n  @@index([userId])\n}\n```\n\n### 2.2 Validation: `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts` (FR-2, FR-34)\n\nThis module is isomorphic: it is used by both the composer form (react-hook-form + zodResolver) and the handlers.\n\n- `audienceRowSchema`: `{ type, refId?, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers }`, with these refinements:\n  - `refId` is required unless the type is SCHOOL or STAFF.\n  - For ROLE, `refId` must be a `Role` value.\n  - For GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE, at least one include flag must be true.\n- `announcementInputSchema`, with these fields:\n  - `title`: trimmed, 1..150 characters\n  - `body`: 1..20,000 characters\n  - `audiences`: 0..20 rows of `audienceRowSchema`\n  - `pinned`, `requiresAck`, `isPublic`\n  - `coverFileId?`, `attachmentFileIds` (0..10)\n  - `mode`: `'draft' | 'publish' | 'schedule'`\n  - `publishAt?` (ISO), `expiresAt?` (ISO)\n\n  Refinements on `announcementInputSchema`:\n  - `mode === 'schedule'` requires `publishAt > now`.\n  - `expiresAt` must be later than `publishAt ?? now`.\n- `announcementPatchSchema`: `announcementInputSchema.partial()`.\n- `feedQuerySchema`: `{ tab: 'all' | 'unread' | 'ack', courseId?, page, pageSize }`.\n- `statsQuerySchema`: `{ filter?: 'unread' | 'unacked', format?: 'csv' }`.\n- `previewAudienceSchema`: `{ audiences }`.\n\n### 2.3 Audience service: `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (FR-3..FR-8, NFR-2)\n\nThis module is generic. It never imports Announcement models (FR-8), and its input type is `AudienceRow = { type: AudienceType; refId: string | null; includeStudents: boolean; includeParents: boolean; includeTeachers: boolean }`. PRD-14 imports it unchanged.\n\n**`getAudienceKeys(userId) → AudienceKeys`** loads one user's keys with at most about 4 indexed queries. The keys are:\n\n```ts\ntype AudienceKeys = {\n  userId: string;\n  role: Role;\n  active: boolean;\n  // As a STUDENT (own) or PARENT (per linked ACTIVE child)\n  gradeLevelIds: Set<string>;\n  sectionIds: Set<string>;   // SectionMember rows\n  courseIds: Set<string>;    // ACTIVE enrollment, non-archived course\n  // As a TEACHER\n  teachCourseIds: Set<string>;   // teacherId or coTeacherIds has, non-archived\n  teachSectionIds: Set<string>;  // homeroom ∪ Course.sectionId of taught courses\n  teachGradeLevelIds: Set<string>; // Section.gradeLevelId of taught current-year courses\n  // Parent only: which child produced each key (FR-22)\n  childByKey: Map<string, { id: string; firstName: string }[]>; // key = `${type}:${refId}`\n};\n```\n\nAll the functions below use these keys.\n\n- **`matchesAudience(row, keys) → boolean`** is a pure function and the single source of the rules (R1). For an inactive user it returns false. Otherwise it matches by type:\n\n  | Type | Matches when |\n  |---|---|\n  | SCHOOL | always |\n  | STAFF | role is ADMIN or TEACHER |\n  | ROLE | role equals `refId` |\n  | GRADE_LEVEL | (`includeStudents` and the user is a STUDENT and `gradeLevelIds` has `refId`) or (`includeParents` and the user is a PARENT and `gradeLevelIds` has `refId`) or (`includeTeachers` and `teachGradeLevelIds` has `refId`) |\n  | SECTION | the same pattern with `sectionIds` and `teachSectionIds` |\n  | COURSE | the same pattern with `courseIds` and `teachCourseIds` |\n\n- **`isUserInAudience(user, rows)`** returns `rows.some(r => matchesAudience(r, keys))`. Keys are passed in when the caller already has them (FR-7).\n- **`audienceWhere(keys) → Prisma.AnnouncementAudienceWhereInput`** builds the SQL form of the same table: an `OR` of `{ type, refId: { in: [...] }, include<Flag>: true }` branches, built only for the non-empty key sets. The feed uses it as `audiences: { some: audienceWhere(keys) }`, which compiles to `EXISTS` (ADR-2).\n- **`resolveAudienceUserIds(rows) → string[]`** expands recipients. It runs one `user.findMany({ select: { id } })` per row/flag branch, takes the union in a `Set`, and then applies one final `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null` filter. Students that feed the parent branches are filtered to ACTIVE first (A3).\n- **`countAudienceByRole(rows)`** runs `resolveAudienceUserIds` and then `user.groupBy(role)`. It serves the preview and reach figures.\n- **`audienceLabels(rows) → string[]`** batch-loads GradeLevel, Section and Course names and produces chips such as \"Grade 7 · Parents\" or \"MATH-7A · Students, Parents\" (FR-18).\n\nAgreement between the matcher and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is not assumed. NFR-10's property test checks `isUserInAudience(u, rows) === resolveAudienceUserIds(rows).includes(u.id)` for every seed user and every seed row.\n\n### 2.4 Announcements service: `src/server/announcements/announcements-service.ts` (FR-9..FR-31, FR-36)\n\n| Function | Responsibility | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `visibleWhere(now)` | `status IN (SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) AND publishAt <= now AND (expiresAt IS NULL OR expiresAt > now)`. Used by the feed, detail, ack, unread-count, files and public news. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-6 |\n| `isVisible(a, now)` | The same predicate in JS, for single rows. | FR-16 |\n| `displayStatus(a, now)` | Derives SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED, EXPIRED, ARCHIVED or DRAFT for the manage view, so the status is correct between cron ticks (R5). | FR-23 |\n| `assertCanTarget(user, rows, isPublic)` | ADMIN may target anything. TEACHER may target only COURSE rows for courses where they are `teacherId` or in `coTeacherIds` (the same test as `course-access.ts`), and SECTION rows where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Every other case, including `isPublic`, throws 403 FORBIDDEN. | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-3 |\n| `createAnnouncement(user, input)` | `requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)` at the route, then `assertCanTarget`, then the zero-recipient check if the mode is not draft (FR-15). A transaction creates the announcement, audience rows and attachment rows and calls `attachFiles(tx, 'announcement', id, [cover, ...attachments])`. Files are attached even for drafts (R9, B7). After commit, `mode = publish` calls `claimAndNotify(id, now)`. | FR-11, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-27 |\n| `updateAnnouncement(user, id, patch)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN, otherwise 404. ARCHIVED rows edited by a non-admin return 409 (A7). If `audiences` or `isPublic` is in the patch, it re-runs `assertCanTarget` on the **resulting** values (R8). The audience is replaced wholesale inside the transaction, and attachments are re-synced (attach new, detach removed). A transition to publish or schedule re-checks for zero recipients. It never clears `notifiedAt` (FR-29). An admin editing someone else's row triggers `audit('announcement.update')`. | FR-12, FR-29 |\n| `archiveAnnouncement(user, id)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN. Sets `status = ARCHIVED`. An admin archiving someone else's row triggers `audit('announcement.archive')`. | FR-12 |\n| `listFeed(user, { tab, courseId, page })` | Loads the keys, then queries `visibleWhere ∧ audiences.some(audienceWhere(keys))`, adding the `courseId` filter when present (`audiences.some{type: COURSE, refId}` after `assertCanViewCourse`). The `tab` filter: `unread` → `reads.none{userId}`; `ack` → `requiresAck ∧ reads.none{userId, acknowledgedAt not null}`. Page 1 prepends up to 3 pinned items (`take 3`, ordered by `publishAt desc`) and excludes them from the main list (A4). The main list is ordered by `publishAt desc, id desc`. Each row includes `reads where userId`, `_count.attachments` and the author name and role. DTOs add `excerpt`, `labels` and, for parents, `forChildren`. | FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-2 |\n| `unreadCount(user)` | `count` over the same `where` as the feed plus `reads.none{userId}`. | FR-32 |\n| `getForViewer(user, id)` | Visible to ADMIN, the author, or a user for whom `isVisible ∧ isUserInAudience` holds. Everyone else gets 404. For audience members only, it upserts `AnnouncementRead { readAt }` and keeps the existing `readAt`. Returns the body (rendered client-side with `MarkdownView`), attachments, the viewer's read row and `canEdit`. | FR-19, NFR-6 |\n| `acknowledge(user, id)` | Requires `isVisible ∧ isUserInAudience`, otherwise 404. A row with `!requiresAck` returns 409 CONFLICT. Upserts with `acknowledgedAt` set once; repeat calls are idempotent and return the original time. | FR-20 |\n| `previewAudience(user, rows)` | `assertCanTarget(user, rows, false)` first, so teachers cannot probe the sizes of other audiences. Then `countAudienceByRole`. Returns `{ total, byRole }`. | FR-14 |\n| `listManage(user, page)` | No visibility filter. TEACHER sees `authorId = me`; ADMIN sees everything. For each row on the page it computes `reach = resolveAudienceUserIds(rows).length`, `read% = reads(readAt) ∩ recipients / reach`, and `ack%` when `requiresAck`. `ponytail:` live reach is computed per page row (pageSize ≤ 50). Snapshot a `recipientCount` if this gets slow. | FR-23 |\n| `getStats(user, id, filter)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN, otherwise 404. Recipients come from the live `resolveAudienceUserIds`, left-joined to reads. Returns the counts `{ recipients, read, acknowledged, readPct, ackPct }` and the rows `{ name, role, readAt, acknowledgedAt }`, filtered by unread or unacked. Reads from users who have left the audience are excluded (R11). | FR-24 |\n| `statsCsv(rows)` | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` with the columns Name, Role, Read at and Acknowledged at, formatted in the school timezone. | FR-24, NFR-7 |\n| `sendReminder(user, id, now)` | Allowed for the author or ADMIN, otherwise 404. Requires `requiresAck ∧ isVisible`, otherwise 409. Claims atomically with `updateMany({ where: { id, OR: [{ lastRemindedAt: null }, { lastRemindedAt: { lte: now − 24h } }] }, data: { lastRemindedAt: now } })`. A count of 0 throws 429 RATE_LIMITED with `{ retryAfter }`. Otherwise it notifies `recipients − acknowledged` with `announcement.reminder` and returns `{ notified }`. | FR-25, AC-5 |\n| `claimAndNotify(id, now)` | `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null, ...visibleWhere(now) }, data: { notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED } })`. If the count is 1, it resolves recipients and calls `notify()` in chunks of 1,000 (R7). This is the only code path that sends `announcement.published`. | FR-27, FR-29 |\n| `getPublicNews({ page })` | `isPublic ∧ visibleWhere(now)`. The DTO is `{ id, title, excerpt, body, publishAt, coverFileId, attachments[{ id, name }] }`, with no author email and no audience. | FR-31 |\n\nHelpers that live beside the service:\n\n- **`src/server/announcements/excerpt.ts`**: `toPlainText(md, max)`, a regex strip plus truncation (ADR-5). Its output is only ever rendered as escaped text (NFR-4). It produces the 200-character card excerpt (FR-18) and the 300-character email body (FR-28).\n- **`src/server/announcements/maintenance.ts`**: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)`. It does `findMany({ where: { status: SCHEDULED, notifiedAt: null, publishAt: { lte: now } }, take: 50, select: { id } })`, then runs `claimAndNotify` for each id and logs `{ claimed }`. It copies the claim pattern in `quiz/maintenance.ts` (FR-27, NFR-11).\n- **`src/server/announcements/files.ts`**: `announcementFileResolver(user, file)`. It loads the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic ∧ isVisible`, it allows access (including when `user` is null). Otherwise:\n  - no user: deny\n  - ADMIN or author: allow\n  - `isVisible ∧ isUserInAudience`: allow\n  - anything else: deny\n\n  It is registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` in `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (FR-30, B8).\n\n### 2.5 Existing modules touched (NFR-8)\n\n| File | Change | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `'announcement.published'` (COMMUNICATION, `defaultEmail: true`, `mandatoryInApp: false`, roles ALL) and `'announcement.reminder'` (COMMUNICATION, `defaultEmail: true`, `mandatoryInApp: true`, roles ALL). | FR-26 |\n| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | Optional `NotifyInput.mandatoryInApp` override (A9). | FR-26 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await publishDueAnnouncements(now) } catch (e) { logger.error }` block alongside the existing passes. | FR-27 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `register('announcement', announcementFileResolver)`. | FR-30 |\n| `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Add `'/api/public/news'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. | FR-31 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` + sidebar component | Add an optional `badgeEndpoint?: string` to `NavItem`, and an Announcements entry for all roles with `badgeEndpoint: '/api/announcements/unread-count'`. The sidebar wraps the icon in MUI `Badge` and polls every 30 s, gated by visibility, copying `NotificationBell`. | FR-32 |\n| `src/config/course-tabs.ts` | `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => '/courses/' + id + '/announcements', roles: ALL_ROLES }`. | FR-21 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | Six announcements, idempotent by `(title, authorId)`. MATH-7A and Grade 7 targets are skipped when missing. Already-published seeds get `notifiedAt = now`, so seeding never sends notifications. | FR-35 |\n\n### 2.6 API layer: `src/app/api/**` (FR-34)\n\nEvery handler is `withHandler` → `requireUser` or `requireRole` → `parseQuery` or `parseBody` (Zod) → one service call → `ok` or `paginated`. No business logic lives in routes.\n\n| Route file | Methods | Role gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| `announcements/route.ts` | GET (feed), POST (create) | any / ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `announcements/unread-count/route.ts` | GET | any |\n| `announcements/preview-audience/route.ts` | POST | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `announcements/manage/route.ts` | GET | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `announcements/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH | any (service gates) / ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `announcements/[id]/archive/route.ts` | POST | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `announcements/[id]/ack/route.ts` | POST | any (service gates) |\n| `announcements/[id]/stats/route.ts` | GET (`?format=csv` → `text/csv` + `Content-Disposition`) | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `announcements/[id]/remind/route.ts` | POST | ADMIN, TEACHER |\n| `public/news/route.ts` | GET (no auth, `rateLimit` by IP, `parsePagination` clamp) | public |\n\nSTUDENT and PARENT callers hitting the ADMIN/TEACHER routes get 403 from `requireRole` (FR-11). The exact request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.7 UI layer: `src/app/(app)/announcements/**` (FR-13..FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-1, NFR-5)\n\nEach page is a server component that enforces access through the same service calls (NFR-3) and renders client components. All UI uses MUI only, and every component is looked up through mui-mcp before use.\n\n| Route | Components |\n|---|---|\n| `/announcements` | `PageHeader` with a \"New announcement\" button for ADMIN and TEACHER (FR-33). MUI `Tabs` for All, Unread and Requires acknowledgement. A list of `AnnouncementCard` (`Card`, `CardMedia` cover thumbnail via `/api/files/:id`, title, author and role, date in the school timezone, `Chip` labels, excerpt, attachment count, a \"For Sam\" `Chip` for parents, and an unread dot with `visuallyHidden` \"Unread\"). `Pagination` and `EmptyState`. |\n| `/announcements/[id]` | Title and metadata, then `MarkdownView` for the body (NFR-4) and `FileList` for attachments. When `requiresAck`, a `Button` reading \"I acknowledge\" that becomes a disabled \"Acknowledged on 14 Sep\" (`formatInSchoolTz`, NFR-7). Edit and Stats links for the author and admins. |\n| `/announcements/new`, `/announcements/[id]/edit` | `AnnouncementComposer` (react-hook-form + zodResolver): `TextField` title, `MarkdownEditor`, `FileUpload` (cover, context `announcement`), `FileUpload` + `FileList` (attachments), and `AudienceBuilder`. `AudienceBuilder` has rows of `Select` type → `Autocomplete` entity (grade levels, sections, courses, roles; teachers see only their own courses and homeroom) → three `Checkbox`es, plus a debounced (400 ms) preview line \"Will reach N people: …\". Further fields: `Switch`es for pinned, requires acknowledgement and public (admins only), a `RadioGroup` for Publish now / Schedule / Save draft, and `DateTimePicker`s for publishAt and expiresAt, converted from the school timezone to UTC on submit. Server errors surface through `useToast()`. |\n| `/announcements/manage` | `DataTable` with the columns status chip (`displayStatus`), title, audience summary, reach, read % and ack %. Row actions are Edit, Stats and Archive (`ConfirmDialog`). |\n| `/announcements/[id]/stats` | `StatCard`s for recipients, read % and ack %. A `DataTable` of recipients with an Unread / Not acknowledged `ToggleButtonGroup`, an \"Export CSV\" link (`?format=csv`) and \"Send reminder\" (`ConfirmDialog`; a 429 response is shown as a toast with the retry time). |\n| `/courses/[id]/announcements` | The feed list component with `courseId`, behind `assertCanViewCourse`. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Create and publish now (FR-10, FR-13..FR-15, FR-27, FR-28)\n\n```\nComposer ──POST /api/announcements──► withHandler → requireRole(ADMIN,TEACHER) → parseBody(announcementInputSchema)\n  → assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)          ── 403 on violation (AC-3)\n  → countAudienceByRole(audiences).total === 0 ?        ── 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (not for drafts)\n  → $transaction: create Announcement{status:PUBLISHED, publishAt:now} + audiences + attachments; attachFiles(...)\n  → (after commit) claimAndNotify(id, now)\n       updateMany(id, notifiedAt null, visible) → count 1\n       → resolveAudienceUserIds → notify({type:'announcement.published', userIds (chunks of 1k), title,\n           body: toPlainText(body,300), link:/announcements/id, mandatoryInApp: requiresAck,\n           email:{template:'generic-notification', data:{title, body, link, ctaLabel:'Read announcement'}}})\n  → 201 { announcement }\n```\n\n### 3.2 Scheduled publish (FR-16, FR-27, AC-4)\n\n```\nCreate with mode=schedule → status SCHEDULED, publishAt=T, notifiedAt null   (no notify)\nBefore T: visibleWhere excludes it (publishAt > now)  → absent from feed, detail 404 for non-authors\nAt/after T: visibleWhere includes it immediately on read (no cron needed)\nCron  POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (CRON_SECRET) → publishDueAnnouncements(now)\n       → findMany(SCHEDULED, notifiedAt null, publishAt<=now, take 50)\n       → claimAndNotify(id) per row; concurrent runs: only one updateMany gets count 1 → exactly one send\n```\n\n### 3.3 Feed read (FR-17, FR-22, NFR-2)\n\n```\nGET /api/announcements?tab=&courseId=&page=\n  → getAudienceKeys(user)            ~4 indexed queries (parent: children → profiles, section members, enrollments)\n  → findMany(visibleWhere(now) ∧ audiences.some(audienceWhere(keys)) ∧ tab filter)\n       EXISTS over AnnouncementAudience(type, refId) index; Announcement(status, publishAt) index\n  → page 1: pinned take 3 first, then the rest newest-first\n  → DTO: excerpt (toPlainText 200), labels (audienceLabels, batched), unread flag, forChildren (keys.childByKey)\n```\n\nThe target is under 200 ms for a parent with 3 children and 2,000 announcements. NFR-10 includes an optional timing check in the integration suite.\n\n### 3.4 Detail, read and acknowledge (FR-19, FR-20)\n\n```\nGET /:id → admin|author|(visible ∧ member) else 404 → member: upsert AnnouncementRead{readAt}\nPOST /:id/ack → visible ∧ member else 404; !requiresAck → 409 → upsert {acknowledgedAt: existing ?? now}\n```\n\n### 3.5 Stats and reminder (FR-24, FR-25, AC-5)\n\n```\nGET /:id/stats → author|admin else 404 → recipients = resolveAudienceUserIds; join reads\n   50 recipients, 30 acked → ackPct 60\nPOST /:id/remind → claim lastRemindedAt (≤ now−24h) → 0 rows → 429 {retryAfter}\n   → notify('announcement.reminder', recipients − acked)  → { notified: 20 }\n```\n\n### 3.6 Files and public news (FR-30, FR-31, AC-7)\n\n```\nGET /api/files/:id (already public route) → access registry → announcementFileResolver(user|null, file)\nGET /api/public/news?page= (no session) → getPublicNews → isPublic ∧ visible → public DTO\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting Rules\n\n- **Security (NFR-3, NFR-6).** Every handler and server page calls `requireUser` or `requireRole`. Ownership, membership and targeting checks live in the service, so pages and routes share them. Non-members get 404; targeting violations get 403.\n- **Sanitisation (NFR-4).** The body renders only through `MarkdownView` (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize). Excerpts and email bodies are plain text from `toPlainText`, rendered as escaped text and never through `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.\n- **Timezones (NFR-7).** All columns are UTC. Composer inputs are interpreted in `getSchoolTimezone()` (imported from `assignments-service.ts`, B15) and converted with `date-fns-tz`. All dates are displayed with `formatInSchoolTz`.\n- **Logging (NFR-11).** All new server code logs through `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. `console.*` is used only in the existing seed style.\n- **UI rule (NFR-1).** MUI only. Toasts go through `useToast`, confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`, pickers through `Autocomplete` and `DateTimePicker`. The existing `eslint-no-restricted-imports` unit test guards against banned libraries. If mui-mcp is unreachable during development, report a blocker.\n- **Scope (NFR-9).** No comments, reactions, translation, SMS or public website pages. Only `getPublicNews` and `/api/public/news` are exposed.\n\n## 5. Test Plan Mapping (NFR-10)\n\n| Layer | File | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit | `tests/unit/announcements/audience-match.test.ts` | `matchesAudience` for every type × flag combination × role, using hand-built keys and no DB (FR-3..FR-6). |\n| Unit | `tests/unit/announcements/permissions.test.ts` | `assertCanTarget` for admin, teacher course, co-teacher, homeroom, foreign course, SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL and `isPublic` (FR-9, FR-10). |\n| Unit | `tests/unit/announcements/excerpt.test.ts` | `toPlainText` stripping and truncation (FR-18, FR-28). |\n| Unit | `tests/unit/validators/announcements.test.ts` | Zod limits and refinements (FR-2). |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/announcements/audience-agreement.test.ts` | For every seed and fixture user × every audience row, `isUserInAudience` equals membership in `resolveAudienceUserIds` (FR-7). |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/announcements/publish.test.ts` | `publishDueAnnouncements` run twice and concurrently produces one notification set; FR-29 no re-notify on PATCH; AC-4. |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/announcements/api.test.ts` | AC-1, AC-2, AC-3 (403), AC-5 (60%, 20 notified, 429), AC-6, AC-7, AC-8 (the fixture creates Pat's 6A child). |\n| E2E | `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts` | Admin composes a Grade 7 parents announcement with ack, Pat reads and acknowledges, admin opens stats. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema and migration `20261112000000_add_announcements`; additions listed in §1 |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts` |\n| FR-3 | §2.3 `resolveAudienceUserIds`, `matchesAudience` (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE); ACTIVE filter (A3) |\n| FR-4 | §2.3 GRADE_LEVEL branches, `teachGradeLevelIds` (current year, non-archived, A6) |\n| FR-5 | §2.3 SECTION branches, SectionMember plus homeroom plus section courses (A1) |\n| FR-6 | §2.3 COURSE branches, ACTIVE enrollment, `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` |\n| FR-7 | §2.3 `isUserInAudience` on `AudienceKeys`; §5 agreement test |\n| FR-8 | §2.3 generic `AudienceRow` input, no Announcement imports |\n| FR-9 | §2.4 `assertCanTarget` ADMIN branch |\n| FR-10 | §2.4 `assertCanTarget` TEACHER branch on create, PATCH and preview; A10 |\n| FR-11 | §2.6 `requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)` on write routes |\n| FR-12 | §2.4 `updateAnnouncement`, `archiveAnnouncement`, `audit()`; A7 |\n| FR-13 | §2.7 `AnnouncementComposer`, `AudienceBuilder` |\n| FR-14 | §2.4 `previewAudience`, §2.3 `countAudienceByRole`; §2.7 debounced preview line |\n| FR-15 | §2.4 zero-recipient check on publish or schedule only (A2) |\n| FR-16 | §2.4 `visibleWhere`, `isVisible`; §3.2 |\n| FR-17 | §2.4 `listFeed` (tabs, pinned 3, newest first, pagination); A4, A11 |\n| FR-18 | §2.4 feed DTO, `excerpt.ts`, `audienceLabels`; §2.7 `AnnouncementCard` |\n| FR-19 | §2.4 `getForViewer` with read upsert; §2.7 detail page with `MarkdownView` |\n| FR-20 | §2.4 `acknowledge`; §2.7 ack button with `formatInSchoolTz` |\n| FR-21 | §2.5 course-tabs entry; §2.4 `listFeed` `courseId` filter with `assertCanViewCourse`; §2.7 course tab page |\n| FR-22 | §2.3 `childByKey`; §2.4 `forChildren` in the DTO; §2.7 \"For Sam\" chip |\n| FR-23 | §2.4 `listManage`, `displayStatus`; §2.7 manage page |\n| FR-24 | §2.4 `getStats`, `statsCsv`; §2.6 `?format=csv`; ��2.7 stats page |\n| FR-25 | §2.4 `sendReminder`, `lastRemindedAt` claim, 429 (A8) |\n| FR-26 | §2.5 `types.ts` entries plus the `notify` `mandatoryInApp` override (A9) |\n| FR-27 | §2.4 `claimAndNotify`, `maintenance.ts` `publishDueAnnouncements`; §2.5 dispatch route hook; §3.1, §3.2 |\n| FR-28 | §3.1 notify email data (`generic-notification`, `toPlainText` 300, \"Read announcement\") |\n| FR-29 | §2.4 `updateAnnouncement` never touches `notifiedAt`; the `claimAndNotify` claim |\n| FR-30 | §2.4 `files.ts` `announcementFileResolver`; §2.5 `contexts.ts` registration |\n| FR-31 | §2.4 `getPublicNews`; §2.6 `public/news/route.ts`; §2.5 `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-32 | §2.5 `NavItem.badgeEndpoint` plus sidebar `Badge`; §2.4 `unreadCount` |\n| FR-33 | §2.7 feed `PageHeader` button for ADMIN and TEACHER |\n| FR-34 | §2.6 route table, `withHandler` and Zod |\n| FR-35 | §2.5 `prisma/seed.ts` (6 announcements, skip-if-missing, `notifiedAt` preset) |\n| FR-36 | §2.3 and §2.4 files under `src/server/announcements/` |\n| NFR-1 | §2.7 MUI-only components; §4 UI rule |\n| NFR-2 | §2.1 indexes; §2.3 `audienceWhere` `EXISTS`; §3.3 |\n| NFR-3 | §2.4 `assertCanTarget`; §2.6 role gates; §4 security |\n| NFR-4 | §2.4 `excerpt.ts`; §2.7 `MarkdownView`; §4 sanitisation |\n| NFR-5 | §2.7 unread dot with `visuallyHidden` \"Unread\" |\n| NFR-6 | §2.4 `visibleWhere`, 404 for non-members; A10 |\n| NFR-7 | §2.7 `DateTimePicker` in the school timezone; §4 timezones |\n| NFR-8 | §2.5 existing modules reused; ADR-1 |\n| NFR-9 | §4 scope |\n| NFR-10 | §5 test plan |\n| NFR-11 | §2.4 `maintenance.ts` logging; §4 logging |\n","numLines":375,"startLine":1,"totalLines":375}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RLejnverU7iJUT3Z4PXL9P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
