{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nYDRSHaUJk7oV3b99QR8S","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:30:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"conventions\": {\n8\t    \"replaces\": \"This file replaces the SH-11 contracts that were here before.\",\n9\t    \"basePath\": \"/api (the existing SchoolHub convention, not /api/v1). Route files are src/app/api/**/route.ts. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n10\t    \"handlerPipeline\": \"withHandler → requireUser / requireRole → parseQuery / parseBody with a Zod schema from src/lib/validators/announcements.ts → one call into src/server/announcements/announcements-service.ts → ok(data) / ok(data, {status: 201}) / paginated(data, meta). No business logic in routes. Requirements: FR-34, FR-36, NFR-8.\",\n11\t    \"successEnvelope\": \"{ \\\"data\\\": <responseSchema> }. Paginated endpoints return { \\\"data\\\": [...], \\\"meta\\\": { page, pageSize, total } } via paginated() in src/server/http.ts. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n12\t    \"pagination\": \"?page (≥1, default 1) & ?pageSize (default 20, max 100 via parsePagination; GET /api/announcements/manage clamps to 50 because it computes live reach per row). Requirements: FR-17, FR-23, FR-31.\",\n13\t    \"errorEnvelope\": \"{ \\\"error\\\": { \\\"code\\\": ApiErrorCode, \\\"message\\\": string, \\\"details\\\"?: unknown } }. VALIDATION_ERROR 400 (Zod: details = error.flatten()), UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n14\t    \"accessErrors\": \"Targeting violations on create, update and preview return 403 FORBIDDEN (AC-3). STUDENT/PARENT on ADMIN/TEACHER routes get 403 from requireRole (FR-11). Callers who may not see a specific announcement (non-member, non-author, or not yet visible) get 404 NOT_FOUND on detail, ack, stats, remind, PATCH and archive, so its existence is not leaked (system-design A10). Requirements: NFR-3, NFR-6.\",\n15\t    \"dates\": \"All timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC strings. The composer converts SchoolSettings.timezone input to UTC before sending. Clients display with formatInSchoolTz. Requirement: NFR-7.\",\n16\t    \"visibility\": \"visible = status ∈ {SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED} ∧ publishAt ≤ now ∧ (expiresAt null ∨ expiresAt > now), evaluated at read time. Requirements: FR-16, NFR-6.\",\n17\t    \"sanitisation\": \"`body` is raw Markdown, rendered client-side only through MarkdownView (rehype-sanitize). `excerpt` is plain text from toPlainText and must be rendered as escaped text. Requirement: NFR-4.\"\n18\t  },\n19\t\n20\t  \"components\": {\n21\t    \"AudienceRow\": {\n22\t      \"description\": \"Generic audience row (FR-8). refId is required unless the type is SCHOOL or STAFF. For ROLE it must be a Role value. For GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE, at least one include flag must be true. Requirements: FR-1, FR-3..FR-6.\",\n23\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n24\t      \"properties\": {\n25\t        \"type\": { \"enum\": [\"SCHOOL\", \"STAFF\", \"ROLE\", \"GRADE_LEVEL\", \"SECTION\", \"COURSE\"] },\n26\t        \"refId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"GradeLevel.id | Section.id | Course.id | Role value\" },\n27\t        \"includeStudents\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true },\n28\t        \"includeParents\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true },\n29\t        \"includeTeachers\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true }\n30\t      },\n31\t      \"required\": [\"type\"]\n32\t    },\n33\t    \"AnnouncementInput\": {\n34\t      \"description\": \"Body of POST /api/announcements. Mirrors announcementInputSchema. Requirements: FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16.\",\n35\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n36\t      \"properties\": {\n37\t        \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 150, \"description\": \"Trimmed\" },\n38\t        \"body\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 20000, \"description\": \"Markdown\" },\n39\t        \"audiences\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceRow\" }, \"minItems\": 0, \"maxItems\": 20 },\n40\t        \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false },\n41\t        \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false },\n42\t        \"isPublic\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false, \"description\": \"ADMIN only. true from a TEACHER → 403 (FR-10)\" },\n43\t        \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"FileObject id uploaded with context 'announcement'\" },\n44\t        \"attachmentFileIds\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"maxItems\": 10, \"default\": [] },\n45\t        \"mode\": { \"enum\": [\"draft\", \"publish\", \"schedule\"] },\n46\t        \"publishAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\", \"description\": \"Required and > now when mode = schedule. Ignored for publish (set to now)\" },\n47\t        \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\", \"description\": \"Must be > (publishAt ?? now)\" }\n48\t      },\n49\t      \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\", \"audiences\", \"mode\"]\n50\t    },\n51\t    \"AnnouncementPatch\": {\n52\t      \"description\": \"AnnouncementInput with every field optional (announcementPatchSchema). audiences, when present, replaces all rows. Requirements: FR-12, FR-29.\",\n53\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n54\t      \"allOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementInput\" }],\n55\t      \"required\": []\n56\t    },\n57\t    \"Author\": {\n58\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n59\t      \"properties\": {\n60\t        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n61\t        \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n62\t        \"role\": { \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\"] }\n63\t      },\n64\t      \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"role\"]\n65\t    },\n66\t    \"Attachment\": {\n67\t      \"description\": \"Download via the existing GET /api/files/:id, gated by the 'announcement' file context (FR-30).\",\n68\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n69\t      \"properties\": {\n70\t        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"FileObject id\" },\n71\t        \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n72\t        \"mimeType\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n73\t        \"size\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n74\t      },\n75\t      \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\"]\n76\t    },\n77\t    \"FeedItem\": {\n78\t      \"description\": \"Feed card DTO. Requirements: FR-17, FR-18, FR-22, NFR-5.\",\n79\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n80\t      \"properties\": {\n81\t        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n82\t        \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n83\t        \"excerpt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 200, \"description\": \"Plain text (toPlainText(body, 200))\" },\n84\t        \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n85\t        \"author\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Author\" },\n86\t        \"publishAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n87\t        \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n88\t        \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"true only for the ≤3 items lifted to the top of page 1\" },\n89\t        \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n90\t        \"labels\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"Audience chips, e.g. 'Grade 7 · Parents'\" },\n91\t        \"attachmentCount\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n92\t        \"unread\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"No AnnouncementRead.readAt for the caller. UI shows a dot with visually hidden text 'Unread'\" },\n93\t        \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n94\t        \"forChildren\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"firstName\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }, \"description\": \"PARENT callers only; empty otherwise. The linked children that put the parent in a GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION or COURSE audience ('For Sam')\" }\n95\t      },\n96\t      \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"excerpt\", \"author\", \"publishAt\", \"pinned\", \"requiresAck\", \"labels\", \"attachmentCount\", \"unread\", \"forChildren\"]\n97\t    },\n98\t    \"AnnouncementDetail\": {\n99\t      \"description\": \"Full record for detail and edit. Requirements: FR-13, FR-19, FR-20.\",\n100\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n101\t      \"properties\": {\n102\t        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n103\t        \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n104\t        \"body\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Raw Markdown. Render only via MarkdownView\" },\n105\t        \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n106\t        \"displayStatus\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"EXPIRED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n107\t        \"author\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Author\" },\n108\t        \"audiences\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceRow\" }, \"description\": \"Returned only when canEdit; [] otherwise\" },\n109\t        \"labels\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n110\t        \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n111\t        \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n112\t        \"isPublic\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n113\t        \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n114\t        \"attachments\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Attachment\" } },\n115\t        \"publishAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n116\t        \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n117\t        \"createdAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n118\t        \"updatedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n119\t        \"myRead\": { \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"], \"properties\": { \"readAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" }, \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" } }, \"description\": \"null when the caller is not an audience member (for example an admin outside the audience)\" },\n120\t        \"canEdit\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"ADMIN, or the author while not ARCHIVED\" },\n121\t        \"canViewStats\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"ADMIN or the author\" }\n122\t      },\n123\t      \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"body\", \"status\", \"displayStatus\", \"author\", \"labels\", \"pinned\", \"requiresAck\", \"isPublic\", \"attachments\", \"canEdit\", \"canViewStats\"]\n124\t    },\n125\t    \"AudienceCounts\": {\n126\t      \"description\": \"Requirements: FR-14, FR-15.\",\n127\t      \"type\": \"object\",\n128\t      \"properties\": {\n129\t        \"total\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n130\t        \"byRole\": {\n131\t          \"type\": \"object\",\n132\t          \"properties\": {\n133\t            \"STUDENT\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n134\t            \"PARENT\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n135\t            \"TEACHER\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n136\t            \"ADMIN\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n137\t          },\n138\t          \"required\": [\"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\", \"TEACHER\", \"ADMIN\"]\n139\t        }\n140\t      },\n141\t      \"required\": [\"total\", \"byRole\"]\n142\t    }\n143\t  },\n144\t\n145\t  \"endpoints\": [\n146\t    {\n147\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n148\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements\",\n149\t      \"description\": \"Feed for the caller (any authenticated role). Only visible announcements whose audience includes the caller, resolved with audiences.some(audienceWhere(keys)) and never by expanding recipients (NFR-2). Page 1 starts with up to 3 pinned items (newest first, pinned=true), followed by the page of remaining items in publishAt desc, id desc order. meta.total excludes those lifted pins. Extra pinned items appear in date order with pinned=false (A4). With courseId, the caller must pass assertCanViewCourse (else 404) and results are limited to rows with a COURSE audience for that course. Expired, scheduled-future, draft and archived items are never returned.\",\n150\t      \"auth\": \"requireUser\",\n151\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n152\t        \"query\": {\n153\t          \"tab\": { \"enum\": [\"all\", \"unread\", \"ack\"], \"default\": \"all\", \"description\": \"unread = no readAt; ack = requiresAck and not acknowledged by the caller\" },\n154\t          \"courseId\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Optional. Course 'Announcements' tab\" },\n155\t          \"page\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"default\": 1 },\n156\t          \"pageSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 100, \"default\": 20 }\n157\t        }\n158\t      },\n159\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n160\t        \"status\": 200,\n161\t        \"body\": {\n162\t          \"data\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/FeedItem\" } },\n163\t          \"meta\": { \"page\": \"integer\", \"pageSize\": \"integer\", \"total\": \"integer\" }\n164\t        }\n165\t      },\n166\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR (bad query)\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (courseId the caller cannot view)\"],\n167\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-22\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-5\", \"NFR-6\"]\n168\t    },\n169\t    {\n170\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n171\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements\",\n172\t      \"description\": \"Create an announcement. assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic) runs first. A TEACHER may target only COURSE rows for courses where they are teacherId or in coTeacherIds, and SECTION rows for the section they homeroom. Anything else, or isPublic=true, returns 403. For mode publish or schedule, zero resolved recipients returns 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (details.reason='NO_RECIPIENTS'). Drafts may have zero recipients. A single transaction writes the announcement, audience rows and attachment rows and calls attachFiles. mode=publish sets status PUBLISHED and publishAt=now, then claimAndNotify sends announcement.published exactly once (generic-notification email, 300-character plain-text body, 'Read announcement' link to /announcements/:id, mandatoryInApp = requiresAck). mode=schedule sets status SCHEDULED and does not notify. mode=draft sets status DRAFT.\",\n173\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n174\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"body\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementInput\" } },\n175\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n176\t        \"status\": 201,\n177\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementDetail\" } }\n178\t      },\n179\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR (Zod: title > 150, body > 20,000, schedule without a future publishAt, expiresAt ≤ publishAt; or NO_RECIPIENTS on publish/schedule)\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT; teacher targeting SCHOOL/STAFF/ROLE/GRADE_LEVEL, a foreign course or section, or isPublic)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (coverFileId or attachment not owned by the caller or not uploaded)\"],\n180\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-26\", \"FR-27\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n181\t    },\n182\t    {\n183\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n184\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/unread-count\",\n185\t      \"description\": \"Sidebar badge count. Uses the same where clause as the feed's 'all' tab plus reads.none{userId, readAt not null}. Polled every 30 seconds, only while the page is visible.\",\n186\t      \"auth\": \"requireUser\",\n187\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n188\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n189\t        \"status\": 200,\n190\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"count\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0 } } }\n191\t      },\n192\t      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\"],\n193\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-32\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]\n194\t    },\n195\t    {\n196\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n197\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/preview-audience\",\n198\t      \"description\": \"Live recipient count for the composer ('Will reach 412 people: 180 students, 214 parents, 18 teachers'). assertCanTarget(user, audiences, false) runs first, so teachers cannot probe the size of audiences they cannot target. Then countAudienceByRole. ACTIVE, non-archived users only, deduplicated. The client debounces calls by 400 ms.\",\n199\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n200\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n201\t        \"body\": {\n202\t          \"audiences\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceRow\" }, \"maxItems\": 20 }\n203\t        }\n204\t      },\n205\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n206\t        \"status\": 200,\n207\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceCounts\" } }\n208\t      },\n209\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (role, or teacher targeting violation)\"],\n210\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n211\t    },\n212\t    {\n213\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n214\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/manage\",\n215\t      \"description\": \"Manage list with no visibility filter, so it includes drafts, scheduled, expired and archived items. TEACHER sees authorId = me; ADMIN sees all. Ordered by updatedAt desc. reach, readPct and ackPct are computed live against the current resolveAudienceUserIds, and reads from users who have left the audience are excluded. Percentages are integers rounded half-up; they are null when reach is 0, and ackPct is null when requiresAck is false.\",\n216\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n217\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n218\t        \"query\": {\n219\t          \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"EXPIRED\", \"ARCHIVED\"], \"description\": \"Optional filter on displayStatus\" },\n220\t          \"page\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"default\": 1 },\n221\t          \"pageSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 50, \"default\": 20 }\n222\t        }\n223\t      },\n224\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n225\t        \"status\": 200,\n226\t        \"body\": {\n227\t          \"data\": {\n228\t            \"type\": \"array\",\n229\t            \"items\": {\n230\t              \"type\": \"object\",\n231\t              \"properties\": {\n232\t                \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n233\t                \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n234\t                \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n235\t                \"displayStatus\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"EXPIRED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n236\t                \"author\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Author\" },\n237\t                \"audienceSummary\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"audienceLabels(rows)\" },\n238\t                \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n239\t                \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n240\t                \"isPublic\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n241\t                \"publishAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n242\t                \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n243\t                \"reach\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n244\t                \"readPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100 },\n245\t                \"ackPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100 },\n246\t                \"updatedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n247\t              },\n248\t              \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"status\", \"displayStatus\", \"author\", \"audienceSummary\", \"reach\", \"readPct\", \"ackPct\"]\n249\t            }\n250\t          },\n251\t          \"meta\": { \"page\": \"integer\", \"pageSize\": \"integer\", \"total\": \"integer\" }\n252\t        }\n253\t      },\n254\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\"],\n255\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-23\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n256\t    },\n257\t    {\n258\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n259\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id\",\n260\t      \"description\": \"Detail. Allowed for ADMIN, the author (any status), or an audience member while the announcement is visible. Everyone else gets 404, including members before publishAt or after expiry. For audience members only, the call upserts AnnouncementRead.readAt and keeps the first readAt. The edit page (/announcements/:id/edit) uses the same endpoint and reads audiences from it when canEdit.\",\n261\t      \"auth\": \"requireUser (service gates)\",\n262\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n263\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n264\t        \"status\": 200,\n265\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementDetail\" } }\n266\t      },\n267\t      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (missing, or not visible to the caller)\"],\n268\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-19\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-6\"]\n269\t    },\n270\t    {\n271\t      \"method\": \"PATCH\",\n272\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id\",\n273\t      \"description\": \"Update. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. A non-admin editing an ARCHIVED row gets 409 CONFLICT (archive is terminal for authors). If audiences or isPublic is in the patch, assertCanTarget re-runs on the resulting values. audiences, when sent, replaces all rows. attachmentFileIds, when sent, re-syncs attachments (attaches new ones, detaches removed ones). A transition from DRAFT to publish or schedule re-checks for zero recipients and, for publish, calls claimAndNotify. Edits to an already-notified announcement, including audience changes, never re-notify, because notifiedAt is never cleared. An ADMIN editing someone else's announcement writes audit('announcement.update'). mode=draft on a PUBLISHED row returns 409 (unpublishing is done by archiving).\",\n274\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n275\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n276\t        \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n277\t        \"body\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementPatch\" }\n278\t      },\n279\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n280\t        \"status\": 200,\n281\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementDetail\" } }\n282\t      },\n283\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR (Zod or NO_RECIPIENTS)\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (role or targeting violation)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (not author/admin)\", \"409 CONFLICT (author editing ARCHIVED; PUBLISHED → draft)\"],\n284\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-27\", \"FR-29\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n285\t    },\n286\t    {\n287\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n288\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/archive\",\n289\t      \"description\": \"Archive: sets status ARCHIVED. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. Idempotent: archiving an already-archived row returns 200 with the current record. An ADMIN archiving someone else's announcement writes audit('announcement.archive').\",\n290\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n291\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"body\": {} },\n292\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n293\t        \"status\": 200,\n294\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"ARCHIVED\" } }\n295\t      },\n296\t      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND\"],\n297\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n298\t    },\n299\t    {\n300\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n301\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/ack\",\n302\t      \"description\": \"Acknowledge. Requires a visible announcement and audience membership; otherwise 404. A row with requiresAck=false returns 409. Upserts AnnouncementRead, sets acknowledgedAt once and also sets readAt if it was empty. Repeat calls are idempotent and return the original acknowledgedAt. The UI shows 'Acknowledged on 14 Sep' in the school timezone.\",\n303\t      \"auth\": \"requireUser (service gates)\",\n304\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"body\": {} },\n305\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n306\t        \"status\": 200,\n307\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"readAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }, \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" } } }\n308\t      },\n309\t      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (not visible or not a member)\", \"409 CONFLICT (requiresAck=false)\"],\n310\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-7\"]\n311\t    },\n312\t    {\n313\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n314\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/stats\",\n315\t      \"description\": \"Per-announcement stats. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. Recipients come from the live resolveAudienceUserIds, left-joined to AnnouncementRead. The counts always describe the full audience, while the filter applies only to the rows. With format=csv, the response is text/csv with Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\\\"announcement-<id>-recipients.csv\\\", built by toCsv from src/server/csv.ts with the columns Name, Role, Read at and Acknowledged at, dates in the school timezone, and the filter applied. Rows are sorted by name.\",\n316\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n317\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n318\t        \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n319\t        \"query\": {\n320\t          \"filter\": { \"enum\": [\"unread\", \"unacked\"], \"description\": \"Optional. unacked is only meaningful when requiresAck\" },\n321\t          \"format\": { \"enum\": [\"csv\"], \"description\": \"Optional\" }\n322\t        }\n323\t      },\n324\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n325\t        \"status\": 200,\n326\t        \"body\": {\n327\t          \"data\": {\n328\t            \"counts\": {\n329\t              \"type\": \"object\",\n330\t              \"properties\": {\n331\t                \"recipients\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n332\t                \"read\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n333\t                \"acknowledged\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n334\t                \"readPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Rounded half-up; null when recipients is 0\" },\n335\t                \"ackPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"null when !requiresAck or recipients is 0. AC-5: 30/50 → 60\" }\n336\t              }\n337\t            },\n338\t            \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n339\t            \"lastRemindedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n340\t            \"rows\": {\n341\t              \"type\": \"array\",\n342\t              \"items\": {\n343\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n344\t                \"properties\": {\n345\t                  \"userId\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n346\t                  \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n347\t                  \"role\": { \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\", \"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\"] },\n348\t                  \"readAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n349\t                  \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n350\t                }\n351\t              }\n352\t            }\n353\t          }\n354\t        },\n355\t        \"csvVariant\": \"200 text/csv; charset=utf-8 (no JSON envelope)\"\n356\t      },\n357\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (not author/admin)\"],\n358\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-7\"]\n359\t    },\n360\t    {\n361\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n362\t      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/remind\",\n363\t      \"description\": \"Send a reminder to recipients who have not acknowledged. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. The announcement must have requiresAck and be visible; otherwise 409. The throttle is claimed atomically: updateMany where lastRemindedAt is null or ≤ now − 24h sets lastRemindedAt = now. If no row is claimed, the response is 429 RATE_LIMITED with details.retryAfter (ISO, lastRemindedAt + 24h). Otherwise it calls notify('announcement.reminder', mandatoryInApp) for recipients minus acknowledged users. If nobody is left to remind, it still claims the throttle and returns notified: 0. AC-5: 50 recipients with 30 acknowledged → notified 20.\",\n364\t      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n365\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"body\": {} },\n366\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n367\t        \"status\": 200,\n368\t        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"notified\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }, \"remindedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" } } }\n369\t      },\n370\t      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND\", \"409 CONFLICT (!requiresAck or not visible)\", \"429 RATE_LIMITED { details: { retryAfter } }\"],\n371\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\", \"FR-26\", \"FR-34\"]\n372\t    },\n373\t    {\n374\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n375\t      \"path\": \"/api/public/news\",\n376\t      \"description\": \"Public news for the future PRD-18 website. No authentication. The path is added to PUBLIC_API_PATHS in src/config/public-routes.ts. Rate-limited by client IP with the existing src/server/rate-limit.ts, which returns 429 RATE_LIMITED. Returns isPublic ∧ visible announcements, newest first. The DTO deliberately omits author identity, audience and read data. Cover images and attachments are served through GET /api/files/:id, which the 'announcement' file resolver allows anonymously only for public, visible announcements.\",\n377\t      \"auth\": \"none (public)\",\n378\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n379\t        \"query\": {\n380\t          \"page\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"default\": 1 },\n381\t          \"pageSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 100, \"default\": 20 }\n382\t        }\n383\t      },\n384\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n385\t        \"status\": 200,\n386\t        \"body\": {\n387\t          \"data\": {\n388\t            \"type\": \"array\",\n389\t            \"items\": {\n390\t              \"type\": \"object\",\n391\t              \"properties\": {\n392\t                \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n393\t                \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n394\t                \"excerpt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 200 },\n395\t                \"body\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Raw Markdown; consumers must sanitise (MarkdownView)\" },\n396\t                \"publishAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n397\t                \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n398\t                \"attachments\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } } }\n399\t              },\n400\t              \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"excerpt\", \"body\", \"publishAt\", \"attachments\"]\n401\t            }\n402\t          },\n403\t          \"meta\": { \"page\": \"integer\", \"pageSize\": \"integer\", \"total\": \"integer\" }\n404\t        }\n405\t      },\n406\t      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"429 RATE_LIMITED\"],\n407\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-9\"]\n408\t    }\n409\t  ],\n410\t\n411\t  \"internalHooks\": [\n412\t    {\n413\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n414\t      \"path\": \"/api/internal/email/dispatch\",\n415\t      \"description\": \"Existing endpoint, gated by CRON_SECRET; its contract is unchanged. It gains an isolated publishDueAnnouncements(now) pass (findMany SCHEDULED ∧ notifiedAt null ∧ publishAt ≤ now, take 50 → claimAndNotify each). The pass is idempotent under concurrent runs. The response may add an 'announcementsPublished' integer next to the existing counters.\",\n416\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-27\", \"NFR-11\"]\n417\t    },\n418\t    {\n419\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n420\t      \"path\": \"/api/files/:id\",\n421\t      \"description\": \"Existing endpoint; its contract is unchanged. It gains the new 'announcement' access context: allowed for anyone (including anonymous callers) if isPublic ∧ visible; otherwise for ADMIN, the author, or a member while visible; otherwise denied.\",\n422\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-30\", \"NFR-6\"]\n423\t    }\n424\t  ],\n425\t\n426\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n427\t}\n428\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b1bd2b-11e1-4a1f-b283-c14aefbd3b9a","uuid":"b516e28c-dd97-49c5-8fd9-caa0e7edc7cf","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:36:53.720Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"replaces\": \"This file replaces the SH-11 contracts that were here before.\",\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (the existing SchoolHub convention, not /api/v1). Route files are src/app/api/**/route.ts. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n    \"handlerPipeline\": \"withHandler → requireUser / requireRole → parseQuery / parseBody with a Zod schema from src/lib/validators/announcements.ts → one call into src/server/announcements/announcements-service.ts → ok(data) / ok(data, {status: 201}) / paginated(data, meta). No business logic in routes. Requirements: FR-34, FR-36, NFR-8.\",\n    \"successEnvelope\": \"{ \\\"data\\\": <responseSchema> }. Paginated endpoints return { \\\"data\\\": [...], \\\"meta\\\": { page, pageSize, total } } via paginated() in src/server/http.ts. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n    \"pagination\": \"?page (≥1, default 1) & ?pageSize (default 20, max 100 via parsePagination; GET /api/announcements/manage clamps to 50 because it computes live reach per row). Requirements: FR-17, FR-23, FR-31.\",\n    \"errorEnvelope\": \"{ \\\"error\\\": { \\\"code\\\": ApiErrorCode, \\\"message\\\": string, \\\"details\\\"?: unknown } }. VALIDATION_ERROR 400 (Zod: details = error.flatten()), UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n    \"accessErrors\": \"Targeting violations on create, update and preview return 403 FORBIDDEN (AC-3). STUDENT/PARENT on ADMIN/TEACHER routes get 403 from requireRole (FR-11). Callers who may not see a specific announcement (non-member, non-author, or not yet visible) get 404 NOT_FOUND on detail, ack, stats, remind, PATCH and archive, so its existence is not leaked (system-design A10). Requirements: NFR-3, NFR-6.\",\n    \"dates\": \"All timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC strings. The composer converts SchoolSettings.timezone input to UTC before sending. Clients display with formatInSchoolTz. Requirement: NFR-7.\",\n    \"visibility\": \"visible = status ∈ {SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED} ∧ publishAt ≤ now ∧ (expiresAt null ∨ expiresAt > now), evaluated at read time. Requirements: FR-16, NFR-6.\",\n    \"sanitisation\": \"`body` is raw Markdown, rendered client-side only through MarkdownView (rehype-sanitize). `excerpt` is plain text from toPlainText and must be rendered as escaped text. Requirement: NFR-4.\"\n  },\n\n  \"components\": {\n    \"AudienceRow\": {\n      \"description\": \"Generic audience row (FR-8). refId is required unless the type is SCHOOL or STAFF. For ROLE it must be a Role value. For GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE, at least one include flag must be true. Requirements: FR-1, FR-3..FR-6.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"type\": { \"enum\": [\"SCHOOL\", \"STAFF\", \"ROLE\", \"GRADE_LEVEL\", \"SECTION\", \"COURSE\"] },\n        \"refId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"GradeLevel.id | Section.id | Course.id | Role value\" },\n        \"includeStudents\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true },\n        \"includeParents\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true },\n        \"includeTeachers\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"type\"]\n    },\n    \"AnnouncementInput\": {\n      \"description\": \"Body of POST /api/announcements. Mirrors announcementInputSchema. Requirements: FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 150, \"description\": \"Trimmed\" },\n        \"body\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 20000, \"description\": \"Markdown\" },\n        \"audiences\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceRow\" }, \"minItems\": 0, \"maxItems\": 20 },\n        \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false },\n        \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false },\n        \"isPublic\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false, \"description\": \"ADMIN only. true from a TEACHER → 403 (FR-10)\" },\n        \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"FileObject id uploaded with context 'announcement'\" },\n        \"attachmentFileIds\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"maxItems\": 10, \"default\": [] },\n        \"mode\": { \"enum\": [\"draft\", \"publish\", \"schedule\"] },\n        \"publishAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\", \"description\": \"Required and > now when mode = schedule. Ignored for publish (set to now)\" },\n        \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\", \"description\": \"Must be > (publishAt ?? now)\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\", \"audiences\", \"mode\"]\n    },\n    \"AnnouncementPatch\": {\n      \"description\": \"AnnouncementInput with every field optional (announcementPatchSchema). audiences, when present, replaces all rows. Requirements: FR-12, FR-29.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"allOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementInput\" }],\n      \"required\": []\n    },\n    \"Author\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"role\": { \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\"] }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"role\"]\n    },\n    \"Attachment\": {\n      \"description\": \"Download via the existing GET /api/files/:id, gated by the 'announcement' file context (FR-30).\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"FileObject id\" },\n        \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"mimeType\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"size\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\"]\n    },\n    \"FeedItem\": {\n      \"description\": \"Feed card DTO. Requirements: FR-17, FR-18, FR-22, NFR-5.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"excerpt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 200, \"description\": \"Plain text (toPlainText(body, 200))\" },\n        \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"author\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Author\" },\n        \"publishAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"true only for the ≤3 items lifted to the top of page 1\" },\n        \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"labels\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"Audience chips, e.g. 'Grade 7 · Parents'\" },\n        \"attachmentCount\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n        \"unread\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"No AnnouncementRead.readAt for the caller. UI shows a dot with visually hidden text 'Unread'\" },\n        \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"forChildren\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"firstName\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }, \"description\": \"PARENT callers only; empty otherwise. The linked children that put the parent in a GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION or COURSE audience ('For Sam')\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"excerpt\", \"author\", \"publishAt\", \"pinned\", \"requiresAck\", \"labels\", \"attachmentCount\", \"unread\", \"forChildren\"]\n    },\n    \"AnnouncementDetail\": {\n      \"description\": \"Full record for detail and edit. Requirements: FR-13, FR-19, FR-20.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"body\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Raw Markdown. Render only via MarkdownView\" },\n        \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n        \"displayStatus\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"EXPIRED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n        \"author\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Author\" },\n        \"audiences\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceRow\" }, \"description\": \"Returned only when canEdit; [] otherwise\" },\n        \"labels\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"isPublic\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"attachments\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Attachment\" } },\n        \"publishAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"createdAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"updatedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n        \"myRead\": { \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"], \"properties\": { \"readAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" }, \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" } }, \"description\": \"null when the caller is not an audience member (for example an admin outside the audience)\" },\n        \"canEdit\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"ADMIN, or the author while not ARCHIVED\" },\n        \"canViewStats\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"ADMIN or the author\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"body\", \"status\", \"displayStatus\", \"author\", \"labels\", \"pinned\", \"requiresAck\", \"isPublic\", \"attachments\", \"canEdit\", \"canViewStats\"]\n    },\n    \"AudienceCounts\": {\n      \"description\": \"Requirements: FR-14, FR-15.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"total\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n        \"byRole\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"STUDENT\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n            \"PARENT\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n            \"TEACHER\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n            \"ADMIN\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\", \"TEACHER\", \"ADMIN\"]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"total\", \"byRole\"]\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements\",\n      \"description\": \"Feed for the caller (any authenticated role). Only visible announcements whose audience includes the caller, resolved with audiences.some(audienceWhere(keys)) and never by expanding recipients (NFR-2). Page 1 starts with up to 3 pinned items (newest first, pinned=true), followed by the page of remaining items in publishAt desc, id desc order. meta.total excludes those lifted pins. Extra pinned items appear in date order with pinned=false (A4). With courseId, the caller must pass assertCanViewCourse (else 404) and results are limited to rows with a COURSE audience for that course. Expired, scheduled-future, draft and archived items are never returned.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireUser\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"query\": {\n          \"tab\": { \"enum\": [\"all\", \"unread\", \"ack\"], \"default\": \"all\", \"description\": \"unread = no readAt; ack = requiresAck and not acknowledged by the caller\" },\n          \"courseId\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Optional. Course 'Announcements' tab\" },\n          \"page\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"default\": 1 },\n          \"pageSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 100, \"default\": 20 }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": {\n          \"data\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/FeedItem\" } },\n          \"meta\": { \"page\": \"integer\", \"pageSize\": \"integer\", \"total\": \"integer\" }\n        }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR (bad query)\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (courseId the caller cannot view)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-22\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-5\", \"NFR-6\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements\",\n      \"description\": \"Create an announcement. assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic) runs first. A TEACHER may target only COURSE rows for courses where they are teacherId or in coTeacherIds, and SECTION rows for the section they homeroom. Anything else, or isPublic=true, returns 403. For mode publish or schedule, zero resolved recipients returns 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (details.reason='NO_RECIPIENTS'). Drafts may have zero recipients. A single transaction writes the announcement, audience rows and attachment rows and calls attachFiles. mode=publish sets status PUBLISHED and publishAt=now, then claimAndNotify sends announcement.published exactly once (generic-notification email, 300-character plain-text body, 'Read announcement' link to /announcements/:id, mandatoryInApp = requiresAck). mode=schedule sets status SCHEDULED and does not notify. mode=draft sets status DRAFT.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"body\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementInput\" } },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 201,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementDetail\" } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR (Zod: title > 150, body > 20,000, schedule without a future publishAt, expiresAt ≤ publishAt; or NO_RECIPIENTS on publish/schedule)\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT; teacher targeting SCHOOL/STAFF/ROLE/GRADE_LEVEL, a foreign course or section, or isPublic)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (coverFileId or attachment not owned by the caller or not uploaded)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-26\", \"FR-27\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/unread-count\",\n      \"description\": \"Sidebar badge count. Uses the same where clause as the feed's 'all' tab plus reads.none{userId, readAt not null}. Polled every 30 seconds, only while the page is visible.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireUser\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"count\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0 } } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-32\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/preview-audience\",\n      \"description\": \"Live recipient count for the composer ('Will reach 412 people: 180 students, 214 parents, 18 teachers'). assertCanTarget(user, audiences, false) runs first, so teachers cannot probe the size of audiences they cannot target. Then countAudienceByRole. ACTIVE, non-archived users only, deduplicated. The client debounces calls by 400 ms.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"body\": {\n          \"audiences\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceRow\" }, \"maxItems\": 20 }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AudienceCounts\" } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (role, or teacher targeting violation)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/manage\",\n      \"description\": \"Manage list with no visibility filter, so it includes drafts, scheduled, expired and archived items. TEACHER sees authorId = me; ADMIN sees all. Ordered by updatedAt desc. reach, readPct and ackPct are computed live against the current resolveAudienceUserIds, and reads from users who have left the audience are excluded. Percentages are integers rounded half-up; they are null when reach is 0, and ackPct is null when requiresAck is false.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"query\": {\n          \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"EXPIRED\", \"ARCHIVED\"], \"description\": \"Optional filter on displayStatus\" },\n          \"page\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"default\": 1 },\n          \"pageSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 50, \"default\": 20 }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n                \"displayStatus\": { \"enum\": [\"DRAFT\", \"SCHEDULED\", \"PUBLISHED\", \"EXPIRED\", \"ARCHIVED\"] },\n                \"author\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/Author\" },\n                \"audienceSummary\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"description\": \"audienceLabels(rows)\" },\n                \"pinned\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n                \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n                \"isPublic\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n                \"publishAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n                \"expiresAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n                \"reach\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n                \"readPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100 },\n                \"ackPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100 },\n                \"updatedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n              },\n              \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"status\", \"displayStatus\", \"author\", \"audienceSummary\", \"reach\", \"readPct\", \"ackPct\"]\n            }\n          },\n          \"meta\": { \"page\": \"integer\", \"pageSize\": \"integer\", \"total\": \"integer\" }\n        }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-23\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id\",\n      \"description\": \"Detail. Allowed for ADMIN, the author (any status), or an audience member while the announcement is visible. Everyone else gets 404, including members before publishAt or after expiry. For audience members only, the call upserts AnnouncementRead.readAt and keeps the first readAt. The edit page (/announcements/:id/edit) uses the same endpoint and reads audiences from it when canEdit.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireUser (service gates)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementDetail\" } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (missing, or not visible to the caller)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-19\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-6\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"PATCH\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id\",\n      \"description\": \"Update. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. A non-admin editing an ARCHIVED row gets 409 CONFLICT (archive is terminal for authors). If audiences or isPublic is in the patch, assertCanTarget re-runs on the resulting values. audiences, when sent, replaces all rows. attachmentFileIds, when sent, re-syncs attachments (attaches new ones, detaches removed ones). A transition from DRAFT to publish or schedule re-checks for zero recipients and, for publish, calls claimAndNotify. Edits to an already-notified announcement, including audience changes, never re-notify, because notifiedAt is never cleared. An ADMIN editing someone else's announcement writes audit('announcement.update'). mode=draft on a PUBLISHED row returns 409 (unpublishing is done by archiving).\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"body\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementPatch\" }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"$ref\": \"#/components/AnnouncementDetail\" } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR (Zod or NO_RECIPIENTS)\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (role or targeting violation)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (not author/admin)\", \"409 CONFLICT (author editing ARCHIVED; PUBLISHED → draft)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-15\", \"FR-27\", \"FR-29\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/archive\",\n      \"description\": \"Archive: sets status ARCHIVED. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. Idempotent: archiving an already-archived row returns 200 with the current record. An ADMIN archiving someone else's announcement writes audit('announcement.archive').\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"body\": {} },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"status\": \"ARCHIVED\" } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/ack\",\n      \"description\": \"Acknowledge. Requires a visible announcement and audience membership; otherwise 404. A row with requiresAck=false returns 409. Upserts AnnouncementRead, sets acknowledgedAt once and also sets readAt if it was empty. Repeat calls are idempotent and return the original acknowledgedAt. The UI shows 'Acknowledged on 14 Sep' in the school timezone.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireUser (service gates)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"body\": {} },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"readAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }, \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" } } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (not visible or not a member)\", \"409 CONFLICT (requiresAck=false)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-20\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/stats\",\n      \"description\": \"Per-announcement stats. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. Recipients come from the live resolveAudienceUserIds, left-joined to AnnouncementRead. The counts always describe the full audience, while the filter applies only to the rows. With format=csv, the response is text/csv with Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\\\"announcement-<id>-recipients.csv\\\", built by toCsv from src/server/csv.ts with the columns Name, Role, Read at and Acknowledged at, dates in the school timezone, and the filter applied. Rows are sorted by name.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"query\": {\n          \"filter\": { \"enum\": [\"unread\", \"unacked\"], \"description\": \"Optional. unacked is only meaningful when requiresAck\" },\n          \"format\": { \"enum\": [\"csv\"], \"description\": \"Optional\" }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"counts\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"recipients\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n                \"read\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n                \"acknowledged\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n                \"readPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Rounded half-up; null when recipients is 0\" },\n                \"ackPct\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"null when !requiresAck or recipients is 0. AC-5: 30/50 → 60\" }\n              }\n            },\n            \"requiresAck\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n            \"lastRemindedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n            \"rows\": {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"userId\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"role\": { \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\", \"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\"] },\n                  \"readAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n                  \"acknowledgedAt\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"csvVariant\": \"200 text/csv; charset=utf-8 (no JSON envelope)\"\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND (not author/admin)\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-6\", \"NFR-7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/announcements/:id/remind\",\n      \"description\": \"Send a reminder to recipients who have not acknowledged. Allowed for the author or ADMIN; others get 404. The announcement must have requiresAck and be visible; otherwise 409. The throttle is claimed atomically: updateMany where lastRemindedAt is null or ≤ now − 24h sets lastRemindedAt = now. If no row is claimed, the response is 429 RATE_LIMITED with details.retryAfter (ISO, lastRemindedAt + 24h). Otherwise it calls notify('announcement.reminder', mandatoryInApp) for recipients minus acknowledged users. If nobody is left to remind, it still claims the throttle and returns notified: 0. AC-5: 50 recipients with 30 acknowledged → notified 20.\",\n      \"auth\": \"requireRole(ADMIN, TEACHER)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"params\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"body\": {} },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": { \"data\": { \"notified\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }, \"remindedAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" } } }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"401 UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"403 FORBIDDEN (STUDENT/PARENT)\", \"404 NOT_FOUND\", \"409 CONFLICT (!requiresAck or not visible)\", \"429 RATE_LIMITED { details: { retryAfter } }\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\", \"FR-26\", \"FR-34\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/public/news\",\n      \"description\": \"Public news for the future PRD-18 website. No authentication. The path is added to PUBLIC_API_PATHS in src/config/public-routes.ts. Rate-limited by client IP with the existing src/server/rate-limit.ts, which returns 429 RATE_LIMITED. Returns isPublic ∧ visible announcements, newest first. The DTO deliberately omits author identity, audience and read data. Cover images and attachments are served through GET /api/files/:id, which the 'announcement' file resolver allows anonymously only for public, visible announcements.\",\n      \"auth\": \"none (public)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"query\": {\n          \"page\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"default\": 1 },\n          \"pageSize\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 100, \"default\": 20 }\n        }\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"status\": 200,\n        \"body\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                \"excerpt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 200 },\n                \"body\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Raw Markdown; consumers must sanitise (MarkdownView)\" },\n                \"publishAt\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n                \"coverFileId\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n                \"attachments\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } } }\n              },\n              \"required\": [\"id\", \"title\", \"excerpt\", \"body\", \"publishAt\", \"attachments\"]\n            }\n          },\n          \"meta\": { \"page\": \"integer\", \"pageSize\": \"integer\", \"total\": \"integer\" }\n        }\n      },\n      \"errors\": [\"400 VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"429 RATE_LIMITED\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-9\"]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"internalHooks\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/internal/email/dispatch\",\n      \"description\": \"Existing endpoint, gated by CRON_SECRET; its contract is unchanged. It gains an isolated publishDueAnnouncements(now) pass (findMany SCHEDULED ∧ notifiedAt null ∧ publishAt ≤ now, take 50 → claimAndNotify each). The pass is idempotent under concurrent runs. The response may add an 'announcementsPublished' integer next to the existing counters.\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-27\", \"NFR-11\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/files/:id\",\n      \"description\": \"Existing endpoint; its contract is unchanged. It gains the new 'announcement' access context: allowed for anyone (including anonymous callers) if isPublic ∧ visible; otherwise for ADMIN, the author, or a member while visible; otherwise denied.\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-30\", \"NFR-6\"]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":428,"startLine":1,"totalLines":428}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015nYDRSHaUJk7oV3b99QR8S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsgSfJPNSmbAQojyJJVv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N6UwaxQjCFPSE6Y7tsdLPQ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":26003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1925,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b1bd2b-11e1-4a1f-b283-c14aefbd3b9a","uuid":"0ca76f9e-2491-4fd5-8f07-a402e0a95ce6","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:36:53.902Z","request_id":"req_011CgsgSf21wgEhr9Zhd6NL4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01N6UwaxQjCFPSE6Y7tsdLPQ":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N6UwaxQjCFPSE6Y7tsdLPQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-12 Announcements & News\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-12 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T18:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack (checked against `package.json`).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace matches it:\n6\t\n7\t- Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict\n8\t- Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8\n9\t- MUI 9.5.0: material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts\n10\t- react-markdown 10.1.0, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1\n11\t- date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse ^5.4.1\n12\t- `@react-email/*` and nodemailer\n13\t\n14\tIntake reported no blockers (`blockers: []`, confidence 94%). No NFR calls for a different stack:\n15\t\n16\t- **NFR-2** (feed for a parent with 3 children over 2,000 rows in under 200 ms): one Prisma query with an `EXISTS`-style `some` filter on `AnnouncementAudience`, using indexed columns.\n17\t- **FR-27** (exactly-once publish notification): an atomic `updateMany ... where notifiedAt IS NULL` claim inside the existing cron route.\n18\t\n19\tNone of this needs a cache, a queue, a job runner or a search engine.\n20\t\n21\t**Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-8, NFR-9).**\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n26\t\n27\t**Context.** NFR-8 requires reusing existing services and components. NFR-1 limits UI to MUI. Everything PRD-12 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n28\t\n29\t**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Each need maps to something that already exists:\n30\t\n31\t| Need | Use | Req |\n32\t|---|---|---|\n33\t| Schema and migration | Prisma 5.20 migration: 2 enums and 4 models, plus back-relations on `User` and `FileObject` | FR-1 |\n34\t| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, shared by the composer form (`react-hook-form` + `@hookform/resolvers`) and the route handlers | FR-2, FR-34 |\n35\t| Route handlers | `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` from `src/server/http.ts` | FR-17, FR-34 |\n36\t| Body editing and rendering | `src/components/MarkdownEditor` and `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize) | FR-13, FR-19, NFR-4 |\n37\t| Cover image and attachments | `FileUpload` and `FileList`, plus `registerFileAccess('announcement', …)` in `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | FR-13, FR-30 |\n38\t| Audience entity pickers | MUI `Autocomplete` (grade, section, course, role) and the existing `UserPicker` where users are involved | FR-13, NFR-1 |\n39\t| publishAt and expiresAt inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker`, converted with `date-fns-tz` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-13, FR-16, NFR-7 |\n40\t| Manage list and recipient table | `src/components/DataTable` | FR-23, FR-24 |\n41\t| CSV export | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-24 |\n42\t| Notifications and email | `notify()`, a new type in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and the `generic-notification` template | FR-26, FR-27, FR-28 |\n43\t| Audit | `audit()` from `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-12 |\n44\t| \"Acknowledged on 14 Sep\" | `formatInSchoolTz` from `src/lib/dates.ts` | FR-20, NFR-7 |\n45\t| Toasts and confirmations | `useToast()`, `ConfirmDialog` | NFR-1 |\n46\t| Logging | `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts` | NFR-11 |\n47\t\n48\t**Consequences.** There are no install or lockfile changes, and the banned-library QA check (NFR-1) stays trivially green. All new code goes in `src/server/announcements/`, `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, `src/app/(app)/announcements/**`, and `src/app/api/announcements/**` plus `src/app/api/public/news` (FR-36).\n49\t\n50\t---\n51\t\n52\t## ADR-2: Use Prisma relation filters for audience membership, with one shared rule module\n53\t\n54\t**Context.** FR-7 and NFR-2 require membership checks through SQL joins, never by loading all recipients. FR-7 and NFR-10 require `isUserInAudience` and `resolveAudienceUserIds` to agree for every seed user. FR-8 requires the module to be generic so PRD-14 calendar events can reuse it.\n55\t\n56\t**Decision.**\n57\t\n58\t1. `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` defines the audience row shape generically: `{ type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers }`. It does not import Announcement.\n59\t2. The module exports three functions, all built from one per-type rule table so the rules are written once:\n60\t   - `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`: per-type Prisma `user.findMany({ where: … , select: { id } })`, unioned into a `Set`.\n61\t   - `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`: the same per-type `where`, AND-ed with `id = user.id`, as a single `count`/`findFirst`.\n62\t   - `audienceWhereForUser(user)`: a Prisma `AnnouncementAudience` `where` fragment (an OR over the type branches) for the feed. The feed then runs `announcement.findMany({ where: { audiences: { some: audienceWhereForUser(user) } } })`. The user's context is precomputed once per request with a few indexed lookups: role, grade level, current-year section ids, active course ids, managed course ids, homeroom section, and the same values for each linked child of a parent. The branches then compare `refId` against small id lists.\n63\t3. Prisma relation filters (`some`) compile to `EXISTS` subqueries. Use `$queryRaw` only if a measured test misses the 200 ms target. Add a `ponytail:` note at that spot.\n64\t4. Indexes in the migration:\n65\t   - `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)`\n66\t   - `AnnouncementAudience(announcementId)`\n67\t   - `Announcement(status, publishAt)`\n68\t   - `Announcement(isPublic, status)`\n69\t   - `AnnouncementRead(userId)`, needed because the composite PK `(announcementId, userId)` doesn't serve lookups by `userId` alone (unread-count and the Unread tab)\n70\t\n71\t**Consequences.** There is no raw SQL by default, and the code stays type-safe. The property-style integration test (NFR-10) checks the shared rule table through both entry points. The feed cost does not grow with recipients: a parent with 3 children produces about 6 small `IN` lists.\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-3: Decide visibility at read time and send the notification through the existing cron route\n76\t\n77\t**Context.**\n78\t\n79\t- FR-16 and AC-4: a scheduled announcement becomes visible at `publishAt <= now` with no cron involved.\n80\t- FR-27: the notification is sent exactly once.\n81\t- The maintenance entry point is `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`. It runs isolated, idempotent passes in `try/catch`, and `src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts` claims work with `updateMany where releasedAt: null`.\n82\t\n83\t**Decision.**\n84\t\n85\t- The visibility predicate is `status IN (PUBLISHED, SCHEDULED) AND publishAt <= now AND (expiresAt IS NULL OR expiresAt > now)`. It is applied in the feed, the detail page, unread-count, public news and the file resolver. A SCHEDULED row whose time has passed is treated as published, so no status flip is needed for visibility.\n86\t- `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` lives in `src/server/announcements/maintenance.ts` and is called from the dispatch route as another isolated `try/catch` block. For each due row it claims the row with `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED } })`. It sends `notify()` only when `count === 1`. Batches are 50 rows, matching `dispatchEmails`.\n87\t- Publish-now uses the same claim and then notifies inline. Later audience edits never touch `notifiedAt`, which satisfies FR-29.\n88\t\n89\t**Consequences.** Concurrent cron runs cannot double-notify. No new scheduler is added. Notification latency for scheduled items equals the cron interval, and AC-4 allows this.\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## ADR-4: Reminder throttle uses an `Announcement.lastRemindedAt` column and 429 RATE_LIMITED\n94\t\n95\t**Context.** FR-25 refuses a second reminder within 24 hours and leaves the status code and storage to the architect. The FR-1 schema has no field for this. `src/server/rate-limit.ts` is per-process and in-memory, so it is the wrong tool for a durable per-announcement business rule. `http.ts` already maps `RATE_LIMITED` to 429.\n96\t\n97\t**Decision.**\n98\t\n99\t- Add a nullable `lastRemindedAt DateTime?` to `Announcement`. This is the only deviation from the FR-1 field list, and intake suggested it.\n100\t- Claim the reminder atomically: `updateMany({ where: { id, OR: [{ lastRemindedAt: null }, { lastRemindedAt: { lt: now - 24h } }] }, data: { lastRemindedAt: now } })`.\n101\t- If `count === 0`, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED', …)`, which returns 429. The details include `retryAfter` (an ISO timestamp).\n102\t- Otherwise notify recipients where the resolved audience has no `AnnouncementRead.acknowledgedAt`.\n103\t\n104\t**Consequences.** The rule survives restarts and multiple instances, and it is race-safe. 429 is the right semantic for \"try again later\". 409 would suggest a state conflict that the user could fix.\n105\t\n106\t---\n107\t\n108\t## ADR-5: Strip Markdown to plain text with a small local helper and no new library\n109\t\n110\t**Context.**\n111\t\n112\t- FR-18 needs a 200-character plain-text excerpt.\n113\t- FR-28 needs the first 300 characters of the body as plain text in the email.\n114\t- NFR-4 requires sanitisation.\n115\t- No Markdown-to-text helper exists in the repo. `remark`/`strip-markdown` are not direct dependencies.\n116\t\n117\t**Decision.** Add `toPlainText(md, max)` in `src/server/announcements/excerpt.ts`. It strips code fences, images, links (keeping the link text), HTML tags, emphasis, heading and list markers with about six regexes, collapses whitespace, and truncates with `…`. Its output is only ever rendered as a React text node or as a react-email text prop, both of which escape it. It is never fed into `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, so the sanitising boundary stays the escaping renderer. The full body always renders through `MarkdownView` (rehype-sanitize).\n118\t\n119\t**Consequences.** No dependency is added. Unusual Markdown, such as nested reference links, may leave stray characters in excerpts. That is cosmetic only. Mark it with `ponytail:`. If excerpts look wrong, switch to `remark` + `strip-markdown`.\n120\t\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t## ADR-6: Add a navigation badge as an optional `badge` field on NavItem, polled like NotificationBell\n124\t\n125\t**Context.** FR-32 needs an unread count on the sidebar. `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` already polls with MUI `Badge`.\n126\t\n127\t**Decision.**\n128\t\n129\t- Add an optional `badgeEndpoint?: string` to `NavItem`. The Announcements entry sets it to `/api/announcements/unread-count`.\n130\t- The sidebar renders MUI `Badge` around the icon and reuses the NotificationBell fetch/poll interval logic, extracted only if it is a direct copy.\n131\t- `unread-count` uses the visibility predicate from ADR-3 and `audienceWhereForUser` from ADR-2, plus `reads: { none: { userId } }`.\n132\t- The unread dot has visually hidden text \"Unread\" (NFR-5).\n133\t\n134\t**Consequences.** This is one optional field and one conditional `Badge`, and existing nav items are unaffected.\n135\t\n136\t---\n137\t\n138\t## ADR-7: Security boundaries\n139\t\n140\t**Context.** NFR-3, NFR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-30 and FR-31.\n141\t\n142\t**Decision.**\n143\t\n144\t- **Role checks.** Every handler starts with `requireRole`.\n145\t- **Teacher audience rules.** These checks live in one function, `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in `announcements-service.ts`, called from both POST and PATCH. A teacher may target:\n146\t  - COURSE, only when `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds` contains the teacher\n147\t  - SECTION, only when `homeroomTeacherId` is the teacher\n148\t\n149\t  Any other type, or `isPublic`, returns 403.\n150\t- **Non-members.** Detail, ack and stats return 404 to non-members. This avoids leaking that an announcement exists, and it matches the platform convention for hidden resources.\n151\t- **File access resolver.** Anonymous access is allowed only for `isPublic && visible(now)`. Everyone else goes through `isUserInAudience`, the author check or the ADMIN check.\n152\t- **Public route.** `/api/public/news` is added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. It selects only public-safe fields: no audience, no author email.\n153\t\n154\t**Consequences.** One choke point governs targeting rules, so the unit tests (NFR-10) cover it directly.\n155\t\n156\t---\n157\t\n158\t## Open items handed to arch-design-system\n159\t\n160\tThese come from the intake defaults, and the stack decisions don't change them:\n161\t\n162\t- FR-5: section membership means current academic year.\n163\t- FR-15: drafts may have zero recipients.\n164\t- FR-17: pins beyond 3 flow into newest-first order.\n165\t- FR-12: archive is terminal for authors.\n166\t- AC-8: the fixture creates Pat's 6A child.\n167\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b1bd2b-11e1-4a1f-b283-c14aefbd3b9a","uuid":"4e3b763b-b585-4f47-b084-8f4f895e4825","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:36:53.925Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-12 Announcements & News\n\nTicket: SH-12 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T18:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (checked against `package.json`).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace matches it:\n\n- Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict\n- Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8\n- MUI 9.5.0: material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts\n- react-markdown 10.1.0, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1\n- date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse ^5.4.1\n- `@react-email/*` and nodemailer\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`blockers: []`, confidence 94%). No NFR calls for a different stack:\n\n- **NFR-2** (feed for a parent with 3 children over 2,000 rows in under 200 ms): one Prisma query with an `EXISTS`-style `some` filter on `AnnouncementAudience`, using indexed columns.\n- **FR-27** (exactly-once publish notification): an atomic `updateMany ... where notifiedAt IS NULL` claim inside the existing cron route.\n\nNone of this needs a cache, a queue, a job runner or a search engine.\n\n**Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-8, NFR-9).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires reusing existing services and components. NFR-1 limits UI to MUI. Everything PRD-12 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Each need maps to something that already exists:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Schema and migration | Prisma 5.20 migration: 2 enums and 4 models, plus back-relations on `User` and `FileObject` | FR-1 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, shared by the composer form (`react-hook-form` + `@hookform/resolvers`) and the route handlers | FR-2, FR-34 |\n| Route handlers | `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` from `src/server/http.ts` | FR-17, FR-34 |\n| Body editing and rendering | `src/components/MarkdownEditor` and `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize) | FR-13, FR-19, NFR-4 |\n| Cover image and attachments | `FileUpload` and `FileList`, plus `registerFileAccess('announcement', …)` in `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | FR-13, FR-30 |\n| Audience entity pickers | MUI `Autocomplete` (grade, section, course, role) and the existing `UserPicker` where users are involved | FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| publishAt and expiresAt inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker`, converted with `date-fns-tz` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-13, FR-16, NFR-7 |\n| Manage list and recipient table | `src/components/DataTable` | FR-23, FR-24 |\n| CSV export | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-24 |\n| Notifications and email | `notify()`, a new type in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and the `generic-notification` template | FR-26, FR-27, FR-28 |\n| Audit | `audit()` from `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-12 |\n| \"Acknowledged on 14 Sep\" | `formatInSchoolTz` from `src/lib/dates.ts` | FR-20, NFR-7 |\n| Toasts and confirmations | `useToast()`, `ConfirmDialog` | NFR-1 |\n| Logging | `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts` | NFR-11 |\n\n**Consequences.** There are no install or lockfile changes, and the banned-library QA check (NFR-1) stays trivially green. All new code goes in `src/server/announcements/`, `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, `src/app/(app)/announcements/**`, and `src/app/api/announcements/**` plus `src/app/api/public/news` (FR-36).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Use Prisma relation filters for audience membership, with one shared rule module\n\n**Context.** FR-7 and NFR-2 require membership checks through SQL joins, never by loading all recipients. FR-7 and NFR-10 require `isUserInAudience` and `resolveAudienceUserIds` to agree for every seed user. FR-8 requires the module to be generic so PRD-14 calendar events can reuse it.\n\n**Decision.**\n\n1. `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` defines the audience row shape generically: `{ type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers }`. It does not import Announcement.\n2. The module exports three functions, all built from one per-type rule table so the rules are written once:\n   - `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`: per-type Prisma `user.findMany({ where: … , select: { id } })`, unioned into a `Set`.\n   - `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`: the same per-type `where`, AND-ed with `id = user.id`, as a single `count`/`findFirst`.\n   - `audienceWhereForUser(user)`: a Prisma `AnnouncementAudience` `where` fragment (an OR over the type branches) for the feed. The feed then runs `announcement.findMany({ where: { audiences: { some: audienceWhereForUser(user) } } })`. The user's context is precomputed once per request with a few indexed lookups: role, grade level, current-year section ids, active course ids, managed course ids, homeroom section, and the same values for each linked child of a parent. The branches then compare `refId` against small id lists.\n3. Prisma relation filters (`some`) compile to `EXISTS` subqueries. Use `$queryRaw` only if a measured test misses the 200 ms target. Add a `ponytail:` note at that spot.\n4. Indexes in the migration:\n   - `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)`\n   - `AnnouncementAudience(announcementId)`\n   - `Announcement(status, publishAt)`\n   - `Announcement(isPublic, status)`\n   - `AnnouncementRead(userId)`, needed because the composite PK `(announcementId, userId)` doesn't serve lookups by `userId` alone (unread-count and the Unread tab)\n\n**Consequences.** There is no raw SQL by default, and the code stays type-safe. The property-style integration test (NFR-10) checks the shared rule table through both entry points. The feed cost does not grow with recipients: a parent with 3 children produces about 6 small `IN` lists.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Decide visibility at read time and send the notification through the existing cron route\n\n**Context.**\n\n- FR-16 and AC-4: a scheduled announcement becomes visible at `publishAt <= now` with no cron involved.\n- FR-27: the notification is sent exactly once.\n- The maintenance entry point is `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`. It runs isolated, idempotent passes in `try/catch`, and `src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts` claims work with `updateMany where releasedAt: null`.\n\n**Decision.**\n\n- The visibility predicate is `status IN (PUBLISHED, SCHEDULED) AND publishAt <= now AND (expiresAt IS NULL OR expiresAt > now)`. It is applied in the feed, the detail page, unread-count, public news and the file resolver. A SCHEDULED row whose time has passed is treated as published, so no status flip is needed for visibility.\n- `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` lives in `src/server/announcements/maintenance.ts` and is called from the dispatch route as another isolated `try/catch` block. For each due row it claims the row with `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED } })`. It sends `notify()` only when `count === 1`. Batches are 50 rows, matching `dispatchEmails`.\n- Publish-now uses the same claim and then notifies inline. Later audience edits never touch `notifiedAt`, which satisfies FR-29.\n\n**Consequences.** Concurrent cron runs cannot double-notify. No new scheduler is added. Notification latency for scheduled items equals the cron interval, and AC-4 allows this.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Reminder throttle uses an `Announcement.lastRemindedAt` column and 429 RATE_LIMITED\n\n**Context.** FR-25 refuses a second reminder within 24 hours and leaves the status code and storage to the architect. The FR-1 schema has no field for this. `src/server/rate-limit.ts` is per-process and in-memory, so it is the wrong tool for a durable per-announcement business rule. `http.ts` already maps `RATE_LIMITED` to 429.\n\n**Decision.**\n\n- Add a nullable `lastRemindedAt DateTime?` to `Announcement`. This is the only deviation from the FR-1 field list, and intake suggested it.\n- Claim the reminder atomically: `updateMany({ where: { id, OR: [{ lastRemindedAt: null }, { lastRemindedAt: { lt: now - 24h } }] }, data: { lastRemindedAt: now } })`.\n- If `count === 0`, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED', …)`, which returns 429. The details include `retryAfter` (an ISO timestamp).\n- Otherwise notify recipients where the resolved audience has no `AnnouncementRead.acknowledgedAt`.\n\n**Consequences.** The rule survives restarts and multiple instances, and it is race-safe. 429 is the right semantic for \"try again later\". 409 would suggest a state conflict that the user could fix.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Strip Markdown to plain text with a small local helper and no new library\n\n**Context.**\n\n- FR-18 needs a 200-character plain-text excerpt.\n- FR-28 needs the first 300 characters of the body as plain text in the email.\n- NFR-4 requires sanitisation.\n- No Markdown-to-text helper exists in the repo. `remark`/`strip-markdown` are not direct dependencies.\n\n**Decision.** Add `toPlainText(md, max)` in `src/server/announcements/excerpt.ts`. It strips code fences, images, links (keeping the link text), HTML tags, emphasis, heading and list markers with about six regexes, collapses whitespace, and truncates with `…`. Its output is only ever rendered as a React text node or as a react-email text prop, both of which escape it. It is never fed into `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, so the sanitising boundary stays the escaping renderer. The full body always renders through `MarkdownView` (rehype-sanitize).\n\n**Consequences.** No dependency is added. Unusual Markdown, such as nested reference links, may leave stray characters in excerpts. That is cosmetic only. Mark it with `ponytail:`. If excerpts look wrong, switch to `remark` + `strip-markdown`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Add a navigation badge as an optional `badge` field on NavItem, polled like NotificationBell\n\n**Context.** FR-32 needs an unread count on the sidebar. `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` already polls with MUI `Badge`.\n\n**Decision.**\n\n- Add an optional `badgeEndpoint?: string` to `NavItem`. The Announcements entry sets it to `/api/announcements/unread-count`.\n- The sidebar renders MUI `Badge` around the icon and reuses the NotificationBell fetch/poll interval logic, extracted only if it is a direct copy.\n- `unread-count` uses the visibility predicate from ADR-3 and `audienceWhereForUser` from ADR-2, plus `reads: { none: { userId } }`.\n- The unread dot has visually hidden text \"Unread\" (NFR-5).\n\n**Consequences.** This is one optional field and one conditional `Badge`, and existing nav items are unaffected.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Security boundaries\n\n**Context.** NFR-3, NFR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-30 and FR-31.\n\n**Decision.**\n\n- **Role checks.** Every handler starts with `requireRole`.\n- **Teacher audience rules.** These checks live in one function, `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in `announcements-service.ts`, called from both POST and PATCH. A teacher may target:\n  - COURSE, only when `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds` contains the teacher\n  - SECTION, only when `homeroomTeacherId` is the teacher\n\n  Any other type, or `isPublic`, returns 403.\n- **Non-members.** Detail, ack and stats return 404 to non-members. This avoids leaking that an announcement exists, and it matches the platform convention for hidden resources.\n- **File access resolver.** Anonymous access is allowed only for `isPublic && visible(now)`. Everyone else goes through `isUserInAudience`, the author check or the ADMIN check.\n- **Public route.** `/api/public/news` is added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. It selects only public-safe fields: no audience, no author email.\n\n**Consequences.** One choke point governs targeting rules, so the unit tests (NFR-10) cover it directly.\n\n---\n\n## Open items handed to arch-design-system\n\nThese come from the intake defaults, and the stack decisions don't change them:\n\n- FR-5: section membership means current academic year.\n- FR-15: drafts may have zero recipients.\n- FR-17: pins beyond 3 flow into newest-first order.\n- FR-12: archive is terminal for authors.\n- AC-8: the fixture creates Pat's 6A child.\n","numLines":167,"startLine":1,"totalLines":167}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01N6UwaxQjCFPSE6Y7tsdLPQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
