{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsgaoo5VuDsKtFQ8dfr6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-12 dev-planning phase is finished. The plan has 21 tasks covering 50 file operations, about 47.5 hours in total, with `status: \"complete\"`.\n\nAll four files are in `artifacts/dev-planning/`: `file-structure.md`, `module-dependencies.json`, `file-ownership-matrix.json`, and `implementation-plan.json`, which was written last. I ran a check after writing them:\n- The plan and the ownership matrix list exactly the same file paths under the same task ids.\n- Every requirement id cited exists in `requirements.json`, and all 36 FR and 11 NFR are covered by at least one task.\n- Task dependencies only point to earlier tasks, so there are no cycles.\n- Every file marked MODIFY already exists in the repo, and every file marked CREATE does not yet.\n\n**Order of work:**\n1. TASK-1 is the database migration.\n2. TASK-2–5 are the input validation, excerpt helper, audience service and notification types.\n3. TASK-6–7 are the main announcements service: TASK-6 covers creating, editing and publishing, and TASK-7 covers the feed, stats, reminders and public news.\n4. TASK-8–12 are the scheduled-publish job, file access, the API routes and the public news route.\n5. TASK-13–18 are the sidebar badge and the pages.\n6. TASK-19 is the seed data; TASK-20–21 are the integration and end-to-end tests.\n\n**Where the plan differs from the architect's design:**\n- **Course route folder:** the design says `courses/[id]`, but the repo actually uses `courses/[courseId]`. The plan uses the real path, because later checks compare the developer's files against these exact paths.\n- **Sidebar:** there is no separate sidebar component. The menu is drawn in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, so TASK-13 adds the unread badge there.\n- **Main service file:** `announcements-service.ts` is split across two tasks, so the ownership matrix lists 